2026-27 Term 1','ACT2111 Introductory Financial Accounting','No co-requisite.','本课程旨在让学生对会计信息系统的设计、控制和操作有深入的了解，以促进管理决策的制定。重点在于确定主要业务流程的信息需求，并在设计会计信息系统时开发适当的业务流程控制。学生将掌握信息系统的基本概念，并运用分析技术(如数据流程图、流程图和REA图)来解释和开发会计信息系统。本课程还将介绍对会计信息系统可靠性的典型威胁，以及处理和减轻与这些威胁相关的风险的适用控制。业务流程中的风险和控制的讨论与计划学习审计课程的学生有关。关于收入、支出和工资周期的特殊主题将被涵盖。

学生将会学习使用金蝶的云星空系统，并学习如何设置系统和处理收入流程支出流程相关的业务处理。','This course is intended to provide students an in-depth understanding of design, control, and operation of accounting information systems that facilitate decision making. The emphasis is on identifying the information needs of major business processes and developing appropriate business process control in the design of accounting information systems.

Students will gain knowledge of the basic concepts of information systems and apply analytical techniques, such as data flow diagrams, flowcharts, and REA diagrams, to interpret and develop an accounting information system.

This course will also introduce typical threats to the reliability of accounting information systems, and applicable controls for addressing and mitigating the risks associated with these threats. The discussion of risks and controls in business processes is relevant to students who plan to take the auditing courses.

Special topics on the revenue, expenditure, and payroll cycles will be covered.

The course also covers the basic usage of an EPP system- the E-Cloud Teaching and Examination Platform and Kingdee Cloud Galaxy Teaching Edition. Students will be guided to configure a Kingdee system, and implement what they will learn at the revenue cycle and expenditure cycle through the Kingdee system.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
