2025-26 Term 2','ACT2111','N/A','本课程是关于用于决策投资企业等目的财务信息分析。重点是培养解释并分析财务报表中所载信息的技能，而不是编制财务报表的技能。我们将详细介绍基本面分析方发以及涉及上市公司的案例分析。主题包括股东价值模型，应计会计与贴现现金流量估值方法的比较，企业盈利能力，增长和估值产生分析，现金流分析，公司治理以及风险分析等。','This course is about the analysis of financial information for purposes like making decisions to invest in businesses. The focus is on developing the skills required to interpret the information contained in financial statements and its use in decision-making rather than on the skills required to prepare financial statements. The methods of fundamental analysis will be covered in detail and applied in cases and projects involving listed companies. Topics include models of shareholder value, a comparison of accrual accounting and discounted cash flow approaches to valuation, the analysis of profitability, growth and valuation generation in a firm, cash flows analysis, and risk analysis. The course is beneficial for students planning to start careers in the financial field (such as investment banking, portfolio management, corporate finance, valuation consulting, financial analysis, etc.). It is also valuable to the broader set of students who wish to go into general management, consulting, etc., and who need to understand the financial ramifications of managerial choices and actions, and who need to communicate with the with finance functions inside and outside the firm on a regular basis.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100024,'ACT4214','中国资本市场的财务舞弊','Financial Shenanigans in the Chinese Capital Markets','ACT - Accounting','4214','A',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','ACT2111 Intro Financial Accounting','','这门课程旨在拓宽学生对会计实践如何被误用以扭曲公司财务报表中财务状况的认识。课程将探讨常用的盈余管理技术，如可自由裁量的应计项目和财务修饰，以及用于检测这些技术的不同识别方法。课程中将使用来自中国资本市场的真实案例作为主要教学辅助材料。通过课堂案例讨论和演示，学生将深入了解中国资本市场中的会计技巧和欺诈行为。','This course aims to broaden students’ awareness of the various ways in which accounting practices can be mis-used to distort the financial position of the firm presented in its financial statements. It explores commonly used techniques for earnings management such as discretionary accruals and financial window-dressing and different discernment methods for their detection. Real-life case examples drawn from the Chinese Capital markets are used as the major teaching aids in this course. Through classroom case discussions and presentations, students will gain practical insights into accounting gimmicks and frauds in Chinese capital markets.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100025,'ACT4221','管理会计的数据分析','Data Analytics for Management Accounting','ACT - Accounting','4221','A',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'ACT2121','','本课程旨在为本科生提供实用的数据分析工具，以支持高效的管理决策。课程以管理会计的基础概念为出发点，结合真实的财务数据和案例研究，教授学生如何运用关键的管理会计框架，如成本行为分析、CVP分析（成本-数量-利润分析）、预算编制、定价策略和绩效指标评估，运用现代数据分析技术进行实际应用。课程重点强调基于Excel的情景分析应用，减少对高级编程技能的依赖。学生还将学习如何使用企业级会计软件和人工智能工具和智能体，以提升决策制定的质量和效率。','This course equips undergraduate students with practical data analysis tools essential for effective managerial decision-making. Building on foundational concepts from managerial accounting, it incorporates real-world financial data and case studies to teach students how to apply key management accounting frameworks—such as cost behavior, CVP analysis, budgeting, pricing strategy, and performance metrics—using modern analytics techniques. The course emphasizes Excel-based applications for scenario analysis, minimizing the need for advanced coding skills. Students will also learn to utilize enterprise accounting software and AI tools and agents to support and enhance decision-making processes.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
