(100027,'ACT4244','人工智能的会计应用','Artificial Intelligence for Accounting Practices','ACT - Accounting','4244','A',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','ACT2111 Intro Financial Accounting','n/a','本课程向经管专业本科生介绍人工智能（AI）的基础知识及其在现代会计实践中的应用。学生将通过动手练习和真实案例研究，探索关键的AI工具和概念——包括智能体、大型语言模型（LLMs）和AI驱动的风险评估模型等。本课程强调AI技术如何能够增强审计分析、财务报告、财务舞弊检测、管理会计和决策制定过程、以及财务报表分析等任务。本课程无需编程，不需要先前的编程经验，但学生将获得与会计专业相关的精选AI工具的实际操作经验。在课程结束时，学生将掌握AI的基础知识，以及能够利用现有AI工具来解决一些会计工作中所面临的具体问题。','This course introduces undergraduate business majors to the fundamentals of artificial intelligence (AI) and its applications in modern accounting practices. Students will explore key AI tools and concepts—including intelligent agents, large language models (LLMs), and AI-driven risk assessment models—through hands-on exercises and real-world case studies. The course emphasizes how AI technologies can enhance tasks such as audit analytics, financial reporting, fraud detection, and managerial decision-making processes, financial statement analysis. This class is coding free so no prior programming experience is required, but students will gain practical exposure to selected AI tools relevant to the accounting profession. By the end of the course, students will be equipped with a foundational understanding of AI and utilize existing AI tools to solve practical problems in accounting works.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
