(100104,'AIE1001','人工智能编程导论','Introduction to AI Programming','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','1001','A',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在培养本科生的基础编程能力，并引导学生入门人工智能应用。课程专为没有编程经验的初学者设计，以 Python 作为主要教学语言，从变量、数据类型、函数到面向对象编程等基础概念循序渐进地讲解，帮助学生打下扎实的编程基础。同时，课程还会简单引入数据结构的概念，培养学生编写模块化、可复用代码的能力。课程中后期将逐步引导学生进入人工智能编程阶段，内容包括使用 NumPy等进行数据处理，实现基础的图像处理与自然语言处理任务，并了解使用先进人工智能工具，如 ChatGPT。通过本课程的学习，学生将建立起扎实的 Python 编程基础和初步的人工智能实践能力，为后续深入人工智能的学习奠定坚实基础。','This course is designed to equip undergraduate students with essential programming skills and a practical introduction to artificial intelligence. Tailored for beginners with no prior experience, the course starts with foundational programming concepts, including variables, data types, functions, and object-oriented programming, using Python as the primary language. Building on this foundation, students will be introduced to basic data structures, and learn to write modular and reusable code. In the middle and later stages, the course transitions to applied AI programming, covering data processing with popular libraries such as NumPy, hands-on techniques in simple image processing and natural language processing, and the use of modern AI tools such as ChatGPT. By the end of the course, students will be well-prepared for more advanced studies in AI.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100105,'AIE1101','氛围编程：用AI创造应用','','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','1101','A',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','This course assumes no prior exposure to computer programming or software development. Students are expected to be curious about artificial intelligence applications and willing to learn through hands-on project work.','N.A.','本课程面向全校本科一年级学生，通过项目驱动和案例驱动的教学方式，旨在引导学生体验人工智能辅助软件开发的全新模式。课程专为零基础或几乎没有编程经验的学生设计，学生将借助 Qwen、DeepSeek 等现代人工智能编程助手（或其他具有同等能力的平台无关工具），把自己的创意逐步转化为可运行的软件应用，同时循序渐进地学习编程基础、计算思维、Prompt 设计、程序调试以及生成式人工智能的负责任使用等核心能力。

不同于传统编程课程以语法和语言特性为起点，本课程采用“边做边学（Learning by Building）”的教学理念，从第一周开始即围绕真实的小项目展开学习。课程项目涵盖趣味游戏、效率工具、AI 助手、交互式网页应用、自动化工具以及创意应用开发等多个主题，使学生在解决真实问题和完成作品的过程中自然掌握编程知识。

课程不仅教授编程，更鼓励学生将创意转化为现实。通过持续的小项目实践，每位学生都将完成属于自己的 AI 应用作品集，并在课程最后展示一项原创 AI 应用。课程旨在帮助学生建立“人人都可以借助 AI 创造软件”的信心，激发他们对人工智能的兴趣，为进一步学习人工智能、程序设计及跨学科 AI 创新应用奠定坚实基础。','This course introduces first-year undergraduate students to AI-assisted software creation through a project-driven and beginner-friendly learning experience. Students with little or no prior programming experience learn to transform ideas into working applications with modern AI coding assistants such as Qwen, DeepSeek, or comparable model-agnostic tools, while gradually developing foundational programming concepts, computational thinking, prompt workflow design, debugging habits, and responsible use of generative AI. Instead of beginning with syntax in isolation, the course starts from authentic mini-projects, including games, productivity tools, AI assistants, interactive web applications, automation tools, and creative personal projects. By the end of the course, students will have built a portfolio of AI-powered applications, presented an original final project, and developed the confidence and learning strategies needed for further study in artificial intelligence, programming, and interdisciplinary AI applications.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100106,'AIE1901','人工智能探索（一）','AI Exploration I','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','1901','A',2.00,1000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程系列（AIE1901-AIE1904）以"项目实践"为核心教学模式，通过阶梯式项目设计满足学生在不同学习阶段对人工智能技术的需求，旨在培养学生对AI的兴趣及使用AI工具解决具体问题的能力。在14周系统化学习中，学生将在导师指导下初步了解人工智能技术的基本原理和工具使用，初步掌握人工智能技术在多个领域的应用场景和可以赋能解决的实际问题。课程深度融合前沿技术案例与科研实践课题，着力培养学生的跨学科思维与创新能力。针对编程零基础学生，课程特别设置"零代码AI开发"相关的项目，帮助学生在无需编写代码的前提下，掌握AI工具的实践应用，使所有学生都能将人工智能技术有效融入日常学习与研究实践。AIE1901是该系列课程的第一门。','The AIE1901–AIE1904 course series employs a staged, project-based methodology designed to address students'' AI learning needs at progressive levels. Each course provides a structured 14-week foundation in AI principles and tools. Through guided projects and real-world case studies, students cultivate interdisciplinary thinking and problem-solving competencies. The course also incorporates no-code AI projects to ensure accessibility for students without programming experience, enabling practical AI applications in academic settings. AIE1901 is the first one in this series.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100107,'AIE1902','人工智能探索（二）','AI Exploration II','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','1902','A',2.00,1000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','AIE1901 AI Exploration I','','本课程系列（AIE1901-AIE1904）以"项目实践"为核心教学模式，通过阶梯式项目设计满足学生在不同学习阶段对人工智能技术的需求，旨在培养学生对AI的兴趣及使用AI工具解决具体问题的能力。在14周系统化学习中，学生将在导师指导下初步了解人工智能技术的基本原理和工具使用，初步掌握人工智能技术在多个领域的应用场景和可以赋能解决的实际问题。课程深度融合前沿技术案例与科研实践课题，着力培养学生的跨学科思维与创新能力。针对编程零基础学生，课程特别设置"零代码AI开发"相关的项目，帮助学生在无需编写代码的前提下，掌握AI工具的实践应用，使所有学生都能将人工智能技术有效融入日常学习与研究实践。AIE1902是该系列课程的第二门。','The AIE1901–AIE1904 course series employs a staged, project-based methodology designed to address students'' AI learning needs at progressive levels. Each course provides a structured 14-week foundation in AI principles and tools. Through guided projects and real-world case studies, students cultivate interdisciplinary thinking and problem-solving competencies. The course also incorporates no-code AI projects to ensure accessibility for students without programming experience, enabling practical AI applications in academic settings. AIE1902 is the second one in this series.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100108,'AIE1903','人工智能探索（三）','AI Exploration III','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','1903','A',2.00,1000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','AIE1902','N.A','本课程系列（AIE1901-AIE1904）以"项目实践"为核心教学模式，通过阶梯式项目设计满足学生在不同学习阶段对人工智能技术的需求，旨在培养学生对AI的兴趣及使用AI工具解决具体问题的能力。在14周系统化学习中，学生将在导师指导下初步了解人工智能技术的基本原理和工具使用，初步掌握人工智能技术在多个领域的应用场景和可以赋能解决的实际问题。课程深度融合前沿技术案例与科研实践课题，着力培养学生的跨学科思维与创新能力。针对编程零基础学生，课程特别设置"零代码AI开发"相关的项目，帮助学生在无需编写代码的前提下，掌握AI工具的实践应用，使所有学生都能将人工智能技术有效融入日常学习与研究实践。AIE1903是该系列课程的第三门。','The AIE1901–AIE1904 course series employs a staged, project-based methodology designed to address students'' AI learning needs at progressive levels. Each course provides a structured 14-week foundation in AI principles and tools. Through guided projects and real-world case studies, students cultivate interdisciplinary thinking and problem-solving competencies. The course also incorporates no-code AI projects to ensure accessibility for students without programming experience, enabling practical AI applications in academic settings. AIE1903 is the third one in this series.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100109,'AIE2001','认知科学导论','Introduction to Cognitive Science','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','2001','A',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程将以通用人工智能（AGI）的视角研讨人类智能的认知基础，深度审视推理、记忆、决策等认知过程中“理性”的观念。理性决策的原则有哪些？为何人有不同的记忆系统、它们如何支撑认知？能否教会机器来推理、使之能比我们更了解我们自己？通过对人类“理性”思维的缺陷和失败的种种示范，本课程将激起同学们对认知科学和人工智能的兴趣，同时探索心智与认知、机器智能、数学推理等密切关联的题目。','This lecture course is a required core course of SAI. It will introduce to students cognitive roots to human intelligence with a vision towards artificial general intelligence (AGI). It will examine in-depth the concept of rationality in reasoning, memory, and decision making. What are the principles of rational decision making? Why are there different memory systems and how they support cognition? Can we teach machines to reason, in a way that understand us better than we do ourselves? By in-class demonstrations of various pitfalls and failures of rationality of the human mind, this seminar aims to instigate students’ curiosity into cognitive science and artificial intelligence, while exploring the intertwining topics of mind and cognition, machine intelligence, and mathematical reasoning.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100110,'AIE2040','人工智能统计基础','Statistical Foundations for AI','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','2040','A',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MAT2040 or MAT2041 or MAT2042;
MAT1001 or MAT1002','','本课程介绍理解、构建和评估人工智能系统所需的统计学基础。课程首先讲授统计建模、估计、似然、不确定性量化、假设检验、bootstrap方法和贝叶斯思想，并进一步联系监督学习、无监督学习和强化学习。主要内容包括经验风险最小化、偏差-方差权衡、正则化、模型选择、验证、回归与分类、降维、聚类、混合模型与EM算法、马尔可夫决策过程，以及过拟合、不确定性等问题。','This course introduces the statistical foundations needed to understand, build, and evaluate AI systems. It begins with statistical modeling, estimation, likelihood, uncertainty quantification, hypothesis testing, bootstrap methods, and Bayesian thinking, and then connects these ideas to supervised learning, unsupervised learning, and reinforcement learning. Topics include empirical risk minimization, bias-variance tradeoff, regularization, model selection, validation, regression and classification, dimensionality reduction, clustering, mixture models and EM, Markov decision processes, and statistical challenges such as overfitting, uncertainty.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100111,'AIE3001','人工智能与人机交互','AI and Human Computer Interaction','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','3001','A',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','AIE1001 or CSC1001 or CSC1002 or CSC1003 or CSC1004 or CSC1005 or CSC1006 or MAT2040 or MAT2041 or MAT2042 (or equivalents demonstrating baseline programming literacy).','N.A.','本课程聚焦人工智能时代的人机交互特别是自然用户交互（Natural User Interfaces），采用“理论讲授、AI编程实践、项目开发”相结合的教学模式，引导学生突破传统图形用户界面（GUI）的设计范式，利用笔记本电脑和智能手机内置的摄像头、麦克风、触摸屏、惯性传感器、定位等设备，结合计算机视觉、语音识别、大语言模型、多模态人工智能和智能体（AI Agent）等技术，设计更加自然、智能、主动的人机交互体验。
课程强调项目驱动与快速原型开发，学生将围绕真实应用场景完成从用户研究、交互设计、AI编程、原型实现到用户测试的完整设计流程。课程最终以小组项目作为成果展示，每组学生需设计并实现一个融合多模态交互与人工智能能力的创新交互系统，为未来智能终端、智能机器人、空间计算、数字媒体及AI原生产品开发奠定基础。','This course introduces the principles and practice of Human Computer Interaction specially focuses on AI-powered Natural User Interfaces (NUI), where users interact with intelligent systems through vision, speech, touch, motion, and contextual sensing rather than traditional graphical user interfaces. Through lectures, laboratory exercises, and project-based learning, students learn to design and prototype multimodal interactive systems using the built-in sensors of laptops and smartphones, including cameras, microphones, touchscreens, inertial sensors, and location services.
Students will explore computer vision, speech recognition, large language models, multimodal AI, and AI agents as core technologies for creating intelligent, context-aware user experiences. The course emphasizes rapid prototyping, user-centered design, and iterative development, enabling students to transform everyday computing devices into natural interaction platforms without specialized hardware.
Working in interdisciplinary teams, students will complete the full interaction design cycle from user research and concept development to implementation, user evaluation, and public demonstration. The course culminates in a team project in which students design and build an innovative AI-powered natural user interface for a real-world application, preparing them for future work in human-computer interaction, intelligent systems, spatial computing, and AI-native product design.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100112,'AIE3005','信息分析与表征','Signal Analysis and Representation','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','3005','A',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','(AIE1001 or CSC1001 or CSC1003 or CSC1005)；(MAT1002 or MAT1012)；(MAT2040 or MAT2041 or MAT2042)','','信息分析與表徵介紹信號與系統分析的基本概念和方法，包括連續時間與離散時間信號、系統性質、線性時不變系統、卷積、衝激響應、傅立葉分析、取樣、量化、DFT/FFT、數位濾波、隨機信號、相關分析和功率譜密度等內容。在此基礎上，課程進一步討論現代信號表示方法，包括時頻表示、頻譜圖、可學習濾波器、神經嵌入表示、有監督表示、自監督表示以及基於基礎模型的信號編碼器等。課程範例涵蓋音訊、視覺、機器人感測器和多模態人工智慧系統。透過課堂講授與基於 Python 的實作環節，學生將學習如何分析真實世界信號，並為感知、識別和基礎信號重建任務設計合適的信號表示。','Signal Analysis and Representation introduces fundamental concepts and methods for analyzing signals and systems, including continuous-time and discrete-time signals, system properties, linear time-invariant systems, convolution, impulse response, Fourier analysis, sampling, quantization, DFT/FFT, digital filtering, random signals, correlation, and power spectral density. Building on these foundations, the course further studies modern signal representation methods, including time-frequency representations, spectrograms, learned filters, neural embeddings, supervised representations, self-supervised representations, and foundation-model-based signal encoders. Examples are drawn from audio, vision, robotics sensors, and multimodal AI systems. Through lectures and Python-based tutorials, students will learn how to analyze real-world signals and design appropriate representations for perception, recognition, and basic signal reconstruction.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100113,'AIE3901','人工智能实践（一）','AI Practicum I','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','3901','A',2.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','{(AIE1001 and 1903 and 1904) or [(CSC1001 or 1003 or 1005) and (CSC1002 or 1004 or 1006）]} and (CSC3100 or CSC3200)','','本课程是一学年制基于项目的实践课程的第一部分，旨在让学生参与到与大学或业界合作方合作的真实人工智能解决方案的端到端开发与部署过程。在两个学期内，学生将以小组形式开展工作，识别实际问题，进行深入的需求分析，设计稳健的人工智能驱动架构与技术，并实现和部署他们的解决方案。课程内容不仅强调人工智能技术的开发，还注重软件工程方面的核心技能，如架构规划、系统集成以及在真实环境中的部署能力。','This course is the first part of a year-long project-based practice course series, allowing students to be involved in the end-to-end process of developing and deploying real-world AI solutions in partnership with university and/or industry stakeholders. Over two semesters, students work in teams to identify practical problems, conduct thorough requirements analysis, design robust AI-driven architectures and technologies, and implement and deploy their solutions. The curriculum emphasizes not only technical AI development but also essential software engineering skills such as architecture planning, system integration, and deployment in real-world environments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100114,'AIE3902','人工智能实践（二）','AI Practicum II','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','3902','A',2.00,3000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','AIE3901 AI Practicum I','','本课程是一学年制基于项目的实践课程的第二部分，旨在让学生参与到与大学或业界合作方合作的真实人工智能解决方案的端到端开发与部署过程。在两个学期内，学生将以小组形式开展工作，识别实际问题，进行深入的需求分析，设计稳健的人工智能驱动架构与技术，并实现和部署他们的解决方案。课程内容不仅强调人工智能技术的开发，还注重软件工程方面的核心技能，如架构规划、系统集成以及在真实环境中的部署能力。','This course is the second part of a year-long project-based practice course series, allowing students to be involved in the end-to-end process of developing and deploying real-world AI solutions in partnership with university and/or industry stakeholders. Over two semesters, students work in teams to identify practical problems, conduct thorough requirements analysis, design robust AI-driven architectures and technologies, and implement and deploy their solutions. The curriculum emphasizes not only technical AI development but also essential software engineering skills such as architecture planning, system integration, and deployment in real-world environments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100115,'AIE3905','人工智能与社会实践 (一)','','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','3905','A',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','AIE 1001-1002 or CSC 1001-1002 or CSC 1003-1004 or CSC 1005-1006 (or equivalents demonstrating baseline programming literacy).','N.A','本课程以“社会实践”为核心方法论，采用“讲座引领、实验验证、实地考察”三位一体的教学模式。课程引导学生走出课堂、深入现场，通过企业参访、社区调研、政策分析及项目实战等多元化途径，深度剖析AI技术在产业创新、城市治理与社会发展中的应用实效与伦理边界。课程致力于培养学生的技术洞察力、社会责任感及跨领域协作能力。 
学生在这门课程中将完成行动前的调研、行动中的反思、行动后的影响评估这一完整责任链条。','"Centered on ""social practice"" as its core methodology, this course adopts a tripartite teaching model integrating lecture guidance, experimental validation, and field investigation. Guiding students to step out of the classroom and into real-world settings, the curriculum utilizes diverse approaches—including corporate visits, community research, policy analysis, and hands-on project implementation—to critically examine the practical efficacy and ethical boundaries of AI technologies across scenarios of industrial innovation, urban governance, and social development.
The course is dedicated to cultivating students'' technical insight, social responsibility, and cross-disciplinary collaborative capabilities. Throughout the semester, students will engage in a complete chain of responsibility, encompassing pre-action research, critical reflection during action, and post-action impact assessment, thereby achieving the integration of knowledge and practice."','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100116,'AIE4901','人工智能毕业设计（一）','AI Capstone Project I','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','4901','A',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Refer to the specific requirements of each project
Enrollment of a student needs approval from the instructor.','','本课程为两学期毕业设计的第一学期的课程，围绕真实场景启动团队式AI项目。项目包括问题界定、利益相关方与需求分析、文献与方案调研、系统架构设计、数据策略与风险评估、负责任AI审查，并生成可运行的基线/原型。课程强调跨学科协作、项目规划与规范化工程/科研实践（版本控制、测试、可复现）。期末需提交完整设计包与可用于下学期扩展实施的基线系统。','This first course in a two-semester capstone sequence initiates a team-based, real-world AI project. The project includes problem scoping, stakeholder/requirement analysis, literature and solution review, system architecture design, data strategy, risk and responsible AI assessment, and produces a working baseline/prototype. Emphasis is on interdisciplinary collaboration, planning, and setting up robust engineering and research practices (version control, testing, reproducibility). By the end of the semester, teams will deliver a design package and a baseline system ready for full-scale implementation in Capstone Project II.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100117,'AIE4902','人工智能毕业设计 II','AI Capstone Project II','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','4902','A',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','监督','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Summer','Refer to the specific requirements of each project
Enrollment of a student needs approval from the instructor','','作为毕业设计（AI Capstone Project）系列课程的第二阶段，本课程将延续毕业设计 I 的团队配置与项目选题。课程重点聚焦于项目的全面实现、迭代优化、严格评估、系统可靠性保障及最终成果交付。学生需提交原型系统或可部署的服务，并完成详尽的技术文档、结题报告及公开汇报。','This second course in the capstone sequence continues the same team and project from AI Capstone Project I, focusing on full implementation, iteration, rigorous evaluation, reliability, and final delivery. Students will deliver a production-ready prototype or deployable service with comprehensive documentation, a final report, and a public presentation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100118,'AIE6001','人工智能高等数学','','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','6001','A',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Linear algebra, proof-based advanced calculus (or mathematical analysis), calculus-based
elementary probability and statistics, elementary stochastic processes.','N/A','本课程深入探讨开发先进人工智能（AI）系统所必需的关键数学基础。内容涵盖现代AI中至关重要的高等数学主题，如线性代数（例如矩阵运算、奇异值分解）、概率论（例如马尔可夫链）、机器学习算法所依赖的基础知识、优化理论（例如梯度下降、二阶方法）、信息论（例如熵，KL散度）。本课程专为已经具备数学基础并希望提升其AI应用能力的学生设计。','This course delves into the critical mathematical foundations essential for developing advanced artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It covers advanced mathematics topics that are crucial for modern AI, such as linear algebra (e.g., matrix operations, singular value decomposition), probability theory (e.g., Markov chains), fundamental for machine learning algorithms, optimization theory (e.g., gradient descent, second order methods), information theory (e.g., entropy and KL divergence). This course is designed for students who already have a basic understanding of mathematics and want to enhance their skills for AI-driven applications.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100119,'AIE6002','大型语言模型','','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','6002','A',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','•Proficient in Python (e.g., numpy, pandas, PyTorch/TensorFlow)
•Knowledge of probability, linear algebra, and calculus
•Basic knowledge of machine learning and neural networks','','本课程提供大型语言模型的全面学习。课程将探讨架构工程、训练技术、效率提升和提示工程。学生将深入了解大型语言模型在各个领域的应用、工具集成、隐私和偏见问题，以及它们的局限性和对齐问题。课程将安排高级主题的客座讲座和课堂演示，以激发实践理解。本课程专为希望在其领域内掌握大型语言模型应用的学生设计。','This course offers a comprehensive study of Large Language Models (LLMs). It will explore architecture engineering, training techniques, efficiency enhancements, and prompt engineering. Students will gain insights into the application of LLMs in various domains, tools integration, privacy and bias issues, as well as their limitations and alignment. There will be guest lectures on advanced topics and in-class presentations to stimulate practical understanding. This course is designed for students who are seeking to master the use of LLMs in their field.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100120,'AIE6003','机器学习中的优化','','AIE - Artificial Intelligence','6003','A',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Undergraduate level of linear algebra, analysis, and probability & statistics are required.','None.','本课程深入探讨机器学习领域中优化的理论基础，重点关注非线性规划。课程内容包括基于梯度的方法、自适应梯度方法以及随机优化；同时还将介绍机器学习与优化交叉的前沿话题，如稀疏优化、极小极大优化、双层优化和黑箱优化。本课程面向希望深入掌握高级优化技术并将其应用于复杂机器学习问题的学生。','This course delves into the theoretical foundations of optimization in machine learning, with a focus on nonlinear programming. Topics include gradient-based methods, adaptive gradient methods, and stochastic optimization. It will also cover emerging topics at the intersection of machine learning and optimization, such as sparse optimization, min-max optimization, bilevel optimization, and black-box optimization. This course is designed for students who are looking to deepen their understanding of advanced optimization techniques and apply them to complex machine learning problems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
