2026-27 Term 1','BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology     
BIO2004 Biochemistry','','微生物学是一门研究肉眼难以看见的微小生物的学科。本课程将对微生物学涉及的各个领域进行讲授，内容包括微生物的多样性（原核微生物、真核微生物、古细菌和病毒）；微生物的结构与功能（形态结构、代谢和信号传导）；微生物的遗传(生长和繁殖)；以及微生物与人类/环境的关系（疾病、免疫、生态以及应用等）。学习本课程将有助于理解微生物的生命活动规律并认识微生物与人类日常生活的密切联系。先修科目：BIO2002细胞与分子生物学和BIO2004生物化学。','Microbiology is a specialized area of biology that deals with organisms ordinarily too small to be seen without magnification. This course covers introductory microbiology on microbial diversity (prokaryotes, eukaryotes, archaea, and viruses), structure and function of microbes (cellular structure, metabolism, and signaling), microbial genetics (growth and reproduction), and interactions of microorganisms with human and their environment (diseases, immunity, and applications). At the end of course students will acquire knowledge of fundamental processes of microbes and appreciate their intimate involvement in the lives of human. Pre-requisite: BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology and BIO2004 Biochemistry.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100230,'BIO3003','生态学','Ecology','BIO - Biology','3003','B',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
