2026-27 Term 1','BIO1001 General Biology','','生态学是研究生物与其环境之间相互作用的领域。在本课程中，学生将探索生态学的基本原理，包括生物与其环境之间的相互作用，种群动态，群落和生态系统结构，生物多样性和可持续性。学生将全面了解生态学的科学领域，熟悉生态学家如何进行研究，以及普通生态学知识的重要性。课程主题包括生物圈、地圈、大气和水圈的共同进化;调节生物的分布和丰度;人口增长模型;物种之间的相互影响;生态系统的结构与功能;营养动力学;通过生态系统的能量和物质流动;生产力;生物地球化学循环。
学生还将学习批判性地评价科学文献，并将有效地与科学家和非科学家交流生态知识，为未来的学术和专业贡献培养必要的技能。','Ecology is the field of study of the interactions between organisms and their environment. In this course, students will explore the fundamental principles of ecology, including the interactions between organisms and their environment, population dynamics, community and ecosystem structure, biodiversity and sustainability. Students will gain a comprehensive understanding of the scientific field of ecology, how ecologists conduct research, and the importance of general ecological knowledge. Topics include coevolution of the biosphere, geosphere, atmosphere and hydrosphere; regulation of the distribution and abundance of organisms; models of population growth; species interactions; structure and function of ecosystems; trophic dynamics; the flow of energy and materials through ecosystems; productivity; biogeochemical cycles.

Students will also learn to evaluate critically scientific literature and effectively communicate ecological knowledge to both scientists and non-scientists, developing essential skills for future academic and professional endeavours.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
