2025-26 Term 2','BIO1001 General Biology/BIO1008 Chemistry and Life Sciences','NA','本科目是提供基本应用遗传工程知识给中学曾修生物课程的学生。

遗传工程课程专注于遗传学和分子生物学的应用。遗传工程又被称之为重组DNA技术，它牵涉到各种操作遗传物质的技巧，特别是从不同物种来的DNA分子，以及把杂交DNA转入物种从而制备新的遗传物质。通过本课程学习，我们将尝试把遗传工程多方面的内容介绍和遗传学及分子生物学的原理结合起来，从而更能理解人类如何在体外更好的操作并利用遗传物质。学生也能更好地进行批判性思维训练和科学读写方面的技巧。','This is a foundation course to provide general background knowledge of Applied Genetics and Genetic Engineering for science and engineering students who have taken biology courses at the level of Gaokao in their secondary schools.

The focus of Genetic Engineering is the study of principles and applications of genetics and molecular biology. Also called recombinant DNA technology, it involves the group of techniques used to cut up and join together genetic material, especially DNA from different biological species, and to introduce the resulting hybrid DNA into an organism in order to form new combinations of heritable genetic material. Throughout the semester we will attempt to relate comprehensive aspects of genetic engineering applications to help gain a better understanding for how the principles of genetics and molecular biology are used to manipulate genetic material in vitro. The development of critical thinking processes and proficiency in scientific reading and writing will also be emphasized throughout the course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100235,'BIO3206','化学生物学','Chemical Biology','BIO - Biology','3206','B',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','(CHM1001 or CHM1011) and (BIO1001 or BIO1008 or BIO2004)','','本课程重点介绍化学生物学，将其作为一门以设计和应用化学工具在分子水平上研究和操控生物系统为核心的学科。学生将从基础概念入手，逐步深入学习核酸和蛋白质化学、化学糖生物学以及荧光探针和质谱等先进光谱和成像技术等关键领域。课程强调生物正交化学及其在活细胞标记中的关键作用，以及化学生物学在现代药物研发和新兴技术中的应用。通过学生报告、案例研究和小组讨论，学习者将获得理论知识并接触前沿技术，从而清晰地理解多学科交叉如何推动化学生物学领域的技术创新。','This course provides a focused introduction to chemical biology as a discipline centered on the design and application of chemical tools to interrogate and manipulate biological systems at the molecular level. Students will begin with foundational concepts and progress through key areas including nucleic acid and protein chemistry, chemical glycobiology, and the use of advanced spectroscopic and imaging techniques such as fluorescence probes and mass spectrometry. The curriculum emphasizes bioorthogonal chemistry and its pivotal role in live-cell labeling, as well as the application of chemical biology in modern drug discovery and emerging technologies. Through student presentations, case studies, and group discussions, learners will acquire theoretical knowledge and exposure to frontier techniques, gaining a clear understanding of how multidisciplinary insights drive technological innovation in chemical biology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
