2026-27 Term 1','BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology','','本课程旨在帮助学生理解大脑如何工作的基本概念。 学生将学习神经元的结构，动作电位的传播和信息传递。 将讨论体感，视觉，听觉，前庭系统以及化学感官中的感觉和感觉处理。 运动控制和运动调节，以及记忆，学习和突触可塑性，脑部疾病的分子基础以及探索神经生物学的方法也将涵盖在内。','This course is designed to help students understand basic concepts behind how the brain works. Students will learn the structure, action potential propagation, and information transfer of neurons. Sensation and sensory processing in somatosensory, visual, auditory, vestibular systems, as well as chemical senses will be discussed. Motor control and movement modulation, as well as memory, learning and synaptic plasticity, the molecular basis of brain disorder, and the ways of exploring neurobiology will also be covered.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
