BIO3903 Research Internship III','','本课程旨在提高本科生对科学研究的兴趣。同时，学生将在教授的指导下获得前沿的专业知识，并获得与生物科学、生物信息学/计算生物学或生物医学工程相关的丰富科研经验。在本课程中，学生可以学习如何独立地从头到尾规划和开展生物医学相关研究课题。 学生应能够反思研究过程、了解其科研需求和困难点、展示研究成果，甚至撰写研究论文。','This course aims to increase the undergraduate student''s interest in scientific research. In the meantime, the student shall gain an advanced professional experience and obtain extensive experience of work related to biological sciences, bioinformatics/computational biology, or biomedical engineering under the supervision of professors. In this course, the undergraduate students can learn, with some independence, how to plan and carry out a research project from start to end. The student shall be able to reflect on the research process, understand its requirements and difficulties, present the research results, and even write a research thesis.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100247,'BIO4102','前沿生物技术','Advanced Biotechnology','BIO - Biology','4102','B',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology','','这门高级本科课程全面探讨推动现代生物技术发展的前沿方法，特别侧重于整合神经科学与治疗研发领域。课程设置包含三个相互关联的模块：1. 分子与细胞工具模块：学生将深入钻研基因工程原理，包括基因组编辑技术和靶向基因递送病毒载体的设计。2. 系统神经科学与电生理学模块：课程涵盖监测与控制神经回路的前沿技术，通过实验概念和案例研究讲解光遗传与化学遗传学对神经元活动的精准调控、解码神经信号的体内多通道电生理记录技术，以及监测动态大脑的长期钙/电压成像方法。重点聚焦生物与工程学的交叉领域，探索人工智能与机器学习在大数据分析、神经数据预测动物行为以及闭环脑机接口开发中的应用。3. 转化应用模块：课程最终考察这些技术如何协同验证临床前治疗候选方案，包括评估认知情感功能的现代行为范式研究，以及神经系统疾病细胞与基因疗法的导论。','This advanced undergraduate course provides a comprehensive exploration of cutting-edge methodologies driving modern biotechnology, with a special focus on integrative neuroscience and therapeutic development. The curriculum is designed around three interconnected modules: Molecular and Cellular Tools: Students will delve into the principles of genetic engineering, including genome editing and the design of viral vectors (e.g., AAV, lentivirus) for targeted gene delivery. Systems Neuroscience and Electrophysiology: The course covers advanced techniques for monitoring and controlling neural circuits. Laboratory concepts and case studies will include optogenetics and chemogenetics for precise manipulation of neuronal activity, in vivo multi-channel electrophysiology for decoding neural signals, and long-term calcium/voltage imaging for visualizing brain dynamics. A significant focus will be placed on the intersection of biology and engineering, exploring how artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning are used to analyze complex datasets, predict animal behavior from neural data, and develop closed-loop brain-computer interfaces (BCIs). Translational Applications: The course concludes by examining how these technologies converge to validate preclinical therapeutic candidates. This includes the study of modern behavioral paradigms for assessing cognitive and affective function, and an introduction to cell and gene therapies for neurological disorders.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100248,'BIO4105','进化生物学','Evolutionary Biology','BIO - Biology','4105','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology','','本课程介绍现代进化生物学的核心理论与研究方法，重点从种群、分子和器官系统三个层面理解生物多样性形成的机制。课程第一部分涵盖自然选择、遗传漂变、基因流、突变、适应、物种形成和系统发育等内容。第二部分讨论基因组进化、分子进化、蛋白家族扩张和功能分化，并以GPCR、嗅觉受体、视蛋白和神经递质受体等为例进行说明。最后一部分以器官复杂性和神经系统进化为重点，包括神经元起源、中枢化、感觉系统、运动控制、行为以及人类脑进化等内容。课程旨在帮助学生建立跨尺度的进化思维，并理解进化理论在神经科学、医学、生物技术和生命科学研究中的重要意义。','This course introduces the core theories and research approaches of modern evolutionary biology, with a focus on understanding the mechanisms that generate biological diversity at three levels: populations, molecules, and organ systems. The course PART I covers natural selection, genetic drift, gene flow, mutation, adaptation, speciation, and phylogenetics. PART II discusses genome evolution, molecular evolution, protein family expansion, and functional diversification, using GPCRs, olfactory receptors, opsins, and neurotransmitter receptors as examples. The final part focuses on organ complexity and nervous system evolution as example, including the origin of neurons, centralization, sensory systems, motor control, behavior, and human brain evolution. The course aims to help students develop cross-scale evolutionary thinking and understand the importance of evolutionary theory in neuroscience, medicine, biotechnology, and life science research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100249,'BIO4106','生命科学前沿研讨','Frontier Life Sciences Topics','BIO - Biology','4106','B',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','BIO2002 & (BIO2004 or BIO3001)','','这门课程通过了解诺贝尔奖获奖成果，探讨生物科学领域的重大突破和这些发现的科学意义、方法学价值及其转化影响。学生将评估每一项发现对医学、公共卫生以及未来研究方向的影响。通过讲座、文献分享和学生主导的研讨会，本课程目的为促进学生对前沿科学的深入理解，并培养其在科学批判性评估和科学交流方面的能力。','This course explores major breakthroughs in biological sciences through an in-depth study of Nobel Prize-winning discoveries, emphasizing their scientific, methodological, and translational significance. Students will evaluate the impact of each discovery on medicine, public health, and future research directions. Through lectures, journal clubs, and student-led seminars, the course fosters deep understanding of cutting-edge science and cultivates skills in critical appraisal and scientific communication.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
