(100251,'BIO4201','表观遗传学','* Epigenetics','BIO - Biology','4201','B',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','BIO1001 General Biology     
or BIO1008 Chemistry and Life Sciences','','本课程的主要目的是向学生介绍表观遗传学和各种人类疾病中异常表观遗传修饰的基本概念。越来越多的研究表明，遗传改变/ DNA序列的改变可能不是许多生物学过程的直接原因，而表观遗传学（包括DNA甲基化，组蛋白修饰和染色质可及性）显得更为重要。同时，还将对表观遗传学研究中应用的新型生物技术进行解释和说明。完成本课程后，学生将对以下内容有基本的了解：
1.表观遗传学的简要历史和基本概念
2.DNA甲基化，组蛋白修饰和非编码RNA的机制和功能。
3.检测表观遗传修饰的方法
4.在发育和人类疾病过程中的表观遗传改变
5.通过调控表观遗传治疗疾病的药物','The principal aim of this course is to introduce students the basic concept of epigenetics and aberrant epigenetic modifications in various human diseases. Increasing studies have showed that genetic change/DNA alteration may not be the direct cause in many biological processes, while epigenetics, including DNA methylation, histone modification, and chromatin accessibility manifest more importance. Meanwhile, the novel bio-techniques have been applied in the studies of epigenetics will be illustrated as well. Upon completion of this course, the students are expected to have a basic understanding of the following:
1.	The brief history and concept of epigenetics
2.	Mechanism and functions of DNA methylation, histone modification, and non-coding RNA.
3.	Methods to detect epigenetic modification
4.	Epigenetic alterations in development and human diseases
5.	Epigenetic drugs for therapies','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100252,'BIO4202','核酸','* Nucleic Acids','BIO - Biology','4202','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','BIO1001 General Biology     
or BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology','','在本课程中，学生会学习关于核酸(包括DNA和RNA)结构与功能的基本原理。本课程会介绍Watson-Crick以及非Watson-Crick核酸具体结构。我们会讨论DNA超螺旋和拓扑以及作用于DNA的各类酶。课程内容亦包括RNA的各项生物功能：（i）编码DNA，RNA，和蛋白质；（ii）催化反应（包括蛋白合成和RNA剪接）；和（iii）调控（包括转录，剪接，编辑，裂解和翻译）。我们会鼓励学生独立选择一个与核酸相关的研究课题并作一个学术报告。','In this course, the students will learn the fundamental principles of the structures and functions of nucleic acids (DNA and RNA). The course will cover basic structural details of Watson-Crick and non-Watson-Crick motifs. The DNA topology and enzymes acting on DNA will be discussed. The diverse coding (for DNA, RNA, and protein), catalysis (protein synthesis and RNA splicing), and regulatory (transcription, splicing, editing, degradation, and translation, etc) functions of RNAs will be discussed. Students are encouraged to independently select a seminar topic from some of the recent nucleic acid-related research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100253,'BIO4203','免疫学','Immunology','BIO - Biology','4203','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
