2025-26 Term 2','BME3001 Intro to BME I','NA','本课程旨在介绍生物传感器的基本理论知识，以及讲解用于分析研究的生物传感设备的设计和性能分析。本课程将具体介绍当前前沿生物传感器技术，以及纳米技术和生物工程技术在构建生物传感器中的应用；同时，侧重于讲解生物传感器在生物医学，环境监测，食品安全，公共卫生和生物安全等领域的应用。在课程结束时，学生应了解生物传感器的工作及设计原理，明白生物传感器的功能和特性，不同生物传感设备的设计，以及生物传感器在不同环境中的应用。学生还能掌握设计生物传感器的技能，能对各种物传感器的工作特性提出建议，并能理解每种技术的相关优点和缺点。','This course aims to introduce the field of biosensors from the aspect of a device design and performance analysis using a biosensor or a medical device. An overview and understanding of the current state of the art for biosensor design, preparation and evaluation will be imparted by integration with the nanotechnology and biomedical engineering technologies. This course will principally focus on biosensors applications in the fields of biomedical science, environmental monitoring, food safety, public health and biosecurity. By the end of the course the students should understand the principle of a biosensor, characteristics of a biosensor, design of different biosensing devices, and applications of biosensors in different settings. The student should also be able to design a biosensor or medical device to perform a given measurement and be aware of the associated advantages and disadvantages of the design.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100264,'BME3200','生物医学信号处理','Biomedical Signal Processing','BME - Biomedical Engineering','3200','B',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','该课程旨在向学生介绍人体生物医学信号分析和处理的基本概念和方法。该课程涵盖的主题包括生物医学信号的基础概念、信号采集、采样、频率分析、时频分析、小波变换、数字滤波等常见的预处理方法，同时介绍常见的生物医学信号（例如心电图ECG、肌电图EMG、脑电图EEG、动作电位等）的特征提取、基于机器学习和深度学习的人工智能AI算法，及其在临床疾病自动分类和诊断中的应用。该课程还将设计实验课环节，学生利用教学实验室环境分组采集不同类型的生物医学信号，然后利用Matlab和Python工具将课程学到的信号处理方法应用到实际的生物医学信号中，使学生能做到学以致用解决实际的生物医学工程的问题。课程还将通过科教融合的方式展示课程内容在前沿科学研究中的实际应用，以拓宽学生的国际视野，增强学生的科研兴趣，启发学生的职业规划，为学生尽早进入本科阶段的课题研究做好相关知识和技能的储备。','This course aims to introduce the basic concepts and methods of biomedical signal processing and analysis. The course covers topics such as biomedical signals definition, signal acquisition, digital sampling, storage, spectral analysis, time-frequency analysis, wavelet transform, digital filtering and other common signal preprocessing methods. It also introduces the feature extraction of common biomedical signals (such as electrocardiogram ECG, electromyogram EMG, electroencephalogram EEG, action potential, etc.), artificial intelligence AI algorithms based on machine learning and deep learning, and the application in the automatic classification and diagnosis of clinical diseases. The course will also include experimental labs, in which students will collect different types of biomedical signals in groups, and then use Matlab and Python tools to apply the signal processing methods learned in the course to actual biomedical signals. In this way, students can apply what they have learned to solve biomedical engineering problems. The course will also demonstrate the practical application of course content in cutting-edge scientific research through the integration of science and education, so as to broaden students'' international vision, enhance their scientific research interests, inspire their career planning, and prepare relevant knowledge and skills for students to enter undergraduate research as early as possible.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100265,'BME3201','生物医学仪器设计','Biomedical Instrument Design','BME - Biomedical Engineering','3201','B',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','该课程将涵盖医疗保健应用的医疗设备设计的关键原理和技术，从医院使用的医疗设备到用于健身监测的可穿戴设备。 该课程将指导学生如何设计生物医学仪器，从概念到原型开发和测试。 学生将学习如何定义医疗仪器设计需求，以及如何相应记录、显示、分析和解释人体的生物电数据（例如心脏活动、呼吸、血压、肌肉活动和大脑活动），并集成所有关键组件来开发用于实际临床的新型医疗设备开发。 课程将讲述医学仪器设计涉及的主要关键技术，例如基本电子电路、运算放大器电路、模拟信号调理、电源、微处理器、印刷电路板 (PCB)、C 或 micro-python 语言嵌入式编程、数据传输协议（USB、WiFi 和蓝牙）、图形 Matlab 和 Python 中的用户界面 (GUI) 设计用于可视化信号，以及各种数据处理技术来提取有关人体健康状况的有用信息。 学生将有机会从传感、嵌入式设计、硬件设计、PC控制软件和信号处理算法等方面独立设计一种新型生物医学设备。该课程的目标是在学术环境中为学生提供尽可能接近现实世界的工业生物医学工程设计经验。本课程可以增强学生独立解决工程问题的能力，丰富学生未来求职或学术生涯的生物医学专业技能。','The course will cover key principles and technologies of medical device design for healthcare applications, ranging from medical devices used in hospitals to wearables for fitness monitoring. The course will guide student on how to design biomedical instruments from concept to prototype development and testing. The students will learn the problem identification of medical instruments and learn how to record, display, analyze and interpret the bioelectrical data of human body accordingly (e.g. heart activity, respiratory, blood pressure, muscle activity and brain activity), and integrate all the key components to develop new medical devices for practical clinical application. Engineering technologies such as basic electronics circuits, op amp circuits, analog signal conditioning, power supplies, microprocessors, printed circuit board (PCB), embedded programming in C or micro-python language, data transfer protocols (USB, WiFi and Bluetooth), graphic user interface (GUI) design in Matlab and Python to visualize the signals, and various data processing technologies to extract useful information about the health status of the human body. The students will have the opportunity to design a new biomedical device from sensing, amplifying, hardware design, PC control software and signal processing algorithms all by themselves. The objective of the course is to provide students with as close to a real-world industrial biomedical engineering design experience as is possible in an academic setting. This course can enhance students’ abilities to solve engineering problems independently and enrich students’ professional skills in biomedical engineering for future job hunting or academic career.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100266,'BME3320','生物医学影像','Biomedical Imaging','BME - Biomedical Engineering','3320','B',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2020-21 Term 1
