2025-26 Term 1','STA2001 Probability and Statistics I      MAT1001 Calculus I      MAT2040 Linear Algebra','','生物医学影像课程涵盖了几种人体生物成像方式的物理学原理，包括X射线和计算机断层扫描，超声成像、磁共振成像、磁性颗粒成像、正电子发射计算机断层扫描、单光子发射计算机断层成像术、光学成像、分子影像、多模成像及内窥成像技术。本课程将介绍几种成像技术的仪器设计，数据採集策略，图像重建技术和在临床上的应用基础。学生将对本课程涵盖的生物成像模式的机理有基本的了解，包括影像形成的内部工作原理以及可能的生物医学应用范围。本课程将进一步介绍生物医学影像的最新进展及应用。基于本课程的学习，学生将能够判断针对特定生命科学的需求选择合适的成像诊断方式，并了解每种方式的局限性和应用前景。','This biomedical imaging course covers the physical principles of major imaging modalities, i.e., X-ray and computed tomography, ultrasonic imaging, magnetic resonance imaging, magnetic particle imaging, positron emission tomography/single photon emission computed tomography, multimodality imaging, optical imaging, molecular imaging, and endoscopic imaging.  This course covers the basics for instrumental design, data acquisition strategies, image reconstruction techniques and clinical applications of these imaging techniques. The student will develop a good understanding of the mechanisms leading to tissue contrast of the bio-imaging modalities covered in this course, including the inner workings of the scanner and how they define the range of possible biomedical applications. This course will briefly introduce the latest advances in biomedical imaging and future applications. Based on this course, the student will be able to judge which imaging modality is adequate for specific life science needs and to understand the limits and promises of each modality.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100267,'BME4001','生物系统与控制','Biological Systems and Control','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4001','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','BIO1001 General Biology / BIO1008 Chemistry and Life Sciences
MAT1001 Calculus I','NA','本课程将向学生提供一个控制工程的视角来以了解多尺度生物系统如何根据自身内部的组织协调性以有效地实现生物功能。其内容涉及到很多层次的生物系统，包括原子层面（众多原子是如何组织成为分子的，分子动力学模拟是研究这个层面的有力工具），分子层面（例如生物分子相互作用网络），直到人体组织（机体层面动力学，包括葡萄糖-胰岛素稳态平衡系统，脂肪稳态平衡系统）。本课程将使用具有科研及临床意义的特定例子来解释概念及原理。','This course aims to provide students with a control engineering perspective of the function, organization, and coordination of multi-scale biological systems and the control mechanisms that enable them to carry out their biological functions effectively. Topics span multiple biological levels ranging from atoms (how the atoms are organized into molecules, with MD simulation as a tool), to molecules (e.g., the interaction network of biomolecules) to human body (the organismal level dynamics, such as glucose-insulin homeostasis, fat-mass homeostasis).  The concepts and principles will be illustrated using specific examples with significant research and clinical implications.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
