2026-27 Term 1','BIO1001 General Biology      BME3001 Intro to BME I','','生物材料至今已经成为生物医学工程领域的重要学科。从医疗器械开发到手术工具设计，生物材料一直引领着生物医学创新。然而，研发可以用于生物医学领域的材料是一个具有跨学科性以及挑战性过程，需要了解材料的体积和表面特性、对材料的各种生物反应、其使用的临床背景、制造工艺、成本、灭菌、包装和监管问题。本课程旨在向学生介绍现阶段在临床与产业种已经广泛应用的各种生物材料。更重要的是，本课程还包括了许多实验动手操作的内容，培养学生对生物材料合成的兴趣和技能，以及将生物材料应用于下游医疗应用的能力。在本课程结束时，学生将全面了解生物材料在生物医学工程中的基本原理及其应用应用。','Biomaterials have grown as a key subject in the biomedical engineering field. From medical device development to surgical tool design, biomaterials lie at the centre of biomedical innovation. Developing materials for use in the biomedical field is a challenging interdisciplinary process and requires an understanding of material bulk and surface properties, the various biological responses to the materials, the clinical context of their use, manufacturing processes, cost, sterilization, packaging and regulatory issues. This course is designed to introduce students to the various classes of biomaterials from the basics of materials preparation to their applications in popular areas of the biomedical field. Additionally, this course also includes experimental sessions cultivating students’ interests and hand-on skills in biomaterial synthesis together with the capabilities to apply the biomaterials in downstream bioapplications. At the end of this course, students will have a comprehensive understanding of the fundamentals and popular applications of biomaterials in biomedical engineering.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100271,'BME4007','组织工程','Tissue Engineering','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4007','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology     
BME3001 Intro to BME I','NA','本课程的目的是帮助学生了解工程细胞的原理，并确保学生可以有效的将这些知识应用于制药产业以及医疗设备产业中生物产品的设计流程。本课程将从理论和实践的角度概述了制药和医疗器械行业基于细胞的产品的理念。本课程将涵盖细胞如何产生生物有效成分（例如蛋白质和碳水化合物药物以及抗体）的基础；如何从细菌和哺乳动物系统中产生生物有效成分；生物制剂生产的工艺设计和优化；商业生物制剂的案例研究；细胞疗法；类器官和人造器官用于疾病模型研究或组织再生治疗；组织工程的原理，包括生物材料、细胞和生长因子，以及这些原理在各种组织中的临床应用。','The aim of this course is to develop an understanding of the principles of engineering cells and apply this knowledge to design processes to produce biologics for the pharmaceutical market or tissue engineered medical devices. This course outlines the concepts of cell-based products for the pharmaceutical and medical device industries from both a theoretical and practical perspective. This course will cover the basis of how biologics (eg protein and carbohydrate drugs and antibodies) are produced by cells; recombinant technologies to produce biologics from bacterial and mammalian systems; process design and optimization for the production of biologics; case studies of commercial biologics; cell therapies; organoids and artificial organs as disease model or tissue regeneration strategy; the principles of tissue engineering, including biomaterials, cells and growth factors, and the clinical application of these principles in various tissues.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100272,'BME4008','人体生物力学','Biomechanics of the Human Body','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4008','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','BIO1001 General Biology      PHY1001 Mechanics      MAT1001 Calculus I','','人体生物力学是近年来高速发展的生物工程学的一个重要分支。本课程为学生提供了整个生物力学的概貌，培养学生将生物医学与力学等定量科学相结合的能力。课程涵盖从单细胞到整个人体的多个层面，例如细胞生物力学，血液动力学，循环系统，组织间隙，眼生物力学，呼吸系统，肌肉与运动，骨生物力学，陆上行动，等等。','This course aims to provide students with a broad overview of biomechanics, which is a rapidly growing field and an important branch of bioengineering. It fosters students the capability of integrating biomedicine with quantitative, physics-based disciplines. Topics span multiple biological levels ranging from single cells to human body, such as cellular biomechanics, hemodynamics, the circulatory system, the interstitium, ocular biomechanics, the respiratory system, muscles and movement, skeletal biomechanics, and terrestrial locomotion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100273,'BME4009','临床实验室科学','Clinical Laboratory Science','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4009','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
