2025-26 Term 2','BME2001 Anatomy/Physiology     
BME3001 Intro to BME I     
BIO2002 Cell and Molecular Biology','NA','本实验课程提供有关操作各种临床实验室测试系统（生物化学、血液学、免疫学等）的基础科学知识、技术、测试和实践培训。学生将掌握测量某些复杂器官系统的某些生理参数所涉及的基本原理，包括消化系统、泌尿系统、肺系统、生殖系统、内分泌系统、心脏系统、神经系统、免疫系统和肌肉骨骼系统。同时，本实验室课程将侧重于涉及临床实验室测试系统操作的实践操作，例如血压计、血细胞计数器、血糖仪、测孕试纸条等。学生将探索生物医学工程师如何使用这些基础知识（例如生物化学和工程技术）为研究实验室和临床环境开发检测设备或工具。','This lab course provides the fundamental science, technologies, tests, and hands on training on operation of a variety of clinical laboratory testing systems (biochemistry, haematology, immunology, et al.). The students will be exposed to the underlying principles involved in the measurement of certain physiological parameters from some of the complex organ systems including the digestive-, urinary-, pulmonary-, reproductive-, endocrine-, cardiac-, nervous-, immune- and musculoskeletal systems. Meanwhile, this lab course will focus on practical sessions involving the operation of testing systems in clinic labs, such as sphygmomanometer, haemocytometeror, cytometer, glucose meters, pregnancy test strips, et al. Students will explore how Biomedical Engineers have used these fundamentals (e.g. biochemistry and engineering techniques) to develop diagnostic equipment or tools for the research laboratory and clinical environment.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100274,'BME4010','3D生物制造与再生医学','3D Biofabrication and Regenerative Medicine 3D','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4010','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','•	Cell and Molecular Biology (BIO2002*)
•	Introduction to Biomedical Engineering (BME3001)','','作为一项新兴技术，生物制造在学术研究和商业创新中获得了广泛的普及。本课程的目的是加深对生物制造技术原理的理解，并将这些知识应用于功能性组织和植入式装置设计过程用于疾病的诊断或治疗。本课程从理论和实践的角度概述增材制造、3D 生物打印和生物组装技术，并将其应用于组织修复和生物植入式装置制造中。本课程将涵盖生物制造的基础和不同类型的生物制造技术，包括已在学术和商业上使用的增材制造、3D 打印、生物打印和生物组装。此外，还将介绍不同类型的生物打印方法，如挤出法打印、液滴打印、立体光刻制备， 或立体生物打印，以及它们在不同下游临床应用中的优缺点。此外，学生将学习生物墨水或生物树脂设计的基本知识，及其潜在的商业化前景。学生也将获得亲手操作3D 生物打印机和微流体系统的实践技能。','As a new emerging technology, biofabrication gains its popularity in academic research and commercial applications. The aim of this course is to develop an understanding of the principles of biofabrication technology towards manufacturing, and apply this knowledge to design processes to construct functional tissues and implants for disease diagnosis or treatment. This course outlines the concepts of additive manufacturing, 3D bioprinting and bioassembly in tissue repair and bioimplant fabrication from both a theoretical and practical perspective. This course will cover the basis of biofabrication and different type of biofabrication technologies including additive manufacturing, 3D printing, bioprinting and bioassembly that have been used academically and commercially. In addition, different types of bioprinting such as extrusion-based, drop-on-demand based, DLP based or volumetric based will be introduced, together with their merits and demerits for different downstream clinical applications. Also, students will learn the basic knowledge in bioink or bioresin design, and the commercialization potential. Most importantly, students will have hand-on experience in 3D bioprinter and microfluidics system.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100275,'BME4011','纳米生物技术','Nanobiotechnology','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4011','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','BME3001 Introduction to Biomedical Engineering I','','纳米生物技术以纳米材料为载体结合多种工程化手段来制造纳米尺度器件并应用体外诊断及体内载药治疗等。它有多重的潜能来推动医学科学及全球健康管理。该课程将覆盖研发纳米尺度新型材料所用到的各种技术以及对于它们的操控来实现对生物系统在分子水平的调控。本课程侧重于为学生提供工程-化学-物理以及生物交叉学科界面的基本信息，引导学生获取一个关于如何将具有独特光学-化学-磁性-以及结构特性的纳米材料应用到医学诊断及治疗的全局视野。修完该课程，学生应具备理解生物分子于不同化学-物理材料界面相互作用，同时有能力制备和应用一些简单的纳米生物材料到生物领域来实现基本的生物分析，生物技术问题以及评估各种纳米材料的生物安全性。','Nanobiotechnology applies nanomaterials-based carriers with numerous engineering methodologies to obtain functional nanoparticles and nanodevices to allow both in vitro and in vivo applications. This course aims to provide basic knowledge in the interface between engineering, chemistry, physics and biology on the nano-scale level. It will cover a vast and diverse array of technologies from developing new materials with dimensions on the nanoscale to investigating whether they can be used to directly control matters on/in the atomic-scale level to study or modulate diverse properties of a biological system on molecular basis. It will provide an overview of how nanosized materials with unique chemical, optical, magnetic and/or structural properties are transforming medical diagnostics and therapy. Novel biotechnology integrated with nanomaterials will be also introduced. At the end of this course students should be able to understand interaction of biomolecules with surfaces of different chemical and physical species, have the capability to produce and apply simple model of nanostructured materials in biological settings to solve simple biotechnical and bioanalytical problems, and assess biosafety of nanomaterials in biological systems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
