2025-26 Summer','BME3001 Introduction to Biomedical Engineering I','','生物医学工程实习是BME学生课程的一个组成部分。他们加入境内或境外的相关领域头部公司/研究机构，完成约12周的实习或研究项目，锻炼和培养学生成为未来卓越工程师和业界翘楚的能力。这次实习旨在帮助学生沉浸在当今专业领域前沿，让他们意识到团队合作，并熟悉行业程序。此外，学生将能够应用他们在港中深获得的知识和技能，测试自己的实践能力。学生可以在研究实习期间撰写进度报告。如果公司在特定领域进行研究，学生也可以考虑将实习项目转化为研究课题。这也将使学生通过产学结合与实践结合，提升对相关领域的深层次理解。','The Biomedical engineering internship is an integral part of the curriculum for BME students. This course provides opportunities for students to complete a 12-week engineering internship in a leading company/research institute during their studies, where their skills of future engineers are highlighted. This internship is designed to help students immerse themselves in the professional world, make them aware of teamwork, and familiarize them with industry procedures. In addition, students will be able to test their skills and apply the knowledge they have acquired at CUHKSZ. Students can write their progress report during a research internship. If the company does research in a particular area, consider turning an internship into a research project. This will also allow the student to get closer to the cutting-edge research and industrial development by combining their knowledge and practical experience.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100279,'BME4015','医疗器械转化设计','Medical Device Translational Design Project','BME - Biomedical Engineering','4015','B',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','BME3001 Introduction to Biomedical Engineering I
BME3006 Biosensors and Medical Devices','None.','该课程旨在培养学生实验室的技术转化为商业化产品的素养，以解决医疗保健问题的理论和实践技能，从项目设计到向观众推销想法。教学模式包括理论讲座、案例研究、动手设计器件、客座讲座，以获得可穿戴/植入式传感器/医疗设备方面的专业知识。学生将学习和练习批判性思维、设计、原型制作和商业化医疗设备方面的技能，例如，基于微机电系统的医疗设备（MEMS 医疗设备）。该课程强调学生动手能力的培养，学生应该能够设计一种可以转化的医疗设备，为参加生物医学设备技术比赛储备能力。在本课程结束时，学生将能够单独撰写商业计划，并接受培训以申请医疗器械相关资金，成为年轻的、崭露头角的未来企业家。','This laboratory-based course introduces students to the theoretical and practical skills of translating laboratory-based technology into a commercialized product to address healthcare problems, from project design to selling ideas to the audience. Students will actively engage in a strategic combination of theoretical lectures, case studies, hands-on device design, guest lectures, and in-person industry exposures to gain expertise in wearable/implantable sensors/medical devices. The students will learn and practice skills in critical thinking, designing, prototyping, and commercializing medical devices, for example, Micro Electro Mechanical Systems-based medical devices (MEMS medical devices). Students will be equipped with the ability to navigate regulatory frameworks and develop commercialization strategies, preparing them for revolution in biomedical engineering. The course emphasizes key components for revolutionary translational pathways, global regulatory compliance, and international market entry strategies. With the aim of providing training for a future entrepreneur, students should be able to design a medical device that can be translational. Eventually, during the entire course duration, the students will learn how to establish their entrepreneurship in the future using their developed business plan. They will be rigorously trained to participate in biomedical device technology-based competitions and present their developed, potent technology-based products; their plans to clear ethical and regulatory guidelines will be assessed. In due course, they will develop the individual capability to establish themselves as start-up entrepreneurs in the future. At the end of this course, students will be individually able to write an effective business plan and trained to apply for medical device-associated funding to be young, budding entrepreneurs.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
