(100396,'CHI2019','文物与中国古典文学','','CHI - Chinese','2019','C',3.00,2000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','CHI1000','','本课程是一门了解中国古代文物与古典文学关系的概述性课程。课程将介绍中国古代文物的基本面貌，古典文学作品如何描写文物，文物如何成为文学创作和抒情的灵感。课程将从文明交流的视角展开，重点介绍政治、礼仪、文化、生活等场景中涉及的如青铜器、古陶瓷、书画、碑刻、造像、建筑以及其他器用等在古典文学中的书写，以及文物里的古典文学装饰与审美，由此探讨如何更好地读懂文物与文学，以及从文学的视角了解中国古代文物的文化和审美价值。','This course provides an overview of the relationship between ancient Chinese relics and classical literature. It will introduce the fundamental aspects of ancient Chinese cultural relics, explore how classical literary works depict these cultural relics, and examine how such objects have inspired literary creation and emotional expression.

Approaching the subject from the perspective of civilizational exchange, this course will focus on analyzing depictions in classical literature of cultural relics embedded in contexts such as politics, rituals, culture, and daily life—including bronze ware, ancient ceramics, calligraphy and painting, steles, statues, architecture, and miscellaneous artifacts. Additionally, it will explore the literary decorations and aesthetic elements found on these cultural relics.

This course aims to examine how to better understand both cultural relics and literature, as well as how to comprehend the cultural and aesthetic values of ancient Chinese cultural relics from a literary perspective.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100397,'CHI3001','现代文学导论','','CHI - Chinese','3001','C',3.00,3000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 2
2021-22 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2022-23 Summer','CHI1000 Chinese 大学中文','','中国现代文学诞生过一大批重要作品，也参与形塑了现代中国的面貌。本课程主要依循现代文学的产生、发展、演变、影响，介绍现代文学史上的重要作家、作品、文学思潮、文学团体与流派。围绕小说、诗歌、散文、戏剧四大文类，学生将研习鲁迅、沈从文、茅盾、徐志摩、老舍、张爱玲、西西、白先勇等人的代表作，并分析文学研究会、创造社、左联、新月派、京派、海派等文学团体与流派的产生脉络、文学理念与艺术风格。本课程旨在引领学生认识现代文学的嬗变、文学价值与历史意义，提升其文学鉴赏与思维能力。','This survey course examines the context and production of modern Chinese literature as well as its contribution to the shaping of modern China. We study the genres of fiction, poetry, prose and drama and focus on the masterpieces by Lu Xun, Shen Congwen, Mao Dun, Xu Zhimo, Lao She, Eileen Zhang, Xixi, Bai Xianyong, etc. We also pay attention to  literary communities or literary schools like Wenxue Yanjiu Hui (“Literary Research Association”), Chuangzao She (“Creation Society”), Zuoyi Zuojia Lianmeng (League of Left-Wing Writers), Xinyue Pai (“Crescent Moon Society”), Jing Pai (“Beijing School”), and Hai Pai (“Shanghai School”).  The purpose of this course is to guide students to grasp the development, styles and historical background of modern Chinese literature and enhance their abilities of literary appreciation and critical thinking.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100398,'CHI3002','实用文写作','','CHI - Chinese','3002','C',3.00,3000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100399,'CHI3008','独幕剧写作','','CHI - Chinese','3008','C',3.00,3000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Summer','CHI1000 Chinese大学中文','','本课程由职业剧作家开设，以创作实践为主，面向写作爱好者，提供独幕剧的基础知识、引导训练和近身指导，通过阅读、讨论、写作和演出，参与体验独幕剧生成的完整过程。课程旨在释放学生的写作潜能，培养和提高学生的剧本创作能力和舞台呈现能力。
课程将借鉴西方现代写作教育中的“创意写作”这一有效观念，改造传统写作课程，成立工作坊，以教师主讲和工作坊这两种形式交互进行。教师主讲环节将依托经典独幕剧作品，进行基础理论和知识的讲授，布置驱动任务，对工作坊中出现的代表性问题进行集中点评。工作坊环节，学生会阅读和讨论经典剧作，发掘和分享个人经验，完成个人化的驱动任务，最终每个工作坊将集体完成一部独幕剧的创作和演出；教师将会深入工作坊，对学生进行近身指导。
学生将在课程中获得来自职业剧作家的一对一指导，打磨作品，发展写作技术；在工作坊中，学生将了解他人经历，拓展自身经验，感受文学创作在日常生活中的意义，同时练习接受和给予建设性批评的艺术，享受阅读和写作的乐趣。','Taught by a professional playwright, this course focuses on creative practice. It introduces the foundational knowledge of one-act plays to writing enthusiasts and offers training guidance and personalized instruction. Through reading, discussion, writing, and performance, students will participate in the complete process of producing a one-act play. The course aims to unleash students'' writing potential and cultivate and enhance their scriptwriting and stage presentation skills.
The course draws on the practical concept of "creative writing" in modern Western writing education and transforms traditional writing courses by interacting lectures with workshops. During the lectures, relying on classic one-act play works, the teacher provides students with fundamental theories and knowledge, assigns driving tasks, and focuses on representative problems arising during the workshop. Complementarily, students read and discuss classic plays, discover and share personal experiences, and complete personalized driving tasks during the workshops. Ultimately each group is required to create and perform a one-act play collectively. Besides, the teacher provides customized instruction during the workshop.
Students will receive one-on-one guidance from a professional playwright to polish their works and develop their writing skills. In the workshop, students can learn about others, expand their experience, feel the significance of literary creation in daily life, practice the art of accepting and giving constructive criticism, and enjoy the pleasure of reading and writing.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,'');

