(100407,'CHI4012','广东方言与岭南文化','','CHI - Chinese','4012','C',3.00,4000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','CHI1000 大学中文','','方言是语言的地域变体。本课介绍广东的几大方言以及它们所反映的中国岭南文化特色。包括：1.广东粤语、客语、闽语的语音、词汇、语法特征的介绍；2. 三大方言的历史形成、分布特点；3. 三大方言与岭南文化特征，包括方言与人名、地名、饮食、心理、风俗、商业、文字、娱乐等的关系。

本课程特点：老师提供丰富的方言例证并作启发式的讲解，其与文化关系的深入探讨由学生通过自学以讨论、撰写论文等形式完成。','Dialect is regional variant of language. This course introduces the major dialects of Guangdong and the features of Lingnan culture reflected in them. The course covers the following points:
1. An Introduction to the Phonetic, phonological, and grammatical characteristics of Guangdong’s Yue, Hakka, and Min dialects; 2.The historical formation and distribution characteristics of these three dialects; 3. The relationship between the three major dialects and Lingnan cultural features, in their connections with personal names, place names, cuisine, psychology, customs, commerce, Chinese characters, entertainment, etc.

This course is characterised by the lecturer providing abundant dialectal examples and heuristic explanations. In-depth exploration of the relationship between dialects and culture is to be completed by students through self-study, discussions, and the composition of academic essays.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100408,'CHI5010','语言、文学与文化高级专题研讨会','','CHI - Chinese','5010','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程的研讨，聚焦三位20世纪杰出的中华学者作家：钱钟书、夏志清、余光中。钱钟书长居中国大陆，夏志清长居海外（美国），余光中长居中国台湾与香港；三个不同的地域，涵盖了整个“大中华”。钱夏余三位于诗文小说创作，各有卓越成就。钱钟书比较中西文化，有其“东海西海，心理攸同”学说；夏志清于文学批评，有其《中国现代小说史》，成一家之言，影响深远；余光中的中西语言论述，尊“善性西化”斥“恶性西化”，让国人增强对美丽母语的自信。一人而兼学者与作家，且其表现众口交誉，他们三位名垂中国20世纪文学史。本课程让学生认识或加强认识他们的作品，尝试分析其成功的个人因素和环境因素；并通过讨论，对中国的语言、文学、文化的特质和发展，有进一步的了解。','This course focuses on three outstanding scholar-writers, namely Qian Zhongshu who spent most of his life in Chinese Mainland, Xia Zhiqing (C.T. Hsia) who had lived in the U.S. since he left China when young, and Yu Guangzhong who had lived in Taiwan, China and Hong Kong, China since he left Chinese Mainland in his youth. All three together forms a group of scholar-writers representing the “Greater China.” Qian, Xia and Yu all excel in their creative writing: poetry, prose and fiction. In East-west comparative culture study, Qian makes his name known for his theory of “Heart and mind share common values between the East and the West.” As regards literary criticism, Xia Zhiqing’s seminal work A History of Modern Chinese Fiction has cast tremendous influences on the academics. In the field of language study, Yu Guangzhong is opposed to what he calls the “bad- westernized Chinese” ; he praises the mother-tongue Chinese for its history-long vitality, its simplicity in grammar and its capability for producing writings of various styles. This course will enable the students to learn the achievements of these three magnificent  scholar-writers, or to enhance students’ knowledge about them. Furthermore, through lectures and tutorials, students are supposed to acquire more knowledge about the characteristics of the Chinese language, Chinese literature and Chinese culture; and also about the developments of these.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100409,'CHI5020','研究方法与论文写作高级专题研讨会','','CHI - Chinese','5020','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','為研究中國語言、文學、歷史、哲學等人文學科的研究生而設計。課程將引導學生尊重學術倫理，遵從學術規範，學習人文學研究論文的寫作技巧和格式（包括人工智能工具）。本課程通過大量使用中英文工具書、數據庫、相關網站和專門設計的練習，訓練學生獨立深入解讀中文文獻、從事人文學研究的基本技巧及相關的文化背景。鼓勵同學們在每週練習中借助人工智慧工具完成作業，並按學術規範嚴格覆核。','This course is designed mainly for graduate students who will deal  with  Chinese  humanities,  such  as  language,  literature, history,  philosophy,  etc.  The  teacher  will  guide  students  to respect academic ethics, comply with academic norms, and learn writing skills, styles and format, including AI tools, in humanities studies.  The  design  of  this  course  emphasizes  on  developing students''  ability to  solve  reading  difficulties,  better understand relevant cultural background,  and find problems in humanities researches  independently,  with   specifically  assigned  exercises through extensive use of Chinese and English reference books, databases and websites. Students are encouraged to using AI tools in weekly exercises with scholarly reexaminations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100410,'CHI5110','语言学专题','','CHI - Chinese','5110','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程旨在使学生熟悉韵律音系学及其在汉语中的应用，主要关注韵律音系学中最近发展的理论、概念和新技术。训练学生从韵律单位（如音节、音步和韵律词）所构成的节奏结构方面分析自然语音、散文和诗歌，为将来学习语言和文学打下坚实的基础。','The purpose of this course is to acquaint students with the prosodic phonology and its application in Chinese, mainly focusing on theories, concepts and new techniques developed recently in metrical phonology. Students will be trained to analyze natural speech, prose as well as poetry in terms of rhythmic structures construed by prosodic units of mora, syllable, foot, and prosodic word, in order to lay a solid foundation for their future studies on language and literature.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100411,'CHI5120','语文学专题','','CHI - Chinese','5120','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100412,'CHI5130','汉语构词与句法研究','','CHI - Chinese','5130','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在引导学生系统认识汉语构词、句法结构及相关语义特征中的核心问题。课程结合汉语语法学的重要理论、研究方法与丰富语料，深入分析现代汉语中词、短语和句子的内部结构及其运作机制。课程亦将帮助学生深化对汉语语法理论的理解，并运用相关理论对语言现象进行解释与论证，为进一步从事汉语语言学研究或处理与中文相关的语言问题奠定基础。','This course aims to guide students in systematically understanding key issues in Chinese morphology, syntactic structures, and related semantic features. By integrating major theories and research methods in Chinese grammar with rich linguistic data, the course provides an in-depth analysis of the internal structures and mechanisms of words, phrases, and sentences in Modern Chinese. It also helps students deepen their understanding of Chinese grammatical theories and apply relevant theories to explain and justify linguistic phenomena, laying a foundation for further research in Chinese linguistics or for addressing Chinese-related language issues.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100413,'CHI5140','佛教历史与语言','','CHI - Chinese','5140','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程介绍佛教发展简史，以及佛教在印度、丝绸之路和中国的语言，包括梵语、俗语（犍陀罗语）和佛教汉语。课程重点关注梵语和犍陀罗语的文献学研究，以及佛教汉语的语言学研究。通过修习本课程，学生将对佛教对汉语的影响有全面的认识，并且能够从语言接触和语法化的角度理解汉语的历时演变。','The course introduces a brief history of Buddhism. In addition, the languages of Buddhism in India, on the Silk Road, and in China, which are vital methods of the spread and development of Buddhism, such as Sanskrit, Prakrits (including Gandhari) and Buddhist Chinese. The course focuses on the philological study on Sanskrit and Gandhari, and linguistic study on Buddhist Chinese. Students will have an overall understanding of the influence of Buddhism on Chinese language by taking the course. They can review the diachronic evolution of Chinese language from the perspective of language contact and grammaticalization.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100414,'CHI5150','汉语方言学','','CHI - Chinese','5150','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课介绍汉语各大方言的音系、词汇、语法。这些大方言包括官话方言、吴方言、湘方言、赣方言、客家方言、粤方言和闽方言。','This   course  will   cover  major   Chinese   dialects''  phonology, lexicon,  and  syntax,  including  Mandarin,  Wu,  Xiang,  Gan, Hakka, Yue, and Min.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100415,'CHI5160','古代文献专题','','CHI - Chinese','5160','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100416,'CHI5210','古典文学专题：小说','','CHI - Chinese','5210','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在指导学生研习中国古典小说，探讨不同小说类型之发展脉络、叙述特色、思想内涵与文化意义。课程首先概述古典小说之源流、体制与影响，在对小说文体有整体认识的基础上，引导学生重点阅读和分析部分经典作品，作出创造性表达。学生将运用文本细读与批判思考的能力，讨论文学传统中的普遍议题，增强对古典小说及其相关时代背景、思想潮流的了解，并加深对古典文学与传统文化的体认。','This course offers a critical survey of some of the masterpieces in Chinese fiction, including the historical development, narrative characteristics, ideological implications, and cultural influence of different sub-genres of fiction. The course begins with an overview of the origins, features, and influences of classical fiction. Building upon a comprehensive understanding of the fictional forms, students are directed to engage in focused reading and analysis of selected canonical works, fostering creative expression. Through close textual reading and critical thinking, students will discuss universal themes within literary traditions, thereby enhancing their comprehension of classical works, their respective historical contexts, intellectual trends, and deepening their appreciation for classical literature and traditional culture.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100417,'CHI5220','古典文学专题：戏曲','','CHI - Chinese','5220','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程概述古典戏曲之体制、形式、剧场及演变发展，重点论析古典戏曲中的四大名剧：《西厢记》《牡丹亭》《长生殿》《桃花扇》。这些作品产生于不同时期，受时代精神与作家个人情志的影响。课程拟循着元明清戏曲的发展历程，探讨经典作品的产生，以及不同剧类之发展脉络、艺术特色、思想内涵与社会意义。由于古典戏曲既是文学也是艺术，我们的讨论会兼顾案头与场上、文本与表演、文学性与戏剧性；部分课堂时间也会用来观赏、分析由原著整理改编的戏曲表演或电影。','This course provides an overview of the structure, form, theatre and evolution of classical opera, with a focus on the four most famous classical operas: The Story of the Western Wing, The Peony Pavilion, The Palace of Eternal Youth and The Peach Blossom Fan. These works were produced in different periods and were influenced by the spirit of the times and the writers'' personal sentiments. Following the development of opera in the Yuan, Ming and Qing dynasties, the course will explore the production of classical works, as well as the development of different types of theatre, their artistic characteristics, ideological connotations and social significance. Since classical opera is both literature and art, our class will strike a balance between the text and the performance, the literary and the dramatic; part of the class time will also be devoted to viewing and analysing performances or films based on the original works.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100418,'CHI5230','古典文学专题：散文','','CHI - Chinese','5230','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100419,'CHI5240','古典文学专题：诗歌','','CHI - Chinese','5240','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程为中国古典诗歌的专题课程。课程选取古典诗话等诗学批评材料，结合代表性古典诗歌篇目细读，探讨相关的古典诗学概念及命题，以引导学生了解中国古典诗歌读解的基本进路，建构诗学史的整体观念，为古典诗歌领域较为深入的研究提供学术路径与框架。','This course aims to show students the history of Chinese classical poetry through the explanation of Chinese classical poetry knowledge and the selection and intensive reading of famous masterpieces and to guide them to understand the artistic characteristics and techniques of classical poetry, and to feel the charm and taste of classical poets.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100420,'CHI5250','古典文学专题：文学批评','','CHI - Chinese','5250','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','','','本科旨在通过讲授中国古代各时期文学批评，使学生掌握中国古代文学批评的基本文献、理论范畴及价値系统，加深对中国古代文学传统的理解。','This course offers a chronological introduction to traditional literary criticism. It will help students to comprehend the fundamental concepts and characteristics of literary criticism and theory and the ways of putting these concepts into practice. It will enhance students’ ability to appreciate and criticize literary works as well as improve their writing skills.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100421,'CHI5310','现代文学专题','','CHI - Chinese','5310','C',3.00,5000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程是“现代文学专题”下的一个分题，名称是“余光中与中国现代文学”。这里的中国现代文学定义比较广阔，指的是“五四”至今的中国文学。本课程先概述中国现代文学的发展，包括论说其主要特色与成就为何，继而以整个中国现代文学为参照系，论述余光中在诗歌、散文、文学评论、翻译、编辑五方面的表现，也即是本人所说的“璀璨的五采笔”。前三者为论述重点。本课程重视作品的实际分析和评价，说明余光中在继承古典与西方文学之际，如何有其创新之处。余光中成就卓越，驰誉中华文学界，通过对余光中作品的阅读讨论，学生当更能认识“唯华有材，于斯为盛”之景象。','This course focuses on “Yu Guangzhong and Modern Chinese Literature”, under the heading of “Special Topics of Modern Chinese Literature”. It will first be a general introduction to modern Chinese Literature since the May-fourth Movement and then reading and discussion on the five literary genres of works of Yu Guangzhong, namely poetry, prose, literary criticism, translation and editorial art. Yu Guangzhong’s works will be viewed in the perspective of the entire body of modern Chinese Literature.  His creative talents will be illuminated when he is compared with the performance of certain masters of modern Chinese literature. Yu Guangzhong is very well known and much respected in the Chinese world of literature. Students will be shown how worthwhile it is in understanding and appreciating this remarkable figure in modern Chinese literature.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
