a.	Read the laboratory manual and the relevant reference material thoroughly, and familiarize yourself with the experiment that you are going to perform.  Familiarize yourself with the experimental apparatus setup and the physical methods you are going to work with.  Look up the relevant reference books and literatures, or consult the demonstrators / instructor whenever necessary.  (Remember: whenever you have any doubt, consult your de','本實驗室課程涵蓋了基本的實驗室和計算機技術，這些技術說明了物理化學的基本原理。這些實驗為學生提供了以下方面的綜合培訓：(1)化學試劑和化學廢物的安全處理； (2)正確使用物理化學常用的實驗室儀器和設備； (3)物理化學中計算機應用的基本技術； (4)利用實驗數據和結果進行理論研究的基本程序和技術； (5) 記錄、處理和報告實驗數據和結果； (6)開展科學文獻檢索。本課程讓學生獲得物理化學基礎實驗實踐的經驗。實驗手冊可從課程講師處獲得。','This laboratory course covers basic laboratory and computer techniques that illustrate the fundamental principles of physical chemistry. These experiments provide students with comprehensive training on (1) the safe handling of chemical reagents and chemical wastes; (2) the correct use of laboratory instruments and equipment commonly used in physical chemistry; (3) basic techniques for computer application in physical chemistry; (4) basic procedures and techniques for researching theory using experimental data and results; (5) Recording, processing and reporting experimental data and results; (6) Conducting scientific literature searches. This course allows students to gain experience in basic experimental practice in physical chemistry. Lab manuals are available from the course instructor.
 This laboratory course includes experiments that involve some basic concepts of equilibrium and change such as chemical kinetics and reaction dynamics. It allows students to acquire fundamental understanding of the chemical reactivity.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
