2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程系统介绍材料科学与工程的基本原理，围绕“加工/制备—结构—性能—服役表现”这一核心范式，阐明材料从原子尺度到微观组织的结构特征如何决定宏观性能与工程应用。课程覆盖材料科学中的关键基础主题，包括相图的解读与应用、扩散机制与动力学、相变与组织演化，以及材料的典型性能与测试思路。在此基础上，课程进一步讨论材料的主要性能领域与工程问题：力学性能、热学性能、电学/光学/磁学性能等，并概述常见材料的生产与加工路线。','This course introduces the fundamental principles of materials science and engineering, focusing on how materials’ composition and internal structure—from atomic bonding and crystal structure to microstructure—govern macroscopic properties and performance. Using the materials paradigm of processing–structure–properties–performance, students learn to connect how materials are produced and processed with the resulting mechanical, thermal, electrical, optical, and magnetic behaviors. Core topics include diffusion and phase transformations, interpretation of phase diagrams, strengthening and deformation mechanisms, corrosion and degradation processes, and an overview of major manufacturing routes.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
