2026-27 Term 1','CHM1001 or CHM1011','','本课程的开设对象主要面向化学和材料专业高年级本科生，主要讲授过渡金属有机化学，重点介绍金属有机化合物（含主族元素和过渡金属）的基本性质及合成方法、金属有机化学的基本反应以及与此直接相关的均相催化。课程共分 12 章节，包括：概论；金属有机化合物的基本性质；含金属-碳/氢 s-键的金属有机化合物；羰基络合物和膦配合物；π-络合物；配体取代反应；氧化加成和还原消除；插入和消除反应；亲电、亲核加成及攫取反应；卡宾和卡拜配合物；均相催化（侧重于从反应机理方面阐述包含金属有机化合物的催化反应）；人工智慧化學。','This course is mainly oriented to the senior undergraduate students in chemistry and materials, which covers the organometallic chemistry of main group elements and transition metals with emphasis on the general syntheses and properties of organometallic compounds, the fundamental organometallic reactions as well as their application to homogeneous catalysis. The course contents are comprised of 12 chapters including: General introduction; General properties of organometallic complexes;
Complexes with a metal-carbon/hydrogen -bond; Carbonyls,
phosphine complexes; Complexes of π-ligands; Substitution reactions; Oxidative addition and reductive elimination; Insertion and elimination; Nucleophilic and electrophilic addition and abstraction; Carbene and carbyne complexes; Homogeneous catalysis (catalytic reactions involving organometallic compounds with an emphasis on mechanistic understanding); Artificial intelligence chemistry.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100454,'CHM4340','现代有机合成','Modern Organic Synthesis','CHM - Chemistry','4340','C',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','MSE6202 Advanced Organic Chemistry','','本课程旨在为学生系统介绍现代有机合成方法学的发展前沿与应用方向。主要内容涵盖光氧化还原催化、自由基化学、传统及镍催化的偶联反应、氧化加成与还原消除、C–H 活化、自由基时钟、卤原子转移以及流动化学等前沿主题。同时，本课程还将引入电化学方法，突出其与光催化和自由基策略的协同作用。课程不仅强调催化反应的机理基础，还关注其实用价值，帮助学生掌握设计高效、可持续合成转化的思维框架，以服务于药物研发、材料科学和化学生物学等领域。','The aim of this course is to provide students with a comprehensive overview of modern organic synthesis methodologies that are shaping the future of chemical research. Topics include photoredox catalysis, radical chemistry, traditional and nickel-catalyzed cross-couplings, oxidative addition and reductive elimination, C–H activation, radical clocks, XAT transfer, and the emerging field of flow chemistry. In addition, electrochemical methods will be introduced to highlight their synergy with photocatalytic and radical approaches. Through these themes, the course emphasizes both the mechanistic foundations and the practical applications of catalytic strategies, equipping students with the conceptual tools to design efficient and sustainable synthetic transformations relevant to pharmaceuticals, materials, and chemical biology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
