(100464,'CHM6210','高等有机金属与配位化学','','CHM - Chemistry','6210','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Possess knowledge  or attend the general chemistry, organic chemistry or inorganic chemistry course.','None.','本课程主要面向化学、材料与能源领域的研究生。它将基础的过渡金属化学与有机化学相结合，发展为有机金属科学与配位化学这一独立的重要学科方向。课程目标在于使研究生能够理解并掌握以下内容：
•	配体与金属之间成键的知识，以及相关的合成与光谱学方面的基础。
•	对有机金属反应基本类型的理解，包括插入反应、氧化加成、还原消除、氧化偶联、亲核加成与亲电加成，并认识这些关键反应在各种重要的催化与非催化过程中的作用机理。
•	相关的基础知识、技能与经验，对未来进入化学工业，或在无机配位化学、有机金属化学或有机合成等研究领域继续发展均有帮助。本课程同样适合需要掌握这一化学重要分支领域最新进展的学生。
阅读并理解该领域当前研究文献的能力。','This course is mainly oriented to the Graduate students in field of chemistry, materials and energy. The fundamental transition-metal and organic chemistry merge to produce organometallic science with coordination chemistry, a major area in its own right.  This course aims at providing graduate students with an appreciation of the following:

• knowledge of ligand-to-metal bonding and related synthetic, and spectroscopic aspects.

• An understanding of the fundamental types of organometallic reaction, such as insertion, oxidative addition, reductive elimination, oxidative coupling, nucleophilic addition and electrophilic addition and how these key reactions operate in various important catalytic and non-catalytic processes.

• The basic knowledge, skills and experience useful to those students progressing into the chemical industry or into research in either inorganic co-ordination chemistry, organometallic chemistry, or organic synthesis. The course will also be useful to those students requiring a current awareness of this major branch of chemistry.

• An ability to read and appreciate the current literature in this area.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100465,'CHM6212','高等生物无机化学','','CHM - Chemistry','6212','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100466,'CHM6322','高等物理有机化学','','CHM - Chemistry','6322','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程是一门面向研究生的进阶课程。本课程介绍了分子结构、键合和热力学的基本概念，然后逐步深入到反应机理、动力学和更高级的主题，将传统的物理有机化学原理与生物有机化学、金属有机化学、超分子化学和材料科学融会贯通。主要内容包括分子轨道理论、构象分析、非共价相互作用、分子识别、酸碱化学、立体化学、反应动力学、同位素效应、线性自由能关系、催化、有机反应机理（加成、消除、取代、重排）、周环反应、光化学和人工智能化学。

本课程兼顾理论基础和实验方法，旨在培养学生将物理有机化学的思维方式应用于各个化学领域。','This course is an advanced course for postgraduate students.

 This course introduces fundamental concepts of molecular structure, bonding, and thermodynamics before progressing to reaction mechanisms, kinetics, and advanced topics. It uniquely integrates traditional physical organic principles with bioorganic chemistry, organometallic chemistry, supramolecular chemistry, and materials science. Key topics include molecular orbital theory, conformational analysis, non-covalent interactions, molecular recognition, acid-base chemistry, stereochemistry, reaction kinetics, isotope effects, linear free energy relationships, catalysis, organic reaction mechanisms (additions, eliminations, substitutions, rearrangements), pericyclic reactions, photochemistry, and artificial intelligence chemistry.

This course emphasizes both theoretical foundations and experimental methods, preparing students to apply physical organic thinking across chemistry disciplines.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100467,'CHM6328','高等无机化学实验','','CHM - Chemistry','6328','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100468,'CHM6330','高等过渡金属化学与催化','','CHM - Chemistry','6330','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Possess knowledge  or attend the general chemistry, organic chemistry or inorganic chemistry course','None.','催化不仅在化学领域中具有重要地位，在其他相关的工业过程中同样发挥着核心作用，为高效和可持续的转化提供了基础。过渡金属配合物长期以来在催化中占据着中心位置，通过配体设计可以精确调控其结构和反应活性。近年来主族元素（第1–17族）逐渐角成为有力的替代者，为传统过渡金属体系提供互补，并为有机合成和材料化学开辟了新的策略。课程中特别强调如何设计和应用过渡金属与主族元素催化剂，以实现可持续且复杂的化学合成。学生还将就催化领域的最新进展进行专题报告，从而培养批判性分析文献及在更广泛科学背景下理解最新成果的能力。','Catalysis is important field not only in the Chemistry but also in other related industrial process,  providing the foundation for efficient and sustainable transformations. Transition metal complexes have long played a central role in catalysis, where ligand design allows fine control over structure and reactivity. In recent years, main group elements (Groups 1–17) have emerged as powerful alternatives, offering complementary pathways to traditional transition-metal systems and opening new strategies in organic synthesis and materials chemistry. Special attention is given to how both transition-metal and main-group catalysts can be designed and applied in sustainable and complex chemical synthesis. Students will also prepare presentations on current advances in catalysis, developing skills to critically analyze the literature and recent discoveries in a broader scientific context.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100469,'CHM6342','现代有机合成方法学','','CHM - Chemistry','6342','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','MSE6202 Advanced Organic Chemistry','None.','本课程旨在为研究生系统介绍现代有机合成方法学的发展前沿与应用方向。主要内容涵盖光氧化还原催化、自由基化学、传统及镍催化的偶联反应、氧化加成与还原消除、C–H 活化、自由基时钟、卤原子转移以及流动化学等前沿主题。同时，本课程还将引入电化学方法，突出其与光催化和自由基策略的协同作用。课程不仅强调催化反应的机理基础，还关注其实用价值，帮助学生掌握设计高效、可持续合成转化的思维框架，以服务于药物研发、材料科学和化学生物学等领域。','The aim of this course is to provide graduate students with a comprehensive overview of modern organic synthesis methodologies that are shaping the future of chemical research. Topics include photoredox catalysis, radical chemistry, traditional and nickel-catalyzed cross-couplings, oxidative addition and reductive elimination, C–H activation, radical clocks, XAT transfer, and the emerging field of flow chemistry. In addition, electrochemical methods will be introduced to highlight their synergy with photocatalytic and radical approaches. Through these themes, the course emphasizes both the mechanistic foundations and the practical applications of catalytic strategies, equipping students with the conceptual tools to design efficient and sustainable synthetic transformations relevant to pharmaceuticals, materials, and chemical biology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100470,'CHM6348','高等有机合成实验','','CHM - Chemistry','6348','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
