(100472,'CHM6503','高等计算化学','','CHM - Chemistry','6503','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','None','None','本课程介绍从头算分子电子结构理论中使用的方法。其重点是基于波函数的方法及其在基础量子力学中的起源。本课程将向学生介绍化学中计算机建模的目标、方法和批判性评估。它将解决建模的四个目标：解释、预测、解释和发现。在探索计算方法如何实现这些目标的过程中，本课程将涵盖生物分子建模、分子电子结构、化学动力学和实验数据解释等主题，还将教学生学习如何设计和执行一系列化学问题的计算并参与实际计算。','This course addresses the methods used in ab initio molecular electronic-structure theory. Its focus is on wave-function-based methods and their origin in fundamental quantum mechanics. The course will introduce students to the goals, methods and critical assessment of computer modelling in Chemistry. It will address the four goals of modelling: explanation, prediction, interpretation and discovery. In exploring how computational methods meet these goals, this course will then cover topics in biomolecular modelling, molecular electronic structure, chemical kinetics, and experimental data interpretation, and will also teach students to learn how to design and carry out computations for a range of chemical problems and engage in hands-on calculations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100473,'CHM6543','先进功能分子材料','','CHM - Chemistry','6543','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100474,'CHM6547','多相催化','','CHM - Chemistry','6547','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','多相催化是支撑现代化工、能源与环保产业的核心技术之一。本研究生课程系统介绍多相催化的现代概念与理论基础，涵盖表面化学、反应动力学与速率理论、反应器工程、催化剂制备与表征，以及新兴的计算方法。课程后半部分将上述原理应用于真实催化体系，包括加氢、氧化、炼油、氨与甲醇合成、环境催化及前沿的单原子催化剂等领域。学生将具备从活性、选择性与稳定性角度批判性评估催化性能的能力，并能将基本原理应用于新型催化问题的分析与解决。','Heterogeneous catalysis is one of the most critical technologies underpinning the modern chemical, energy, and environmental industries. This graduate-level course introduces modern concepts and theoretical foundations of heterogeneous catalysis, including surface chemistry, reaction kinetics and rate theory, reactor engineering, catalyst preparation and characterization, as well as emerging computational approaches. The second half of the course applies these principles to real-world catalytic systems such as hydrogenation, oxidation, refinery processes, ammonia and methanol synthesis, environmental catalysis, and cutting-edge single-atom catalysts. Students will develop the ability to critically evaluate catalytic performance in terms of activity, selectivity, and stability, and to apply fundamental principles to novel catalytic problems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
