2026-27 Term 1','Basic elements of probability theory (e.g., expectation, variance, probability density functions), basic linear algebra concepts (e.g., linear spaces and inner product, determinant, linear system of equations, eigenvalues-eigenvectors), basic calculus (e.g., derivative, gradient, integration).','','机器学习在近年来变得愈发重要,这是由于它能够从数据中提取关键特征和知识，并基于此做出准确的预测，驱动大批智能化应用。随着AI技术的兴起以及自动决策过程的需求,各行各业对机器学习专业人才的需求显著增加。本课程旨在为研究生和优秀本科生提供所需的机器学习知识和技能。具体而言,本课程侧重概率机器学习理论和模式，包括但不限于贝叶斯统计、参数和非参数法建模、注意力机制、变压器模型，状态空间模型,以及其他经典和新兴的概念、模型、理论和算法。此外,这门课程还将展示机器学习在信号处理和无线通信中的实际应用。','Machine Learning has become increasingly important in recent years due to its ability to extract insights from data and make accurate predictions. With the rise of artificial intelligence and the need to automate decision-making processes, the demand for machine learning professionals has grown significantly. This postgraduate course in Machine Learning aims to provide students with the knowledge and skills required to meet this demand and excel in this very rapidly growing field. Specially, this postgraduate course in Machine Learning provides a comprehensive overview of the fundamentals of probabilistic learning theory and models, cutting-edge topics include but not limited to Bayesian statistics, parametric and nonparametric modelling, attention mechanisms, transformer, state-space-model, as well as other classic and emerging concepts, models, and algorithms. Additionally, this course will demonstrate real-world applications of machine learning in signal processing and wireless communications. By taking this course, students will gain a solid foundation in the fundamental concepts and techniques of machine learning and its applications to real-world problems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
