2024-25 Summer','ECE2001 (or related course) and CSC3002  (or related course)','CSC3100  (or related course)','本課程旨在介紹 VLSI 電路設計自動化 (CAD) 中應用的基本概念和演算法。範圍將涵蓋數位系統物理設計的各個領域，包括電路分區、佈局規劃、佈局、佈線和時序優化。','This course aims to present the fundamental concepts and algorithms applied in Design Automation (CAD) of VLSI circuits. The scope will include various areas in Physical Design of digital systems, including circuit partitioning, floorplanning, placement, routing, and timing optimization.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100549,'CIE6139','编码理论与应用','','CIE - 计算机与信息工程','6139','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Summer','Good knowledge of basic linear algebra and probability is required. Mathematical maturity is essential because all information is captured in definitions/theorems/proofs. So a strong background in proof based courses is highly recommended.','','这是研究生水平的编码理论介绍，重点关注清晰的数学定义、基本结构和算法。 它将涵盖现代编码理论研究以及理论计算机科学和离散数学相关领域中广泛使用的几种基本方法。 第一部分涵盖了编码理论的基本概念，包括线性码和码的界限，并继续介绍代数构造，例如里德-所罗门码及其扩展，以及它们的列表解码算法。 第二部分致力于当前研究中正在开发的主题。 潜在主题列表包括极性代码、图形代码、云存储代码、索引编码和其他应用程序。','This is a graduate-level introduction to coding theory, focusing on clean mathematical definitions, essential constructions, and algorithms. It will cover several foundational methods that are widely used in modern research in coding theory and adjacent areas of theoretical computer science and discrete mathematics. The first part covers basic concepts of coding theory including linear codes and bounds on codes, and continues with algebraic constructions such as Reed-Solomon codes and their extensions, and their list decoding algorithms. The second part is devoted to topics being developed in current research. List of potential topics includes polar codes, codes on graphs, codes for the cloud storage, index coding, and other applications.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
