2025-26 Term 2','Students who can pass Introductory level Chinese proficiency test or any of the U-core Chinese (for international students) series courses (CLC1101, CLC1201, CLC1301 and CLC1401).','N/A','课程旨在为国际生提供中国诗歌以及与之相关的文化教学，满足国际生对中国诗歌文学、文化与历史等方面知识的需 求。课程以专题内容为纲，借助教材、名家朗诵、表演视频等多模态方式，围绕诗歌与隐逸文化、诗歌与节日、节气、诗歌与音乐、诗歌与绘画等话题展开教学，使其对中国诗歌文学与相关文化有初步的了解，提升其对中国文学、文化的兴趣，并能具备一定的文学鉴赏能力。本课程的教学对象为能通过初级汉语水平测试或者上过 CLC1101、CLC1201、CLC1301 与 CLC1401 中任意一门课的国际学生。','The course aims to enhance international students’ understanding of Chinese literature, culture, and history through exposing them to Chinese poetry and related culture. With the help of multimodal teaching (such as texts, pictures and videos), the course will focus on topics such as poetry and seclusion culture; poetry and festivals or solar terms; poetry and music; poetry and painting, etc. After studying this course, the students will be expected to develop a greater interest in Chinese literature and culture and a higher ability in appreciating Chinese literature. This course is designed for international students who can pass Introductory level Chinese proficiency test or have taken any of the U-core Chinese (for international students) series courses (CLC1101, CLC1201, CLC1301 and CLC1401).','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100575,'CLC2301','日常交际中的中国文化','','CLC - Chinese Language and Culture','2301','C',3.00,2000,'Chinese','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2023-24 Summer','In principle, students should have completed CLC1301 or CLC1401 or have gained similar competency.','NA','CLC2301旨在介绍中国人在日常交际中所展现的文化要素及其文化心理背景。通过学习本课程，学生将了解中国的文化习俗及其深层的文化内涵。此外，本课程还着重培养国际学生的有效沟通能力，使他们能够在实际交际中更加得心应手。课程涵盖了中国文化中与日常交际息息相关的多个方面的内容，如礼节与客套、自谦与敬人、自尊与含蓄等。在实操环节，课程将结合语言技能和文化知识，通过模拟真实情境进行阅读、口语表达等练习，同时引导学生进行跨文化对比，以加深对中国文化的理解。','This course aims to introduce the cultural elements that Chinese people demonstrate in their daily communication and their cultural psychological underpinnings. Through this course, students will gain a deeper understanding of Chinese cultural customs and their profound cultural connotations. Additionally, the course focuses on cultivating effective Chinese communication abilities among international students, enabling them to navigate real-world interactions more adeptly.
The course covers various aspects of Chinese culture closely related to daily communication, including etiquette, politeness, expressions of humility and respect, self-esteem, and implicit communication. During practical sessions, students will engage in simulated scenarios, combining language skills and cultural knowledge to practice reading, speaking, and other communication skills. They will also explore cross-cultural comparisons to enhance their appreciation of Chinese culture.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
