2025-26 Term 2','CSC1003 Intro to CS and JP','','本课程是一门计算实验课程，旨在提升学生的编程实践能力。学生应已修读上一学期的 CSC1003 课程，并具备基本的 Java 和 Python 编程知识。在本课程中，每位学生需独立完成两个约 1000 行代码 的中型 Java 项目和一个约 500 行代码 的小型 Python 项目。学期初，教师与助教将提供项目选题列表，学生可从中选择并确定研究方向；学期末须提交可执行程序、源代码及相关技术文档。课程结束时，将组织期末考试，以全面考查学生对项目开发过程及相关编程知识的掌握情况。','This course is a computational laboratory course designed to enhance students’ programming practice and problem-solving skills. Students are expected to have completed CSC1003 in the previous semester and to possess foundational knowledge of Java and Python programming. In this course, each student is required to independently complete two medium-scale Java projects of approximately 1,000 lines of code and one small-scale Python project of about 500 lines of code. At the beginning of the semester, instructors and teaching assistants will provide a list of project topics from which students may select and determine their own research focus. By the end of the semester, students must submit executable programs, source code, and the corresponding technical documentation. A final examination will be conducted to comprehensively assess students’ understanding of the project development process and related programming knowledge.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100584,'CSC1005','计算机工程导论：程序设计与应用','Introduction to Computer Engineering: Programming and Applications','CSC - Computer Science','1005','C',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程全面介绍了计算机编程的基础概念，针对理工科学生的需求量身定制。以Python作为主要教学语言，学生将掌握以下内容：计算机系统概述、编程原则、函数、输入/输出（I/O）、数据结构与算法、面向对象编程（OOP）、大语言模型（LLM）辅助编程以及提示工程。课程结束时，学生将具备设计、实现和调试简单Python程序的技能和知识，为学习科学和工程专业奠定坚实的基础。','This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the foundational concepts of computer programming, tailored to the needs of science and engineering students. Utilizing Python as the primary teaching language, students will grasp: computer systems overview, programming principles, functions, input/output (I/O), data structures & algorithms, and object-oriented programming (OOP). By the end of this course, students will be equipped with the skills and knowledge required to design, implement, and debug simple Python programs, laying a strong foundation for studying science and engineering majors.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100585,'CSC1006','人工智能在科学与工程中的应用','Artificial Intelligence for Science and Engineering','CSC - Computer Science','1006','C',1.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','人工智能在科学与工程中的应用对人工智能 (AI) 及其对各种科学和工程学科的影响进行了介绍性探索，包括物理、数学、化学、材料科学、生物学和机器人技术。该课程专为新生设计，强调对人工智能概念及其在解决这些领域的现实问题中的应用的高层次理解。学生将参与案例研究、演示和讨论，深入了解人工智能如何推动创新并改变现代科学和工程实践。','Artificial Intelligence for Science and Engineering offers an introductory exploration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and its impact on various scientific and engineering disciplines, including physics, mathematics, chemistry, materials science, biology, and robotics. Designed for freshmen, the course emphasizes a high-level understanding of AI concepts and their applications in solving real-world problems across these fields. Students will engage with case studies, demonstrations, and discussions, gaining insights into how AI drives innovation and transforms modern science and engineering practices.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100586,'CSC2003','Java 程序设计导论','Introduction to Java Programming Java','CSC - Computer Science','2003','C',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','','','本课程介绍 Java 编程语言的基本功能，包括原始和非原始数据类型、控制流构造、内置类库、基本 GUI 设计（可选）以及面向对象的编程概念，如类、对象、方法重载和封装。作业和项目包括使用内置和程序员定义的类，执行基本的输入和输出操作，以及解决更复杂和实际的编程问题。','This course introduces the basic features of the Java programming language including primitive and non-primitive data types, control flow constructs, built-in class libraries, basic GUI design (optional), and object-oriented programming concepts like classes, objects, method overloading, and encapsulation.  Assignments and projects are included using built-in and programmer-defined classes, performing basic input and output operations, and solving more complex and practical programming problems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
