(100628,'CSC4220','矩阵计算','Matrix Computation','CSC - Computer Science','4220','C',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MAT 2040, MAT 2041, MAT 2041A','','这是一门关于数值线性代数和矩阵计算的实践课程，重点讲解与算法方法相关的计算技术，这些方法对机器学习、优化、统计和科学计算等领域的应用至关重要。矩阵计算方法补充了专注于离散对象（例如列表、树和图）的算法，随着人工智能技术的快速发展，这些方法正变得越来越重要。课程涵盖的主题包括用于求解线性系统、线性最小二乘问题、特征值和奇异值问题的算法，以及迭代方法，例如 Arnoldi 方法、Krylov 子空间方法（包括 GMRES 和预条件 CG）。课程还将详细介绍条件作用和数值稳定性的基本概念。此外，还将介绍一些现代算法范式，例如随机化技术。','This is a hands-on course on numerical linear algebra and matrix computations emphasizing computational techniques dealing with algorithmic methodologies that are critical for applications in machine learning, optimization, statistics and scientific computing. Matrix computation methods complement algorithms focusing on discrete objects such as lists, trees and graphs, and those methods are becoming ever more critical with the rapid advances in AI technology. The topics covered include algorithms for solving linear systems, linear least squares problems, eigenvalue and singular value problems as well as iterative methods such as Arnoldi methods, Krylov subspace methods (including GMRES and preconditioned CG). Fundamental ideas of conditioning and numerical stability will also be covered in detail. In addition, several modern algorithmic paradigms such as randomization techniques will also be covered.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100629,'CSC4240','数据空间','Data Spaces','CSC - Computer Science','4240','C',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Programming and basic understanding of data management and networking','','数据空间是跨系统和组织实现去中心化数据共享和集成的框架，旨在实现安全可控的数据访问。本课程将涵盖数据空间的多个方面：技术（数据管理、数据模型和数据通信)；搜索和发现；去中心化、异构性、互操作性、本体和转码；安全（信任、身份识别、来源和可追溯性、访问控制——策略和机制)；隐私；经济；法律、监管、治理和商业，包括国际化和标准化。本课程包含重要的项目内容。','Data Spaces are a framework for decentralized data sharing and integration across different systems and organizations, enabling secure and controlled data access. This course will cover Data Spaces in many dimensions and from many perspectives: technical (data management, data models, and data communications); search and discovery; decentralization, heterogeneity, interoperability, ontologies, and transcoding; security (trust, identification, provenance and traceability, access control—policies and mechanisms); privacy; economic; legal, governance, business, and regulatory, including international aspects and standardization. The course will have a significant project component.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100630,'CSC4301','聚类算法专题','','CSC - Computer Science','4301','C',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'Programming, Data structures.','','聚类是数据科学中使用的基本工具。 设计一个聚类方法，需要解决几个设计问题：（1）如何计算距离； （2）如何处理异常值、噪声和缺失值； (3) 使用什么优化函数； (4)有多少个簇； (5)如何找到簇。 最重要的是确定适合数据的距离函数，例如多维数值数据、时间序列、文本、类别、集合和图形。 寻找聚类被视为最小化给定函数的算法优化问题,此外还研究了计算效率和聚类结果的评估。','Clustering is a basic tool used in data science. To design a clustering method, we need to solve several design problems: (1) how to calculate distance; (2) how to deal with outliers, noise and missing values; (3) what optimization function is used; (4) how many clusters; (5) how to find the clusters. The most important is to decide distance function suitable for the data, such as multi-dimensional numerical data, time series, text, categories, sets, and graphs. Finding the clustering is considered as an algorithmic optimization problem minimizing the given function. Computational efficiency and evaluation of clustering results are also studied.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100631,'CSC4302','人工智能数据分析','','CSC - Computer Science','4302','C',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','Students must have some basic computer skills, Internet use and web service experiences. Knowledge of data structures and basic algorithms woud be useful.','','该课程涵盖的主题包括用于解决人工智能 (AI) 和认知科学问题的大数据分析的原理、算法、软件工具和示例应用。 我们将研究移动、边缘、云、数据中心和人工智能计算系统中现实应用中的人工智能、机器学习、深度学习、分析库、数据结构的基础知识。','The course is colisted for CSC 4302, CIE 6006, and CSC 6127 programs. The grading of the undergraduate and postgraduate students will be separately done with slightly different homework and exam questions and different weights applied.  Topics covered include the principles, algorithms, software tools, and example applications of big data analytics applied for solving artitificial intelligence (AI) and cognitive science problems. We will study the basics of AI, machine learning, deep learning, analytics libraries, data structures in real-life applications in mobile,  edge, cloud, datacenter and AI computing systems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
