CSC1001 Introduction to Computer Science: Programming Methodology','','本课程主要讲述基本网络协议和编程实践，包括TCP/IP协议，HTTP协议，socket编程，RPC协议等；并介绍实际场景下网络系统的设计和实现，包括分布式文件系统和通信框架。','The course introduces basic network protocols and programming practices, such as TCP/IP, HTTP, socket programming, and RPC. It also presents the design and implementation of real-world networked systems, including distributed file systems and communication frameworks.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100633,'CSC4305','人工智能与医学专题研究','','CSC - Computer Science','4305','C',2.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','AI-based Courses, Computer Programming, Senior Students in SDS','','本课程旨在为学生提供医学人工智能（AI）领域的概念、理论和实践知识。包括与医疗诊断相关的人工智能概念和术语、机器学习基础、决策系统、病理信息感知和健康计算，以及用于疾病诊断的多模态融合方法, 并参与实际的研究项目项目。本课程还涵盖人工智能在医学领域的应用，包括疾病诊断、疾病预测、个性化治疗计划。本课程还指明了智慧医疗未来的趋势和挑战。通过本课程，学生将获得人工智能理论以便在医疗诊断中实施人工智能解决方案，并具备利用人工智能开展医学研究的知识与能力。

注册本课程的 SDS 学生必须就选定的主题进行独立学习。每个人都应每周与
导师会面，就他们的研究撰写书面报告（实验研究或指定书籍/论文的研
究），并进行最后的公开演讲。导师将基于报告和演示文稿给学生评分。','The course provides students with a comprehensive understanding of the conceptual, theoretical, and practical aspects of artificial intelligence (AI) in medicine as a practical project. It includes AI concepts and terminology relevant to clinical medicine, machine learning fundamentals, AI-enabled decision support systems, advanced sensing technologies for pathological information acquisition and computing, and multi-modal fusion methods for diagnosis. This course covers AI applications in medical areas, including disease diagnosis, disease prediction, and treatment plan generation. Also, future trends and challenges in AI + medicine are pointed out. Through this lecture, students will gain a foundation of AI concepts to implement AI solutions in healthcare and be equipped with the knowledge and skills to conduct AI-enabled medical research.

The registered SDS students are required to carry out independent study on a selected topic. Each one is expected to meet with the supervisor weekly, write written reports on their studies (either an experimental study, or a study of assigned books/papers), and will make a final public presentation. The grading will be based on the reports and presentation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
