(100649,'CSC5051','自然语言处理','','CSC - Computer Science','5051','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','','','这门课程提供了对自然语言处理（NLP）的全面研究。我们将深入探讨词表示、语言模型的构建、深度学习在NLP中的应用和大型语言模型（LLMs）。特别地，我们将讨论大型语言模型的架构工程、数据工程、提示工程、上下文工程、训练技巧以及效率提升。学生将了解到自然语言处理和大型语言模型在各个领域的应用，如文本挖掘、搜索引擎、人机交互、医疗法律咨询、低资源语言和AI for Science，以及如何处理数据隐私、偏见和伦理问题。课程还将研究NLP和LLMs的局限性以及模型对齐问题。该课程包括高级主题的客座讲座和课堂演示。','This course introduces fundamental concepts and techniques, as well as different tasks in natural language processing. Topics include, but are not limited to the mathematical foundation for natural language processing, information theory, text representation, word segmentation and tokenization, part-of-speech tagging, syntactic and semantic parsing, named entity recognition, relation and event extraction, coreference resolution, sentiment analysis, reading comprehension, key-phrase extraction and generation, summarization, dialogue system, machine translation, etc. Students are expected to learn the latest progress in this area and understand the necessary techniques as well as the tasks and use appropriate algorithms/models to finish a course project.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100650,'CSC5052','语言信息处理','','CSC - Computer Science','5052','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','College Calculus, Linear Algebra

Basic probability and statistics

Basic Machine Learning

Basic Artificial Intelligence','N/A','口语是人类自然口头交流的基础，也是通过口语学习知识的手段。口语处理（SLP）是计算机处理人类语音信号的技术。SLP正成为人工智能的关键技术。与自然语言处理（NLP）不同，SLP除了包括语言信息外，还包括语音语调、重音、强度和说话速度中出现的焦点、强调和情感等语言以外的信息。此外，口语对话是与人类进行自然交流的一种方式。SLP的组成部分包括语音检测、语音的声学建模、语音的语言建模、语音增强、说话人检测/建模、语音识别/合成、口语对话建模、增量式语音处理和端到端建模。SLP技术有各种应用，如自动语音增强、说话人识别/认知/辨别、语音识别/合成、口语对话系统、增量式语音转文本/语音机器翻译等。深度神经网络的最新进展在SLP研究中取得了巨大的进步，并已应用于通过监督学习、半监督学习、无监督学习和自监督学习来解决SLP问题。在本课程中，学生将获得NLP技术的基本技能和最新的研究进展','This course introduces spoken language processing with an emphasis on deep learning and other state-of-the-art methods for automatic speech recognition, speech synthesis, voice conversion, speaker recognition, affect detection, dialogue management, and applications to digital assistants and spoken language understanding systems. Through project work, students will apply the learned theory in the development of selected spoken language processing systems, evaluation, and optimization of system performance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100651,'CSC5055','计算机图形学','','CSC - Computer Science','5055','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MAT1001 or MAT1011, MAT1002 or MAT1012, MAT2040, CSC3100','','本课程主要涵盖计算机图形学的四个部分：光栅化、曲线和网格、光线跟踪、动画/模拟。具体来说，它包括变换、照明、着色、管线、纹理映射、几何、光传输、采样、材质、光线跟踪、光学、相机、AR/VR等。

课程结束后，学生应了解现代计算机图形学的基础知识和实践技能，并能够编写自己的实时渲染程序。','This course introduces computer graphics algorithms, software and hardware platforms, focusing on both basic concepts and state-of-the-art techniques, and their cutting-edge applications in multiple problem domains in graphics. Topics include ray tracing, the graphics pipeline, transformations, texture mapping, shadows, sampling, global illumination, splines, animation, colour, and so on. After completing the course, students will be able to grasp fundamentals of computer graphics algorithms, real-time rendering, graphics hardware, and OpenGL programming.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100652,'CSC5056','人机交互','','CSC - Computer Science','5056','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','CSC2003 or CSC3002 or CSC3200','','本课程将概述人机交互领域，并向学生介绍关键的交互与体验设计范式、方法和途径。课程将帮助学生掌握相关理论、方法与技术，以研究不同的设计情境，开发并制作新颖设计理念的原型，以及探讨技术设计中的伦理问题。本课程还将介绍人机交互领域的一些前沿技术，例如面向人机交互的人工智能（AI for HCI）、软件智能体和虚拟现实。学生将以团队形式开展一个为期一学期的设计项目，其中两个主要的阶段性成果将作为作业进行考核。','This course will provide an overview of the field of Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) and will introduce students to key interaction and experience design paradigms, approaches and methods. The course will equip students with theory, methods, and techniques to investigate different design situations, develop and prototype novel design ideas, and engage with the ethical dimensions of technology design. This course will also introduce some state-of-the-art technologies in HCI, such as AI for HCI, software agents, virtual reality. Students in this course will work with a team on a semester-long design project, with two major deliverable milestones assessed as assignments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
