(100660,'CSC6021','人工智能','','CSC - Computer Science','6021','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1','First year university level linear algebra, probability and statistics. Discrete mathematics such as sets, Boolean logic and graphs. Some level of computer programming skills.','NA','本课程对人工智能（AI）的基本概念进行了技术介绍。我们涵盖四个主要部分：（1）通过搜索解决问题，约束满足，游戏， Google alpha-go； (2)  用逻辑来进行知识表述和推理，专家系统。（3）概率分布，贝叶斯定理，马可夫链，隐马可夫模型，朴素贝叶斯分类，贝叶斯网络，决策图； （4）自然语言处理（NPL）。前三部分是传统的人工智能技术，它们是当今人工智能和计算机科学的基础。关于 NPL 的第 4 部分是由于最近对 ChatGPT 的极大兴趣。这部分将是 NLP 模型的动手编码练习，从Appendix 7 简单的单词到向量模型到 BERT 和 GPT 模型，以便学生学习当前 NPL 的实用技能。前 3 部分占 2/3 的课程工作量,有考试，而 NLP 占 1/3 的工作量，有课堂演示和报告，没有考试。典型的人工智能课程还包括机器学习和神经网络。但这些内容现在大多是在单独的课程教授，本课不讲这些内容，利用省下来时间来细致的做 NLP 模型。','Artificial intelligence (AI) aims at solving problems using computer algorithms that mimic human intelligence. This course provides a intermediate level introduction of fundamental principles and techniques of AI. We cover four   major parts of AI: (1) Solving problems by search, constraint satisfaction, game playing; (2) Knowledge representation and reasoning using logic,  expert systems; (3) Probability distributions, Bayes theorem, Naïve Bayes classification, Markov and Hidden Markov processes, Bayesian networks and decision graphs;  (4) Natural Language Processing （NPL）models. The first three parts are traditional AI techniques, they are bread and butter in today’s AI and computer science. Part 4 on NPL is due to recent enormous interests in ChatGPT. We begins with introduction to NLP tasks and focus hands-on coding homeworks on NLP models from
simple word2vec models to BERT and GPT models, so students learning practical up-to-date current NPL skills. The first 3 parts will be 2/3 of course load with an exam, and NLP will be 1/3 course effort, with class presentation and report, no exam. Typical AI course include machine learning and neural networks. But these subjects are now taught in separate class. To avoid redundancy, we use the time to do NLP models.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100661,'CSC6022','机器学习','','CSC - Computer Science','6022','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Basic elements of probability theory (e.g., expectation, variance, probability density functions), basic linear algebra concepts (e.g., linear spaces and inner product, determinant, linear system of equations, eigenvalues-eigenvectors), basic calculus (e.g., derivative, gradient, integration).','None','机器学习在近年来变得愈发重要,这是由于它能够从数据中提取关键特征和知识，并基于此做出准确的预测，驱动大批智能化应用。随着AI技术的兴起以及自动决策过程的需求,各行各业对机器学习专业人才的需求显著增加。本课程旨在为研究生和优秀本科生提供所需的机器学习知识和技能。具体而言,本课程侧重概率机器学习理论和模式，包括但不限于贝叶斯统计、参数和非参数法建模、注意力机制、变压器模型，状态空间模型,以及其他经典和新兴的概念、模型、理论和算法。此外,这门课程还将展示机器学习在信号处理和无线通信中的实际应用。','Machine Learning has become increasingly important in recent years due to its ability to extract insights from data and make accurate predictions. With the rise of artificial intelligence and the need to automate decision-making processes, the demand for machine learning professionals has grown significantly. This postgraduate course in Machine Learning aims to provide students with the knowledge and skills required to meet this demand and excel in this very rapidly growing field. Specially, this postgraduate course in Machine Learning provides a comprehensive overview of the fundamentals of probabilistic learning theory and models, cutting-edge topics include but not limited to Bayesian statistics, parametric and nonparametric modelling, attention mechanisms, transformer, state-space-model, as well as other classic and emerging concepts, models, and algorithms. Additionally, this course will demonstrate real-world applications of machine learning in signal processing and wireless communications. By taking this course, students will gain a solid foundation in the fundamental concepts and techniques of machine learning and its applications to real-world problems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100662,'CSC6031','高等计算机体系结构','','CSC - Computer Science','6031','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','CSC3050 Computer ARchitecture
CSC3150 Operating System','N/A','本课程以量化分析的方法来讨论计算机主要组件的各种优化技术以提升计算机系统效能. 本课程在先前掌握的计算机体系结构基础知识（CSC3050）之上，进一步探讨提升各类计算机组件及整个系统性能的技术。课程内容涵盖存储器层次结构、指令级并行（超标量、超长指令字VLIW和乱序执行处理器）、数据级并行（向量处理、SIMD和GPU）以及线程级并行（细粒度、粗粒度、同时多线程和共享内存多处理）等概念。课程项目包括开发一个体系结构模拟器（例如RISC-V向量扩展RVV模拟器），以及对某一选定主题研究论文的综述.','The course builds on prior knowledge of basic computer architecture (CSC3050) and explores techniques to enhance performance across various computer components and the entire system. It covers the concepts of Memory Hierarchy, Instruction-Level Parallelism (Superscalar,VLIW, and Out-of-Order processors), Data-Level Parallelism (Vector, SIMD, and GPU), and Thread-Level Parallelism (fine-grained, coarse-grained, simultaneous multithreading, and shared-memory multi-processing). The course includes a project on developing an architecture simulator, such as a RVV (the RISC-V Vector Extension) simulator, and a survey of a selected topic of advanced research papers.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100663,'CSC6032','高等操作系統','','CSC - Computer Science','6032','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','修过 CSC3150 操作系统','No','本课程将概述一些高阶操作系统及其底层设计原理。讨论的问题包括分散式操作系统及虚拟化技术。学生将被要求选择一个相关于分散式操作系统或是虚拟化技术的题目，在期末时在课堂上做学术报告。','This course will present an overview of some advanced operating systems and their underlying design principles. Issues discussed will include virtualization techniques for virtual machines and containers, memory management on GPU, I/O management for GPU, and file systems for GPU.   Each enrolled student will be asked to design an OS for such systems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
