(100702,'CSC6137','生成模型','','CSC - Computer Science','6137','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','CSC6022 Machine Learning
Previous exposure to
1. probability and statistics
2. Linear algebra
3. Multivariate calculus
4. Optimization
5. Basic programming','','生成模型已经成为机器学习中重要的课题。本课程旨在作为对这一主题的入门介绍，将为生成模型提供理论基础。在本课程中，学生将不仅学习生成模型技术的理论基础，还将通过研究文章阅读和讨论了解最新方法。课程内容涵盖了生成对抗网络（GAN）、变分自编码器、归一化流、自回归生成模型、基于分数的生成模型以及概率扩散模型等多个主题。学生还将通过充分的背景知识培训，掌握阅读相关研究论文的能力。','Generative models have emerged as a pivotal subject within the realm of machine learning. This course serves as an introductory exploration into this fascinating domain, offering a foundational understanding of generative models. Throughout this course, students will delve into the theoretical foundations underpinning generative model techniques. Furthermore, they will gain insights into state-of-the-art (SOTA) methods through engagement with research articles and collaborative discussions. The curriculum encompasses a comprehensive array of topics, encompassing GANs (Generative Adversarial Networks), Variational Autoencoders, normalizing flows, autoregressive generative models, score-based generative models, and probabilistic diffusion models. An integral facet of the course involves training students to adeptly comprehend and analyze related research papers by equipping them with the necessary background knowledge.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100703,'CSC6138','高等矩阵计算','','CSC - Computer Science','6138','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MAT 2040, MAT 2041, MAT 2041A','','这是一门关于数值线性代数和矩阵计算的实践课程，重点讲解与算法方法相关的计算技术，这些方法对机器学习、优化、统计和科学计算等领域的应用至关重要。矩阵计算方法补充了专注于离散对象（例如列表、树和图）的算法，随着人工智能技术的快速发展，这些方法正变得越来越重要。课程涵盖的主题包括用于求解线性系统、线性最小二乘问题、特征值和奇异值问题的算法，以及迭代方法，例如 Arnoldi 方法、Krylov 子空间方法（包括 GMRES 和预条件 CG）。课程还将详细介绍条件作用和数值稳定性的基本概念。此外，还将介绍一些现代算法范式，例如随机化技术。','This is an advanced course on numerical linear algebra and matrix computations emphasizing numerical techniques dealing with vectors and matrices that are critical for applications in machine learning, optimization, computer vision, and signal processing. The topics covered include algorithms for solving linear systems, linear least squares problems, eigenvalue and singular value problems as well as iterative methods such as Arnoldi methods, Krylov subspace methods (including GMRES and preconditioned CG), the Kaczmarz method, etc. Fundamental ideas of conditioning and numerical stability will also be covered in detail. In addition, several modern algorithms and principles for large-scale matrix computations and problems are studied such as convolutions, fast fourier transforms, and randomization techniques.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100704,'CSC6139','高等高性能计算','','CSC - Computer Science','6139','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','CSC3100 Data Structures or
CSC3200 Data Structures and Advanced Programming','','本课程为学生提供高性能计算领域的高级研究专题。课程内容涵盖：基于GPU的高性能计算、大规模分布式内存计算集群的设计与应用、MPI（消息传递接口）的设计与使用、并行程序性能分析、高性能计算中的缓存与寄存器复用、容错高性能计算、能效高性能计算，以及面向人工智能（AI）与机器学习（ML）的高性能计算。','This course provides students with advanced research topics in high performance computing. Topics include: High performance computing with GPUs, the design and use of large scale distributed memory computing clusters, the design and use of MPI, analyzing the performance of parallel programs, reuse of cache and registers in high performance computing, fault tolerant high performance computing, energy efficient high performance computing, high performance computing for AI and ML.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
