2025-26 Term 2','Programming experience and understanding of data management, operating systems, and networking at an undergraduate level.','None','数据空间是跨系统和组织实现去中心化数据共享和集成的框架，旨在实现安全可控的数据访问。本课程将涵盖数据空间的多个方面：技术（数据管理、数据模型和数据通信)；搜索和发现；去中心化、异构性、互操作性、本体和转码；安全（信任、身份识别、来源和可追溯性、访问控制——策略和机制)；隐私；经济；法律、监管、治理和商业，包括国际化和标准化。本课程包含重要的项目内容。','Data Spaces are a framework for decentralized data sharing and integration on an "as needed" basis across different systems and organizations. They enable secure and controlled data access without requiring a common database schema. This course will cover Data Spaces on many dimensions and from many perspectives: technical (data management, data models, and data communications); search and discovery; decentralization, heterogeneity, interoperability, ontologies, and transcoding; security (trust, identification, provenance and traceability, access control—policies and mechanisms); privacy (regulatory requirements, policies, and mechanisms—anonymization); economic (including incentives and markets); legal, governance, business, and regulatory, including international aspects and standardization. The course will also have a significant group project component with students designing and implementing data spaces in groups, from inception, to requirements, implementation, demonstration, and evaluation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
