(100732,'CSS5010','社会科学研究方法','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5010','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','Nil.','Nil.','本课程旨在为学生提供理论与实用工具，使其能够设计、实施与评估严谨的社会学研究。课程将系统介绍探究性研究的基础原理，引导学生完成研究问题的构建、文献综述及研究计划书的撰写。课程主题涵盖定量与混合研究方法设计、抽样和数据收集策略。课程全程贯穿科研伦理与数据管理实践的探讨，培养学生开展方法论严谨、伦理规范且贴合政策需求的研究能力。','This course introduces research methods in the social sciences. The purpose of the course is to teach the theory behind and application of research methods. It starts with broad questions about fundamental principles that undergird any approaches to social inquiries, the basic research process and the measurement of rigor, and then proceed to the discussion of specific techniques in qualitative, quantitative, and mixed methodologies, such as case study, content analysis, survey research, and statistical analysis. As part of the course, students will learn how analytical tools and software assist data analysis. Students are expected to improve research capacities in analytical thinking, devising research questions, searching and reviewing literature, formulating hypotheses, selecting and performing appropriate tests, interpreting results, and drafting research proposals.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100733,'CSS5020','社会科学统计分析','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5020','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程提供在社会科学领域开展实验和相关研究所需的各种统计知识和技能。内容包括统计学基础知识和假设检验、功效和效应大小、相关和多元回归、调节和中介、简单和因子方差分析、重复测量和混合设计、因子分析、分类数据分析和路径分析。学生可以学习如何处理定量问题并有效地交流统计结果。','This course provides a wide range of statistical knowledge and skills needed to conduct experimental and correlational research in social sciences. Contents include basics about statistics and hypothesis testing, power and effect size, correlation and multiple regression, moderation and mediation, simple and factorial analysis of variance, repeated-measure and mixed designs, factor analysis, categorical data analysis, and path analysis. Students can learn how to work with quantitative problems and effectively communicate the statistical results.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100734,'CSS5030','研究专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5030','C',6.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100735,'CSS5110','社会学高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5110','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','CSS5010 Social Science Research Methods','None','课程研究社会学的基本理论和最新研究进展。课题包括但不限于种族、国籍和民族；儿童和青少年的行为；家庭问题和关系；心理健康和失调；社会中的文化偏见；社会和大众媒体；性别成见；技术和社会；社会运动；食品和饮食习惯；异常社会行为；文化、艺术和社会。','The course examines the fundamental theories and updated research progress in sociology. Topics will include but not limited to race, nationality, and ethnicity; children and teenagers'' behaviour; family issues and relations; mental health and disorders; culture biases in society; social and mass media; gender stereotypes; technologies and society; social movements; food and eating habits; deviant social behaviour; culture, art and society.
Through the analysis of different articles related to those topics, students will understand how they can leverage methods such as Multiple Correspondence Analysis, clustering methods, neural network, social network analysis, topic modeling, sentiment analysis, Difference in Difference, Agent based modeling and different kind of regression models (logistic, negative binomial…etc) to produce breakthrough in the field of Sociology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100736,'CSS5120','计算语言学','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5120','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','Comfort with basic Python (variables, loops, functions, lists/dicts) or willingness to ramp up in Week 1. We provide a self-paced Python primer.
No linear algebra, calculus, or ML background required. We build the needed intuitions as we go.
A laptop. All programming runs in Google Colab (browser-based, no install) plus free-tier access to an LLM chat/API and an AI coding tool (Cursor / Claude / equiv.).','','语言是社会科学和人文学科的原材料——访谈、法律、演讲、新闻、小说、聊天记录、调查问卷回复等等。本课程将教你如何将语言视为数据，以及如何运用如今处于研究和产业核心的语言技术进行构建。','Language is the raw material of the social sciences and humanities — interviews, laws, speeches, news, novels, chat logs, survey responses. This course teaches you how to treat language as data and how to build with the language technology that now sits at the center of research and industry.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100737,'CSS5130','经济学高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5130','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','','','该课程研究经济学的基本理论和最新研究进展。课程将深入讨论经济学中的一个或几个常见主题，包括劳动经济学、金融经济学、计量经济学、国际经济与发展经济学、卫生经济学、宏观经济学、微观经济学、公共与制度经济学等。','The course examines the fundamental theories and updated research progress in economics. It will engage in in-depth discussion of one or several of the common topics in economics, including labour economics, financial economics, econometrics, international economics and development economics, health economics, macroeconomics, microeconomics, public and institutional economics, among others.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100738,'CSS5140','发展问题实证研究高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5140','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程会向学生介绍发展的实证研究，重点关注政治制度、治理和国家与社会关系如何塑造发展成果。我们将阅读并讨论政治经济学、治理和发展交叉领域的工作，特别关注识别策略、衡量和研究设计。
该课程被设计为以学生为主导的讨论研讨会。我将主要充当协调人的角色。每周，一到两名学生将担任讨论领导者，所有学生都应做好积极参与阅读的准备。
该课程的核心组成部分是与实证相关主题的最终研究项目
发展。您将在本学期的三个检查点开发这个项目。','This graduate seminar introduces students to empirical research on development, with a focus on how political institutions, governance, and state–society relations shape development outcomes. We will read and discuss work at the intersection of political economy, governance, and development, with particular attention to identification strategies, measurement, and research design.
The course is designed as a student-driven discussion seminar. I will act primarily as a facilitator. Each week, one or two students will serve as discussion leaders, and all students are expected to come prepared to engage actively with the readings.
A central component of the course is a final research project on a topic related to empirical
development. You will develop this project across three checkpoints during the semester.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100739,'CSS5150','区域与城市发展高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5150','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','Not applicable','Not applicable','本课程面向研究生，重点在于运用定量方法和技术分析复杂的城市与区域发展问题。课程旨在加深学生对城市与区域发展议题的理解，并教授学生如何运用先进的空间与统计工具，评估城市政策、可持续发展决策及其对区域与城市发展的影响。学生将学习区域与城市研究中的关键理论与前沿议题，如城市空间结构、集聚效应、创新学习、城市气候、城市能源与环境正义等。','Advanced Topics in in Regional and Urban Development is a postgraduate-oriented course that focuses on applying quantitative methods and techniques to analyze complex urban and regional development issues. The course aims to deepen students'' understanding of urban and regional development issues and to teach them how to use advanced statistical and econometric tools to assess urban policies, planning decisions, and their impact on regional development. Students are guided through critical theories and research directions in regional and urban studies, such as agglomeration effects, innovation learning, urban spatial structure, urban environment, real estate, urban transport, and urban crime.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100740,'CSS5160','国际政治高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5160','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100741,'CSS5170','全球化高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5170','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程探讨当代全球化复杂且充满争议的动态。课程将深入审视全球经济架构、数字主权、文化流动、城市景观、跨国移民、生态危机、健康不平等以及新兴裂痕等高级议题。学生将围绕超国家治理、系统性不对称、抵抗运动以及（去）全球化潜在未来等主题展开深度研讨。课程注重批判性分析能力培养、理论整合训练，并致力于理解全球化作为一个在多元危机时代面临深刻挑战的互联体系。','This course explores the multifaceted and contested dynamics of contemporary globalization. It critically examines advanced topics including global economic architectures, digital sovereignty, cultural flows, urban terrains, transnational migration, ecological crises, health inequities, and emergent fractures. Students will engage in in-depth discussions on themes such as supranational governance, systemic asymmetries, resistance movements, and potential futures of (de)globalization. The course emphasizes critical analysis, theoretical synthesis, and understanding globalization as an interconnected system facing profound challenges in an era of polycrisis.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100742,'CSS5180','人口学高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5180','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'','','本课程将介绍人口学的基本原理和方法。将重点强调人口数据在人口健康状况描述、趋势发现和预测中的作用。内容包括人口数据的来源及解释、比率、比例和比值、标准化、完整和简化生命表、生育、死亡和迁移的估算与预测，人口变量之间的相互关系、人口动态和人口模型。所有分析将使用开源统计软件R进行编程。本课程面向对统计学和人口健康感兴趣的学生。','This course will provide an introduction to the fundamental principles and methods of demography. The role of demographic data in describing the health status of a population, spotting trend and making projection will be highlighted. Topics include sources and interpretation of demographic data, rates, proportions and ratios, standardization, complete and abridged life tables, estimation and projection of fertility, mortality and migration, Interrelations among demographic variables, population dynamics, and demographic models. All the analyses will be programmed using R, an open-source statistical software. This course is targeted at students who are interested in statistics and population health.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100743,'CSS5190','游戏心理学：人工智能、创造力与心理健康','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5190','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Nil.','Nil.','《游戏你的心理：人工智能、创造力与心理健康》是一门综合课程，结合心理学理论与交互技术（如电子游戏和机器人）的实践开发。学生将学习如何设计、原型制作并测试自己的游戏和应用，同时探讨这些工具如何影响认知与行为过程、文化动态、心理健康以及治疗实践。每周模块将理论基础——包括情绪、认知、人格与伦理设计——与Unity游戏开发、用于健康与福祉、教育与创造力的严肃游戏、社交机器人以及实验设计相结合。学习者不仅会创造和评估交互技术，还会在实践中应用心理学理论。通过案例研究、应用实验和成品项目，参与者将获得概念性洞察力与技术技能，帮助他们利用交互技术推动治疗、学习与个人发展。','Game Your Psychology: AI, Creativity & Mental Health is a comprehensive course that combines psychological theory with hands‑on development of interactive technologies such as video games and robotics. Students will learn to design, prototype, and test their own games and applications while investigating how these tools shape cognitive and behavioral processes, cultural dynamics, mental health, and therapeutic practices. Weekly modules integrate theoretical foundations — including emotion, cognition, personality, and ethical design — with Unity game development, serious games for wellbeing, education, and creativity, social robotics, and experimental design. Learners will both create and evaluate interactive technologies, applying psychological theories in practice. Through case studies, applied labs, and final projects, participants gain conceptual insight and technical skills, preparing them to harness interactive technologies for therapy, learning, and personal development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100744,'CSS5210','社会科学统计分析高级专题','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5210','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','CSS5020 Statistics for Social Science
CSS5211 Advanced Statistical Modeling in Social Science','','本课程探讨高级分析的计算工具和统计软件包，包括多层次分析、结构方程建模、分类数据分析、时间序列分析、社会复杂性建模、社会模拟建模等。要求提交研究论文。','This course introduces advanced statistical tools for social science research. Contents include multilevel analysis, structuring equation modelling, categorical data analysis, difference-in-difference analysis, social complexity modelling, social simulation modelling, social network analysis, among others.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100745,'CSS5211','社会科学高级统计模型','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5211','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','','','本课程介绍社会科学研究中常用的高级统计模型。涵盖主题包括线性与非线性模型、广义线性模型（GLM）、多层级/分层模型、因果推断方法（如匹配法、工具变量法）以及模型不确定性。课程重点在于使用R语言进行实际应用、结果解读与结果复现。','This course introduces advanced statistical models commonly used in social science re- search. Topics include linear and nonlinear models, generalized linear models (GLMs), multilevel/hierarchical models, causal inference techniques (e.g., matching, instrumental variables), and model uncertainty. Emphasis is placed on application, interpretation, and reproducibility using R.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100746,'CSS5220','计算社会科学应用软件','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5220','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','None','None','本课程旨在培养学生运用计算方法处理社会科学研究问题的能力。本课程侧重于以下目标：1）发展适合社会科学研究的计算思维能力；2). 学习Python和相关软件包（如NumPy、Pandas、NLTK、NetworkX、mesa）的实用编码技能；3）学习该领域的趋势性话题和技术，例如API部署、LLM、开源AI平台。学生将通过讲座、练习、课外阅读和期末项目相结合的方式充分参与课程。','Learning how to program is an essential skill for a computational social scientist. In this course, students will learn two of the most popular programming languages in today’s world: Python and R. It covers basic to intermediate topics with applications related to social science.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100747,'CSS5230','社会科学机器学习','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5230','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程将培训学生掌握机器学习的基本技能。它将涵盖从机器学习角度启动和运行计算研究项目所需的一切，包括标准机器学习流程中使用的关键技术：数据处理、分类模型、回归模型、参数调整、模型评估和误差分析。学生将学习用于预测数据分析的简单高效的机器学习算法，并通过在社会科学任务中应用机器学习算法获得实践经验。','This course will train students in the fundamental skills of machine learning. It will cover everything needed for getting up and running with computational research projects from a machine learning perspective, including the key techniques used in standard machine learning pipelines: data processing, classification models, regression models, parameter tuning, model evaluation, and error analysis. Students will learn simple and efficient machine learning algorithms for predictive data analysis and gain hands-on experience by applying machine learning algorithms in social science tasks.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100748,'CSS5240','社会科学数据视觉化','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5240','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','社会资料科学家有效交流研究成果的能力可能比他们的研究工作更重要。课程开始时，学生将学习资料交流和可视化理论与概念。具体来说，学生将学习讲故事的艺术以及认知和感知理论，了解人类如何在视觉媒介中处理和综合信息。在课程的后半部分，学生将学习为资料探索和交流生成丰富、翔实和交互式可视化的技术和方法。这些技术将使用 R 和 Microsoft Excel/Power BI 软件实现。','The ability of social data scientists to effectively communicate their research findings is probably more important than their research work. At the beginning of the course, students will learn data communications and visualization theories and concepts. Specifically, students will learn about the art of story-telling and the theory of cognition and perception to understand how humans process and synthesize information in a visual medium. In the later part of the course, students will learn techniques and methods for generating rich, informative, and interactive visualizations for data exploration and communication. These techniques will be developed using software implementations in R and Microsoft Excel/Power BI.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100749,'CSS5250','心理测试','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5250','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','NA','NA','本课程涉及测验的心理测量和实践问题。心理测量部分介绍测量理论，重点是经典测验理论和相关问题，如信度、效度和测验分析。此外，还可能介绍泛化理论和项目反应理论，重点是实际应用。测验的实际问题包括心理测验在不同环境中的使用和解释，包括教育、临床和组织环境。','This course addresses psychometrical and practical issues of testing. The psychometrical part introduces measurement theories with a focus on classical test theory and related issues such as reliability, validity, and test analysis. Generalizability theory and item response theory may also be introduced with a focus on practical applications. The practical issues of testing include the use and interpretations of psychological tests in different settings, including educational, clinical, and organizational settings.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100750,'CSS5260','社会科学实验方法','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5260','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100751,'CSS5270','因果推断','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5270','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','None','','本課程介紹社會科學研究中因果推斷的核心邏輯。學生將學習什麼是因果效果，以及為何因果效果難以估計；研究者如何透過實驗與觀察性研究設計來識別因果效果；為何因果研究設計可能在實務中失效；如何解讀因果研究的發現並延伸至其他情況或群體；以及在經驗證據的基礎上，研究者可以提出哪些因果主張。透過結合 R 語言的數據分析與案例研究，學生將獲得評估因果研究以及產出具高可信度之因果研究的實務能力。','This course introduces the logic of causal inference in social science research. Students learn what causal effects are and why they are difficult to estimate, how researchers identify causal effects using experimental and observational designs, why causal designs may fail in practice, how to interpret and generalize causal findings, and what can be responsibly claimed from empirical evidence. Through a combination of data analysis in R and real-world case studies, students develop practical skills in evaluating and producing credible causal research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100752,'CSS5280','复杂系统的建模和分析','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5280','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Students should be familiar with linear algebra in order to follow the materials effectively.','Students are suggested to develop basic Python programming skills during the semester in order to complete assignments effectively.','本课程介绍复杂系统的建模与分析。课程包括两大部分。第一部分建立复杂系统理论的基础，定义什么是复杂系统，并考察其区别于线性、可预测系统的特征。第二部分聚焦于复杂系统常用的建模与分析方法，包括元胞自动机、基于主体的建模和网络分析。通过讲授、实际操作和课外阅读，学生将获得如何将这些技术应用于现实问题的实践理解。课程结束时，学生将在复杂系统的理论与实践上具备坚实基础，并能将所学知识与技能应用于包括社会科学在内的多种领域。','This course introduces the modelling and analysis of complex systems. The course includes two general parts. The first part establishes the foundations of complex systems theory. It defines what constitutes a complex system and examines the distinguishing characteristics that set it apart from more linear and predictable systems. The second part focuses on commonly used modelling and analysis methods for complex systems. This includes cellular automata, agent-based modelling, and network analysis. Through lectures, hands-on exercises, and extracurricular readings, students will gain a practical understanding of how to apply these techniques to real-world problems. By the end of this course, students will have a solid foundation in the theory and practice of modelling and analyzing complex systems. They will be able to apply the knowledge and skills they have acquired to a wide range of domains, including social sciences.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100753,'CSS5290','应用时间序列分析','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5290','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100754,'CSS5310','可持续性计算：方法和应用','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5310','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100755,'CSS5320','可持续发展的数据科学','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5320','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','Not applicable','Not applicable','本课程通过应用视角，培养学生解决当代环境和可持续性挑战所需的关键数据科学技能。课程强调实际应用，介绍用于收集、清洗、分析和可视化空间及表格环境数据的工具和技术。学生将处理多样化的数据集，从卫星图像和监测站到社会经济数据，并构建用于解决现实问题的可复现流程。课程侧重于利用数据为环境政策、能源转型规划和可持续发展决策提供信息，培养学生将多源、大规模数据转化为可操作见解的能力。','This course equips students with critical data science skills to address contemporary environmental and sustainability challenges through an applied lens. Emphasizing practical applications, it introduces tools and techniques for collecting, cleaning, analysing, and visualizing spatial and tabular environmental data. Students will work with diverse datasets, from satellite imagery and monitoring stations to socioeconomic data, and build reproducible pipelines for real-world problems. The course focuses on using data to inform environmental policy, energy transition planning, and sustainable development decisions, preparing students to translate multi-source, large-scale data into actionable insights.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100756,'CSS5330','大语言模型与社会','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5330','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100757,'CSS5340','计算心理学','','CSS - Computational Social Science','5340','C',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','None','None','本课程为计算心理学的入门课程。计算心理学是一门交叉学科，整合了心理学、数据科学和计算建模的理论与方法。课程面向心理学零基础的学生，阐述如何用计算方法研究人类行为、认知与情感。主要内容包括认知机制建模、决策制定模型，以及行为数据分析。通过本课程，学生将掌握计算模型的开发原理，学会用模型模拟和解释心理学过程；同时获得处理心理学数据集和应用编程工具进行建模分析的实践能力。课程为学生从事计算心理学和社会科学研究和应用奠定基础。无需心理学基础；基本的统计学和编程知识对学习本课程有帮助，但非必需。','This course provides a foundational introduction to computational psychology—an interdisciplinary field at the crossroads of psychology, data science, and computational modeling. Designed for students without prior background in psychology, it explores how human behavior, cognition, and emotion can be studied through computational approaches. Topics may include cognitive mechanisms, decision-making models and behavioral data analysis. By the end of the course, students will understand how computational models are developed and used to simulate psychological processes. Students will also gain knowledge in working with psychological datasets and applying programming tools to model and analyze psychological processes. The course prepares students to engage with current computational research and applications in psychology and social science. No prior experience in psychology is required; basic familiarity with statistics and programming is helpful but not required.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
