(100765,'CSS6220','统计学习','','CSS - Computational Social Science','6220','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Prior coursework in linear algebra and calculus, as well as programming experience with Python,is preferred.','Not applicable','本课程基于加雷思-詹姆斯（Gareth James）等人撰写的同类题材的优秀课文，旨在学习机器学习预测模型背后的统计理论和概念。虽然 Gareth 等人的原文对没有很强统计学背景的读者很友好，但本课程将强调有监督和无监督建模和预测背后的统计理论。','This course is based on the excellent text of a similar title by Gareth James et al. It is meant for learning the statistical theories and concepts behind the prediction models in machine learning. While the original text by Gareth et al. is friendly toward readers who do not have a strong statistics background, this course will emphasize the statistical theories behind supervised and unsupervised modeling and prediction.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100766,'CSS6230','社会科学数据计算概论','','CSS - Computational Social Science','6230','C',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Students are expected to have basic knowledge of R, including familiarity with running scripts and fundamental data handling, as the course involves practical exercises using R.','','本跨学科课程向学生介绍社会计算的基本理论、方法、技术和应用。学生将从两个角度了解这一新兴学科：第一，集体信息生产和处理的基本原理，以及研究这些原理的方法。主题包括众包、社交媒体、集体智慧、信息聚合、分布式问题解决和信息可视化。第二，社会计算技术设计和使用的社会技术方面。主题包括参与、贡献、隐私和安全。通过本课程，学生将学习如何以系统而严谨的方式解决社会计算中的问题。','This interdisciplinary course introduces students to fundamental theories, methods, technologies and applications of social computing. Students learn about this emerging discipline from two perspectives: First, basic principles of collective information production and processing, and methods for studying these principles. Topics include prediction markets, games with a purpose, citizen science, open source software development, social media and information visualization. Second, socio-technical aspects of the design and usage of social computing technologies. Topics include participation, contribution, privacy and security. Students learn how to solve problems in social computing in a systematic and rigorous fashion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
