2026-27 Term 1','This course is open to all doctoral students in humanities and social sciences.','NA','本课程将提供撰写论文的实践讲习班，帮助学生准备和编辑论文。该课程还将提供提高交流和公开演讲技能的讲习班。每个学生每学年至少要做一次演讲。总共有7个工作坊，每个工作坊持续2.5个小时。本课程旨在提高学生的学术写作和口头表达能力。该课程为"及格/不及格"，因为它是一门非学分课程，一学期只不定期开7次课。','This course will provide hands-on workshops in writing a thesis, and help the student prepare and edit it. It will also provide workshops to improve communication and public-speaking skills. Each student is required to do at least one presentation in each academic year. There are in total 5 workshops, each lasting for 2 hours. The purpose of this course is for the students to sharpen their academic writing and oral presentation skills. It is graded Pass/Fail because it is a non-credit course that only meets five times irregularly during the semester.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100773,'DAI1000','人工智能与数字素养','','DAI - Digital and AI Literacy','1000','D',1.00,1000,'Major','Distinction/Pass/Failure','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','Null','Null','本课程全面介绍信息技术和人工智能的最新进展，为学生提供适应人工智能时代所需的核心知识。学生将学习现代信息技术及重要定律、人工智能的最新进展、信息安全以及人工智能的社会影响。课程还将通过实践练习，聚焦于现实案例，帮助学生适应信息技术和人工智能领域的快速发展。','This course provides a comprehensive introduction to Information Technology (IT) and Artificial Intelligence (AI), equipping students with essential know-how for the AI era. Students will explore key IT applications and laws, recent developments of AI, cybersecurity, and the societal implications of AI. Hands-on practices will focus on real-world use cases, empowering students to adapt to rapidly evolving innovations in IT and AI.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100774,'DDA1000','新生启导与学业规划','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','1000','D',1.00,1000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','這是一門專為數據科學學院本科新生設計的結構化啟導科目。科目中開展多樣化學習活動，幫助新生適應和順利過渡到大學階段學習，並引導他們了解數據科學及人工智能相關領域的快速發展及其社會影響。通過專家講座、校友分享、小組討論和自我反思等活動，引導學生為下一階段的專業學習和大學生活訂立目標及作出規劃。','This course comprises a structured induction programme that comprises diverse learning activities to help newly arrived students transition into university education and to guide the students through the fast-growing subject fields related to data science, AI and their social impact. Through lectures, invited talks by external experts, alumni sharing, group discussion, and self-reflection, students will be guided to set goals and plan for study at the School of Data Science and university life toward the upper years.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
