(100800,'DDA4310','计算成像','Computational Imaging','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4310','D',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','(MAT3007 or MAT3007H); (MAT2040 or MAT2041 or MAT2041A or MAT2042)','','计算成像是融合光学、图像传感器、算法、软件于一体的新一代成像技术，它突破了传统成像技术信息获取深度（高动态范围、低照度）、广度（光谱、光场、三维）的瓶颈。本课程以计算成像的新设计方法、新算法和应用场景为主线，通过梳理基础知识、高级算法、前沿课题来对当下先进计算成像完整剖析。涵盖了视觉系统，ISP、高动态范围成像、光场成像、光谱成像、噪声分析、三维成像、仿真及端到端光学算法联合设计课题。','Computational imaging breaks the limitation of traditional digital imaging to acquire the information deeper (e.g., high dynamic range imaging and low light imaging) and broader (e.g., spectrum, light field, and 3D imaging). Driven by industry, especially mobile phone manufacturer medical and automotive, computational imaging has become ubiquitous in our daily lives and plays a critical role in accelerating the revolution of industry. This course includes the topics of basic/advanced imaging methods, advanced topics, and covers visual system, ISP, HDR, light-field imaging, spectrum imaging, low light imaging, 3D imaging, and end-to-end camera design.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100801,'DDA4320','随机矩阵及其应用','Random Matrices and Their Applications','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4320','D',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1','STA2002 Probability and Statistics II;
Remark: Knowledge on STA4002 will be favorable.','','在简要介绍了圆律、Marchenko-Pastur律和 Tracy-Widom律之后，我们将研究一些在大数据中经常出现的矩阵，包括样本相关矩阵和 Haar不变矩阵等。 除此之外，我们还将研究球面不变矩阵和行列式点过程之间的关系，从而导出了特征值范数的独立性。 最后将介绍随机矩阵的某些应用。','After a brief introduction of the circular law, the Marchenko-Pastur law and the Tracy-Widom law, we will work on a few matrices which appear in big data frequently. They are sample correlation matrices and Haar-invariant matrices. Besides these we will study the relationship between spherical invariant matrices and determinantal point processes. As a consequence, independence of the norms of eigenvalues are derived. Finally certain applications of random matrices will be presented.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100802,'DDA4330','现代最优化','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4330','D',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1
2023-24 Summer','MAT3007 Optimization or MAT3007H Honours Optimization','','本课程介绍了理解现代最优化理论的主要结果和最重要的研究方向所必需的所有基本要素。在人工智能展示了惊人成就后，很明显
优化将在现代计算数学中发挥核心作用。然而，为了成功地应用这项技术，我们有必要了解优化方法能做什么和不能做什么。我们需要区分可解和不可解的问题，并正确估计求解所需的计算资源。所有这些信息都是由复杂性理论提供的，它确定了我们能力的极限，并提出了尽可能好的优化方案。这是我们课程的主题。所有结果都以严格的数学形式呈现，这使得我们的结论独立于当前的硬件开发水平。','In this course, we present all basic elements which are necessary for understanding the main results and the most important research directions of the Modern Optimization Theory. After demonstration of spectacular achievements of Artificial Intelligence, it became clear that Optimization is going to play a central role in modern Computational Mathematics. However, in order to apply successfully this technique, it is necessary to know what we can and what we cannot do by Optimization Methods. We need to distinguish solvable and unsolvable problems and estimate properly the computational resources required for their solution. All this information is provided by Complexity Theory, which establishes the limits of our abilities and presents the best possible optimization schemes. This is the main subject of the first part of our course.
In the second part, we show how to apply this general knowledge in order to go beyond the theoretical limits and solve modern applications, which very often have a very big size.
All results are presented in a rigorous mathematical form, which makes our conclusions independent of the current level of the hardware development. For participants, only a basic knowledge of Nonlinear Analysis is needed.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100803,'DDA4340','金融中的计算方法','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4340','D',2.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','CSC1001 Introduction to Computer Science: Programming Methodology or CSC1003 Introduction to Computer Science and Java Programming

STA2001 Probability and Statistics I or STA2003 Probability','N/A','随机数生成；蒙特卡洛模拟方法的基础及在金融数学中的应用；蒙特卡洛方法中的方差减少方法；随机微分方程及其基于蒙特卡洛方法的数值求解。','Random number generation; the fundamentals of Monte Carlo (MC) simulation and applications in financial mathematics; variance reduction techniques for MC simulation and related issues; stochastic differential equations and their numerical solutions by means of MC simulation and their implementation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100804,'DDA4350','卫星定位与位置服务','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4350','D',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'','MAT 2041 - Linear Algebra and Applications
CSC 1003，Introduction to Computer Science and Java Programming','这门课程包括三部分。第一部分是卫星定位。这部分将介绍全球导航卫星系统的定位原理，定位误差源和定位算法。定位算法包括最小二乘法和卡尔曼滤波。第二部分是室内定位。这部分将简单介绍室内定位的基本原理，通用定位方法和室内定位的前沿技术。第三部分是位置服务。这一部分将演示定位在室内外不同场景的应用。课程将重点介绍定位在空间智能中的应用。通过本课程的学习，可理解和掌握室内外定位的基本原理及其在人工智能和数据科学等其他领域的应用。','This course will consist of three topics: The first topic is satellite positioning. It will introduce the fundamental principle of Global Navigation Satellite System (GNSS), including satellite orbit, error sources and positioning algorithms, which will include Least Squares and Kalman Filter. The second topic is indoor positioning. It will introduce briefly the fundamental principle of indoor positioning, common approaches and the state-of-the-art technologies of indoor positioning. The third topic is location-based services. It will demonstrate various location-based solutions for indoor and outdoor environments, especially focus on application of spatial intelligence. With the knowledge learned from this course, student will have a good understanding of the principle of indoor/outdoor positioning, and capable to apply positioning technologies in other fields such as artificial intelligence and data science.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100805,'DDA4360','动态定价与需求学习','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4360','D',1.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Basic calculus and linear algebra; probability theory; statistics','','本课程将介绍动态定价与需求学习背后的数学原理，这一主题已引起业界和学术研究的广泛关注。我们将讨论带学习的参数化与非参数化定价方法、离散选择模型与产品组合优化、面向数据驱动决策问题的模型选择、将行为因素纳入定价模型，以及算法价格共谋等内容。','This course provides an introduction to the mathematics underlying dynamic pricing and demand learning, a topic that has attracted significant attention from both industry and academic research. We will discuss parametric and non-parametric approaches to pricing with learning, discrete choice models and assortment optimization, model selection for data-driven decision problems, incorporating behavior aspects into pricing models, and algorithmic price collusion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100806,'DDA4370','随机微分方程','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','4370','D',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','- STA4001 Stochastic Processes or STA4001H Honours Stochastic Processes
- Analysis of real-valued functions of one variable','','本科目將介紹隨機微分方程的基礎理論。科目內容將分為以下幾個部分：

1. 分析學基礎
2. 測度與積分精要
3. 概率論基礎
4. 伊藤公式與隨機微積分
5. 隨機微分方程 (SDEs)

根據學生的數學背景，上述內容可能會有所調整，以涵蓋隨機微分方程理論中更進階的主題，例如：鞅（Martingales）、Girsanov 變換、鞅問題或隨機偏微分方程。','The course will give an introduction to stochastic differential equations.
It will be structured according to the following sections:

1.  Basics from analysis

2. Compact course on measure and integration

3. Basics from probability theory

4. Ito’s formula and stochastic calculus

5. Stochastic differential equations (SDEs)

Depending on the mathematical background knowledge of the participants, there might be changes to the above list aiming at more advanced topics in the theory of SDEs, such as martingales, Girsanov transformation, martingale problems or stochastic partial differential equations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
