2025-26 Term 2','','','介绍随机过程基本理论和各种应用。主题包括马尔可夫过程，更新理论，随机游动，分支过程，布朗运动，平稳过程，鞅和点过程, 以及排队理论和库存模型的应用。','A stochastic process is a mathematical model for random phenomena which change in time. With examples such as coin tossing, betting, queueing system, branching process, and stochastic networks, this course introduces a basic theory for modelling stochastic processes. It intends to help students to perform applied and theoretical studies on stochastic processes. Topics include martingales, Poisson processes, Markov processes, Brownian motions and stochastic differential equations. A basic probability course is prerequisite for this course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100812,'DDA6010','优化理论与算法','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','6010','D',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 1
