(100827,'DDA6201','数据和决策分析专题（一）：优化理论与算法','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','6201','D',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 1
2020-21 Term 2
2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Calculus, Linear Algebra, Statistics, and Python.','','本课程介绍优化的基础理论与算法。课程首先回顾数学基础知识及无约束优化的最优性条件，随后讲解梯度法、收敛性分析、牛顿法及高斯 - 牛顿法。接着，课程将研究凸集上的优化、可行方向法、拉格朗日乘子法以及对偶性的基本原理。针对约束优化及结构化问题，课程将介绍惩罚函数法、增广拉格朗日法以及交替方向乘子法（ADMM）。对于大规模、非凸及非光滑优化问题，课程涵盖通用近似梯度投影框架、Lasso、组 Lasso（Group Lasso）、近端算子、Bregman 距离、近端梯度法、Nesterov 型加速方法、增量梯度法以及随机近似法。课程最后部分通过介绍带动量的随机梯度下降（SGD with Momentum）、AdaGrad、RMSProp、Adam(W)、Shampoo 和 Muon 等算法，将经典优化理论与现代神经网络训练相结合。学生将掌握这些方法的核心思想，分析其收敛行为，并学会针对不同的优化问题选择合适的算法。','This course introduces the fundamental theory and algorithms of optimization. It begins with a mathematical review and optimality conditions for unconstrained optimization, followed by gradient methods, convergence analysis, Newton methods, and Gauss–Newton methods. The course then studies optimization over convex sets, feasible-direction methods, Lagrange multipliers, and the basic principles of duality. Penalty methods, augmented Lagrangian methods, and the alternating direction method of multipliers are introduced for constrained and structured problems. For large-scale, nonconvex, and nonsmooth optimization, the course covers the general approximate gradient projection framework, Lasso, group Lasso, proximity operators, Bregman distances, proximal-gradient methods, Nesterov-type accelerated methods, incremental-gradient methods, and stochastic-approximation methods. The final part connects classical optimization with modern neural-network training by introducing SGD with momentum, AdaGrad, RMSProp, Adam(W), Shampoo, and Muon. Students will learn the main ideas behind these methods, analyze their convergence behavior, and select suitable algorithms for different optimization problems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100828,'DDA6202','机器学习中的优化模型和方法','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','6202','D',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1','Linear algebra, Calculus, Probability, Introduction to optimization','','本课程是一门高级课程，涵盖了优化与深度学习交叉的几个主题。本课程目的是提供对深度学习和大模型中的优化模型和算法的深入了解，以便学生可以更好地利用深度学习和大模型来解决实际问题。大多数内容都是基于近年来的研究，部分出现在“深度学习的优化：理论和算法”中（网址为https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.08957）。本课程主题包括神经网络的优化（包括智能初始化和信号传播分析，景观分析和可视化，NTK理论），机器学习中的流行优化算法（Adam，AdaGrad等），大模型中的优化，双层优化，多目标优化和多任务学习等。优化和机器学习的知识对本课程有帮助，但不是必需的。微积分、概率、线性代数的良好基础是基本要求。','This course is an advanced course that lies in the intersection of optimization and deep learning. The goal is to provide an in-depth understanding of optimization and deep learning, so that the students can better utilize deep learning and large foundational models to solve real problems. Most contents are based on research in recent years, partially summarized in the instructor''s survey "optimization for deep learning: theory and algorithms" https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.08957. Topics include optimization for neural nets (including smart initialization and signal propagation analysis, landscape analysis and visualization, NTK theory), popular optimization algorithms in machine learning (Adam, AdaGrad, etc.), optimization for large foundational models, bilevel optimization, multi-objective optimization and multi-task learning, etc. Prior exposure to optimization and machine learning is preferred, but not required. Solid foundation in calculus, linear algebra and probability is required.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100829,'DDA6203','数据和决策分析专题（三）排队论','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','6203','D',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','STA4001','None','本课程介绍队列的建模技术。课程内容涵盖单服务器与多服务器系统的精确分析、网络模型以及基本守恒定律。此外，课程还将讲解重流量（heavy-traffic）渐近近似方法，并以时变需求、策略性行为、结构性依赖关系以及专用调度策略作为总结。','This course introduces modeling techniques for queues. Topics cover exact analysis of single- and multi-server systems, network models, and fundamental conservation laws. It also covers heavy-traffic asymptotic approximations and concludes with time-varying demand, strategic behavior, structural dependencies, and specialized scheduling.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100830,'DDA6204','数据和决策分析专题（四）神经网络训练：理论与实践','','DDA - Data and Decision Analytics','6204','D',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2020-21 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Linear algebra. Calculus. Probability and Statistics. Machine Learning.','','本课程为博士阶段课程，旨在系统性地构建学生对神经网络训练（尤其是大语言模型）的原则性理解与实践认知。课程将数学基础、实证分析与系统考量相结合，阐释现代模型如何训练、训练成功或失败的原因，以及如何提升训练的有效性与效率。通过讲座、实验及开放性项目，学生将学会分析训练行为、评估不同解释的合理性，并设计可复现的改进方案，以优化真实的训练流程。','This PhD-level course develops a principled and practical understanding of neural network training, with particular emphasis on large language models. It connects mathematical foundations, empirical analysis, and systems considerations to explain how modern models are trained, why training succeeds or fails, and how training can be made more effective and efficient. Through lectures, experiments, and an open-ended project, students learn to analyze training behavior, evaluate competing explanations, and design reproducible improvements to real training pipelines','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
