2026-27 Term 1','MAT1001 or MAT1003 or MAT1010 or MAT1011','N/A','本课程旨在向理工科学生介绍信号与系统的基础概念和技术。内容包括：信号与系统概念，线性时不变系统，周期信号的傅里叶级数表示，连续时间傅里叶变换，离散时间傅里叶变换，抽样，拉普拉斯变换，z-变换。','This course provides science and engineering students with exposure to the basic concepts and techniques in signals and systems. Topics include introduction to signals and systems, linear time-invariant systems, Fourier series representation of periodic signals, the continuous-time Fourier transform, the discrete-time Fourier transform, sampling, the Laplace transform, the z-transform.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100908,'ECE3040','线性系统导论','Introduction to Linear Systems','ECE - Electrical Computer Eng','3040','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2024-25 Summer','The course is targeted towards senior undergrads and graduate students (not entry-level class).
(1)	Minimum requirement is familiarity with concepts in calculus and linear algebra, such as ordinary differential equations and matrix operations;
(2)	Basic knowledge of system & control including the Laplace transform, transfer function, etc;
(3)	Knowledge in basic programming (Matlab).','','本课程是一门面向高年级本科生或初级研究生的多输入多输出、线性、时不变系统课程。课程内容包括状态空间和输入输出表示；解及其性质；多变量极点和零点；可达性、可观性和最小实现；稳定性；系统范数及其计算；线性化技术。本课程的内容是系统与控制理论的许多学科分支的基础，对后续学习诸如最优控制、非线性控制、鲁棒控制、智能控制、系统辨识和参数估计、路径规划、机器人控制等都具有重要和基本的作用。','A senior undergraduate or beginning graduate level course in multi-input multi-output, linear, time-invariant systems. Topics include state-space and input-output representations; solutions and their properties; multivariable poles and zeros; reachability, observability, and minimal realization; stability; system norms and their computation; linearization techniques.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100909,'ECE3050','通信系统原理','Principles of Communication Systems','ECE - Electrical Computer Eng','3050','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Calculus, Probability','','这是一门关于现代电信系统和技术的基础课。本课程涵盖基本频谱分析、经典模拟通信技术和数字通信技术。学生将从本课程中学习现实世界通信系统的基本概念和工作原理。本课程为学习先进的无线/有线通信技术奠定基础。','This is a fundamental course on modern telecommunication systems and technologies. The course covers the basic spectrum analysis, classical analog communication techniques and digital communication techniques. Students will learn from the course the basic concepts and operation principles of a real-world communication systems. The course serves the basis for learning advanced wireless/wired communications technologies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100910,'ECE3060','机械人学概论','Introduction to Robotics','ECE - Electrical Computer Eng','3060','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程将带领学生了解机器人领域的有趣知识。课程涵盖机器人学相关的基础专业内容，如：1）机器人的定义与分类；2）空间坐标系与齐次变换等相关数学概念；3）机器人的前/逆向运动学、DH计算方法、雅可比矩阵、运动奇异；4）工作空间分析、轨迹计算；5）机器人运动与力的控制过程。此外，课程亦会讲解机器人系统相关的延申内容，包括：1）机器人传感器与驱动器；2）人机交互；3）机器人在部分领域应用的深度剖析。课程可增进学生对工程理论与实践应用间的理解，并为进修学院其他高年级课程打下良好基础。','The course will bring students to the interesting world of robotics technology. The course covers the basic and fundamentals including: 1) basic concepts and classification of robots; 2) relevant mathematical concepts like coordinate frames and homogeneous transformations; 3) forward and inverse kinematics of a robot with the Denavit-Hartenberg notation, Jacobians, motion singularity; 4) workspace analysis, and trajectory generation; 5) robot motion and force control. In addition, the course will also introduce extended knowledge about robotic systems, such as 1) robot sensors and actuators; 2) human-robot interface, and 3) in-depth introduction of robot applications in particular fields. The course will provide students broadened insight on how to interconnect engineering theories to applications, and good basis for future courses.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100911,'ECE3070','计算机组成原理与系统','Computer Organization and Systems','ECE - Electrical Computer Eng','3070','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Analog Circuit Design， Digital Circuit Design，Semiconductor Devices','','本课程介绍现代计算机系统的基本原理，阐述计算机的设计方法及其执行程序的工作机制。课程内容涵盖软件与硬件之间的交互关系，包括指令集体系结构（ISA）、算术逻辑单元（ALU）、数据通路、控制单元以及存储系统等主题。主要内容包括指令执行、流水线技术、性能评估、存储层次结构和输入/输出操作，重点分析数据在处理器、存储器与外设之间的传输过程。学生还将学习与性能、效率和成本相关的设计权衡，从而深入理解体系结构设计对系统行为的影响。课程结束后，学生将具备扎实的计算机组成基础，为进一步学习人工智能加速芯片、嵌入式系统和操作系统奠定良好的理论基础。','This course introduces the fundamental principles that define how modern computers are designed and how they execute programs. It explores the interaction between software and hardware through topics such as instruction set architectures, arithmetic logic units (ALUs), datapaths, control units, and memory systems. Core subjects include instruction execution, pipelining, performance evaluation, memory hierarchy, and input/output operations, emphasizing how data moves between the processor, memory, and peripheral devices. Students will also study design trade-offs related to performance, efficiency, and cost, gaining a clear understanding of how architectural choices impact system behaviour. By the end of the course, students will have developed a solid foundation in computer organization, providing essential knowledge for further study in AI accelerator, embedded systems, and operating systems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
