(100919,'ECE3510','数字信号处理','Digital Signal Processing','ECE - Electrical Computer Eng','3510','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MAT1001 Calculus I (or MAT1003 Analysis I)

MAT2040 Linear Algebra

ECE/EIE3001 Signals and System

Proficiency in advanced calculus and familiarity with introductory complex variable theory and matrix operations are required. Previous exposure to linear system theory for continuous-time signals, Laplace transform, and Fourier transform are required; exposure to discrete-time signals, discrete-time Fourier transform, and z-transform is assumed, but relevant concepts will be reviewed again in this course. No experience with discrete Fourier transforms is assumed.','N/A','数字信号是时间、频率、或空间上的连续变量的采样序列，数字信号处理通过变换分析来理解和处理这些采样序列，是机器学习与人工智能里进行特征提取的重要技术手段，在语言处理、雷达、通信、生物医学、地震学、图像与视觉处理、传感与控制等有广泛应用。本课程介绍数字信号处理的理论基础和基本技术，围绕“滤波”这一核心思想方法，介绍并设计数字滤波器以及相关理论工具。具体内容包括：离散时间信号的表达和离散系统、离散傅立叶变换(DFT)、快速傅立叶变换(FFT)、短时傅立叶变换（STFT）、采样与量化、数字域信号处理、变换分析、FIR和IIR滤波器设计、加窗、卷积技术、以及一些数字信号处理的应用专题。','A digital signal is a sequence of samples of continuous variables in time, frequency, or space. Digital signal processing uses transform analysis to understand and process these sample sequences, making it an important technique for feature extraction in machine learning and artificial intelligence. It is widely applied in fields such as language processing, radar, communications, biomedical engineering, seismology, image and vision processing, sensing, and control. This course introduces the theoretical foundations and basic techniques of digital signal processing, including the introduction and design of digital filters. Specific topics include: representation of discrete-time signals and discrete systems, Discrete Fourier Transform (DFT), Fast Fourier Transform (FFT), Short-Time Fourier Transform (STFT), sampling and quantization, digital domain signal processing, transform analysis, FIR and IIR filter design, windowing, convolution techniques, as well as selected application topics in digital signal processing.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
