(100933,'ECE4300','人机交互系统设计','Systems Design in Human-Computer Interaction','ECE - Electrical Computer Eng','4300','E',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Basic programming knowledge is required, including understanding of fundamental programming theory. Students should have completed one or more of the following programming courses: Python (CSC-1001/CSC-1002), Java (CSC-1003/CSC-1004), C# or C++ (CSC-3002)

Students who have previously taken ECE3200: Video Game Design and Development are strongly encouraged to enroll, as the Unity skills and design mindset from that course provide an excellent foundation for this class. Prior experience with Unity or similar interactive development platforms is also highly beneficial.','CSC-4001 Software Engineering (Recommended but not required)','本课程的目的在于向学生介绍供人类使用的交互式计算系统的基本理论，实现方法和评估技能，包括用户界面设计、用户体验、可用性评估、多模态交互（如语音、手势、触觉交互）等，同时，这门课程还将涉及人机交互技术的前沿进展，例如虚拟现实、增强现实、脑机接口、移动设备交互等。学生需要根据从课堂教材以及其他的研究汲取的知识，以个人和团队合作的方式对互动系统和使用者界面进行设计，实践和评估。','The purpose of this course is to introduce students to the basic theory, implementation methods and evaluation skills of interactive computing systems for human use, including user interface design, user experience, usability evaluation, multimodal interaction (e.g., speech, gesture, haptic interaction), etc. At the same time, this course will also cover the leading-edge advances in human-computer interaction technologies, such as virtual reality, augmented reality, brain-computer interfaces, mobile device interaction,  etc. Students will be expected to work individually and in team assignments to design, implement, and evaluate various interactive systems and user interfaces based on knowledge culled from class material and additional research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
