2019-20 Summer','ECO3121 is required. In addition, students should have some exposure to intermediate economics, and at least one semester training in calculus, linear algebra, probability, statistics.','No co-requisite.','本课程介绍了现代机器学习中的基本概念和方法，包括其在经济学和商业实践中的应用。该课程首先简单介绍数据管理和Python语言编程，然后将涵盖机器学习中的经典内容，例如（1）统计学习理论（偏差-方差权衡）；（2）线性回归模型；（3）逻辑回归和线性判别分析；（4）重抽样方法；（5）模型选择、正则化以及降维法；（6）非线性模型；（7）基于树的方法；（8）神经网络。','This course introduces basic concepts and methods of modern machine learning, with their applications in economic and business practice. The course will start with a brief introduction to data management and programming with Python, and then cover a number of classic topics in machine learning such as (1) statistical learning theory (bias-variance trade-off); (2) linear regression models; (3) logistic regression and linear discriminant analysis; (4) resampling methods; (5) model selection, regularization and dimension reduction; (6) nonlinear models; (7) tree-based methods; (8) neural networks.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
