2025-26 Term 2','ECO2011 Basic Microeconomics    ECO2021 Basic Macroeconomics','No co-requisite.','本课程将系统介绍国际贸易的理论与实证、历史演变以及当代热点问题，涵盖比较优势理论、贸易如何影响收入分配与经济发展、贸易政策工具及其福利影响，并结合全球化与地缘政治视角，探讨国际贸易规则、国际协议及其对全球商务的深远影响。课程将帮助学生理解国际贸易与全球化、国际经济格局和地缘政治变动之间的互动关系，培养分析当代贸易争端、供应链变化和跨国企业战略的能力。','This course provides a dynamic overview of international trade by exploring the historical evolution of trade, the development of core theories like comparative advantage, and the impact of trade on economic development and income distribution; it also examines the interplay of trade with globalization and geopolitics, analyzes how international agreements and policies shape global commerce, and prepares students to evaluate contemporary issues such as shifting supply chains and the influence of international organizations on global markets.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100966,'ECO3620','数据分析与宏观经济政策','Data Analysis and Macroeconomic Policies','ECO - Economics','3620','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','ECO2021 Basic Macroeconomics','No co-requisite.','本课程将通过真实世界的数据分析，探讨主要的宏观经济政策话题。学生将通过使用Excel、Python以及AI辅助工具等应用程序，掌握数据可视化、趋势解读等实用技能，并学会如何运用这些技能为政策制定提供参考。课程注重培养数据素养，帮助学生借助技术手段，将宏观经济学知识与实际决策有效结合。同时，课程还将讨论当前前沿研究中的关键宏观经济议题，涵盖劳动力市场、通货膨胀、货币与财政政策、开放经济、金融体系、经济增长、经济周期、收入不平等，以及人工智能在政策研究中的影响等内容。','This course explores major macroeconomic policy areas through the lens of real-world data analysis. Students will develop hands-on skills using tools like Excel, Python, and AI-assisted apps to visualize data, interpret trends and inform policy thinking. Emphasis is placed on building data fluency and using technology to bridge macroeconomics with decision-making. Cutting-edge studies on critical macroeconomic topics will be discussed, including issues of labor market, inflation, monetary and fiscal policies, open economy, financial systems, economic growth, business cycles, inequality and the implications of AI in policy research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100967,'ECO3630','国际金融','International Finance','ECO - Economics','3630','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Prerequisites of this course include ECO2011 Basic Microeconomics and ECO2021 Basic Macroeconomics. College level algebra and simple calculus will be used during the lectures. Familiarity with statistical and econometric inference is beneficial but not required.','No co-requisite.','本课程旨在帮助学生理解和把握国际金融的相关理论和实证研究。课程内容主要涵盖国际收支和经常账户，汇率的决定，开放经济体宏观政策分析，汇率制度，资本管制和跨境资本流动，以及金融全球化背景下的中国经济。本课程融合理论模型与实际案例分析，旨在培养学生的分析能力和批判性思维。通过学习相关工具和方法，学生将能够更加深入地理解国际金融市场动态，并对相关政策进行有效评估。','This course offers an in-depth exploration of international finance theories and empirical analyses. Topics covered include global imbalances, current account determination, exchange rate determination, open-economy macroeconomic policies, exchange rate regimes, capital controls and cross-border capital flows, and Chinese economy in the context of financial globalization. Through a blend of theoretical models and real-world case studies, this course aims to equip students with analytical tools and critical thinking skills to effectively analyze international financial markets and evaluate policies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100968,'ECO3650','发展经济学','Development Economics','ECO - Economics','3650','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Basic Microeconomics (ECO2011), Basic Macroeconomics (ECO2021), and (Basic Statistics (ECO2121) or (STA2001 or STA2003 or STA2001H)). Knowledge of econometrics (e.g., ECO3121) will be highly useful.','No co-requisite.','本课程介绍有关发展中经济体的经济增长与发展的主要理论和实证发现。课程将首先引入增长理论并讨论其在发展中国家的应用，随后讨论文献中关于经济发展各个方面的研究进展，包括结构转型、人口迁移、要素市场、卫生条件、教育和贸易。','This course covers the main theories and empirical findings about economic growth and development across developing economies. We will first introduce growth theories and discuss their implications to developing countries, and then move on to discuss specific aspects of economic development in the recent literature, including structural transformation, migration, factor markets, health, education, and trade.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100969,'ECO3710','中国经济','China Economy','ECO - Economics','3710','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 2
