2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2020-21 Summer
2021-22 Summer','ECO2011 Basic Microeconomics
ECO2021 Basic Macroeconomics
ECO3121 Introductory Econometrics','None','在这门课程中，我们将涵盖以下主题：中国经济改革的政治逻辑，中国经济增长奇迹的制度基础，腐败/反腐败问题，中国的劳动力市场转型，中国融入世界经济，中国金融市场，中国的创新与创业，中国的环境问题等等。第一周，我们将共同选择八个话题来进行本学期的讨论。每个话题我们将用三个课程来讲解：在前两个课程中，讲师将会授课并介绍两到三篇主要文章。在第三个课程中，学生将展示当周的另外两篇必读文章，并进行讨论。学生将以4或5人小组的形式注册展示一次，并对他们展示的学术文章撰写一份评审报告。该课程主要基于研究论文的讨论。我们不指定教科书。','In this course, we will cover topics including: the political logic of China''s economic reform, the institutional foundations of the Chinese economic growth miracle, corruption/anti-corruption, labor market transitions in China, China’s integration into the world economy, Chinese financial market, China’s innovation and entrepreneurship, China’s environmental issues, among others. In Week One, we will collectively choose 9 topics to cover for the semester. We will spend three sessions on each topic: In the first two sessions, the instructors will lecture and present two/three main articles. In the third session, students will present two other required readings for that week and engage in discussions. Students will sign up to present once, in a group of 4 or 5, and will also write a referee report on the academic article they present on. The course will be mostly based on discussions of research papers. We do not assign a textbook.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
