2026-27 Term 1','No Prerequisites','No Co-requisites','本课程向学生介绍现代的宏观经济理论。本课程旨在让学生全面了解现代宏观经济分析的一些基本模型，同时讨论与这些理论模型相关的一些主要实证问题。本课程涵盖的主题将包括家庭和生产者的问题、长期增长模型、理解短期经济波动的商业周期理论、资产定价和新凯恩斯主义模型以及宏观经济政策分析。
课程材料假设学生接受过中级宏观经济学和微观经济学的培训。还需要足够的大学代数、微积分和统计学知识。','This course introduces students to modern, advanced macroeconomic theory. The course aims to give students a thorough understanding of some fundamental workhorse models for modern macroeconomic analysis, and at the same time discuss some of the major empirical questions related to these theoretical models. The topics covered in this course will include households’ and producers’ problems, models on long term growth, real business cycle theories to understand short-run economic fluctuations, asset pricing and new Keynesian models as well as macroeconomic policy analysis.
The course material assumes students have trainings on intermediate level macroeconomics and microeconomics. Adequate knowledge on college-level algebra, calculus and statistics is also required.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
