2026-27 Term 1
2020-21 Summer','Students should have some exposure to intermediate economics, and undergraduate training in calculus and linear algebra. Undergraduate level of econometrics is required.','No co-requisite.','该课程介绍金融数据分析的计量工具。课堂讨论的主题包括：市场有效假说、概率统计的基本概论、线性回归、时间序列模型、机器学习方法、因子模型、以及相关方法。课程的重点是这些方法如何解决金融问题。本课程还教授学生如何使用 Python 实现这些方法，并利用现代 AI 辅助编程工具提高实证研究能力。','The course provides econometrics tools for data analysis in empirical finance. Topics covered include: efficient markets hypothesis, basic tools in probability and statistics, linear regression, time series models, machine learning prediction, factor models, and related methods. The emphasis will be placed on how these tools are applied to solve real-world finance problems. The course also teaches students how to implement these methods in Python and leverage modern AI-assisted coding tools to improve empirical research workflows.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
