2026-27 Term 1','None','None','这是一门应用计量经济学研究生课程。本课程旨在探讨各类计量经济学模型的估计、设定与推断方法。通过给定数据集进行模型构建与参数估计是本课程的主要特色，因此我们将着重强调计量经济理论与实际应用之间的互动关系。课程内容涵盖模型选择问题、数据转换、异方差性、序列与空间相关性、样本选择偏差、内生性问题、工具变量估计法、双重差分估计法、断点回归/拐点设计等专题。','This is a graduate level course in applied econometrics. This course is intended to deal with model estimation, specification, and inference with various econometric models. Modelling and estimating appropriate econometric models using given data sets are major characteristics of our class, so we will emphasize the interplay between econometric theory and applications. This course will consider model selection problems, data transformations, heteroskedasticity, serial and spatial dependence, sample selection, endogeneity, instrumental variable estimation, difference-in-differences estimation, regression discontinuity/kink design etc.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(100995,'ECO6112','博弈论及商业应用','','ECO - Economics','6112','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2017-18 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','博弈论是以数学建模为基本方法，研究理性决策者在策略环境中之行为的学科。其为经济学、社会学、生物学、心理学等诸多领域提供了理论研究的重要方法论，以及实证研究的微观基础。本课程将介绍博弈论的基础概念和分析方法，包括不同信息环境下的策略与扩展式博弈，以及谈判、拍卖、合约等各种应用。','Game Theory is the study of mathematical models in analyzing strategic scenarios for rational agents. It has been widely adopted as the theoretical toolkit as well as the micro-foundation of empirical studies in multiple areas, such as economics, sociology, biology and psychology. This course provides an introduction to concepts and analytical methods in strategic/extensive games of complete and incomplete information, as well as various applications such as bargaining, auctions and contracts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
