2026-27 Term 1','i.	 Only for Year 2 students of the MSc Economics Programme (Including the 2023 Partnership Master’s Programme Students).
ii.	 CGPA at CUHK-Shenzhen should be no less than 2.0
iii. If you are on the probation list, you are not eligible for applying this course.','a) Successful enrollment on this course is subject to approval from the Programme Director. The application procedures are as follows. i. Students are required to submit 1) a course application form which states the student, employer and internship information; 2) a signed contract with the employer. ii. Students will receive the email notification about the application result. Upon the approval, the students will be added onto this course on SIS.

b) If you would like to enroll ECO6121 Graduati','本课程旨在帮助学生提升专业技能和积累实践经验。通过修读此实习课程，学生不仅能学习如何将经济学理论知识运用于实践，同时还能掌握职业发展所需技能及积累相关工作经验，为成功的职业生涯做好充分准备。实习结束后，学生需要提交书面报告，阐述他们在实习过程中学到的知识，以及如何应用理论知识来解决实习期间遇到的实际问题。学生还需要定期（每两周）与指导老师通话会面，报告实习进展并听取反馈意见。所有会议内容和评论都应作为课程辅助材料进行存档。','This course aims to provide students with professional skills and real-world experiences. Internships in Economics will be structured to help students combine in-class theory with real-world applications in business, government, consulting and research, as well as gain the skills and experiences that are necessary to prepare for a successful career. Upon completion of the internship, students are required to submit written reports that describe what they have learned from the internship experience and how they apply theories to address practical problems encountered during the internship period. Students are also required to meet with faculty sponsors regularly (every two weeks) via conference calls to report progress and receive feedback. All meeting details and comments should be documented as the supporting materials required by the course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101005,'ECO6122','行为经济学','','ECO - Economics','6122','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2018-19 Term 2
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','ECO2011: Basic Microeconomics (or equivalent), and ECO3121: Introductory Econometrics (or equivalent)','No co-requisite.','本课程覆盖行为经济学的最近研究话题，主要侧重于利用计量回归、实验室实验以及田野实验的实证分析与应用。行为经济学作为一门基础工具学科，被广泛应用于经济学研究其他分支。本课程将着重介绍个人和群体的行为如何偏离传统的新古典经济学分析范式，主要话题包括1）偏好（风险、时间和社会偏好）；2）信念和个体学习（过度自信、估测偏差、归因偏差等）；以及（3）决策分析（认知能力、注意力配置、框架效应等）。这些分析工具被应用于多个经济学分支，包括劳动经济学、发展经济学、公共经济学、健康经济学、金融和环境经济学等。','This class covers recent topics in behavioral economics, with a focus on empirical applications using tools including non-experimental data analysis, lab experiment, and field experiment. This is a fundamental research field, related to almost all areas of existing economics. Our topics include deviations from the standard neoclassical model in terms of (i) preferences (risk, time, and social preferences), (ii) beliefs and learning (overconfidence, projection bias, and attribution bias), and (iii) decision-making (cognition, attention, and framing). Applications will cover a wide range of fields, including labor economics, development economics, public economics, health economics, finance, and environmental economics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
