2018-19 Summer','Students should have some exposure to intermediate economics, and undergraduate training in calculus and linear algebra. Undergraduate level of econometrics is required.','No co-requisite.','本课程将介绍现代机器学习算法，并侧重于其在商业与经济领域中的应用。课程涵盖的主题包括：监督与无监督学习、线性与非线性回归、分类、模型选择、交叉验证、正则化、降维、基于树的方法以及神经网络。本课程将重点探讨这些算法在商业与经济数据中的实际应用，并介绍如何使用Python实现这些方法。','Description (English)	This course provides an introduction to modern machine learning algorithms, with a focus on their applications in business and economics. Topics covered include supervised and unsupervised learning, linear and nonlinear regression, classification, model selection, cross-validation, regularization, dimension reduction, tree-based methods, and neural networks. Emphasis is placed on applications using business and economics data. The course also covers how to implement these methods using Python.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
