2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在帮助学生系统理解，自1978年市场化改革与对外开放以来，中国如何通过快速工业化、城镇化、国际化与数字化，从一个相对封闭、实行中央计划经济的欠发达经济体，跃升为世界第二大经济体。课程将深入剖析政府与市场的协同机制、全球宏观环境变迁以及技术变革如何共同塑造中国经济增长模式的演进路径，并探讨其对应对未来挑战的深层启示。在系统回顾历史发展成就的基础上，本课程将重点聚焦中国在经济结构转型、社会发展、生态环境及地缘政治等多维度面临的现实挑战，探讨中国如何致力于构建更加开放、创新、包容与可持续的增长模式，以实现中国与世界的共同繁荣与和平发展。课程考核成绩将由期中考试、个人项目、小组项目及期末课程论文四部分综合评定。','This course helps students to understand how the market-oriented economic reform and opening since 1978 have transformed China from a closed, centrally planned, and under-developed economy into the second largest economy in the world through rapid industrialization, urbanization, internationalization, and digitalization. It examines how the role of the state and the market, the global environment, and the technology are shaping the evolving growth model of China, and the implications on future challenges. In addition to a review of historical achievements, the course will discuss a broad range of economic, social, environmental and geopolitical challenges as China strives to build a more open, innovative, inclusive, and sustainable growth model for the peace and prosperity of China and the World. Course grade will be based on a mid-term exam, an individual project, a group project and a final essay.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
