iii. If you are on the probation list, you are not eligible for applying this course.','','通过本课程，学生将有机会将经济学理论知识应用于社会实践。学生能熟悉了解需要应用经济学思想、概念和技能的工作内容，学习与经济学相关的新技能，并熟悉对专业领域工作的期望。本课程将通过与实习单位雇主直接沟通来跟踪学生的表现。','This course is a professional learning experience that provides students with an opportunity to apply economic knowledge to “real world” experiences. The practicum enables students to become familiar with work that requires the application of economics ideas, concepts and skills, to learn new skills related to economics, and to become familiar with the expectations for work in the professional world. The programme will keep track of students’ performance by directly contacting the host employers.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101019,'ECO6136','金融经济学','','ECO - Economics','6136','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','ECO2011 and (MAT1001 or MAT1010 or MAT1011) and (ECO2121 or STA2001 or STA2003)
i.e., basic microeconomics, basic calculus, and basic statistics.
Intermediate microeconomics is a plus, but not required.','none','本课程介绍投资和资产定价。它概述了金融市场和工具，包括股票、债券、期货、期权和其他衍生品。无套利原则用于为债券和衍生品定价。然后，使用风险回报框架来理解最优资产配置和证券的均衡定价。本课程涵盖的主题包括经典主题，如二叉树和Black-Scholes模型、资本资产定价模型、两基金分离定理，以及在时间允许的情况下探索套利极限的最新行为模型。','This course is an introduction to investments and asset pricing. It provides an overview of financial markets and instruments including stocks, bonds, futures, options, and other derivatives. The no-arbitrage principle is used to price
bonds and derivatives. A risk-return framework is then used to understand optimal asset allocation and equilibrium pricing of securities. Topics covered in this course include classic topics such as binomial-tree and Black-Scholes models, Capital Asset Pricing Model, two-fund separation theorem, and recent behavior models that explore the limits of arbitrage if time permitted.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
