2026-27 Term 1','No prerequisite.','No co-requisite.','本课程为经济学家介绍数学主题。旨在复习和巩固与我们博士课程未来课程相关的知识。本课程将涵盖的主题包括基本实分析、线性代数、微积分、概率论、统计学、最优控制和动态规划理论。
您需要培养这个职业所需的基本数学技能：阅读学术论文、评估（和撰写）证明、将数学与经济直觉联系起来等。最重要的是，我们希望学生能够在学术生涯中习惯数学作为一种语言。','This course introduces topics of mathematics for economists. It is intended to refresh and consolidate the knowledge that is relevant to future courses in our Ph.D. program. The topics will be covered in this course include basic real analysis, linear algebra, calculus, probability theory, statistics, optimal control, and dynamic programming theory.
You are expected to develop basic math skills needed in this profession: read academic papers, evaluate (and compose) proofs, bridge math to economic intuition, etc. Most importantly, we hope the students could get used to math as a language in their academic careers.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
