2026-27 Term 1','PhD Math pre-Course','N/A','这是宏观经济学核心研究生序列的第一门课程。其主要目标是使学生掌握严谨的理论框架和定量工具，以分析现代动态一般均衡模型。本课程将重点关注宏观经济总量（如总消费、总投资、劳动供给等），并探讨在何种情况下将这些总量变量作为微观经济变量的代理变量进行研究是充分的。课程内容涵盖动态宏观经济学的基础，包括长期增长理论和经济周期分析。整个课程将讲授相关方法和工具，特别是动态均衡理论和动态优化，包括相关的编程技术。 本课程材料假设学生已具备硕士水平的宏观经济学和微观经济学训练背景。此外，还要求学生具备大学水平的代数、微积分、统计学和实变分析知识。','This is the first course in the core graduate macroeconomic sequence. Its primary objective is to equip students with the rigorous theoretical frameworks and quantitative tools necessary to analyze modern dynamic general equilibrium models. We will focus on aggregates in this class (such as aggregate consumption, investment, labor supply, etc) and when it is sufficient to study these variables as a proxy for microeconomic variables. This course covers the foundations of dynamic macroeconomics, including long-run growth theory and business cycle analysis. Methods and tools will be presented throughout the course, in particular we will learn dynamic equilibrium theory and dynamic optimization, including related coding technics. The course material assumes students have trainings on master level macroeconomics and microeconomics. Adequate knowledge on college-level algebra, calculus, statistics, and real analysis is also required.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
