(101072,'EIE4005','编码及密码学导论','Introduction to Coding and Cryptography','EIE - Electronic Info Engineering','4005','E',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Summer','MAT2040 Linear Algebra
STA2001 Probability and Statistics I

It is recommended (but not required) that students have taken a course in discrete mathematics (such as CSC3001).','','编码理论和密码学是离散数学在信息和通信系统中的两种应用：编码理论研究用于信息传输和存储的纠错码；密码学则是保护信息免受对恶意攻击的学科。

本课程的目标是介绍这两个领域并了解它们的基本数学工具。涵盖的主题包括：线性码、循环码、BCH 和 Reed-Solomon 码、经典密码学、私钥（对称）和公钥（非对称）密码学。若时间允许，基于学生兴趣，可能包括其他主题。','Coding theory and cryptography are two applications of discrete mathematics to information and communication systems: coding theory is the study of error-correcting codes for reliable information transmission and storage; cryptography is the science of protecting information against adversarial attacks.

The goal of this course is to introduce these subjects and to understand the basic mathematical tools for them. Topics to be covered include: linear codes, cyclic codes, BCH and Reed-Solomon codes, classical cryptography, private-key (symmetric) and public-key (asymmetric) cryptography. Other topics may be included depending on the availability of time and the interest of the students.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
