2026-27 Term 1','No prerequisite/co-requisites needed.','No prerequisite/co-requisites needed.','本课程旨在探究语言与社会互动之间的关系，重点探讨语言在不同地区和社会情境下的使用。本课程将侧重考察年龄、性别、社会阶层、多语群体等社会人口变量以及语体、权力关系以及社会网络等社会语用变量在语言使用中的作用，以增强学生对语言变化及多样性的了解，并培养他们对跨文化差异的敏锐感知能力。','This course explores the interaction between language and social interactions. Topics focus on language use in different regional settings and different social contexts. Among the socio-demographic variables included for analysis are age, gender, social class and multilingual communities. Also included for analysis are socio-pragmatic factors such as speech register, power relations and social networks. Special attention is given to the appreciation of language variation and diversity and the development of intercultural sensitivity.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101084,'ENB3003','文体分析','','ENB - English Studies','3003','E',3.00,3000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','N/A','N/A','本科目将培养学生对学术和职业场合经常使用的各种体裁的分析能力。这类体裁的主要例子包括法律英语、科技英语、广告英语，商务英语、以及新闻和促销传播等用途的英语。除了了解这些体裁的特征外，学生还将学习如何通过应用专门用途英语（ESP）框架来分析特定语言学习者/用户群的语言需求，以便更充分了解不同语言使用环境对体裁特征的影响。','This course will enable students to analyze a range of different academic and professional genres in the English language. Key examples of such genres include various styles of academic communication including Legal English, Scientific English, English for advertising, business, journalism and promotional communication and so on. In addition to gaining a receptive understanding of such varieties, students will also learn how to analyze the language needs of particular groups of language learners/users through the application of an English for Specific Purposes (ESP) framework in order to diagnose the characteristics of particular genres in distinct contexts of use. In addition to written texts, students will also learn to analyze spoken discourses in formal and informal settings, including press conferences, media interviews, counseling sessions, and various types of social interactions.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101085,'ENB3004','跨文化交际','','ENB - English Studies','3004','E',3.00,3000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
