(101094,'ENB4201','西方法律制度导论','Introduction to Western Legal Systems','ENB - English Studies','4201','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在介绍西方两大法律体系：普通法系和大陆法系。重点阐述这两大法律体系的基本概念和原理，探讨它们在实践中的运行，并将会与中华人民共和国的法律制度进行比较。本课程旨在帮助学生理解法律以及法律本身在社会的作用，同时培养学生批判性地分析和评估中国正在进行的司法改革进程。','This course aims at introducing two major legal systems of the world, namely, civil law and common law. It examines the basic concepts and principles of the two systems, demonstrates how they function in practice, and compares them with the legal system of the People’s Republic of China (PRC). Upon successful completion of this course, students should be able to describe and explain some general ideas about the operation of law and its various social roles. This course also aims to equip students with the capacity to analyze and explain the PRC’s ongoing legal reform proposals, processes and procedures both accurately and critically.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
