2026-27 Term 1','Successful completion of all four courses of the ENL series or equivalence as recognized by HSS.','ENB4201','本科目旨在让学生了解和熟悉商法的基本概念和术语，以便为相关的法律科目的学习以及法律文书写作奠定基础。','This course aims to provide students with the essential concepts and terminology in commercial law, which will help them in learning other courses related to legal operation of business and writing legal documents. It helps students develop a conceptual structure which serves as the foundation for their studies of legal writing by enabling them to acquire a host of essential specialist terms.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101096,'ENB4203','法律文书写作','Writing for Legal Communications','ENB - English Studies','4203','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','None but successful completion of ENB4202 (Legal English: Concepts and Terminology in Commercial Law) may be beneficial.','','本科目旨在培養學生在法律相關情境中的英語寫作能力，並加深他們對「書面」與「口頭」法律溝通之差異的概念性理解。課程不僅把寫作視為一項技術技巧，更把其視為法律共同體中具有文化重要性的實踐：法律社群正是藉由書面文本來穩定、傳遞及爭議法律意義。
學生將學習分析與撰寫多種法律及法律相關文本（例如備忘錄、公司會議文件、正式商務與法律信函以及基礎法律意見書），並探討書面文本在不同法律文化中的角色，特別是普通法體系（高度依賴判例法和先例）與大陸法體系（高度依賴成文法典與法典化）如何透過書寫建構、保存與重新詮釋法律意義。除實際寫作與修改練習外，學生亦將培養對法律文本之意圖性及非預期意義的批判意識，了解法官、律師、政府官員及當事人等讀者如何解讀這些文本，以及書面法律溝通如何形塑法律專業身份與責任。','This course aims to develop students’ legal English writing skills in the context of law-related practices, and to deepen their conceptual understanding of the differences between legal writing and legal speaking as modes of communication with distinct conditions, requirements and impacts. Writing is treated not only as a technical skill, but also as a culturally important activity through which legal communities stabilise, transmit, and contest meaning over time.
   Students will learn to analyse and on occasions even draft a range of legal and law-related documents (including, for example, memoranda,  formal correspondence, and basic legal briefs). They will also examine the role of written texts in different legal cultures, focusing in particular on how common law systems (which rely heavily on case law and precedent) and civil law systems (which rely heavily on codes and statutes) construct, preserve and reinterpret legal meaning through writing. In addition to drafting and editing exercises, students will develop critical awareness of how written legal texts may convey both intended and unintended meanings, how readers such as judges, lawyers, officials and clients interpret those texts, and how written legal communication shapes professional identity and responsibility.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101097,'ENB4204','法律话语分析','','ENB - English Studies','4204','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','NA','NA','法律可以通过法律秩序的来源和实践衍生出的特殊使用规则来定义。这些规则晦涩、模糊，而且复杂。我们将首先概述法律话语，然后探讨其在各种短语和阶段中的各种功能、结构和语言特征。学生将深入了解法律语境中语言使用的互动规则和目标。','Law can be defined by special rules of use that derive from the sources and practices of a legal order that are widely known for their challenging obscurity, ambiguity, and complexity. We will start with a general overview of legal discourse, and then proceed to the various functional, structural, and linguistic features of such discourse in a variety of phrases and stages. Students will develop a thorough understanding of the interactional rules and goals of language use in the legal context.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101098,'ENB4205','英语法律案例','Cases in English Legal Wo r ld','ENB - English Studies','4205','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','部分西方国家沿用普通法系，其社会制度历经渐进式改革，也通过一系列具有里程碑意义的司法判例得以完善。在一些重要的司法判例中，宪法与法律规定的权利义务的内涵与影响得以诠释。本课程将带领学生研究一系列实践中的法律案例，探讨人们的日常生活如何与这些司法判例产生紧密联系。学生将以普通法系英语国家的重要判例为学习内容，探讨公民的权利义务如何通过判例重塑，进而完成教学目标。在司法实践中，部分国家采用判例法制度，在解释判例的过程中引发了种种争议，课程的后半部分将针对此类争议进行探讨。此外，本课程将用三周时间聚焦1946-1948年进行的东京审判及南京审判，审视因日本军队在亚洲对中国及其他国家的公民犯下战争罪行而启动的法律程序。

课程内容采取讲座与研讨相结合的形式，旨在帮助学生深刻理解经典判例中旧与新的司法解释各有怎样的特点，探讨经典判例重塑法律适用的规则与原则。

课程将鼓励学生就每项判决的合理性展开辩论，并探讨是否存在可以优化的部分，形成替代性方案。','Western societies with common law legal systems have been reformed, in progressive and other ways partly through a series of landmark law cases. Through a series of case studies of law in action, this course will examine how people’s everyday life may be closely related to landmark judicial decisions about the meaning and implications of legal and constitutional rights and obligations. This objective will be achieved through students discussing important landmark cases in the English-speaking common law world, which have reshaped aspects of citizens’ rights and obligations. The remainder will discuss different issues that arise from attempts to study interpretive issues relating to the judicial application of case-law precedents. In addition, cases that arose from war crimes committed in Asia by Japanese forces against Chinese and other Asian citizens will be addressed over three weeks in relation to the Tokyo war crimes trials 1946-1948 and follow up Nanjing war crimes tribunal criminal trials.

Through a mixture of lectures and tutorials, this course also aims to develop students’ understanding of the character of judicial interpretation and reinterpretation of landmark cases and how these have reshaped applicable legal rules and principles.

Students will be encouraged to debate on the merits of each decision and alternative possible decisions. 

The course will also describe and explain the vital role within landmark cases of unpredictable judicial activism and discretion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101099,'ENB4207','国际知识产权法','International Intellectual Property Law','ENB - English Studies','4207','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','None but it may be useful if students have passed ENB4201 (Introduction to Western Legal Systems).','','本课程从权利、责任和诉讼程序等方面向学生介绍国际知识产权法领域的独特沟通过程。旨在帮助学生在界定可执行权利和义务的相关公约和条约的法律实践中，熟悉国际知识产权活动中的言说性和沟通性。

对于拥有国际知识产权（IIP）的个人和组织来说，充分了解相关的法律问题和律法至关重要，有助于更有效地保护自己的知识产权资产。知识产权法是指在全球范围内管理知识产权（IP）的创造、保护、共享和使用的一整套法律。知识产权是指任何得到法律认可保护的创造、发明、创新或发现的客体；通过专利、版权、商标和商业秘密等产权许可保护其权益。

学生将学习国际知识产权问题的产生原因和后果，如纠纷、诉讼、名誉损害和经济损失。这些问题需要理解一般法律原则和相关沟通实践来解决。

学生将从法律条文性、字面性和比喻性表达的作用和挑战中，具体探讨国际知识产权法的多种语言层面，将其作为解读晦涩术语的重要沟通工具。','This basic-level course introduces students to the distinctive communication process of the world of IIPL law in terms of discourses about rights, responsibilities, and procedures of litigation. Its main objective is to help students become familiar with the discursive and communicative aspects of international IP activities related to the practical application of relevant conventions and treaties defining enforceable rights and obligations.

Individuals and organizations that own international Intellectual property rights (IIP) need to have a good understanding of related legal issues and laws so that they can protect their IP assets more effectively. IIP Law refers to a set of laws that govern the creation, protection, sharing, and use of intellectual property (IP) in the global context. IP refers to any creation, invention, innovation, or discovery legally recognised as subject to protection from copying. It gains protection through the issuance of different forms of rights, including patents, copyrights, trademarks, and trade secrets.

Students will study how IIP issues can arise that result in disputes, lawsuits, reputation damage, and financial loss addressed by general legal principles of law and associated communicative practices that need to be understood.

Students will specifically address various linguistic dimensions of IIPL, including the role and challenges of legalistic, literal, and figurative language expressions operating as communicative devices vital to the expression of a range of sometimes enigmatic and technical meanings.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101100,'ENB4208','商业与公司法','Commercial and Corporate Law','ENB - English Studies','4208','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','在现今商业社会，对相关的从业人员而言，对商业与公司法有基本认识是十分重要的。因此，本课程会介绍与商业买卖交易和商业组织相关的法律。主要内容包括：民法，财产，合同，商业组织（合伙企业，公司，并购等）和证券监管的法律规范。此课程将以中国现行的法律法规为主，同时参考美国或其他地区同类型的法律。学生们在学习中会逐步意识到东、西方在商业与公司法领域的法律原则与规范的相似性。另外，本课程还会简要介绍法律规则背后的经济理论，从而培养学生批判性思考能力。','A basic acquaintance with commercial and corporate law is instrumental to practitioners in the commercial world. This course introduces the laws relevant to the sale and distribution of goods, and business transactions, and business organizations. Topics include principles of private law, property, contract, business organizations (partnership, corporate, M&A, etc.), and securities regulations. We focus on the current legal rules in China but will refer to the laws in the U.S. and other jurisdictions occasionally when it provides a better angle. We will see, though, that commercial and corporate laws in the East and the West are similar, once capturing their essences.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101101,'ENB4301','句法学','','ENB - English Studies','4301','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Successful completion of all four courses of the ENL series or equivalence as recognized by HSS.','ENB3001 (English Linguistics)','本科目将介绍句法原理及语法理论背后的基本概念。科程探讨短语、从句、及句子的结构，以及短语和从句各部分之间的功能关系，重点介绍句法分析的基本原理与从实证中获得的论据。通过观察、描述和分析选自英语及不同语言的实例，学生将学会领悟人类语
言结构之美，增强科学观，获得处理句法问题的经验和解释与论证的能力。学生亦能参与实操练习和课程管理平台上的讨论,强化自学能力。','This course is an introduction to the principles of syntax and to the basic concepts underlying theories of grammar. It examines the structure of phrases, clauses and sentences, and the functional relationship between parts of phrases and clauses. It concentrates on the fundamentals of syntactic analysis and arguments drawn from empirical evidence. By focusing on observation, description and practical analysis of a wide range of phenomena from English and other language data accessible to them, students will learn to appreciate the beauty of human language structures, acquire explanatory and argumentative skills, develop science-forming capacities, and gain hands-on experience of tackling syntactic problems. They will also enhance self-learning abilities through practice exercises and via Blackboard discussion forum.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101102,'ENB4302','语义学','Semantics','ENB - English Studies','4302','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','none','none','n/a','This course is an introduction to semantics, the study of meaning in language. It aims to provide students with hands-on experience within the framework of formal semantics, whilst simultaneously providing a more general overview of the field and pointing out shortcomings of the formal approach. By the end of the course, students will be able to describe and explain a wide variety of semantic phenomena in English and other languages. Topics include: word meaning and concepts, lexical relations, compositional semantics and the syntax-semantics interface, generalized quantifiers, event semantics, tense and aspect, pronouns and dynamic semantics, presupposition, and theories of implicature.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101103,'ENB4303','语用学','','ENB - English Studies','4303','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程研究日常语言使用背后的假设，并探讨这些假设如何与话语的明确内容和话语上下文相互作用，以创造新的语意层次。我们研究的现象包括：指示、预设、暗示、言语行为、信息结构、谈话和轮流、话语关系和礼貌。我们将融合许多不同理论框架的见解，包括格莱斯和新格莱斯语用学、言语行为理论、关联理论、对话分析、礼貌理论和概率语用学。课程结束时，学生将对明确内容之外的意义要素有更好的认识和分析能力。','This course investigates the assumptions which lie behind the ordinary use of language, and explores how those assumptions interact with the explicit content of an utterance and the discourse context to create new levels of meaning. Phenomena which we will investigate include: deixis, presupposition, implicature, speech acts, information structure, conversation moves and turn-taking, discourse relations, and politeness. We will incorporate insights from a number of different theoretical frameworks, including Gricean and neo-Gricean pragmatics, speech act theory, relevance theory, conversation analysis, politeness theory, and probabilistic pragmatics. By the end of the course, students will have a much greater awareness of, and ability to analyse, elements of meaning beyond explicit content.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101104,'ENB4304','认知语言学','','ENB - English Studies','4304','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','Successful completion of all four courses of the ENL series or equivalence as recognized by HSS.','ENB3001 (English Linguistics)','n/a','This course provides an overview of cognitive linguistics, an approach to language which emphasizes general cognitive principles over domain-specific rules. The course covers cognitive approaches to meaning, such as frame semantics, conceptual metaphor theory, image schemas and conceptual blending; and cognitive approaches to grammar, such as Langacker’s Cognitive Grammar and Construction Grammar. The aim is to familiarize students with the key phenomena and theories of cognitive linguistics and equip them with tools for analyzing and comparing different languages. We will also see how cognitive tools can be applied beyond linguistics to areas such as literature, humor, journalism and advertising.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101105,'ENB4305','语料库语言学','','ENB - English Studies','4305','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101106,'ENB4306','自然语言处理导论','Introduction to Natural Language Processing','ENB - English Studies','4306','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','ENB4308 Computer Programming for Language Processing','None.','本課程是一門涉及人類語言和計算機科學交叉領域的入門課程。同學們將學習如何使用計算機完成與人類語言相關的任務，例如把中文翻譯成英文，過濾垃圾郵件，以及查找當天新聞中的主題等。同學們還將了解計算方法如何幫助語言學家解釋語言現象，包括自動區分詞義和短語結構。此外，同學們還將了解參數估計和推理等基于統計的自然語言處理方法。','Natural Language Processing addresses fundamental questions at the intersection of human languages and computer science. In this interdisciplinary introductory course, students will learn how computers can do useful things with human languages, such as translating from Chinese into English, filtering junk email, and finding the main topics in the day''s news. Students will also learn about how computational methods can help linguists explain language phenomena, including automatic discovery of different word senses and phrase structure. Students will learn about robust approaches to parameter estimation and inference as well.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101107,'ENB4307','社会计算概论','','ENB - English Studies','4307','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','NA','NA','本课程探讨数字科技如何彻底改变人们互动、协作与大规模知识生产的方式。课程前半部聚焦于群众协作、群众外包（crowdsourcing）以及数字轨迹资料的收集与分析，探讨社会计算的兴起及其伴随的伦理与方法论挑战。学生将实际操作文本、图像与网络分析工具，以理解线上行为中的模式。课程后半部则聚焦于大型语言模型（LLMs）与生成式人工智能的最新发展，探讨这些技术如何重塑研究实践、创造力、劳动模式与治理结构。通过实作与批判性反思，学生将获得理解与分析当代社会计算环境的实用技能与理论视角。','This course examines how digital technologies have transformed the way people interact, collaborate, and generate knowledge at scale. The first half of the course explores the rise of social computing through mass collaboration, crowdsourcing, and the collection of digital trace data across platforms—along with the ethical and methodological considerations they entail. Students will engage with tools for analyzing text, images, and networks to uncover patterns in online behavior. The second half turns to the recent shift driven by large language models (LLMs) and generative AI, examining how these technologies are reshaping research practices, creativity, labor, and governance. Through hands-on projects and critical reflection, students will gain both practical skills and conceptual insights into the evolving landscape of computational social inquiry.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101108,'ENB4308','面向语言处理的计算机程序设计','Computer Programming for Natural Language Processing','ENB - English Studies','4308','E',3.00,4000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
