2019-20 Summer','PHY1002 Physics Laboratory','','课程提供机会给学生动手操作能源和工程相关实验。所选实验主要目的是让学生学会制成太阳能电池和半导体发光二极管器件；了解燃料电池和生物燃料如何工作；以及学习如何用电子扫描显微镜、光谱仪、太阳能模拟器、半导体分析仪等进行测试。','This course provides hands-on practice for students in performing experiments in energy science and engineering. These experiments are selected to experience how semiconductor devices for energy conversion are made, such as photovoltaic cells and light emitting diodes; how fuel cell and bio diesel work; and to characterize those devices with scanning electron microscope (SEM), spectrometer, solar simulator, and semiconductor parameter analyzers etc..','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101111,'ENE3003','能源系统的热质传输','Heat and Mass Transfer for Energy Systems','ENE - Energy Engineering','3003','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2018-19 Term 2
2020-21 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1','Students must take MAT1001 or MAT1010 or MAT1011 first.','','本课程介绍传热与传质的基本原理，重点聚焦其在能源系统中的应用。内容涵盖三种基本传热方式的物理起源及其速率方程、热扩散方程、边界与初始条件、稳态与非稳态导热、数值解法、边界层方程、内部与外部强制对流、自然对流以及热辐射。课程特别强调能源工程中热工系统的分析与设计。学生将学习评估关键热工部件，如换热器、散热片以及涉及沸腾与冷凝的系统。课程还将介绍传质的基本概念，并探讨其与传热过程之间的类比关系。通过学习，学生将具备分析与设计能源相关热工系统的能力。','This course introduces the fundamental principles of heat and mass transfer, with a focus on applications in energy systems. Topics include the physical origins of the three heat transfer modes and their rate equations, the heat diffusion equation, boundary and initial conditions, steady-state and transient conduction, numerical methods, the boundary layer equation, external and internal forced convection, free convection, and thermal radiation. Emphasis is placed on the analysis and design of thermal systems central to energy engineering. Students will learn to evaluate key components such as heat exchangers, fins, and systems involving boiling and condensation. The fundamentals of mass transfer and its analogy to heat transport are also introduced. Students will develop the skills necessary to analyze and design energy-relevant thermal systems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101112,'ENE3004','光伏材料与器件基础','Fundamentals of Photovoltaic Materials and Devices','ENE - Energy Engineering','3004','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2017-18 Term 2
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','《光伏材料与器件基础》课程全面介绍了太阳能转换的科学原理与技术基础。课程首先概述了光伏系统以及太阳辐射的基本原理，随后深入讲解半导体物理基础以及光与半导体材料之间的相互作用，这些知识对于理解太阳能电池的工作机制至关重要。在此基础上，课程系统讲解了太阳能电池的结构、运行原理及其性能特点。课程内容涵盖第一代（晶体硅）、第二代（薄膜）以及第三代（新兴）太阳能电池技术，帮助学生全面了解太阳能电池的发展历程、关键材料与工艺技术，为高效太阳能解决方案的设计与应用打下坚实基础。','Fundamentals of Photovoltaic Materials and Devices provides a comprehensive introduction to the science and technology of solar energy conversion. The course begins with an overview of photovoltaic (PV) systems and the principles of solar radiation. Students will explore the foundational concepts of semiconductor physics and the interaction between light and semiconducting materials, which are critical for understanding how solar cells function. The course then delves into the structure, operation, and performance characteristics of photovoltaic devices, with detailed coverage of first-generation (crystalline silicon), second-generation (thin-film), and third-generation (emerging) solar cell technologies. Through this progression, students gain a solid understanding of both the physical principles and technological advancements that drive the development of efficient solar energy solutions.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101113,'ENE3005','电化学与电池基础','Fundamentals of Electrochemistry and Batteries','ENE - Energy Engineering','3005','E',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2018-19 Term 2
