2025-26 Term 2
2017-18 Summer
2019-20 Summer','CHM1001 General Chemistry','','课程介绍电化学基础知识及其在储能和供电方面的应用。电化学技术如锂离子电池、燃料电池等在电动汽车、电网储能等方面发挥着越来越重要的作用。
课程涵盖了电化学能量转换的理论知识部分，包括电化学、热力学、反应动力学和物质传输等现象；将介绍传统电池、液流电池、超级电容器等器件背后的工作原理；讨论这些电化学器件在电动汽车、电网储能等领域的应用情况；也会介绍产氢电解池及燃料电池。最后课程会讨论在新能源背景下的电化学能量转换技术的广泛意义。','This course introduces the fundamentals of electrochemistry and its application for storing energy and supplying electricity. Electrochemical technologies such as lithium-ion batteries and fuel cells are playing an increasingly important role in the energy sector as electric vehicles and grid energy storage become more widely used.

This course covers the theoretical aspects of Electrochemical Energy Conversion including electrochemistry, thermodynamics, reaction kinetics and transport phenomena. The principles behind different electrochemical devices (such as conventional batteries, flow batteries and supercapacitors) will be explained. The applications of electrochemical devices for electric vehicles and grid storage will be discussed. Electrolytic hydrogen production and fuel cells will also be introduced. Finally, the course will discuss the broader implications of Electrochemical Energy Conversion within the context of New Energy.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
