(101123,'ENE4007','能源经济学','Energy Economics','ENE - Energy Engineering','4007','E',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 2
2020-21 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','The applicants are expected to have a basic knowledge of calculus and linear algebra.','','本课程旨在向学生介绍与能源生产和消费相关的经济学原理。其主要目标是将经济学应用于能源市场、政府监管与政策、环境影响与保护，以及新技术等具体问题。
本课程将涵盖经济学的基本概念，包括效用与偏好、供给与需求函数、成本收益分析、市场均衡、项目评估与管理、外部性以及博弈论。此外，课程还将探讨多种与能源经济学相关的理论和实证主题，如能源需求、能源供应、能源定价、能源效率，以及能源与气候变化之间的关系等。
通过本课程，学生将深入理解能源、环境、经济与可持续发展之间的相互作用及潜在外部性。学生将掌握进行能源分析的技能，以评估政府政策和法规对能源需求和供应、价格、碳排放等方面的影响。','This course aims to provide students with an introduction to the economic principles related to energy production and consumption. The primary objective is to apply economic concepts to specific issues concerning energy markets, government regulations and policies, environmental impact and conservation, as well as emerging technologies.The course will cover fundamental concepts in economics, including utility and preferences, supply and demand functions, cost-benefit analysis, market equilibrium, project evaluation and management, externalities, and game theory. Additionally, a diverse range of theoretical and empirical topics will be explored, such as energy demand, energy supply, energy pricing, energy efficiency, and the relationship between energy and climate change.Through this course, students will gain an understanding of the interactions and potential externalities among energy, the environment, the economy, and sustainability. They will also develop skills in conducting energy analyses related to the effects of government policies and regulations on energy demand and supply, prices, carbon emissions, and more.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
