2026-27 Term 1','ECE2001 Basic Circuit Theory','','本课程旨在向理工科学生介绍电力电子技术的基础概念和技术。内容包括：变换器的拓扑，开关如何用半导体器件实现，变换器动态模型和控制，交流直流变换器，电网纹波，磁性器件和谐振电路等。','This course introduces to the students in the field of science and engineering on the fundamental concept and technology of power electronics technologies, including converter topologies, switch realization with semiconductor devices, converter dynamics and control, rectifier circuits, power system harmonics, magnetics components and  resonant converters.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101125,'ENE4009','电力系统稳定性与控制','Power System Stability and Control','ENE - Energy Engineering','4009','E',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','The course is targeted towards senior undergrads and graduate students.
(1)	Minimum requirement is familiarity with concepts in calculus and linear algebra, such as ordinary differential equations and matrix operations;
(2)	Basic knowledge of system & control is preferred;
(3)	Knowledge in basic programming (Matlab).

Students must take MAT2040 or MAT2041 or MAT2041A or MAT2042 before registering for this class.

Signal and system is recommended to be taken before registering for this class.','','随着全球电力系统的复杂度和规模不断增加，尤其是智能电网技术的出现以及可再生能源和分布式发电的广泛使用，电力系统的稳定性和动态性能已成为重要的研究课题。本课程旨在提供对于现代电力系统的动态和稳定性理论的深入理解，并介绍和实现不同的控制和机器学习算法来应对高可再生能源注入下电力系统稳定性和动态性能所面临的新挑战。','With the growing complexity and size of power systems throughout the world, stability and dynamic performance of power system components have become crucial subjects of study. This has been further triggered by the emergence of the smart grid technology, integrated with renewable energy and distributed generation. This course aims to provide an understanding of the advanced concepts of dynamics and stability theory as applied to modern power systems. Furthermore, different control and learning algorithms are presented and implemented to addressing new challenges on stability and dynamic performance in power systems with high renewables.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
