A course in electrical power systems (e.g., ENE3050 or ENE6001) is very helpful but not strictly required.','None.','本课程介绍智能电网的基本组成部分、智能电网与传统电网的主要区别、可再生能源发电在智能电网中的应用、分布式能源的控制以及储能技术。它帮助学生学习如何优化智能电网、提高电网的成本效益、效率以及可靠性。','This course introduces the fundamental components of smart grids, the main differences between smarts grid and traditional grids, application of renewable energy generation sources in smart grids, and control of distributed energy resources (DERs), and energy storage technologies used in power generation. It helps students learn how to optimize smart grids so that they are cost effective and efficient and how to increase grid reliability.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101134,'ENE6011','電力電子','','ENE - Energy Engineering','6011','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1','','','本课程旨在向理工科学生介绍电力电子技术的基础概念和技术。内容包括：变换器的拓扑，开关如何用半导体器件实现，变换器动态模型和控制，交流直流变换器，电网纹波，磁性器件和谐振电路等。','This course introduces to the students in the field of science and engineering on the fundamental concept and technology of power electronics technologies, including converter topologies, switch realization with semiconductor devices, converter dynamics and control, rectifier circuits, power system harmonics, magnetics components and  resonant converters.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101135,'ENE6012','能源經濟學','','ENE - Energy Engineering','6012','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Students should know basic energy concepts (types, conversion, efficiency, balance, units) and basic programming skills for data analysis.','None','本课程将从工程学视角深入介绍能源经济学，探讨经济学原理如何应用于能源系统、市场和政策。学生将在课程结束时掌握评估能源市场与政策的工具，理解能源决策中固有的经济权衡，并深入了解当前面临的挑战，如脱碳与能源获取问题。所获得的知识与技能将为学生未来从事能源政策、产业规划相关职业，或进一步在能源与环境经济学领域研究奠定基础。','This course provides an in-depth introduction to energy economics from an engineering perspective. It examines how economic principles apply to energy systems, markets, and policy. Students will leave the course with a toolkit for evaluating energy markets and policies, an appreciation of the economic trade-offs inherent in energy decisions, and insight into current challenges like decarbonization and energy access. The knowledge and skills gained will prepare students for careers or research in energy policy, industry planning, or further academic study in energy and environmental economics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
