(101138,'ENE6015','人工智能在能源系統中的應用','','ENE - Energy Engineering','6015','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Knowledge of basic energy concepts, linear algebra, calculus, and elementary probability theory. Python is recommended.','','本课程介绍人工智能的基本原理及其在能源系统中的最新进展。课程首先讲解机器学习、深度学习和基础模型的原理，强调数学直觉与数据驱动的推理方法。课程内容从两个互补视角展开：能源科学的人工智能与能源工程的人工智能。前者探讨人工智能如何加速能源相关领域的科学发现，例如材料设计、催化研究与实验数据分析；后者则关注人工智能在工程系统中的建模、预测、优化与控制，以实现稳定、高效和可持续的能源运行。通过课堂讲授、演示与学生展示，本课程旨在培养学生理解、评估与应用人工智能方法的能力，以推动可持续与智能化的能源发展。','This course introduces the fundamental concepts and recent advances of AI and their applications in energy systems. It begins with the principles of machine learning, deep learning, and foundation models, emphasizing mathematical intuition and data-driven reasoning. The course covers two complementary perspectives: AI for Energy Science and AI for Energy Engineering. The first explores how AI accelerates scientific discovery in energy-related domains such as materials development, catalysis, and experimental data interpretation. The second focuses on how AI enables modeling, forecasting, optimization, and control for engineering systems that support stable, efficient, and sustainable energy operation. Through lectures, demonstrations, and presentations, the course builds the ability to interpret, evaluate, and apply AI tools for sustainable and intelligent energy development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101139,'ENE6016','功率半導體器件基礎','','ENE - Energy Engineering','6016','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2023-24 Summer','Calculus, Ordinary differential equation','None.','功率半导体器件对于电力电子行业至关重要。它们在可再生能源等领域中发挥着至关重要的作用。本课程旨在介绍半导体基础知识和功率半导体器件的物理原理，包括功率MOSFET和结型场效应晶体管等。此外，还将涵盖功率半导体器件制造和在电动汽车等领域的主要应用。本课程面向材料与科学工程、物理学、电子与计算机工程、新能源科学与工程、数据科学等多个学科的学生。学生将掌握必备知识，为学术生涯或半导体相关行业的要求做好准备。','Power semiconductor devices are essential to the power electronics industry. They play a vital role in renewable energy conversions. This course is to introduce the fundamentals of semiconductors and the physics of power semiconductor devices, including power MOSFET and Junction Field-Effect Transistors. Moreover, device fabrications and major applications of power semiconductor devices such as electric vehicles (EV) will be covered. The course is catering for students in a broad discipline such as Materials and Science Engineering, Physics, Electrical and Computer Engineering, New Energy Science and Engineering, and Data Science. Students will master essential knowledge and prepare themselves in either advancing their academic career or meeting the requirements of semiconductor-related industries.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101140,'ENE6031','太陽能工程','','ENE - Energy Engineering','6031','E',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程系统讲授太阳能工程，重点在于实用系统设计与性能分析。课程内容涵盖太阳辐射与几何基础、太阳能热利用技术、光伏原理及聚光太阳能发电系统。学生将学习如何评估与设计太阳能集热器、光伏组件及完整能源系统，并掌握建模软件与经济分析工具的应用。课程特别关注系统集成、电网及混合能源应用，以及实际运行管理，帮助学生具备开发高效、经济型太阳能解决方案的技术能力，以推动全球能源转型。','This course offers a systematic study of solar energy engineering with a focus on practical system design and performance analysis. It covers the fundamentals of solar radiation and geometry, solar thermal technologies, photovoltaic principles, and concentrated solar power systems. Students will learn to evaluate and design solar collectors, PV modules, and complete energy systems, utilizing modeling software and economic analysis tools. Special emphasis is placed on system integration, grid and hybrid applications, and real-world operation, equipping participants with the technical expertise to develop efficient, cost-effective solar energy solutions to support the global energy transition.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
