2024-25 Summer','Successful completion of ENG1001/ENG1001M or equivalence.','There are no co-requisites for this course.','本课程旨在通过引导学生阅读和讨论不同的体裁英文材料来进一步培养他们的英语泛读技能。通过各种阅读活动，学生们将会对阅读的必要性以及如何进行阅读有更深刻的理解。本课程的评估包括书面作业、阅读考试（侧重阅读技能运用）、以及平时表现（其中包括学生在课堂上的表现以及线下参与BB论坛讨论的情况）。','This course is designed to further develop students’ extensive reading skills. This will be achieved through a focus on reading and discussion of a variety of genre and reading sources. Students will be introduced to activities during the semester to increase their understanding of how they read and why they read. Assessment for this course is a written assessment (due in Week 7), a reading examination requiring the students to show practical application of the skills covered in the course (Week 7) and a participation mark that includes student involvement in class and the on-line discussion forum.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
