2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','电脑游戏设计是融合了艺术，心理学，科学技术和商业的综合学科。这门选修课会介绍叙事艺术和电脑游戏中的互动叙事，尤其是角色塑造和叙事逻辑构建，以及新兴的艺术游戏类型。同时这门课还会涉及到在游戏制作团队中工作时与客户的沟通挑战与技巧。','To truly understand game design is to understand an incredibly complex web of creativity, psychology, art, technology, and business. This course is designed to introduce the basics of a broad artistic and conceptual understanding of interactive narrative in video games. Students are encouraged to set aside their preconceptions about video games, so that they can approach this subject with an open mind.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101197,'ENG3102','英语教学与评估初探','','ENG - English','3102','E',3.00,3000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2021-22 Summer
2022-23 Summer','Successful completion of all University-core English courses (any one the following three sets):
1. ENG1001; 1002;
2. ENG1001M; ENG1002M;
3. ENL1001;1003.','','ENG3102是为有意成为语言教师或攻读教育硕士的学生开设的选修课。本课程旨在帮助学生了解语言教学的基本理论和教学法，并把理论应用于课堂实践。学生会设计与听、说、读、写、语法和词汇教学相关的教学计划和活动，及把互动的体验式的教学活动用于自己的教学。此外，学生还将学习设计适切的评价活动和试题。完成本课程后，学生能掌握基本的教学法和教学理论，设计新的及借鉴已有的教材和评价活动，采用适合不同背景和需求的学生的教学法来教学。','ENG3102 intends to be an introductory course for those students who plan to take English language education as their profession or pursue a postgraduate study in education. The course is designed to equip students with basic understanding of key concepts and theories in second language education, and skills in putting such theories into classroom practices. Students will receive training in developing engaging course materials and classroom activities to teach listening, speaking, reading, writing, vocabulary, and grammar to second language learners through interactive classroom activities and experiential learning. They will also learn to integrate assessment into classroom teaching to enhance their students’ learning. At the end of the course, students will be able to develop and adapt teaching and assessment materials to meet the needs of their students in different contexts based on the language teaching theories they have studied.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101198,'ENG3103','语言与性别导论','','ENG - English','3103','E',3.00,3000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Summer
2023-24 Summer','Having taken ENG2001 (English for Academic Purposes II) or ENG2001M (English for Medical Professionals III) or ENL1004 (Reading and Writing for Language Majors II).','','本课程旨在训练学生对语言表达和性别之间的思辨力和分析力，探究性别概念和语言表达之间的双向影响。课程内容将学习相关的性别与语言研究的核心术语与理论，性别在语言表达差异上的主要研究分析方法。通过经典文献和案例分析帮助学生了解语言在塑造人类社会实践中的描述功能以及话语功能。','This course is to train students to think critically and analytically about the relation between linguistic communication and gender and sexuality. It examines how the concepts of gender and sexuality affect human communication and how communication constructs these concepts in return. Key terms and theories concerning gender and language studies will be introduced. Major methodological approaches to the analysis of gendered/sexualized representation in language will be discussed. Different topics and cultural contexts in which gendered/sexualized linguistic practices take place will also be addressed. Through studying classic literatures and cases, students are expected to gain insights of how language is not only descriptive but discursive in shaping our social practices.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101199,'ENL1001','英语视听说（一）','','ENL - English for Language Students','1001','E',3.00,1000,'English','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2020-21 Term 1
2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','NIL','NIL','本课程为人文社科学院计划修读语言类本科专业的学生所设计，旨在培养他们的在学术与日常生活所需的听说能力。课程将通过大量练习，培养学生有效参与小组讨论以及在公开场合运用清晰的逻辑思维进行演说的能力。此外，课程还将通过要求学生撰写听力学习日记的形式，培养学生独立的英语学习习惯，为日后学习打下坚实基础。本课程也会介绍一些英语语音与音韵方面的基础知识，以提高同学们的语音语调的认识与重视，从而让自己的口语水平达到一个新的高度。','This course is designed for students who plan to major in language programs (BA in Translation Studies and BA in English Studies) during their first year of studies. Lessons are designed towards enhancing students’ listening and speaking skills in the context of English for academic purposes, but likewise for application in real world situations. Students will receive training in how to engage effectively in discussion, with a consideration for the language and etiquette of group collaboration. Students will also analyze and practice the conventions involved in making presentations, so as to be able to express their ideas logically and coherently in public. In addition, this course aims to promote independent learning through encouraging students to keep self-study listening journals, a fundamental practice for their future studies. Finally, the course will introduce students to the basic principles of phonology and phonetics, a foundation upon which their English may reach a more advanced level of proficiency.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,'');

