2025-26 Term 2','FIN2010 & (MAT1010 or (MAT1001 or MAT1011) )','','金融学基础是现代金融经济学的入门课程。本课程强调推导和理解离散时间下的资产定价模型，和对于有风险的现金流的估值。本课程首先介绍消费者在不确定性条件下的行为选择，进而以此为基础来理解均衡资产定价理论和非套利资产定价理论：包括类似于
资本资产定价模型（CAPM） 的传统模型，套利定价理论(APT)，新阿罗-德布鲁理论，基于消费的资产定价模型(CCAPM)，和包括鞅定价方法。尽管本课程以理论为主，课程中也会讨论一些金融学中经典的实证puzzle。

本课程为金融学和经济学的二年级本科生而设计。掌握微积分，线性代数，概率论和统计学会极大的帮助学习本课程。','Foundation of Finance is an introduction to the foundations of modern financial economics. The focus throughout will be on the development and interpretation of discrete-time models of asset pricing, and the valuation of risky cash flow. After developing and studying the details of consumer decision-making under uncertainty, it uses that general framework as a basis for understanding both equilibrium and no-arbitrage theories of securities pricing, including traditional models like the capital asset pricing model (CAPM) and the arbitrage pricing theory (APT), newer Arrow-Debreu theories, and the consumption capital asset pricing model (CCAPM), and martingale pricing methods. The course is primarily theoretical. However, I may discuss some empirical puzzles in finance. This course is intended for second year undergraduate students in finance and economics. A working knowledge of calculus, linear algebra, and probability plus statistics is especially useful.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
