2018-19 Summer','ECO2121 or (STA2001 or STA2003)','MAT3010 (Calculus for Economic Analysis II)','本课程旨在通过结合金融案例，帮助学生打下坚实的概率论基础。强烈推荐所有希望将来学习更多统计、经济、金融的学生选修本课程，尤其是那些希望了解更多量化研究及实践的同学。','This is a finance elective course for students who wish to gain a solid understanding of probability. The course targets students who have taken ECO2121 but not STA2001. The course aims to fill the gap between ECO2121 and STA2001 with a focus in statistical application in finance. This course is highly recommended to all finance students, especially those who plan to learn more about the quantitative subjects in finance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101372,'FIN3030','货币银行学','Money and Banking','FIN - Finance','3030','F',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Financial Management and Basic Macroeconomics','No co-requisite.','本课程探讨金融机构与市场的理论与事实证据，考察银行和非银行金融机构如何运作、创造流动性及管理风险。学生将分析主要金融市场（货币、债券、股票和衍生品市场）、央行政策及中央银行数字货币(CBDC)和稳定币等创新。课程特别关注中国金融体系的独特制度结构和监管环境，为学生提供适用于全球和中国金融环境的实用见解。','This course examines the theory and empirical facts of financial institutions and markets, exploring how banks and non-bank entities operate, create liquidity, and manage risk. Students will analyze key financial markets (money, bond, equity, and derivatives), central banking policies, and innovations like CBDCs and stablecoins. The curriculum emphasizes China''s financial system, with its unique institutional structures and regulatory environment, providing students practical insights relevant to both global and Chinese financial contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
