2019-20 Summer','FIN2010','N/A','本课程全面介绍风险投资（VC）与私募股权（PE）这两大金融创新与另类投资的核心驱动力。学生将系统学习完整的投资生命周期，从项目发掘与估值开始，逐步深入交易结构设计、谈判协商，最终聚焦退出策略。课程内容涵盖高增长初创企业的估值方法（如现金流折现法、可比公司分析、实物期权理论），以及投资协议条款（如条款清单、分阶段注资、投资者与创业者的激励协调）等关键议题。此外，学生还将分析IPO、并购清算等退出方式对投资回报的影响。通过案例研究、真实条款清单解析及互动实践，学生将掌握评估初创企业、设计投资架构及驾驭VC/PE生态体系的实战能力。本课程适合有志于成为创业者、投资者或从事金融相关职业的学生，帮助他们在私人市场中精准识别机遇与风险，并深入理解风险投资与私募股权在塑造创新经济中的核心作用。','This course offers a comprehensive introduction to venture capital (VC) and private equity (PE) as critical drivers of financial innovation and alternative investment. Students will examine the full investment lifecycle, beginning with deal sourcing and valuation, moving through structuring and negotiation, and concluding with exit strategies. The curriculum covers essential topics such as valuation techniques for high-growth startups—including discounted cash flow (DCF), comparables, and real options—as well as the intricacies of contract design, such as term sheets, staged financing, and incentive alignment between investors and entrepreneurs. Additionally, students will explore exit strategies like IPOs, acquisitions, and liquidation, analyzing their impact on investment returns. Through a blend of case studies, real-world term sheets, and interactive exercises, students will develop practical skills to evaluate startups, structure investments, and navigate the VC/PE ecosystem.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
