2026-27 Term 1','ECO2011 Basic Microeconomics, ECO2021 Basic Macroeconomics and FIN2010 Financial Management','','本课程旨在建立对中国及世界金融市场中金融市场和基本制度知识的系统化认识。
本课程将介绍金融市场的基本原则，例如金融市场，金融机构，国际金融以及监管和中央银行的职能。通过课堂项目及演示，我们也会拓展到涵盖中国金融体系的特定特征。课程将会用到《中国金融体系手册》(by Amstad, Sun, Xiong) 中的部分内容。

如果时间允许，本课程也将涵盖以下内容：金融市场概述，货币的定义及其功能，利率和期限结构的确定，资产定价理论，金融机构（尤其是银行）经济学，金融监管，国际金融，例如汇率和全球资本流动，中央银行的作用和银行监管及金融危机的案例研究。

具体来说，我们也将通过讲座和课堂中的项目来讨论和研究中国金融市场的特点：加密货币与中国，中国的第三方平台，利率市场化，中国的储蓄率，中国的货币市场，中国的债券市场，中国股市，中国房地产市场，中国评级机构，中国衍生品市场，中国银行，中国影子银行，中国市场准入，人民币国际化，中国人民银行，中国监管机构等。','The objective of this course is to develop a general understanding of the financial markets and fundamental institutional knowledge about financial markets in China and the World.

The course provides an introduction to the principles of financial markets in general, such as the functions of financial markets, financial institutions, international finance as well as regulations and central banking. Through class projects and presentations, the general introduction is extended to cover specific features of the Chinese financial system. We will also use parts of The Handbook of the Chinese Financial Systems (by Amstad, Sun, Xiong).

If time permits, the course will cover the following topics: an overview of financial markets, the definition of money and its functions, the determination of interest rates and term structure, theories of asset pricing, the economics of financial institutions (particularly banks), financial regulations and supervisions, international finance such as the exchange rates and global capital flows, the role of central banks and banking regulations and case studies of financial crises,

In particular, the following special features of the Chinese financial markets will be discussed and studied through lectures and class projects: cryptocurrencies and China, third party platforms in China, interest rate liberalization, China’s saving rate, the Chinese money market, the Chinese bond market, the Chinese stock market, the Chinese housing market, Chinese rating agencies, the Chinese derivative market, Chinese banks, Shadow banking in China, Market access in China, RMB internationalization, the People’s Bank of China, regulators in China.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
