2026-27 Term 1','(FIN2010 or ECO2011)&(ECO2121 or STA2001 or STA2003 or STA2001H)','','本课程探讨心理学和金融学的交叉点，挑战金融市场理性决策的传统假设。学生将研究认知偏差（例如过度自信、损失厌恶、从众行为）和情绪因素如何影响投资者行为和市场结果','This course explores the intersection of psychology and finance, challenging traditional assumptions of rational decision-making in financial markets. Students will examine how cognitive biases (e.g., overconfidence, loss aversion, herd behavior) and emotional factors influence investor behavior and market outcomes.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
