2026-27 Term 1','FIN2010 Financial Management &(ECO2121 Basic Statistics or (STA2001 Probability and Statistics I or STA 2003 Honours Probability and Statistics I or  STA2001H Honours Probability and Statis) )','No co-requisite.','本课程向学生介绍公司的基本财务决策。它包括以下一些基本概念：财务决算方法；现金流预测和风险分析；债权和股权的融资和定价；资本成本等。此外，本课程还向学生介绍证券发行过程以及做财务规划和预测的相关技术。','This course introduces students to the fundamental financial issues of the corporation. It covers basic concepts of capital budgeting methods; cash flow forecasting and risk analysis; debt and equity sources of financing and valuation; and the cost of capital. It also introduces students to the process of security issuance and techniques of financial planning and forecasting.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101388,'FIN4220','股权估值','Equity V aluation','FIN - Finance','4220','F',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','FIN2010 Financial Management &    FIN2020 Foundation of Finance','No co-requisite.','本课程涵盖了企业决策中的基本问题。本课程的重点是开发一个实用框架，将各种企业决策和市场摩擦联系起来，以理解对企业价值的影响。我们还将介绍业务、实体和资产类别的估值技术和分析方法。重点将是从企业经理和业务实体的角度而不是从个别资产或投资组合分析的角度来确定价值。本课程为学生提供了一个互动和有启发性的学习环境。并且让学生初步理解和运用所学知识来分析公司股权价值。

本课程的学习目标是为学生提供工具和技术，使其能够（a）建立一个系统性框架来进行公司估值,（b）将企业财务理论与实践联系起来，并（c）应用估值技术来评估并购、资本预算等。所有这些工具和技术将对计划从事以下任何领域的职业生涯的学生大有裨益：金融分析、投资、资产管理。','This course covers fundamental questions in corporate decision makings and determinants of firm value. Ultimately, the class focuses on developing a practical framework to understand the implications on firm value. We will also introduce valuation techniques and analyses of businesses, entities, and asset classes. The class exposes students to an interactive and stimulating learning environment. In the same time, we introduce students to the art and science of value investing. The learning outcomes of this course are to equip students with tools and techniques to be able to (a) build a systematic framework to value any businesses, (b) link corporate finance theories to practice as well as (c) apply valuation techniques to evaluate M&A, capital budgeting etc.All of these tools and techniques will be useful for students intending to pursue professional careers in any of the areas of: financial analysis, investments, and asset management.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101389,'FIN4230','价值投资','V alue Investing','FIN - Finance','4230','F',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','FIN2010 Financial Management, ACT2111 Introductory Financial Accounting','No co-requisite.','本课程向学生介绍价值投资的原则、策略与实践。学生将学习如何分析企业、评估内在价值，并运用基本面分析识别被低估的证券。课程内容包括财务报表解读、关键估值指标、经济护城河、安全边际，以及市场心理的作用。通过课堂讲授、案例研究与实务练习，学生将探讨如何将价值投资理念应用于现实情境，如股票筛选、投资组合构建与风险管理。课程强调一种有纪律的长期投资方法，鼓励学生以企业主而非投机者的思维进行投资决策。','This course introduces students to the principles, strategies, and practices of value investing — an investment philosophy popularized by Benjamin Graham and Warren Buffett. Students will learn how to analyse businesses, evaluate intrinsic value, and identify undervalued securities using fundamental analysis. Topics include financial statement interpretation, key valuation metrics, economic moats, margin of safety, and the role of market psychology. Through lectures, case studies, and hands-on exercises, students will explore how to apply value investing concepts to real-world scenarios, including equity screening, portfolio construction, and risk management. The course
emphasizes a disciplined, long-term approach to investing, encouraging students to think like business owners rather than speculators.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
