2025-26 Term 2','Students are expected to have basic knowledge of probability theory and statistics, including familiarity with linear regression. They should also understand fundamental financial concepts such as the Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM), Dividend Discount Models (DDM), and basic derivative instruments. Prior experience with Excel is required. Experience with programming (e.g., Python or VBA) is beneficial but not mandatory.','','本课程专注于计算金融中的电子表格建模。旨在教授学生如何使用Excel和VBA构建模型并解决金融问题，包括投资组合分析、公司估值和期权定价。课程以实践为导向，通过大量的案例和实例帮助学生将所学技能应用于现实问题。此外，学生还将学习如何利用Python和人工智能来增强电子表格的功能。','This course focuses on spreadsheet modeling in computational finance. It is designed to teach students how to use Excel and VBA to build models and solve financial problems, including portfolio analysis, company valuation, and option pricing. The course is implementation-oriented, incorporating a wide range of examples and case studies to help students apply their skills to real-world problems. Additionally, students will learn how to leverage Python and AI to enhance spreadsheet functionality.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
