2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','在过去的几十年中，金融领域发展的基本假设是投资者和管理者普遍理性和证券的价格一般"有效"。 然而，近年来的传闻证据，理论研究和成功的范例实证研究表明，这种基本假设并不足以刻画的实际金融市场的各种功能。
本课程中，我们将运用心理学和更现实的设定，以引导和发展金融市场的替代理论。通过讲座、案例研究、讨论等方法，我们将会研究行为金融学如何作为传统模式的补充，解释投资者的交易模式以及资产定价、企业融资和各种金融市场实践中的行为。','Over the past several decades, the field of finance has developed a successful paradigm based on the notions that investors and managers were generally rational and the prices of securities were generally "efficient."  In recent years, however, anecdotal evidence as well as theoretical and empirical research has shown this paradigm to be insufficient to describe various features of actual financial markets.  In this course we will use psychology and more realistic settings to guide and develop alternative theories of financial markets. We will examine how the insights of behavioral finance complement the traditional paradigm and shed light on investors'' trading patterns, the behavior of asset prices, corporate finance, and various Wall Street institutions and practices.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
