2020-21 Summer','','','本课程在全球背景下为金融机构的基础构架和风险管理提供了总体概述，从风险管理的角度阐明了金融机构的决策思路，分析了金融机构面临的主要风险类型。该课程的主体内容涵盖了对多种金融风险的分析，如利率风险，信贷风险，资金流动性风险，外汇风险，市场风险等等，并介绍了用于衡量此类风险的相关技巧与分析方法。
各个课题之间的统一主题为将现代金融理论应用于金融机构尤其是商业银行的财务决策和管理过程中。主要涵盖了金融机构在市场监管和社会“企业责任”框架下所涉及的主要决策领域，同时采用定性和定量的方法计量和管理决策中相关风险。该课程为许多其他相关的金融课程奠定了重要基础。','This course provides an overview of the infrastructure and the financial risk management of financial institutions in a global context. The subject of decision-making in financial institutions is approached from a risk perspective, where main types of risk confronted by financial institutions are explained and analysed. The main topics covered are various financial risks, for example, interest rate risk, credit risk, liquidity risk, foreign exchange risk and market risk, etc. The application of relevant techniques and quantitative methods are introduced to measure and manage those risks.
The unifying theme in this course is the application of modern finance theory to the financial decision making and management of financial institutions, especially commercial banks. The course covers the major decision areas for financial institution management within the framework of a regulatory and "corporate responsible" environment. Overall, the course provides a cornerstone to many of the other courses offered in the Department of Finance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
