(101427,'FIN6136','估值分析','','FIN - Finance','6136','F',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','It is recommended that you have some prior knowledge of accounting principles such as financial statements, cash flows, and accounting methods. It is also desirable to have a certain level of statistical knowledge as we will be dealing with data and distributions throughout the course. A prior understanding of basic finance theory is helpful but not required.','No co-requisite.','本课程涵盖了企业决策中的基本问题。本课程的重点是开发一个实用框架，将各种企业决策和市场摩擦联系起来，以理解对企业价值的影响。我们还将介绍业务、实体和资产类别的估值技术和分析方法。本课程为学生提供了一个互动和有启发性的学习环境。并且让
学生初步理解和运用价值投资的理论和技巧来分析公司。

本课程的学习目标是为学生提供工具和技术，使其能够（a）建立一个系统性框架来进行公司估值,（b）将企业财务理论与实践联系起来，并（c）应用估值技术来评估并购、资本预算等。所有这些工具和技术将对计划从事以下任何领域的职业生涯的学生大有裨益：金融分析、投资、资产管理.','This course covers fundamental questions in corporate decision makings and determinants of firm value. Ultimately, the class focuses on developing a practical framework to understand the implications on firm value. We will also introduce valuation techniques and analyses of businesses, entities, and asset classes. The class exposes students to an interactive and stimulating learning environment. In the same time, we introduce students to the art and science of value investing. 

The learning outcomes of this course are to equip students with tools and techniques to be able to (a) build a systematic framework to value any businesses, (b) link corporate finance theories to practice as well as (c) apply valuation techniques to evaluate M&A, capital budgeting etc.

All of these tools and techniques will be useful for students intending to pursue professional careers in any of the areas of: financial analysis, investments, and asset management.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
