ECO6231 Econometrics I','N/A','本课程对公司金融展开深度探究，主要围绕该领域前沿发展议题展开教学，研究方向涵盖劳动金融学、环境、社会及治理（ESG），以及人工智能与公司金融的交叉融合领域。课程还将系统讲解双重差分（DID）、断点回归设计（RDD）等多种实证研究方法，并探讨此类方法在学术文献中的具体应用场景。课程以精心筛选的论文汇报与研讨为核心组织形式，旨在向学生介绍数个前沿活跃的研究方向，同时帮助学生掌握一套通用性较强的实证分析工具，支撑其自主开展学术研究。','This course provides an in-depth exploration of corporate finance, mainly
covering topics related to recent developments in the field, including
labor and finance, ESG, and the intersection of artificial intelligence with
corporate finance. We will also examine a variety of empirical
methodologies—such as difference-in-differences (DID) and regression
discontinuity designs (RDD)—and discuss how these approaches are
applied in the academic literature. The course is structured around
carefully curated paper presentations and discussions, with the aim of
introducing students to several vibrant research areas and equipping them
with a versatile empirical toolkit for pursuing their own research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
