(101444,'FIN6303','高级资产定价专题 （一）','','FIN - Finance','6303','F',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2019-20 Summer
2020-21 Summer','This course is intended for Ph.D. students. The students who are taking this course should have already taken econometrics, microeconomics and introductory financial economics. In particular, we will assume familiarity with large-sample theory for least-squares, generalized method of moments, and maximum likelihood estimation methods. Knowledge of continuous-time asset pricing models will be helpful, but not required. The numerical work for this class will be done in Matlab or Python. Prior experience working with Matlab/Python is not required, but willingness to learn Matlab/Python is.','','高级资产定价专题（一）','This course focuses on theoretical and empirical tools and results in macro-finance, asset pricing, and portfolio choice. The lectures will be a blend of asset pricing theory, econometric methods, and a critical review of empirical studies. With an emphasis on empirical and computational methodology, the course will broadly cover cross-sectional and time-series models in asset pricing; consumption-based models; intermediary asset pricing.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101445,'FIN6304','高级资产定价专题（二）','','FIN - Finance','6304','F',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Summer','FIN6201 Financial Economics
FIN 6303 Advanced Topics in Asset Pricing I

ECO6231 Econometrics I
ECO6233 Econometrics II','','本课程以实证金融与会计研究的设计与实现为核心，强调通过 WRDS 平台处理大规模财务与会计数据。课程将结合 Python、SAS 和 Stata，指导学生掌握从获取、清洗、匹配到分析数据的完整流程，涵盖 CRSP、Compustat、I/B/E/S、SDC 以及 SEC 披露等主要数据库。课程围绕三大经典实证案例——Fama–French 因子构建、事件研究以及盈余公告后漂移（PEAD）——展开，并配合因果识别策略、结构模型、机器学习及文本分析等前沿方法的讲解与应用。
通过本课程的学习，学生将能够：
•	熟练使用主流财务与会计数据库，并整合多源数据进行实证分析
•	运用标准与高级的实证方法研究资产定价与公司金融问题
•	批判性地评估研究设计，并为不同问题选择合适的实证策略
•	建立可复现的研究流程，用于实证研究的开展与展示
本课程面向金融与会计方向的二年级博士生，旨在为学生提供技术能力与研究视角，帮助其在顶级期刊的实证研究中做出高水平贡献。','This course provides a hands-on introduction to the design and implementation of empirical research in finance and accounting, with an emphasis on working with large-scale financial datasets through the WRDS platform. Using Python, SAS, and Stata, students will learn how to acquire, clean, link, and analyze data from key sources such as CRSP, Compustat, I/B/E/S, SDC, and SEC filings. The course is organized around three core empirical case studies—Fama–French factor construction, event studies, and post-earnings-announcement drift—complemented by sessions on identification strategies, structural models, machine learning applications, and textual analysis. By the end of the course, students will be able to:
•	Navigate major financial and accounting databases and integrate multiple sources for empirical analysis
•	Implement standard and advanced empirical methods in asset pricing and corporate finance
•	Critically evaluate research designs and identify appropriate empirical strategies for different questions
•	Develop reproducible workflows for conducting and presenting empirical research
The course is intended for second-year PhD students and aims to equip them with both the technical skills and research perspective needed to contribute to empirical debates in top-tier journals.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
