2026-27 Term 1','','','行为金融经济学','This course will introduce the modern advances in behavioral economics/finance and bounded rationality, including time inconsistent preferences and self-control, judgment under risk and uncertainty, imperfect knowledge and social emotions, and show the economic implications of those psychologically richer models. Meanwhile, it aims to answer the question why individuals are “biased”, and tend to find the link of some aspects of psychological regularities. Students are expected to read papers that attempt to synthesize existing models in psychology, economics, and finance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
