2025-26 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程探讨具有卓越科学、美学、教育以及旅游价值的自然遗产，并重点关注其成因。我们将检视联合国教科文组织世界地质公园和世界遗产名录中的一部分代表，介绍他们的地质与地貌特征。学生将全面洞察典型的地貌景观、构造景观、化石地等地学遗产。通过在自然美景中系统化地学习地球科学知识，同学们会更加理解“绿水青山就是金山银山”的含义，并且珍惜人与自然的和谐共生。','This course explores natural heritage sites of exceptional scientific, aesthetic, educational, and tourism value, with a focus on their formation processes. We will examine selected representatives from UNESCO Global Geoparks and World Heritage Sites, and introduce their geological and geomorphological features. Students will gain a comprehensive understanding of geoheritages including typical landscapes, structural landscapes, fossil sites and etc. Through the systematic study of Earth Science knowledge from the beautiful natural landscapes, students will be able to appreciate the concept of “Lucid Waters and Lush Mountains Are Invaluable Assets”, and cherish the harmonious coexistence between humanity and nature.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101519,'GEB2206','城市生态与保护','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2206','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2023-24 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程将研究城市环境中的生态系统，并探索城市作为生态系统的概念。课程将介绍在城市环境中特别相关或独特的基础生态学原理以及保护所面临的挑战，涵盖的主题包括气候变化、生物多样性保护、入侵物种的影响与管理、城市可持续发展、公共卫生与野生动物以及全球化的影响。课程内容分为三大部分：首先介绍城市生态学的基础知识，其次深入分析城市空间中发生的生态过程，最后探讨城市作为多方面生态系统的概念。课程还将重点研究这些主题在大湾区背景下的情况。','This course will examine the ecological systems within urban environments and explore the concept of cities as ecosystems. It will present fundamental ecological principles that are particularly relevant or distinctive in urban settings and the challenges related to conservation, covering topics such as climate change, biodiversity conservation, the effects and control of invasive species, urban sustainability, public health and wildlife, and the impact of globalization. The curriculum is organized into three primary sections: an introduction to the basics of urban ecology, an in-depth analysis of ecological processes occurring within urban spaces, and an exploration of cities as multifaceted ecosystems. This course will also provide a focused examination of these themes within the context of the Greater Bay area.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101520,'GEB2207','解码过去：考古学中的自然科学','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2207','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','该跨学科课程从地质学、生物学、材料科学以及环境科学的视角出发，深入探究人类起源与文明发展的深时历史。
本课程将探讨以下两个方面：其一，数百万年间环境与气候的变迁对人族演化及全球迁徙的塑造作用；其二，人类文化的实物证据研究。课程着重介绍用于重建过去的多种方法，涵盖放射性测年法至古DNA分析等，并剖析不同时代、不同地域的工具特征及同位素特点等物质证据，如何揭示早期人族向现代人类社会的转变进程。
学生将不仅了解我们对人类历史的认识，更将理解这些知识是如何获得的。','This interdisciplinary course explores the deep history of human origins and the development of civilization through the lens of geology, biology, material science and environmental science.
The course places emphasis on two aspects:
1) how environmental and climatic changes over millions of years shaped the evolution and global migration of the hominins; and 2) physical evidence of human culture.
The course underscores the methods used to reconstruct the past, from radiometric dating to ancient DNA analysis, and investigates how material evidence–including tools gathered across different time periods and regions as well as isotopic signatures–reveals the transition from early hominins to modern human societies.
Students will learn not only what we know about human history, but how we know it.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101521,'GEB2301','迷人之光：照亮未来的光技术','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2301','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
