2019-20 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','根据联合国一份报告的预测，到2050年世界上超过三分之二的人口将居住在城市。为应对城市化带来的诸如交通拥挤和环境污染的巨大挑战，许多城市采用智慧城市的概念和相关技术来优化城市运营。本课程旨在通过研究构建智慧城市的关键模块，即传感器，网络和数据分析和呈现技术，找出到底是什么让智慧城市变得智能。通过本课程的学习，学生将能够理解他们所居住的智慧城市是如何运作的。','According to a report of United Nations, more than two-thirds of the world’s population will live in cities by 2050. In response to the enormous challenges of urbanization such as traffic congestion and environmental pollution, many cities embrace the Smart City concept to optimize city operations. This course aims to find out "What made Smart City smart" by exploring the key building blocks of Smart City, which are sensors, networks, and data analysis/presentation technologies. By taking this course, students are expected to understand what actually lies behind smart cities they are residing in.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101533,'GEB2504','科技与社会','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2504','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 1
