2022-23 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程向学生介绍科学与技术研究(STS)，一个影响力日益增长的新兴领域。借鉴社会学、人类学、历史学与哲学等学科视角，STS着眼于分析科技与社会之间的关系与互动。通过学术文章、新闻报道、多媒体和课堂讨论，我们将关注社会政治语境如何影响科技的实践应用、及由此带来的社会影响。本课程旨在启发理工科背景的学生反思自己的科研经验，并思考研究带来的社会影响，以及帮助具有人文社科背景的学生培养关于科学知识的生产及其影响的批判性理解。','This course introduces students to science and technology studies (STS), an interdisciplinary field that examines the relationships between science, technology, and society through sociological, anthropological, historical, and philosophical lenses. Using a variety of resources—including academic articles, news reports, multimedia, and in-class discussions—we will explore how socio-political contexts shape scientific and technological practices and, in turn, how these practices influence society. The course is designed to inspire STEM students to critically reflect on their research experiences and consider the broader societal impacts of their work. At the same time, it equips humanities and social science students with tools to analyze the processes and implications of scientific knowledge production.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101534,'GEB2505','心灵、人脑与人工智能','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2505','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101535,'GEB2506','新技术与治理','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2506','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','大数据、人工智能、机器学习、区块链、智慧城市、聊天机器人等概念在我们日常生活中越来越普遍。这些新兴技术和技术进步构成了新的治理范式的基础，引导社区合作和提高公共服务质量。然而，它们同时也面对实践和道德上的困境，可能加剧潜在不公平和偏见。这些数字化和人工智能技术应用面临哪些挑战？我们如何在数字时代实现善治的目标？
这门课将通过研究全球案例讨论新技术如何产生有价值的信息资源, 以及如何将其整合到政府和机构政策和实践中。通过这门课程，学生们将对科技和人文之间的互动有更深入的了解，同时加深对未来数字技术和人工智能在治理中应用趋势的认识。','Big data, artificial intelligence, machine learning, blockchains, chatbots…  these concepts and technologies are becoming increasingly prevalent in our everyday lives. These emerging technologies and technological advancement form the basis of a new governance paradigm, guiding communities towards effective collaboration, elevating public service quality and increasing policy responsiveness. However, they also present new challenges to governance in both practical and ethical dimensions, sparking discussions on potential unfairness and biases. The key questions include, what are the challenges to these digital and AI technological applications? How can we achieve the goals of good governance in the digital era?
By examining global case studies, the course engages with important contemporary debates surrounding how new technologies produce data and information as valuable resources, and how they are integrated into governmental and institutional policies and practices. Through the course, students are expected to gain a better understanding of the interaction between technology and humanities while develop an awareness of future trends in the application of digital technology and artificial intelligence in governance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101536,'GEB2507','AI驱动的虚拟世界与严肃游戏在社会应用中的探索','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2507','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','GFN1000/GFH1000','GFN1000/GFH1000','我们生活在一个越来越被人工智能（AI）和沉浸式技术（如虚拟现实和增强现实）所塑造的世界中。这些技术正在改变我们与信息以及彼此之间的互动方式。随着人工智能和虚拟世界的不断发展，理解它们的应用和对社会的影响正成为21世纪的一项关键技能。本课程旨在为学生提供对AI驱动的虚拟环境和严肃游戏开发的基础性理解，并探索这些技术在社会背景中的应用。潜在应用领域包括社会模拟、福祉、教育、可持续性等。到课程结束时，学生将对虚拟环境开发的技术方面及其在社会背景中的实际应用有一个全面的了解。本课程面向所有大学生开放，无论他们是否具备人工智能、游戏开发或社会科学方面的先修知识。','We live in a world increasingly shaped by artificial intelligence (AI) and immersive technologies, Virtual Reality and Augmented Reality. These technologies are transforming how we interact with information and each other. As AI and virtual worlds continue to advance, understanding their applications and societal impacts is becoming a crucial skill for the 21st century. This course aims to provide students with a foundational understanding of AI-driven virtual environments and serious games development, and explore how these technologies can be applied in societal contexts. Examples of potential applications include social simulations, wellbeing, education, sustainability, and other domains. By the end of the course, students will have a broad understanding of both the technical aspects of virtual environment development and their practical applications in societal contexts. The course is designed to be accessible to all university students, regardless of their prior knowledge in AI, game development, or social sciences.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101537,'GEB2508','人工智能与社会','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2508','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程借鉴科学技术研究（STS）的理论视角，探讨人工智能与社会之间的交叉与互动。课程将考察社会政治进程如何塑造人工智能相关实践，同时分析新兴技术又如何反过来改变社会。相关主题包括人工智能系统所涉及的社会伦理议题、技术与宏观政治经济结构的交织关系，以及文化制度因素如何影响人工智能的应用、监管与治理。本课程旨在引导理工科学生批判性地反思自身的科研经验以及思考人工智能技术更广泛的社会影响，同时帮助人文社科学生在技术日新月异的时代掌握必备的人工智能素养。','This course draws on perspectives and theories from Science and Technology Studies (STS) to examine the interplay between AI and society. It investigates how socio-political contexts shape the development and deployment of AI technologies, and, in turn, how emerging AI technologies transform social practices, institutions, and everyday life. Key topics include the social and ethical issues surrounding AI systems, their entanglement with dominant political economy structures, and the ways cultural and institutional factors shape AI application, regulation, and governance. The course aims to foster critical reflection among STEM students on their research experiences and the broader societal implications of their work, while equipping humanities and social science students with foundational AI literacy necessary for engaging with a technologically evolving world.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101538,'GEB2509','AI赋能创意：从灵感到应用','','GEB - GE Areas: Area B','2509','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','人工智能的发展正在改变人类思考、创造以及解决现实世界问题的方式。本课程从跨学科视角探索人工智能、人类创造力、用户体验与数字创新之间的关系。课程旨在帮助不同学科背景的学生理解人工智能如何支持以人为本的问题解决，并应对现代社会中的现实挑战。课程结合理论基础与实践探索，引导学生学习人机交互、用户体验以及创造性思维等核心概念，从而更好地理解人类需求并发展创新理念。通过使用人工智能辅助工具进行实践，学生将探索新兴技术如何促进创造性表达，以及如何设计以用户为中心的解决方案。通过技术探索与批判性思考的结合，本课程培养学生采用迭代式、以人为本的方法开展创新实践的能力。','The rise of AI is transforming the way humans think, create, and solve real-world problems. This course explores the relationship between AI, human creativity, user experience, and digital innovation from an interdisciplinary perspective. It enables students from diverse backgrounds to understand how AI can support human-centered problem solving and address challenges in modern society. Combining theoretical foundations with practical exploration, students will examine key concepts in human-computer interaction, user experience, and creative thinking to better understand human needs and develop innovative ideas. Through hands-on practice with AI-assisted tools, students will explore how emerging technologies can facilitate creative expression and the design of user-centered solutions. By integrating technological exploration with critical reflection on human needs, the course fosters an iterative, human-centered approach to innovation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
