2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','我们如何了解过去？又如何依靠现有的记忆、文字和实物资料和过去对话？对于像1789年的法国大革命和1791年的海地革命这样复杂的历史事件，我们如何搜集、积累足够的信息以了解其全貌？如果只有零碎的叙事片段，我们又能否认知如万历十五年这样的所谓没有“重大标志性历史事件”的时期？
理解过去是复杂而又精细的工作。本课程将从两个方面介绍历史研究中的基本问题和方法。课程将聚焦历史学家眼中的“材料”，引导学生获取、整合和分析材料。同时，课程也将介绍历史学的基本理论与方法，讨论历史学家如何组织零散的材料，批判地分析材料并提出问题、构建起关于过去的叙事。本课程致力于培养学生对历史学研究的基本理解，并掌握基本的研究技巧。','How do we know about the past? How do we access the past through what is available today, be it memory, texts, or objects? How to collect information about complex historical events, the French Revolution of 1789 or the Haitian Revolution of 1791 for instance? Is it possible to summarise even an ‘eventless’ period with only a few coherent narratives, such as the year 1587 ce in the imperial court of the Ming Dynasty?
   Getting to know about the past is a complicated process that demands careful work. This course introduces the basic problems and methods of research into history. It will unfold around two keywords. First, it will discuss what historians call ‘sources’, as well as how to access them, evaluate them, and analyse them for research. Second, it will introduce the concept of ‘historiography’, namely the ways historians organise sources—often fragmented information—into narratives about the past through analyses.
   Through the course, students are expected to develop a basic understanding of historical research and its elementary skills. It will also help students cultivate their critical ability to draw arguments from limited sources, to efficiently interrogate the sources, and to understand the complexity of history.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101560,'GEC2109','中国历史之传统与变革','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2109','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','中国历史源远流长，既有深厚的传统，又不断变革与更新。本课程将以王朝为基本的分期，讲授从远古至二十一世纪的中国历史，着重介绍独特的政治制度及其变迁、以儒家为主兼容并包的思想体系和士人文化。本课以讲座为主，结合导修，在传递历史知识的同时，也将引领同学阅读一些基础性的一手历史文献，期增进对于中国历史和文化之了解。','Throughout China’s long history, a few themes went on stage repeatedly. These themes were reiterated, renewed, and reformed. This course provides an overview of Chinese history since antiquity. It introduces these recurring themes by the periods of dynasties. We highlight the continuities and permutations of political systems, the diverse strands of thought which Confucianism often dominated, and the culture of the gentry class. The course is organised primarily around lectures, which are joined by tutorials. It will train students to do the close reading of provided primary materials. Students are also expected to learn the key topics in the study of Chinese history.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101561,'GEC2110','西方历史之传统与变革','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2110','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程是对“西方”从远古到 20 世纪的社会、政治、经济、文化、宗教机构和信仰以及思想史的纵览和批判性研究。该课程主要通过讲演（Lecture）进行，不仅强调最重要的传统，而且强调西方历史中的连续性、习惯、仪式、变化和革命。涵盖的部分包括：古希腊、罗马共和国和帝国、文艺复兴、宗教改革和科学革命、法国大革命和拿破仑、工业化以及殖民化和去殖民化。

“西方历史之传统与变革”这门课也旨在教授历史学的基本技能，指导学生如何评估不同类型的主要来源和论点，对这些来源进行有效的总结，整合各种史料，并进行基础历史研究。在熟悉历史上了解过和没了解过的维度的同时，学生将获得专业历史学家用来解释和书写历史的基本技能。','This course is a survey and critical examination of the social, political, economic, cultural, religious, and intellectual history of “the West” from the Middle Ages to the 20th century. It willintroduce students to history as a dynamic and multifaced disciplinary area based on critically examining and interpreting source materials. It will challenge the idea of history as a monolithicdiscipline based on retaining dates and events. Instead, students will learn how historical questioning and methodologies have evolved through time depending on the problems and interests of different periods and cultures. This course will also clarify the connection between history and the present time and between history and other disciplines, such as philosophy, sociology, and economy. Finally, through the critical analysis of selected topics of the medieval, early modern, and modern periods, students will learn the essential skills of a professional historian, such as source analysis and interpretation and argument building.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101562,'GEC2111','粤港澳大湾区社会史','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2111','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
2021-22 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','粤港澳大湾区是当今中国乃至世界最重要的经济带之一。理解粤港澳大湾区明清以降社会变迁史尤为重要，因为该长时段历史不仅反映区域社会如何塑造国家形象与表达自身认同，也记录中国与世界的交互。本课程旨在从全球史与区域史视角，探讨明清以来粤港澳社会文化形成的历史过程，聚焦中西文化汇聚、地方与国家认同、政治制度、商业贸易、宗教节日、移民社会。','The Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Bay Area is one of the most important economic belts in China and the world. It is vital to understand the history of the Bay Area since the Ming and Qing Dynasties, because this long period of history not only reflects how the local society shaped its national image and expressed its own identity, but also records China''s interaction with the world. This course aims to explore the historical process of social and cultural developments of Guangdong, Hong Kong and Macao since the Ming and Qing Dynasties from perspectives of global history and regional history, focusing on the convergence of Sino-west cultures, local and national identity, political system, commerce and trade, religion and festivals, as well as migrant society.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101563,'GEC2112','滚滚红尘：近世中国的日常生活','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2112','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
