(101582,'GEC2403','医学人文学：医学与社会的跨学科方法','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2403','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程将向学生介绍医学人文这一交叉学科研究领域。该领域认为健康与疾病问题首先与人的生存体验相关，因此不应仅从生物医学角度进行研究。历史、哲学、艺术或文学能教会我们哪些关于健康、疾病、医疗实践和护理政策的知识？人文科学如何影响医疗实践，反之亦然？通过分析各类资料（小说、散文、艺术品、图画小说、电影），我们将探讨人文艺术如何提供思考健康、疾病、康复和护理的不同视角，这些视角与生物医学提出的视角相辅相成，而非相互对立。','This course will introduce students to the Medical Humanities, an interdisciplinary research field that acknowledges questions of health and illness as related in the first place to the experience of being human and hence deserving to be studied beyond a mere biomedical viewpoint. What can history, philosophy, art, or literature teach us about health, disease, practices, and care policies? How can humanities have an impact on medical practice and vice-versa? By analyzing various sources (novels, essays, artworks, graphic novels, movies), we will examine how arts and humanities offer different ways of thinking about health, illness, healing, and care, which are complementary rather than opposite to those proposed by biomedical science.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101583,'GEC2404','社交媒体与都市青年文化','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2404','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000
Exclusion: ENB3005 Language and Media','GFH1000/GFN1000','社交媒体正在改变都市人的交流、创作、生产、消费、和娱乐方式。它打破了城市的地理区隔，形成了新的数字社区。本课程旨在重点关注数字平台塑造城市背景下的年轻人以及被他们塑造的方式。它将批判性地研究社交媒体对流行文化、身份形成、社群建设、粉丝圈、名人经济和文化消费的影响。通过这种探索，学生们将考察如何将社交媒体研究与当代都市青年的生活实践联繫起来。该课程鼓励学生利用自己在社交媒体使用和青年文化参与中的个人经历与所学的概念和理论框架联繫起来，批判地思考年轻一代都市人的日常生活实践。','Social media is transforming the way of urbanites communication, creation, production, consumption and entertainment. It breaks down the geographical divisions of cities and creates new digital communities. Focusing on the ways in which digital platforms shape and are shaped by young people in urban contexts, this course will critically examine the impact of social media on pop culture, identity formation, community building, fandom, celebrity economy, and cultural consumption. Through this exploration, students will examine how social media research intersects with the lived experiences of contemporary urban youth. This course encourages students to connect their personal experiences in social media using and engagement with youth culture to the concepts and theoretical frameworks introduced, developing a critical thinking of the everyday practices of the younger urban generation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101584,'GEC2405','当代韩国文化与社会','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','2405','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2024-25 Summer','GFH1000 & GFN1000
All class materials will be in English, and no prior knowledge of the Korean language is required.','GFH1000 & GFN1000','韩国流行文化在全球范围内获得了广泛认可。"韩流"一词指的是韩国文化产品的广泛流行及其在地区和国际上的影响。本课程将通过分析韩国最具代表性的流行文化，全面探讨当代韩国文化和社会。通过阅读、观影、讨论和展示，学生将接触关键文化资源，更深入地理解塑造当今韩国社会的社会和文化背景。本课程将采用多模态批评性话语分析作为主要理论方法，该方法研究语言、图像、声音、动作和版式等多种模式如何共同创造意义，同时批判性地分析这些交流中所包含的社会、文化和权力关系。','Korean popular culture has gained significant global recognition. The term Hallyu refers to the widespread popularity of Korean cultural products and their regional and transnational influence. This course provides a comprehensive exploration of contemporary Korean culture and society by analyzing South Korea’s most representative forms of popular culture. Through readings, screenings, discussions, and presentations, students will engage with key cultural resources to develop a deeper understanding of the social and cultural contexts that shape South Korean society today. The main theoretical approach employed in this course will be multimodal critical discourse analysis, an approach to studying communication that examines how meaning is created through the interaction of multiple modes, such as language, images, sound, gesture, and layout, while also critically analyzing the social, cultural, and power relations embedded in these communications.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
