2024-25 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程将涉及1500年以后全球史，以各地区的贸易和文化交流为主线，关注移民、征服、外交，宗教，商业活动所引起的民族、商品、科技，思想等跨区域的互动，以及这些互动如何影响人们的观念和生活方式。','This course will study the long history of growing interconnection between various parts of the world since 1500. We will examine how such global connections involved not only trade of commodities but also transfer of peoples, cultures, ideas and technologies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101596,'GEC3111','《三国志》导读','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','3111','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','魏蜀吴三国鼎立的时期是中国历史上英雄辈出的传奇时代，而记录这一段历史的陈寿（233-297）《三国志》也在中国悠久的史书传统中具有重要地位，和《史记》《汉书》《后汉书》并称为“前四史”，并且为后世围绕三国主题层出不穷的历史小说和戏曲文艺提供了源源不绝的素材。直至当代，在影视、动漫、游戏等新型媒介领域仍然拥有可观的受众。本门课程分12次讲授和6次导修。讲授《魏书》中的《武帝纪》《文帝纪》《明帝纪》《后妃传》《何晏传》《华佗传》《乌丸传》《倭传》，《蜀书》中的《诸葛亮传》，以及《吴书》中的《吴主传》。议题涵盖高层政治的演进，婚姻与家庭中的女性，思想潮流的转变，健康与身体等生命知识，以及当时的周边世界。','The period of Three Kingdoms (189-280 C.E.) is widely regards as a period full of heroic and romantic legend. The history text of this period, the Records of the Three Kingdoms (三國志), composed by Chen Shou (233-297), is also regarded as the official and authoritative historical text. The Records of the Three Kingdoms, together with the Records of the Historian (史記), the History of Han (漢書) and the History of Later Han (後漢書), form the well-known “Early Four Histories” 前四史 of the Twenty-Four standard Histories (二十四史), and are considered as the best of the corpus. This course combines 12 lectures and 6 tutorials. Instructor will lead students to read 10 original texts in this book, which are Annals of Emperor Wu, Emperor Wen and Emperor Ming, Biographies of empresses and concubines, Biographies of He Yan, Hua Tuo, Wuwan, and Wo in the Book of Wei, Biography of Zhuge Liang in the Book of Shu, and Biography of the Lord of Wu in the Book of Wu. Introduction and discussion will focus on the changing of political power, the story of women, the turning of thoughts, the ideas of health and body, and the world in that time.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101597,'GEC3112','近代中国的法律、社会与家庭生活','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','3112','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程介绍近代中国法律、社会与家庭生活之间不断演变的互动关系。我们以近代国家如何管理家庭生活的诸多社会面向出发，旨在了解这种互动关系在整个中国晚清时期和二十世纪是如何演变的。我们将阅读从晚清到中华人民共和国时期的法律文献，了解法律结构的变化对中国家庭的影响。我们还将从社会身份的多重构造探讨被排除在儒法国家秩序之外的群体及其社会意义。从理论上讲，本课程与现代中国正在进行的关于民法实施的辩论呼应，将检视的问题包括：犯罪与惩罚在法律层面是如何随着时间的推移而变化的？法律在塑造社会对违反家庭规范和价值观的行为的态度方面发挥了什么作用？这门课还将反思中国法律制度与民间文化在传统与现代的转型过程中所产生的深远影响。','This course introduces the evolving interactions among law, society and family life in modern Chinese society. Focusing on social and state institutions governing family life, we aim to understand how did this interaction change throughout China’s Late Imperial period and into the Twentieth Century. Our readings of primary and secondary sources drawn from the Qing through the PRC periods will show the effect of structural legal change at the local level of the Chinese family. We will also explore the social meanings of exclusion from the Confucian family-lineage system along the dynamic process of identity making. Theoretically, the course engages with the ongoing debate over the exercise of civil law in modern China. How do the legal dimensions of crime and punishment change over time? What role does the law play in shaping social attitudes toward behaviours against family norms and values? The class also provides opportunities to reflect upon the overall evolution of China’s legal system and popular culture throughout this dynamic period.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
