(101599,'GEC3202','城市韧性：应对现代城市挑战','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','3202','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','现代化城市面临着日益多样的挑战，涵盖了从自然灾害到技术中断、流行病以及人为危机等各个方面。这门课程旨在鼓励学生积极思考和反思现代城市所面临的诸多挑战。它旨在为学习者提供识别、评估和解决城市环境面临的多方面挑战所需的知识和技术。在整个课程中，学生将探讨与管理城市风险和促进韧性相关的基本概念、理论、现实场景和实践方法。','Modern cities are encountering an increasingly diverse set of challenges, spanning from natural disasters to technological disruptions, pandemics, and man-made crises. This course is crafted to encourage students to actively contemplate and reflect upon the myriad challenges modern cities face. It equips learners with the knowledge and techniques necessary to recognize, evaluate, and address the multifaceted challenges that urban environments confront. Throughout the course, students will explore fundamental concepts, theories, real-life scenarios, and practical approaches related to managing urban risks and fostering resilience.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,'');

