(101610,'GEC3410','媒体技术与数字生活','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','3410','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2023-24 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','在数字化时代，媒体技术已成为我们日常生活中不可或缺的一部分，影响着我们的交流互动、个人身份认同乃至社会结构。本课程将深入探讨数字媒体技术与个人及当代社会之间的复杂关系。全面的课程设置将带领学生深入了解媒体技术发展、数字媒体产业动态以及这些技术对个人生活的影响。在课程中，学生将结合自己的媒体技术使用经历，探讨这些技术的伦理和社会影响。本课程将促进学生对媒体技术、社会和个人之间相互作用的批判性理解，也将使学生在未来更负责任、更高效地使用媒体技术。','In the digital age, media technologies have become an integral part of our daily lives, shaping our interactions, identities, and social structures. This course aims to offer an in-depth exploration of the complex relationship between digital media technologies, individuals, and contemporary society. Through a comprehensive curriculum, students will delve into the evolution of media technologies, the dynamics of the digital media industry, and the various ways in which these technologies influence every aspect of individuals’ lives. Throughout the course, students will be encouraged to reflect on their own experiences with media technologies and to consider the social and ethical implications of their use. Overall, this course will foster students’ critical understanding of the interplay between media technology, society, and individuals. Students will be equipped with the knowledge and skills necessary to navigate the digital landscape responsibly and effectively.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101611,'GEC3501','英语世界法律界改变社会的里程碑式法律案例','','GEC - GE Areas: Area C','3501','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000

English Major Students cannot select this course','西方普通法法律体系的社会已经通过一系列具有里程碑意义的法律案例，以渐进的方式和其他方式进行了改革。通过一系列法律案例，本课程将研究人们的日常生活如何与具有里程碑意义的司法裁决密切相关，这些裁决涉及法律和宪法权利和义务的含义和影响。这一目标将通过学生讨论英语普通法世界中具有里程碑意义的重要案例来实现，这些案例重塑了公民权利和义务的各个方面。其余部分将讨论在研究与判例的司法应用有关的解释问题时出现的不同问题。此外，还将在三周内讨论日本军队在亚洲对中国和其他亚洲公民犯下的战争罪行的案件，这些案件与 1946-1948 年东京战争罪行审判以及随后的南京战争罪行法庭刑事审判有关。

通过讲座和辅导相结合的方式，本课程还旨在培养学生对具有里程碑意义的案件的司法解释和重新解释的性质的理解，以及这些案件如何重塑适用的法律规则和原则。

鼓励学生就每项决定的优缺点和其他可能的决定进行辩论。

本课程还将描述和解释不可预测的司法能动性和自由裁量权在具有里程碑意义的案件中的重要作用。','Western societies with common law legal systems have been reformed, in progressive and other ways partly through a series of landmark law cases. Through a series of case studies of law in action, this course will examine how people’s everyday life may be closely related to landmark judicial decisions about the meaning and implications of legal and constitutional rights and obligations. This objective will be achieved through students discussing important landmark cases in the English-speaking common law world, which have reshaped aspects of citizens’ rights and obligations. The remainder will discuss different issues that arise from attempts to study interpretive issues relating to the judicial application of case-law precedents. In addition, cases that arose from war crimes committed in Asia by Japanese forces against Chinese and other Asian citizens will be addressed over three weeks in relation to the Tokyo war crimes trials 1946-1948 and follow up Nanjing war crimes tribunal criminal trials.

Through a mixture of lectures and tutorials, this course also aims to develop students’ understanding of the character of judicial interpretation and reinterpretation of landmark cases and how these have reshaped applicable legal rules and principles.

Students will be encouraged to debate on the merits of each decision and alternative possible decisions. 

The course will also describe and explain the vital role within landmark cases of unpredictable judicial activism and discretion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
