(101618,'GED2005','时间何往？时间、技术与人类处境','','GED - GE Areas: Area D','2005','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','为什么科技不断承诺为我们“节省时间”，我们却越来越觉得时间不够用？为什么有些人的生活像是在不断加速，而另一些人却长期处于等待之中：等待考试、工作、签证、医疗、家庭责任，或一个尚未到来的未来？当生命本身是有限的，我们又如何理解一个“有意义的人生”？本课程以时间为核心视角，引导学生重新思考自我、人类价值与现代生活处境。时间看似自然、客观、普遍，但本课程将带领学生理解时间如何作为一种社会、技术、文化、伦理与存在现象被建构。我们将考察钟表、日历、学校、工作场所、数字平台、家庭和医疗制度如何塑造人们关于加速、等待、节奏、照护、老去、死亡、记忆和希望的经验。课程将讨论以下核心问题：社会如何规定一个人何时算“太早”“太晚”“高效”“成功”“年轻”或“老去”？为什么速度常常被等同于进步？谁有资格慢下来，谁又不得不等待？不同文化与社群如何理解工作时间、家庭时间、神圣时间、老龄化、死亡与未来？学生将通过阅读、观察、时间日记、节奏分析、课堂讨论与批判写作，对时间经验进行学术分析。完成本课程后，学生将能够运用“时间”这一视角理解自我、人类价值与意义追寻。','Why do we always feel short of time, even when technologies promise to save it? Why do some people experience modern life as constant acceleration, while others spend much of life waiting—for exams, jobs, visas, medical care, family responsibilities, or uncertain futures? What does it mean to live meaningfully when time is limited?
This course takes time as a lens for examining the self, human values, and the modern condition. Although time appears natural and universal, students will learn to understand it as a social, technological, cultural, ethical, and existential phenomenon. We will explore how clocks, calendars, schools, workplaces, digital platforms, families, and medical institutions shape our experiences of speed, waiting, rhythm, care, aging, death, memory, and hope. Key questions include: How do temporal norms define who is
“early,” “late,” “productive,” “successful,” “young,” or “old”? Why speed is often treated as progress? Who has the privilege to slow down, and who is forced to wait? How do different cultures and communities understand work time, family time, sacred time, aging, death, and the future? Students will analyze temporal experience through readings, observation, temporal diaries, rhythm analysis, discussion, and critical writing. By the end of the course, students will be able to use time as a lens for understanding selfhood, human values, and the search for meaning.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
