2022-23 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程将探索形上学和心灵哲学的一些核心问题。课程可能涉及以下方面的理论，因授课教师而异：心灵（精神上）与身体（非精神上的物质实体）之间的联系和关系、意向性的话题、感质的问题、人工智能、个人身份认同、自由意志、因果关系、表象与实在、物体及其属性、空间和时间，以及终极实在的本质。','This course explores some central problems in metaphysics and philosophy of mind. Varying according to the instructor, the course may address theories on the connection and relationship between the mind (the mental) and the body (non-mental physical reality), the topic of intentionality, the question of qualia, artificial intelligence, personal identity, free will, causation, appearance and reality, objects and their properties, space and time, and the nature of ultimate reality.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101625,'GED2108','比较哲学','','GED - GE Areas: Area D','2108','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程以跨文化研究视角与方法，比较不同文化与地区哲学传统之异同，亦藉此深入研析其各自不同之特色。课堂讨论内容或将包含生命意义、社会价值、道德哲学、心灵哲学、伦理学、政治哲学、宇宙论、形上学、自然哲学、知识论、科学历史与哲学、美学、语言哲学、逻辑、神学等哲学议题。每学期课程聚焦点将视授课教师之专长与规划而定，阅读材料可能包含中英文哲学原典与研究文献。

该课程教授学生有关跨文化比较哲学中涉及的各种关键和棘手问题。要理解另一个文化，必须在某种程度上了解其哲学承诺，使得这些问题在我们当前的时代变得越来越重要。','A cross-cultural approach not only compares and contrasts divergent traditions of philosophy that have developed in different cultures and regions (like Western and Chinese philosophical traditions), but also reinforces and deepens our understanding of their respective features. Topics to be examined may include the meaning of life, social values, moral philosophy, philosophy of mind, ethics, political philosophy, cosmology, metaphysics, natural philosophy, epistemology, history and philosophy of science, aesthetics, philosophy of language, logic, theology, etc. The focus will vary according to the instructor, and reading materials may include both English and Chinese primary and secondary sources.

The course teaches students about various crucial and vexed issues involved in cross-cultural comparative philosophy. To understand another culture, one must to some extent understand its philosophical commitments, rendering these issues increasingly vital in our current age.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
