2025-26 Summer','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','伦理理论是关于行为对错、品性好坏的理论。它们指示我们如何做善人、道德的人。它们探讨关于快乐、幸福、生活意义和道德责任的问题。
规范伦理学领域讨论的一些基本理论包括：结果论、义务论、契约论和美德论。
“元”伦理学领域探讨关于道德事实、道德知识、道德语言的高阶问题，以及道德与心理学、进化之间的关系等。
（选题因教师而异。具体信息参见最新课程纲要。）','Double coded with PHI2110.
Ethical theories are theories about right and wrong action, good and bad moral character; they tell us about how we should live as good, moral people. They address questions concerning topics such as happiness, well-being, meaning in life and moral obligation.
Some of the basic and standard normative theories that might be discussed include consequentialism, deontological approaches, contract theories, and virtue ethics.
Topics may include “meta” questions about moral truths, moral knowledge, moral language, and the relation between morality, psychology, human evolution, etc.
(Topics may vary by instructor. See the up-to-date Course Outline for further information.)','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
