(101661,'GED3308','西方与中国科幻小说中「人」与「社会」议题','','GED - GE Areas: Area D','3308','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2018-19 Term 2
2021-22 Term 2
2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','本课程旨在研析西方与中国科幻小说如何再探、反思并重构
「人」与「社会」相关议题。阅读文本包括英国科幻经典玛丽‧雪莱《科学怪人》、赫伯特‧乔治‧韦尔斯《莫洛博士岛》与阿道斯
‧赫胥黎《美丽新世界》，以及美国「科幻小说黄金时代」作家艾萨克‧阿西莫夫的短篇小说；亦涵盖中国科幻重要作品，如晚清碧
荷馆主人《新纪元》、台湾张系国 《星云组曲》与大陆何夕《达尔
文陷阱》。课堂讨论将涉及神学、伦理学、动物与人类界线、心与身关系、人工智能、乌托邦／反乌托邦、现代化、殖民主义、中西
比较文化等议题。我们将从西方与中国之「文学传统」、「现代科学发展史」与「近代政治社会脉络」等面向，精读与剖析西方与中
国科幻作品中的蕴意与哲思。','This course aims to examine how the questions of “man” and “society” are revisited, rethought and reframed in science fiction. We will study both the classics of British science fiction—such as Mary Shelley’s Frankenstein, H.G. Wells’ The Island of Dr. Moreau and Aldous Huxley’s Brave New World—as well as the short stories by American authors of the “Golden Age of Science Fiction,” like Isaac Asimov. In addition, we will study the works of Chinese science fiction, like Biheguan Zhuren’s The New Era (Late-Qing China), Chang Shi-kuo’s Nebula Suite (Taiwan), and He Xi’s Darwin Trap (mainland China).
Class discussion concerns a wide range of topics, including but not limited to theology, ethics, the animal-human boundary, the mind-body relation, artificial intelligence, Utopia/Dystopia, modernization, colonialism, and Western-Chinese comparative culture. We will analyze the subtle meaning and philosophical significance of the above-mentioned texts of Western and Chinese science fiction in light of the traditions of Western and Chinese literatures, the historical developments of modern science and technology in Western and Eastern worlds, and the socio-historical backgrounds of modern Europe, American and China.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101662,'GED3309','“西方与中国诗歌中的「爱情」问题” ：从古典到现代”','','GED - GE Areas: Area D','3309','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2020-21 Term 1
2021-22 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2018-19 Summer
2021-22 Summer
2025-26 Summer','GFH1000/GFN 1000','GFH1000/GFN 1000','本课程探论西方与中国「情诗」中恋慕、欲望、想象、记
忆、自我、隐喻、转喻、寓意、诗学、美学、神话、宗教、社 会、政治、文化等议题。我们将阅读西方文学经典中的希罗马史诗与诗歌、中世纪歌谣、文艺复兴十四行诗、浪漫主义诗歌、现代主义诗歌，以及中国文学经典中的诗经、楚辞、唐宋诗、宋 词、明清诗词与现代诗。
课堂讨论西方从古典到现代的重要诗人，如荷马、莎芙、《圣经》中〈雅歌〉之佚名作者、弗吉尔、奥维德、但丁、佩脱拉
克、若弗雷·吕德尔、亨利希·封·莫龙根、莎士比亚、约翰·多恩、约翰·米尔顿、拜伦、波特莱尔、叶慈；亦研析中国古典诗词与现代诗大家，如《诗经》之佚名作者、屈原、宋玉、张籍、元稹、李商隐、杜牧、晏殊、欧阳修、柳永、晏几道、李清照、陆游、纳兰性德、徐志摩、周梦蝶、郑愁予与罗智成等。
本课程将引领学生，从「诗学传统」、「文学与思想风潮」与
「政治社会脉络」等面向，精读与剖析古今中西情诗中的艺术技巧与情思蕴意。讨论内容涉及希腊神话、基督教、宫廷式爱情、文艺复兴、浪漫主义、现代主义、民族主义、都市漫游者，以及中国神话、佛教、中国政治文化、香草美人传统、抒情传统、中
国现代性、传统与现代辨证、文化翻译、比较诗学。','Description (English)	This course on Western and Chinese poetry aims to complicate and problematize the question of “love” in relation to emotion, desire, imagination, memory, self, metaphor, metonym, allegory, poetics, aesthetics, mythology, religion, society, politics, culture, etc. We will read both Western canons of Greco-Roman epic and poetry, Medieval ballads, Renaissance sonnets, Romantic verses and Modernist poems as well as Chinese classics of The Book of Odes, Chu verses, Tang-Song poetry, Song lyrics, Ming-Qing poetry and lyrics, and Modern poetry.
Among the poets to be examined are Homer, Sappho, the anonymous poet of “Song of Songs” in The Bible, Virgil, Ovid, Dante, Jaufre Rudel, Heinrich von Morungen, Petrarch, Shakespeare, John Donne, John Milton, Lord Byron, Charles Baudelaire and W.B. Yeats in Western literature from the ancient to the modern, and the anonymous poets of Book of Odes, Qu Yuan, Song Yu, Zhang Ji, Yuan Zhen, Li Shangyin, Du Mu, Yan Shu, Ouyang Xiu, Liu Yong, Yan Jidao, Li Qingzhao, Lu You, Nalan Xingde, Xu Zhimo, Zhou Mengdie, Zheng Chouyu, Luo Zhicheng et cetera in classical and modern Chinese literature.
This course guides students to analyze the nuanced significance and artistic skills of Western and Chinese “love poems” in light of the traditions of Western and Chinese poetics, the trends of literature and thought in authors’ time, and/or the socio-political contexts of texts.
The class discussion concerns a wide range of topics, including but not

	limited to Greek mythology, Christianity, courtly love, Renaissance, Romanticism, modernism, nationalism, Flâneur, Chinese mythology, Buddhism, Chinese political culture, the allegorical tradition of “fragrant grass and beautiful woman,” the lyrical tradition, Chinese modernity, the dialectic between the modern and the traditional,
cultural translation, comparative poetics, etc.”','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101663,'GED3310','究天人之际：《史记》导读','','GED - GE Areas: Area D','3310','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','GFH1000/GFN1000','GFH1000/GFN1000','《史记》是中国历史学最具代表性的著作之一，在文学史上也有重要地位，被称为“史家之绝唱，无韵之离骚”。本课程将选取《史记》中具有代表性的篇章进行解读，领略史学名著的风采，思考天人之际，古今之变。','"Records of the Grand Historian" is one of the most representative works in Chinese historiography and also holds an important position in the history of literature, acclaimed as "the unparalleled song of historians, Lisao without rhyme." This course will select representative chapters from "Records of the Grand Historian" for interpretation, allowing students to appreciate the charm of this renowned historical masterpiece.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
