(101675,'GEW2002','重新思考大湾区的环境保护','','GEW - GE Areas: Wide Area','2002','G',2.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Summer','GFH/GFN','GFH/GFN','环境保护是现代文明中不可或缺的部分，这在自然资源稀缺或缺乏可能为人类生活和社会可持续发展带来限制时尤其重要。环境保护无疑是人类的共同目标，但地区环境可能会增加人类与环境之间的复杂性，从而为知识追求创造多重视角。以香港和深圳为例，这两个毗邻的城市位于珠江三角洲东部，共同享受着大量的海洋资源。然而，这两个城市都受到过去几十年经济快速转型和工业发展所带来的污染的严重影响。针对这全球性问题，各方在科学研究、国际政策落实和加强地方治理等方面作出了共同努力，为环境修复带来曙光。在取得了进步的同时，环境问题仍然是人类当前的巨大挑战。
本课程旨在让学生重新审视当前在国家、地域、地区甚至个人层面的环境保护策略，引导他们研究大湾区的一些普遍环境问题、社会普遍做法和一些具有代表性的跨区域合作。本课程将先概述环境科学的一般原则，然后聚焦于水资源的问题、沿海地区污染的管理和相关的区域合作。香港中文大学及香港中文大学(深圳)的学生将会参与实地考察及科学考察，以亲身体验所在城市及邻近地区的现状。导修讨论和写作将为学生提供学习机会，从政策和合作带来的可能性、意义和由此产生的问题等方面，反思和评估大湾区当前环境政策和区域间合作的实施情况。这课程将为学生提供一个跨越人类经验和知识的平台，让他们交流思想，提出新的想法，并作为本地居民和全球公民踏上通往更美好世界的旅程。','Environmental protection has long been indispensable in modern civilization, especially where scarcity or lack of natural resources might hamper the sustainable development of human life and society. While environmental protection is undoubtedly a common goal for the humanity, local contexts might add to the intricacy between humans and their environment, and thus create multiple perspectives for intellectual pursuits. Hong Kong and Shenzhen, for example, two neighbouring cities situated in the east of the Pearl River Delta, share and enjoy a lot of marine resources. However, both cities have been heavily impacted by pollutions arising from rapid economic transformations and industrial developments in the last few decades. For such a global issue, concerted efforts have been made in scientific studies, implementation of international policies and strengthening of local governance to bring restoration into light. Progress has been made but environmental issues remain a huge challenge to mankind.

This course aims to engage students in re-examining some current strategies for environmental protection at national, regional, local and even personal levels, by guiding them to study selected prevailing environmental problems, general practices of the society and some representative interregional collaborations in the Greater Bay Area. While general principles in environmental science will be outlined, this course will focus on water resources, management of pollution in the coastal area and regional collaborations upon the issues. To gain first-hand experience in the present situation of their own city and neighbouring regions, students from CUHK and CUHK(SZ) will participate in field trips and scientific investigations. Tutorial discussions and writing assignments are learning opportunities for students to reflect on and evaluate the implementation of current environmental policies and interregional collaborations in the Greater Bay Area, in terms of the possibilities those policies and collaborations have brought, their significance and issues arising from them. The course serves as a platform across human experience and knowledge for students to exchange ideas, propose new ideas and embark on the journey to a better world as local inhabitants and global citizens.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101676,'GEW2101','岭南：历史与社会','','GEW - GE Areas: Wide Area','2101','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Summer','','','“岭南”地处五岭以南，五岭为东西走向的山脉，是华南和华中之间重要的地理和文化分界线，在近代中国的历史发展中具有重要地位。本课程旨在以长时段的历史视野，从商业、移民、知识与文化等主题，回溯岭南地区与国家、世界五百年的交织流转，从人文历史深度视角认识岭南、增进认同。本课程同时结合文献与田野，在文字中发现历史之余，参访文博机构、乡村社庙、社团企业等。通过走出书斋、走进社会的方式，帮助学生加深对岭南地区人文历史的理解和感悟。
香港中文大学与香港中文大学（深圳）学生将共同修读本课程，有助于粤港两地学生的文化交流，增进相互理解。课程考核方式包括个人和小组作业。','Lingnan is located in the south of the Five Ridges, the mountain areas running from east to west that serve as a clear geographical and cultural demarcation between South and Central China. Lingnan plays a significant role in the historical development of Modern China. This course aims to overview 500 years of interweaving between Lingnan region, state and the world from the perspective of business, migration, knowledge and culture in the long-term history to understand Lingnan and enhance cultural recognition. At the same time, this course combines archival studies and fieldtrips. Besides discovering history through archive material, we will also visit museums, villages, temples, communities, and enterprises. Through contact with cultural and historical sites, students can deepen their understanding and perception of the social and cultural history of Lingnan.
Students from the Chinese University of Hong Kong (CUHK) and the Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen (CUHKSZ) will jointly enroll in this course to promote cultural exchange and enhance mutual understanding. The course assessment methods will consist of individual assignments and group projects.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101677,'GEW2201','从天际到大地：大湾区的自然篇章','','GEW - GE Areas: Wide Area','2201','G',3.00,2000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Summer','Not for students from CUHK × CUHK(SZ) Aerospace Science and Earth Informatics Double Major Programme','GFH1000/GFN1000','地球是错综复杂而脆弱的系统。地球上相邻区域地形的差异，可能导致两地不同的气候、地质和海洋资源。粤港澳大湾区位于中国南部沿海地区，属于受东亚季候风影响的亚热带气候。香港和深圳是大湾区内的两个城市，地理位置上接壤于珠江口东部。然而，在海洋、地质和大气系统的相互作用下，塑造了两地各自的气候模式，也影响了自然资源的供应和分布。
这科目以大湾区的地球物理学、宏观气候和海洋科学，以及香港和深圳地区的微气候为主题，旨在让学生探索地球和天空的相互联系，透过跨学科学习，反思人类对自然环境的责任。课程涵盖的主题包括气象物理学、基础地质学、天文学与气候的关联、人类活动对气候的长期影响以及自然灾害。此外，课程还包括参观气象机构、地质公园和高科技海洋公司。','The Earth is an intricate and fragile system. Slight differences in the terrain of neighbouring areas on the Earth can lead to variations in climate, geology, and marine resources. The Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area (GBA) is located in the southern coastal area of China and has a subtropical climate influenced by the East Asian Monsoon. Two cities of the GBA, Hong Kong and Shenzhen, are geographically neighbours on the eastern side of the Pearl River estuary. Still, the interaction of oceanic, geologic, and atmospheric systems has shaped their local weather patterns and influenced the availability and distribution of natural resources.
This course highlights the geophysics, macroclimate, and marine science of the GBA and the microclimate in Hong Kong’s and Shenzhen’s areas. It aims to engage students in exploring the interconnectedness of the Earth and the sky through interdisciplinary subjects, thereby reflecting on human responsibilities to the natural environment. The topics to be covered include the physics of meteorology, the principles of geology, astronomical relevance to climate, human influence on long-term climate, and natural disasters. Additionally, the course includes visiting meteorological institutions, geoparks, and high-tech marine companies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101678,'GEW3401','当代中国实地调研','','GEW - GE Areas: Wide Area','3401','G',3.00,3000,'GenEd','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Summer','','','与传统的教师主导的讲座理论课程不同，本课程是以学生为中心的实践类课程，以中国社会情境下的实地调研作为学习活动的主轴，致力于重建学生的学习主体性与真实社会现象之关系。课程将会介绍实地调研的核心概念、经典中国社会实地调查研究、中国社会实地调研的相关研究技术、中文实地调研报告的撰写等内容，但本课程更重要的内容是指导学生浸入中国社会亲自开展实地调研，激发学生对社会现象的关注度和好奇心，通过基于事实的调查、分析和讨论理解隐藏于现象背后的社会矛盾，并据此尝试提出具有可行性的解决方案。尽管实地调研是社会学相关领域的重要研究技术，但该技术作为现代科学素养的重要组成部分，通过强调“回到事实本身”批判性地反思任何形式的本本主义和权威主义，对来自各专业的学生都颇有意义。除此之外，本课程帮助学生了解当代中国，培养和塑造当代大学生“知中国，服务中国”的理想信念和公民意识。因此，修读完本课程可自动豁免修读国情教育“CEC1020毛泽东思想和中国特色社会主义理论体系概论（实践部分）”。','This course, unlike traditional teacher-led lectures focused on theory, is a hands-on, student-centered class that emphasizes conducting field research within Chinese societies as its core learning approach. It seeks to reconnect students’ learning experiences with social realities. The course covers essential concepts of field research, classic field research of Chinese societies, research techniques for conducting fieldwork in Chinese societies, and guidelines for writing Chinese field research reports, etc. However, the most crucial part of this course involves guiding students to engage directly with Chinese communities for their research projects. This immersion aims to spark students’ curiosity about social phenomena, encourage them in investigating, analyzing and discussing underlying social contradictions, and then attempt to develop viable solutions. While field research is primarily associated with sociology-related fields, it is an integral aspect of modern scientific literacy that promotes critical thinking against dogmatism and authoritarianism by advocating for “returning to the facts themselves,” holding significant meaning for students from all majors. Furthermore, this course cultivates students’ understanding of Chinese societies and enhances their belief and civic awareness of “knowing China and serving China.” Thus, students who completed this course could be exempted from taking the course “CEC1020 Group Projects on ‘Thoughts of Modern China’” in Civic Education.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
