2025-26 Summer','Nil.','Nil.','自远古开始，人类就对大自然充满好奇。古希腊哲人开展了以理性探索物理世界和生命世界的传统，为现代科学奠定了基础。科学家发现了物理定律、生命法则，甚至控制生命的方法。这些发现，促使我们重新审视人类如何理解自己的理解。在地球的这一边，中国哲人却发展了一套与西方不同的世界观。比较中西世界观，将会加深我们对两者的认识。
本科让同学认识并比较中西科学发展，了解人类如何探索、认识，以至改变大自然，认识及比较科学在西方和中国的发展，并反思人在大自然中的地位。老师将从多部影响深远的典籍中，选辑一系列篇章，供学员阅读和分析。这些篇章涉及哲学、科学及其历史等不同范畴。本科著重提升同学读原典、论原典的能力。同学须发挥批判思维，就指定篇章进行深入讨论，并提交论文，表述个人反思和分析的结果。','Humans have long been curious about Nature. In the West, ancient Greek philosophers took the lead in exploring the physical world and the world of life with reason and hence laid the foundations of modern science. Scientists discovered physical laws, the laws governing life and even ways of controlling life. Implications of these discoveries force the humankind to re-assess their understanding of human understanding. On the oriental side of the globe, Chinese philosophers developed a different view of Nature. The comparison between Western and Chinese views will contribute to our understanding of both.
This course invites students to explore how the humankind investigated, understood and changed Nature, to study and compare the development of science in Western and Chinese cultures, and to reflect on the humans’ place in Nature. Students will be required to read, discuss and write about a wide range of texts in philosophy, science and its history. Reading materials will be selected from influential literatures. Emphasis will be placed on students’ capacity to respond critically to these texts in written as well as oral presentations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101681,'GGE5001','学术论文写作和演讲','','GGE - Academic Writing & Presentatio','5001','G',2.00,5000,'GenEd','Distinction/Pass/Failure','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'','','本课程专为研究型研究生设计。它旨在培养研究生们在国际学术背景下的学术英语写作技巧和沟通能力。它将提供撰写学位论文及学术研究论文的实践技能。它还将提供研讨会以提高沟通和公开演讲技巧。课程包括研讨式工作坊、作业布置和期末考试。通过本课程的学习，研究生们将会掌握撰写学术论文及学术交流的专业技能。','This course is specifically designed for research postgraduate students. It aims to develop academic English writing skills and communication competence in international academic context. It will provide hands-on practice in writing an academic research thesis and research paper. It will also provide workshops to improve the communication and public speaking skills. There are workshops, assignments and a final examination. At the end of this course, postgraduate students are expected to master professional skills of writing academic proposals, thesis and scientific papers, and presenting research results.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101682,'GGE5001A','学术论文写作和演讲','','GGE - Academic Writing & Presentatio','5001A','G',2.00,5000,'GenEd','Distinction/Pass/Failure','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程专为人文社科专业博士生设计，旨在拓展其学术写作与演讲方面的英语应用能力。学生通过学习本课程内容将提升他们英语写作的有效性、批判性思维能力及口语沟通能力。本课程通过真实写作案例分析、深入讲解和及时有效的练习来帮助学生提升他们运用英语开展学术写作演讲的能力与信心，掌握学术写作规范与遵守学术道德，并引导学生借助GenAI等新技术进一步提升他们与之相关的能力和表现。期待选修本课学生能够积极参与各项相关教学活动，本课成绩评分采用: “优秀“、“及格”和 “不及格”三档评分机制。','This course is specifically designed for doctoral students in humanities and social science to equip them with advanced English language skills required to accomplish a variety of tasks in their academic writing and presentation, with a focus on enhancing skills in writing effectiveness, critical thinking, and oral communication within the academic contexts. Through engaging activities, working with authentic academic texts, and completing assignments, students will gain confidence and ease in their using the English language, participating in discussions, producing well-structured research papers and giving presentations; at the same time, they will improve their knowledge and awareness of accepted practice and norms in academic writing, especially in dealing with ethical issues involved in such activities. The course will also help students to embrace the use of new technologies and applications of Gen AI as appropriate tools to improve their related competence and skills. Students are expected to participate actively and contribute their input in the activities throughout the course and their performance is assessment through a Distinction/Pass/Fail scheme as stated in this plan.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
