2025-26 Term 2','IELTS 6.5 or above.','TOEFL not less than 79 (iBT) or not less than 550 (PBT)','本课程专为研究型研究生设计。它旨在培养研究生们在国际学术背景下的学术英语写作技巧和沟通能力。它将提供撰写学位论文及学术研究论文的实践技能。它还将提供研讨会以提高沟通和公开演讲技巧。课程包括研讨式工作坊、作业布置和期末考试。通过本课程的学习，研究生们将会掌握撰写学术论文及学术交流的专业技能。','This course is specifically designed for reseach postgraduate students. It aims to develop academic English writing skills and communication competence in international academic context. It will provide hands-on practice in writing an academic research thesis and research paper. It will also provide workshops to improve the communication and public speaking skills. There are workshops, assignments and a final examination. At the end of this course, postgraduate students are expected to master professional skills of writing academic proposals, thesis and scientific papers, and presenting research results.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101686,'GGE5001G','学术论文写作和演讲','','GGE - Academic Writing & Presentatio','5001G','G',2.00,5000,'GenEd','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','人工智能学院','人工智能学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程专为人工智能学院博士生设计，旨在拓展其学术写作与演讲方面的英语应用能力。学生通过学习本课程内容将提升他们英语写作的有效性、批判性思维能力及口语沟通能力。本课程通过真实写作案例分析、深入讲解和及时有效的练习来帮助学生提升他们运用英语开展学术写作演讲的能力与信心，掌握学术写作规范与遵守学术道德，并引导学生借助GenAI等新技术进一步提升他们与之相关的能力和表现。期待选修本课学生能够积极参与各项相关教学活动，本课成绩评分采用:  “及格”/ “不及格”二档评分机制。','This course is specifically designed for research postgraduate students. It aims to develop students’ academic English writing skills and communication competence in international academic context. It will provide hands-on skills or workshops in writing an academic research thesis and paper, and help students prepare and edit it. It will also provide workshops to improve the communication and public speaking skills.. Upon completion of this course, students are expected to master professional skills of writing academic proposals, thesis and scientific papers, and presenting research results.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101687,'GLB1010','全球化与中国','Globalization and China','GLB - Global Studies','1010','G',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','NA','','本课程旨在勾勒当代全球化的主要特征，以及新时期中国在这一背景下面临的挑战与机遇。在全球治理中，除国家这一传统参与者外，各类非国家行为体也发挥了重要作用。本课程还将聚焦当代中国在多个具体议题上面临的困境，并探讨可能的解决路径与未来发展方向。','This course examines the key features of contemporary globalization and the challenges and opportunities China faces in this context. In global governance, alongside states as traditional participants, various non-state actors play significant roles. The course also focuses on the dilemmas China encounters in specific issues and explores potential solutions and future directions.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101688,'GLB1020','社会科学研究方法','','GLB - Global Studies','1020','G',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','None','None','这门课程旨在向学生介绍量化社会科学研究的基本原则，并着重于政治学方面的应用。在大数据时代，掌握数据分析和因果推断方面的技能对更好理解复杂的社会现象并为企业，政府和其他组织所面临的问题寻找解决方案是至关重要的。在这门课程中，学生首先会学习如何提出研究问题，如何构建理论和可验证的假设，以及如何测量他们所感兴趣的变量。与此同时，学生会获得统计方面的基础知识并学习统计软件的基本操作。在课程结束时，希望学生可以更好的阅读并批判政治学方面的最新研究并掌握开展社会科学研究所需要的基础技能。','This course introduces students to the basic principles of conducting quantitative social science research, with an emphasis on political science. In the age of big data, it is essential to acquire skills in causal inference and data analysis to better understand complicated social phenomena and find solutions to problems faced by firms, governments, and other organizations. Students will first learn how to formulate research questions, how to develop theories and testable hypotheses, and how to measure variables they are interested in. Meanwhile, students will acquire basic skills in statistics and become familiar with statistical software. By the end of this course, the hope is that students can better read and criticize the latest research in political science and start to develop their research projects.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101689,'GLB1101','全球研究综述','','GLB - Global Studies','1101','G',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101690,'GLB1102','国际关系导论','','GLB - Global Studies','1102','G',3.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101691,'GLB2010','世界政治学概论','Introduction to Wo rld Politics','GLB - Global Studies','2010','G',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','N/A','','为什么国家会发动战争？在什么情况下国家更可能签署贸易协定或发动贸易战？应对气候变化、移民或恐怖主义等全球性挑战的最佳途径是什么？领导人是如何做出外交政策决策的？本课程旨在向学生介绍世界政治中的关键问题，以及用于分析其成因的主要方法。课程还将讨论各种理论和政策在实践中的应用案例。学生将实践把理论应用到不同情境中，包括撰写政策备忘录和进行真实世界事件的模拟。','Why do countries go to war? When are countries more likely to sign trade agreements or start a trade war? What is the best approach to manage global challenges such as climate change, migration, or terrorism? How do leaders make foreign policy decisions? This course will introduce you to key issues in world politics and the main analytical approaches used to evaluate their causes. We will also discuss a wide variety of examples of how theories and policies work. You will then apply theory in a variety of scenarios, including writing policy memos and performing simulations of real-world events.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101692,'GLB2020','国际组织概论','Introduction to International Organization','GLB - Global Studies','2020','G',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','There are no formal prerequisites for this course. However, students are expected to have a general interest in international politics and basic familiarity with key concepts in global affairs. The course is designed as an intermediate-level module and serves as a foundation for further study in international relations, international law, and global governance.
The course is taught through a combination of lectures and seminars (1.5 hours each per week). Students are expected to participate actively in discussions and complete two written assignments during the semester:
Essay 1 (25%) – a short analytical paper.
Essay 2 (50%) – a longer research paper (4000 words).
Regular participation and independent reading are essential for successful completion of the course.','','本课程旨在引导学生系统地了解国际组织及其在全球治理中的作用。课程将探讨国家、区域组织及跨国行为体如何通过建立和运用国际制度来应对和平、发展、人权与环境保护等全球性议题。内容涵盖国际组织的主要理论与制度设计原则，并结合联合国、世界银行、非洲联盟、东盟、欧盟等全球与区域组织的实例进行分析。课程特别关注多元化的制度模式以及非西方合作理念在当代多边体系中的崛起。通过学习，学生将掌握分析国际组织结构、功能与演变的理论工具，为进一步研究全球政治与国际治理奠定坚实基础。','This course introduces students to the study of international organisations and their role in shaping global governance. It examines how states, regional bodies, and transnational actors create and use international institutions to address collective problems such as peace, development, human rights, and environmental protection. The course explores major theories of institutional design and legitimacy and applies them to global and regional organisations including the United Nations, World Bank, African Union, ASEAN, the European Union, and others. Emphasis is placed on the growing diversity of institutional models and the emergence of non-Western approaches to multilateral cooperation. The course aims to provide students with analytical tools to understand and evaluate the structure, function, and evolution of international organisations in a rapidly changing world.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101693,'GLB2030','外交学导论','Introduction to Diplomacy','GLB - Global Studies','2030','G',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','The course is taught through a combination of lectures and seminars (1.5 hours each per week). Students are expected to participate actively in discussions and complete all required readings before class. Each student will deliver at least two short presentations during the term and take part in one structured simulation exercise replicating a multilateral negotiation.
Students are also required to submit two essays:
Essay 1 (2,000 words), due at the end of Week 6, analysing a specific diplomatic episode or negotiation.
Essay 2 (4,000 words), due 15 May, developing a research-based argument on a topic related to diplomacy, negotiation, or institutional reform.
Prior knowledge of international relations is helpful but not required. The course is designed to introduce students to both the conceptual foundations and practical applications of diplomacy in global affairs.','','本课程旨在引导学生系统地学习外交学的基本理论与实践，了解其作为国际关系核心制度的历史演变与当代发展。课程内容涵盖从传统国家间外交到数字外交、经济外交与人道外交等新兴议题，探讨谈判、代表与沟通等核心概念及其在全球化背景下的延伸。课程结合西方与非西方视角，重点分析亚洲、非洲及拉丁美洲等地区在重塑外交规范与制度中的作用。通过讲授、案例分析与模拟谈判活动，学生将掌握理解和评估外交实践的分析框架与实务技能，培养在多元文化与政治环境中思考国际事务的能力。','This course introduces students to the study and practice of diplomacy as a central institution of international relations. It examines the evolution of diplomatic thought and practice from classical traditions to contemporary global challenges, including digital, economic, and humanitarian diplomacy. Students will explore key concepts such as negotiation, representation, and communication, alongside emerging themes like networked diplomacy and non-state actors. The course integrates Western and non-Western perspectives, highlighting how regions such as Asia, Africa, and Latin America contribute to reshaping diplomatic norms and institutions. Through lectures, case studies, and a simulation exercise, students will develop analytical and practical skills for understanding how diplomacy operates across different cultural and political contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101694,'GLB2040','比较政治导论','* Introduction to Comparative Politics','GLB - Global Studies','2040','G',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程介绍国内政治制度、过程及其结果的研究，涵盖国际间及各国内部的情况。课程将调查比较政治领域中的关键概念及主要理论贡献，为学生提供对政治系统变异及其重要性的基础理解。学生将学习比较方法，作为分析政治与社会现象的框架，并透过当代及历史案例进行探讨。通过这种比较视角，学生将深入了解政治系统如何影响治理及公民生活，并为他们在全球化背景下批判性思考政治动态做好准备。','This course is an introduction to the study of domestic political institutions, processes, and outcomes across and within countries. It surveys key concepts and major theoretical contributions in the field of comparative politics, offering students a foundational understanding of how political systems vary and why these variations matter. Students are introduced to the comparative method as a framework for analyzing political and social phenomena, using both contemporary and historical cases from around the world. Through this comparative lens, students will gain insights into how political systems shape governance and citizens'' lives, preparing them to think critically about political dynamics in a globalized world.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
