(101696,'GLB3010','中国与世界经济','China and World Economy','GLB - Global Studies','3010','G',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程从国际政治经济学（IPE）的视角，系统分析中国在全球经济中的崛起、互动与影响。我们将超越“中国威胁论”与“中国机遇论”的二元叙事，探究中国的国内制度、政治优先项及经济挑战如何塑造其对外经济政策，以及全球经济如何反过来制约和影响中国的国内发展。
通过案例研究——从贸易战、亚洲投资发展银行、“一带一路” 到科技竞争，学生将掌握分析中国经济外交的核心工具，理解中国与世界经济互动的多层逻辑。','This course employs the perspective of International Political Economy (IPE) to systematically analyze China''s rise, interactions, and influence within the global economy. Moving beyond the binary narratives of the “China Threat Theory” and “China Opportunity Theory,” we will investigate how China''s domestic institutions, political priorities, and economic challenges shape its foreign economic policies, and conversely, how the global economy constrains and influences China''s internal development.
Through case studies – ranging from trade wars, the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank, the Belt and Road Initiative, to technological competition – students will acquire the core analytical tools for examining China’s economic statecraft and comprehend the multi-layered logic underlying its interactions with the world economy.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101697,'GLB3020','国际政治经济','Global Political Economy','GLB - Global Studies','3020','G',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程探讨政治与经济如何塑造当今世界，重点分析政府与市场之间的互动，以及权力与财富的关系。学生将学习国际政治经济学（IPE）的主要理论和争论，并研究全球经济体系自二战以来的演变——从冷战后的全球化浪潮到当今的地缘经济竞争、贸易保护主义和数字时代的新挑战。

课程涵盖国际贸易、金融危机、全球产业链重组等核心议题，同时讨论国内政治（如社会不平等、民粹主义）如何影响全球经济格局。','This course examines the political forces shaping today’s global economy, exploring the dynamic relationship between governments and markets, as well as the interplay of power and wealth. Students will learn key theories and debates in international political economy (IPE) and analyze how the global economic system has evolved—from the post-World War II era to today’s era of geopolitical competition, economic nationalism, and digital globalization.

The course covers major issues such as trade wars, financial crises, global supply chains, and the growing influence of emerging economies. It also explores how domestic politics (like inequality and populism) interact with global economic trends.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
