(101699,'GLB3060','全球变化与环境可持续性','Global Change and Environmental Sustainability','GLB - Global Studies','3060','G',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','Nil.','Nil.','這門課程旨在讓學生全面了解全球環境變化與可持續發展之間複雜的相互作用。課程將探討多種全球變化的驅動因素，特別是氣候變化，以及它們對自然和人類系統的相互影響。重點將從科學、社會、經濟和政治層面考察環境的可持續性，以及實現可持續未來所面臨的挑戰和機遇。

在整個課程中，學生將批判性地評估全球變化對生態系統、自然資源和人類福祉的影響，並探討科學、技術、政策和集體行動在應對這些重要環境問題中的角色。課程將利用來自世界各地的案例研究來說明不同環境挑戰及其促進可持續發展的策略。','This course is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of the complex interplay between global environmental change and the pursuit of sustainability. The course will explore various drivers of global change particularly climate change and their interconnected impacts on natural and human systems. Emphasis will be placed on examining the scientific, societal, economic, and political dimensions of environmental sustainability, and the challenges and opportunities associated with achieving a sustainable future.

Throughout the course, students will critically evaluate the implications of global change on ecosystems, natural resources, and human well-being, and explore the role of science, technology, policy, and collective action in addressing these critical issues. Case studies from around the world will be utilized to illustrate the diverse environmental challenges and the strategies employed to promote sustainability in different contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101700,'GLB3103','国际关系时事专题','','GLB - Global Studies','3103','G',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','','','国际关系理论：现实主义，自由主义，经济结构主义
作为政治科学和社会科学的子领域之一，国际关系学研究民族国家、非政府组织和个人在政治、经济和安全等领域的跨国界互动。它试图解释民族国家、非政府组织和个人跨国界的合作与冲突的原因和方式。本课程旨在从理论角度向学生介绍这一子领域。它将会帮助学生熟悉国际关系研究中最有影响力和最流行的理论及方法。它还将帮助学生了解一些跨越国界的当代重大现实问题。','International Relations Theories: Realism, Liberalism, and Economic Structuralism
International Relations, as one of the subfields of Political Science in particular and Social Sciences in general, studies the interaction of nation-states, non-governmental organizations, and individuals across national borders in the areas, such as politics, economics, and security.  It explains why and how nation-states, non-governmental organizations, and individuals across national borders cooperate and conflict.  This course is designed to introduce this subfield to students from a theoretical perspective.  It will familiarize students with the most influential and popular theoretical approaches to the study of international relations.  It will also help students understand some major contemporary issues across national borders.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
