2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','The course is taught in three-hour sessions. Every student should complete four presentations: three during the class, one at the end of the semester (a presentation for the term paper), 10-15 minutes each. Also, students are requested to write a term paper for the class (about 3000-4000 words) on a topic relating to the class subject he/she chooses.','None','本课程旨在为学生系统介绍国际关系研究的核心概念、主要理论流派及其在当代世界政治中的实践应用，并重点引导学生从理论视角深入理解21世纪最重要的双边关系之一：中美关系。课程通过聚焦不同理论观点之间的辩论与对话，探讨这些理论如何帮助理解中美之间冲突与合作的复杂性，以及中美关系对全球经济发展、能源市场稳定、亚洲、中东和非洲的政治军事稳定、外层空间利用、全球气候变化和网络安全等重大议题的影响。
本课程注重“理论联系实际”，通过经典与前沿文献研读、学生报告、课堂讨论与辩论，训练学生批判性评估国际关系理论与实践的能力。此外，课程将结合任课教师的研究专长与最新学术成果，拓宽学生的学术视野，培养其独立思考与学术研究能力。','This course is intended to introduce students to the core concepts and major theoretical approaches in the study of international relations and their application to contemporary world politics. It places particular emphasis on helping students develop a theoretically informed understanding of one of the most important bilateral relationships in the 21st century — Sino-US relations. By highlighting key debates and conversations among different theoretical perspectives, the course explores how these theories help explain the complexity of conflict and cooperation between China and the United States, as well as the impact of Sino-US relations on global economic development, the stability of energy markets, political and military stability in Asia, the Middle East and Africa, the uses of outer space, global climate change, and cyber security, among other issues.
This course emphasizes the integration of theory and practice. Through intensive readings of both classical and contemporary literature, student presentations, and in-class debates and discussions, students are expected to develop the ability to critically evaluate theoretical arguments and practical issues in international relations. In addition, the course provides opportunities for instructors to introduce their own areas of expertise and recent research findings, thereby broadening students’ academic and intellectual horizons and cultivating their independent thinking and research skills.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101711,'GLB5210','全球政治经济学基础','','GLB - Global Studies','5210','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 1
