2026-27 Term 1','','','N/A','This course introduces students to the study of domestic political institutions, processes, and outcomes across and within countries. It surveys key concepts and major theoretical contributions in comparative politics, offering students a foundational understanding of how political systems vary and why these variations matter. Students are introduced to the comparative method as a framework for analyzing political and social phenomena, using both contemporary and historical cases from around the world. Through this comparative lens, students will gain insights into how political systems shape governance and citizens'' lives, preparing them to think critically about political dynamics in a globalized world.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101714,'GLB5340','比较公共意见','','GLB - Global Studies','5340','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
