2026-27 Term 1','Nil.','Nil.','N/A','This course provides an introduction to the field of security studies. It will explore what it means to apply a scientific approach to the study of international security, what are the main models used in this field, and what are the most pressing developments that concern global security. Through this course, the students will be able to answer the following questions: what is security in international relations? Why do wars happen, and how can we prevent or solve them? How do we tackle new challenges to international security? Furthermore, throughout the course we will explore empirical cases of conflict and (in)security, so that students learn to apply classic theories to explain real-world events.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
