2026-27 Term 1','This is an advanced course. Recommended for Ph.D. students and advanced master’s students interested in applying to Ph.D. programs.','','本课程旨在帮助学生了解东亚，预测该地区的可能发展，并批判性地思考这些发展对全球机构、国家和个人的潜在长期影响。学期结束时，学生将掌握有效分析关键问题的知识技能。','This course aims to help students to understand East Asia, anticipate probable developments in the region, and think critically about the potential long-term impact of those developments on institutions, countries, and individuals across the globe. By the end of the semester, the students are expected to develop the intellectual skills to effectively analyze key events and issues happening in East Asia.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101728,'GLB5610','比较欧洲政治','','GLB - Global Studies','5610','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程对欧洲代议制政府和政治研究中的主要实质性和知识主题进行系统的考察。随着现代欧洲随着欧盟 （EU） 的发展而发生转变，本课程还将分析重点放在欧洲的一体化以及国家和欧盟代表和政府层面之间的相互作用。','This course provides a systematic examination of the major substantive and intellectual themes in the study of representative government and politics in Europe. As modern Europe has undergone a transformation with the development of the European Union (EU), this course also places its analytical focus on the integration of Europe and the interplay between the national and the EU levels of representation and government.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
