(101730,'GLB5630','中美关系','','GLB - Global Studies','5630','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','The seminar is taught in three-hour sessions. Every student should complete four presentations: three during the class, one at the end of the semester (a presentation for the term paper), 15 minutes each. Also, students are requested to write a term paper for the class on a topic relating to the class subject he/she chooses.','Nil.','大多数国际观察人士将中美关系视为21世纪最重要的双边关系，指出中美间的冲突与合作对全球经济发展、能源市场稳定、亚洲、中东和非洲的政治军事稳定、外层空间利用、全球气候变化和网络安全等问题的影响。对于如何界定中美关系，中美的学术分析人士和政策制定者都没有明确的共识。
本课程侧重于从历史和理论的角度理解中美关系在多个领域的变化。“熟悉理论”意味着你还将阅读一些国际关系理论，这些理论可能有助于解释不同层级的冲突与合作。
本课程旨在帮助学生更深入地理解中美关系的复杂性，以及影响这一双边关系的众多因素，包括国内、国际、历史、政治、经济、文化、观念和地缘政治因素等等。','Most international observers have characterized the US-China relationship as THE most important bilateral relationship in the 21st century – pointing to the impact of Sino-US conflict and cooperation on global economic development, on the stability of energy markets, on the political-military stability of Asia, the Middle East and Africa, on the uses of outer space, on global climate change, and on cyber-security among other issues. Needless to say there is no clear consensus academic analysts and policy makers on either side as to how to characterize Sino-US relations.

This course focuses on the historical and theoretical understanding of the changes in US-China relations, across a number of domains. “Theoretically informed” means that you will also read about some theories of international relations that might help explain changing levels of conflict and cooperation.

The aim of this course is to help students gain a deeper understanding of the complexity of Sino-US relations, as well as the numerous factors that affect this bilateral relations in general, including domestic, international, historical, political, economic, cultural, ideational, and geopolitical factors, etc..','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101731,'GLB5640','政治制度分析','','GLB - Global Studies','5640','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','Before each class, students are expected to read all assigned (required) articles and book chapters. Each student must complete at least one presentation, and each presentation should not exceed 15 minutes. The presentation slides should be uploaded 24 hours before each class, and all students are expected to read the slides before coming to class. During the final exam, students will write short essays on 2-4 questions.','','本课程将从比较的角度带领学生了解当代世界政治制度的设计、维护和改革。它旨在帮助学生发展有关制度的主要理论方法和该学科的主要辩论的系统知识。通过学习这门课程，学生将了解政治机构的重要性以及这些机构如何影响政治、社会和经济。','This course will take students through the design, maintenance and reform of political institutions in contemporary world from a comparative perspective. It aims to help students develop systemic knowledge about major theoretical approaches to institutions and major debates in the subject. By taking this course, students will understand the importance of political institutions and how these institutions shape political, social and economic outcomes.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101732,'GLB5650','中国政治治理','','GLB - Global Studies','5650','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101733,'GLB5660','比较区域研究专题研讨课（一）','','GLB - Global Studies','5660','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','*Course A. East Asia (Prof. Jongyoon Baik)*
This seminar is conducted in three-hour sessions. During the weeks when readings are assigned, students are expected to thoroughly read all articles and book chapters. In Week 5, students will choose the research method they will use for simulation and presentation based on their research agenda. In Weeks 7 and 11, students will act as "interviewers" and ask their own interview, survey, or survey experiment questions to the class, who will serve as the "interviewees." All students are expected to actively participate by answering questions and providing feedback. Based on the feedback, the interviewers will revise their questions and "implement" the interview, survey, or survey experiment by asking questions to their friends (the "samples") over the following two weeks. Then, in Weeks 10 and 14, they will present their research agenda, explain why they chose to ask certain questions in specific ways, analyze the interview, survey, or survey e','','该研讨会课程往往涵盖比较区域研究流提供的现有课程未涵盖的重要主题，例如中东研究、非洲研究、拉丁美洲研究、区域研究理论以及其他特定主题，例如经济、文化和宗教区域。','This seminar course tends to cover important topics that have not been covered by the existing courses offered by the Comparative Area Studies Stream, such as Middle East Studies, Africa Studies, Latin America Studies, theories of area studies, and other specific topics such as economic, cultural, and religious regions.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101734,'GLB5840','美国政治','','GLB - Global Studies','5840','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101735,'GLB5850','东亚政治','','GLB - Global Studies','5850','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','N/A','','本课程旨在通过比较政治学的视角，探讨东亚地区（中国、朝鲜、韩国和日本）的政治现象。具体议题包括政治历史、制度架构、经济发展以及国家与社会的关系。课程还将涵盖这些国家之间的国际关系，以及当前热点问题，如媒体的角色、人口老龄化和移民政策。通过分析性阅读和课堂讨论，学生将提升批判性阅读能力，并深化对东亚政治的理解。','The goal of this course is to examine the politics of East Asia—China, the two Koreas, and Japan—through the lens of Comparative Politics. Specific topics include political history, institutions, economic development, and state-society relations. The course will also cover inter-state relations among these countries, as well as current issues such as the role of media, ageing populations, and immigration. Students will enhance their critical reading skills through analytical readings and in-class discussions.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101736,'GLB5860','国际关系专题讨论（二）','','GLB - Global Studies','5860','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Nil.','Nil.','本课程旨在系统介绍国际关系学科的研究前沿，聚焦21世纪塑造世界政治未来走向的核心议题。课程内容涵盖本学科其他课程未涉及的重要领域，同时为教师提供展示其学术专长和最新研究成果的平台，以拓展学生的理论视野和学术思维。通过高强度文献研读、专题报告、课堂辩论与研讨等教学形式，培养学生对国际关系重大问题的批判性思考能力，并最终引导其完成特定主题的深度研究。课程具体内容将由授课教师在临时委员会的指导下确定。','This course is intended to introduce students to the research frontier in the study of international relations and contemporary issues that define the future trends of world politics in the 21st century. It may also cover relevant and important topics of international relations not covered by other courses in this stream. In addition, it provides an opportunity for teachers to introduce their own expertise and more recent research areas and findings to students thus broadening their academic and intellectual horizon. Students are expected to do intensive pre-readings, presentations, in-class debate and discussions, and ultimately conduct their own research on specific topics. Course contents will be decided by course instructors under the supervision of ad hoc committees.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
