(101738,'GLB5880','全球政治经济专题讨论（二）','','GLB - Global Studies','5880','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本研讨课从比较政治经济学的视角，考察产业政策的理论与实践——即国家通过政策干预来塑造经济结构、推动技术升级和实现长期发展的努力。课程将理论框架与对现实世界中政策设计与实施的细致分析相结合，把产业政策视为一种政治与制度过程，而非抽象的经济处方；这一过程在不同国家、不同时期以及不同发展阶段中以不同方式运作。

东亚是本课程的核心经验案例，但分析方法具有明确的比较性。课程将东亚的经验与当今发达工业化国家的历史发展路径，以及发展中地区当代的产业政策实践进行对比研究。这种比较视角有助于学生理解：为何类似的政策工具——如补贴、贸易保护或国家投资——会因国家能力、政治制度和国际约束的不同而产生截然不同的结果。

课程强调产业政策在过去如何发挥作用，以及在当今如何运作。它将早期工业化和战后发展战略与当前全球经济中产业政策的重新兴起联系起来，后者受到全球化、技术竞争、气候变化以及国家安全关切的共同塑造。在整个课程中，我们还将分析产业政策与贸易政策之间的互动，包括国际规则、贸易争端以及塑造各国政策空间的地缘政治压力。','This seminar examines the theory and practice of industrial policy—state efforts to shape economic structure, technological upgrading, and long-run development—through a comparative political economy perspective. It combines theoretical frameworks with close attention to real-world policy design and implementation, treating industrial policy not as abstract economic prescriptions but as a political and institutional process that operates differently across countries, time periods, and levels of development.

East Asia serves as the central empirical anchor of the course, but the analysis is explicitly comparative. East Asian experiences are studied alongside historical development paths in today’s advanced industrial economies and contemporary industrial policy efforts in developing regions. This comparative approach allows students to understand why similar policy tools—such as subsidies, trade protection, or state investment—can produce very different outcomes depending on state capacity, political institutions, and international constraints.

The course emphasizes how industrial policy worked in the past and how it works today. It links early industrialization and postwar development strategies to the renewed role of industrial policy in the current global economy, shaped by globalization, technological competition, climate change, and national security concerns. Throughout the course, we also analyze the interaction between industrial policy and trade policy, including international rules, trade disputes, and geopolitical pressures that shape the policy space available to governments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
