(101740,'GLB5910','比较区域研究专题讨论（二）','','GLB - Global Studies','5910','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本研讨课程旨在涵盖比较区域研究方向现有课程未涉及的重要议题，例如中东研究、非洲研究、拉丁美洲研究、区域研究理论，以及其他特定主题（如经济、文化、宗教区域等）。课程具体内容将由授课教师在临时委员会的指导下确定。','This seminar course tends to cover important topics that have not been covered by the existing courses offered by the Comparative Area Studies Stream, such as Middle East Studies, Africa Studies, Latin America Studies, theories of area studies, and other specific topics such as economic, cultural, and religious regions. Course contents will be decided by course instructors under the supervision of ad hoc committees.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101741,'GLB5920','比较区域研究专题讨论（三）','','GLB - Global Studies','5920','G',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','N/A','This course is a seminar on selected topics in comparative political economy (CPE), broadly construed. We will study how states and markets are historically constructed, how they interact with social cleavages and culture, and how they shape development, democracy, and contemporary political conflict. Substantively, the course covers state formation and private order, colonialism and historical legacies, democracy and elite competition, the cultural origins of political behavior, economic shocks and backlash, and governance and accountability in low-capacity settings, while emphasizing careful research design and identification strategies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
