2026-27 Term 1','Successful completion of all U-core English courses or ENL serial courses or equivalence recognized by HSS.','NIL','本课程致力于培养各专业学生均需掌握的高级写作技能，尤其强调提高学生以简练而精准的语言呈现逻辑清晰观点的能力。课程将花费头几周的时间专门强化标点符号的正确使用与句子结构的深入分析。接下来，本课程将聚焦于论点的审视与表达，引导学生通过分析常见的逻辑谬误来学会辨识并避免主观臆断、过度推测、个性化或笼统化的论点。同时，学生将学习撰写论据明确、逻辑严密、客观公正且具备高度可验证性的论文。本课程秉承“写作即过程”的理念，通过引导学生草拟大纲、撰写初稿，并经过多轮修改与打磨，最终达到提升写作能力的目的。课程的最终目标是让学生够熟练掌握撰写结构清晰、逻辑性强、语言精炼且准确的论文所需的各项写作能力。','This course focuses on developing advanced writing skills for students across academic disciplines, with special attention to enhancing the abilities of students to produce logical and succinct arguments. The course will begin with a few weeks reviewing punctuation use and clause analysis. The core of the course will focus on the examination and production of claims. Students will learn how to recognize and avoid subjective, speculative, and overly personalized, specialized, or generalized arguments. The students will produce essays that structure arguments with compelling logic and make precise, objective, verifiable claims. Students will learn about the Affective and Intentional Fallacies and other logical fallacies. Students will approach writing as a process, through the production of an outline and several drafts of an essay which they will continue to revise and refine throughout the term. The final objective of the course will be production of a clear, logical, precise and concise essay that has been polished and proofread to a high level of exactitude.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
