2026-27 Term 1','','','该课程向人文与社会科学学院一年级学生提供入门级的社会学知识和观点。该课程的目标是帮助学生对社会学有基本的了解并理解社会学家如何处理不同问题。为此，该课程将向学生展示一些重要的的社会学视角以及社会学家进行经验研究的方法。此外，它将介绍社会学家如何运用这些社会学视角来研究与我们日常生活相关的问题，包括性别和家庭、文化与互动、教育、工作和全球化等不同领域。通过分析与日常生活相关的例子，学生将获得社会学视角和分析能力。','This course offers introductory sociological knowledge and perspectives to first year students in School of Humanities and Social Science. The goal of this course is to help students to gain a basic sense of what is sociology and understand how sociologists approach different issues. To do so, general sociological perspectives and the approaches sociologists take to conduct empirical studies will be demonstrated to students. It will then introduce how sociologists use these general perspectives to study issues related to our daily life, including the realms of gender and family, culture and interaction, education, work, and globalization. Through analyzing examples that pertain to everyday life, students will be equipped with sociological perspectives and analytical skills.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
