(101773,'HSS4001','华人社会的教育发展','','HSS - Humanities and Social Science','4001','H',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','NO prerequisite.','','本课程属于教育学类，适合对华人社会（如中国内地、港澳台地区、新加坡等）的教育现象感兴趣或未来想从事中小学教师、教育研究、人工智能教育应用开发等相关工作的学生。修读本课程无需具备教育学基础。本课程旨在帮助学生，通过了解华人社会的整体教育情况，认识教育、社会与人的关系，把握教育现象的基本特征，从而桥接其主修专业与教育学，拓展职业发展可能性。本课程将介绍基本的教育学概念、研究范式和方法，探讨华人社会的历史、文化、哲学、制度及政策等议题。此外，本课程还将讨论人工智能在教育中的应用场景、伦理和社会议题，以应对当前技术变革对教育的挑战。','This course focuses on education and is ideal for students interested in educational phenomena in Chinese societies (such as Chinese mainland, Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan, Singapore) or those pursuing careers in primary and secondary school teaching, educational research, or AI education application development. No prior knowledge of education is needed. The course aims to help students understand the overall educational landscape in Chinese societies, recognize the relationship between education, society, and individuals, and grasp the basic characteristics of educational phenomena. It bridges their major with education studies and expands career opportunities. The course covers fundamental concepts of education science, research paradigms and methods; explores topics like history, culture, philosophy, institution and policies within Chinese societies; and discusses scenarios involving applications ethics social issues concerning artificial intelligence to address challenges posed by current technological transformations in education.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101774,'HSS5001','专业实习','','HSS - Humanities and Social Science','5001','H',1.00,5000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','实习课程的核心目的在于让学生进入一个真实标准工作环境的实践平台。学院实习指导老师与单位实习主管将为学生提供指导与支持，确保实习工作能够成为一次具备价值且富有成效的经历。学生若成功完成本课程，将有效掌握未来职业生涯中的关键技能，同时该课程也为学生探索不同职业领域创造了契机。','The purpose of the Internship course is to provide each student practical experience in a standard work environment. The Faculty Internship Advisor and On-site Supervisor will assist students in making the job a valuable and productive experience. Success in this course will help ensure development of skills necessary for a lasting and rewarding career in the future. It may also be used as an opportunity to explore career fields.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
