(101800,'IBA4011','信息系統学实证研究初探','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','4011','I',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','MIS2051 IT in Business Applications','None','本研讨课程旨在为四年级本科生在信息系统（IS）领域的实证研究所需的方法、工具和批判性思维技能提供一个初步介绍。学生需在选修本课程前熟练掌握大学微积分内容。在老师指导下，学生将学习主流的实证研究方法（例如计量经济学、实验、机器学习），并演示如何运用这些方法研究电子商务、社交媒体、数字化转型和IT治理等信息系统现象。本课程内容将根据学生的兴趣和导师的专业知识而有所不同，并将随着信息系统学科格局的变化而不断发展。','This seminar course aims to give final year students an overview of the methods, tools, and critical thinking skills necessary to conduct rigorous empirical research in Information Systems (IS). Successful completion and mastery of College Calculus is required prior to enrolling in this course. Under the guidance of instructor(s), students will study in depth the mainstream empirical research methods (e.g., econometrics, experiments, machine learning) and demonstrates how they can be employed to investigate IS phenomena such as e-business, social media, digital transformation, and IT governance. The contents of this course may vary based on the interests of the students and the expertise of the instructors, and will continue to evolve with the changing landscape of the information systems discipline.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101801,'IBA4013','信息系統学分析研究方法导论','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','4013','I',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'• Having completed at least one course related to machine learning/artificial
intelligence from the following list:
ECO3080 Machine Learning for Business
ECO3090 Machine Learning for Financial Economics
MIS2011 AI for Business: A Practical Introduction  
MIS3011 Advanced AI for Business: From Theories to Applications
MIS3012 LLMs in Business - From Prompt Engineering to AI Agents
MGT3650 AI in Strategic and Entrepreneurial Management
MKT3060 Quantitative Marketing Methods in the AI Age
FIN3090 AI Applications in Finance
• AND at least one economics course from the following list:
ECO1020 Principles of Economics
ECO2011 Basic Microeconomics
ECO2021 Basic Macroeconomics','None','本课程帮助学生获得设计、执行和批判信息系统学分析研究的知识和能力。它强调分析研究方法——包含经济学、运筹学基础和计算方法，以解决当代信息系统问题，例如信息基础设施/信息产品的经济学、商业决策以及高效的大数据分析。此课程旨在帮助学生培养识别新兴且有影响力的分析研究主题的能力，并选择合适的研究方法进行调查。具体内容可能会因参加本课程的学生的兴趣和授课教师的不同而在每个学期有所变化。','This course helps students acquire the knowledge and skills to design, execute, and critique analytical research in Information Systems (IS). It emphasizes analytical approaches—economic, OR-based, and computational—to address contemporary IS problems such as economics of information infrastructure/information goods, business decision-making, and efficient big data analytics. This course aims to help students develop the ability to identify new and impactful analytical research topics and select appropriate research methods to conduct the investigation. The specific contents may vary from semester to semester based on the interests of the students attending this course and the faculty members teaching this course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101802,'IBA4315','⾼级⼈⼯智能与商业应⽤','Advanced Artificial Intelligence and Business Applications','IBA - Information Management and Bus','4315','I',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','Students must successfully complete at least two of the following courses:

MAT1005 Mathematics for Business and Economics
MAT2040 Linear Algebra
MAT1010 Calculus for Economic Analysis I
STA2001 Probability and Statistics I
STA2002 Probability and Statistics II
STA3010 Regression Analysis
ECO2121 Basic Statistics
MIS2051 IT in Business Applications
ECO3080 Machine Learning for Business

Students are expected to have basic knowledge of machine learning and experiences of Python programming. Students with limited technical backgrounds can still take the course but may need to exert additional efforts to master certain technical materials compared to their more technically-versed peers.','','在过去的十年中，人工智能（AI）已经彻底改变了众多行业。世界经济论坛预测，到 2030 年，AI 将创造 133 百万个新工作，取代 7500 万个现有工作，并可能为全球 GDP 贡献高达 15 万亿美元。本课程旨在探讨高级人工智能（AI）的基本技术与其在商业环境中的实际应用。课程将涵盖与现代 AI 相关的各种新兴主题，例如机器学习、深度学习、AI 工具和平台、大型语言模型、ChatGPT、以及在组织中管理 AI 的方法。我们还将探讨生成式 AI 工具 （例如， ChatGPT、 Bing Chat、 Microsoft Copilot）在各行业中的最新商业应用。学生将有机会接触和部署各种新开发的 AI 工具和平台。最后，我们将讨论如何在组织流程中管理 AI。

总体而言，该课程的主要目的是帮助学生们建立对人工智能的技术和管理理解，并通过案例分析和实践项目来获得开发、部署和评估各种人工智能工具的经验。值得注意的是，该课程并不旨在教授你如何成为一名编程人员或机器学习工程师。','In the past decade, Artificial Intelligence (AI) has revolutionized numerous industries. The World Economic Forum predicts AI will generate 133 million new jobs, displace 75 million existing ones, and could contribute up to $15 trillion to the global GDP by 2030. However, a global AI skills shortage is evident, with demand for AI professionals massively outstripping supply. This is an introductory undergraduate course that explores the fundamental concepts and practical applications of artificial intelligence (AI) in the business context. Various emerging topics related to modern AI, such as machine
learning, deep learning, AI tools and platforms, large language models, ChatGPT, managing AI in organizations, will be covered. For students who are not actively immersed in AI before, we will provide a brief technical overview for the methodologies underlying cutting-edge AI technologies. More importantly, we will cover recent business applications of AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Bing Chat, Microsoft Copilot) in various industries (e.g., media, healthcare, retail, finance). Students will have an opportunity to access and deploy a wide range of newly-developed AI tools and platforms. Lastly, we
will discuss how to manage AI in organizational processes.

Overall, the primary purpose of this course is to help students to develop technical and managerial understanding of AI and get experience in the development, deployment and assessment of various AI technologies through hands-on case analysis and project exercises. Notably, the course is not meant to teach you how to be a coder or ML engineer.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
