(101823,'IBA6209','决策导向的因果数据分析','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6209','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','ECO2121 Basic Statistics or equivalent courses for basic statistics','','本课程侧重于应用因果推断来推动有效的、基于证据的决策。在现实的复杂环境中，区分单纯的相关性与真实的因果关系对于预测结果和规避风险至关重要。本课程旨在弥合统计理论与实际决策之间的鸿沟，为学生提供在实施干预措施之前评估其潜在影响的工具和思维框架。
学生将探索用于构建决策场景模型的框架，识别数据中的偏差，并估算反事实情况——即如果选择不同的路径会发生什么。通过掌握这些方法，学生将能够更好地优化资源配置，评估政策有效性，并制定更好的高风险决策。本课程的最终目标是将数据分析从一种描述性工作转化为指导决策的引擎。','This course focuses on the application of causal inference to drive effective, evidence-based decision-making. In complex business environments, distinguishing between mere correlation and true causation is critical for predicting outcomes and mitigating risk. This course bridges the gap between statistical theory and practical strategy, providing students with the tools and thinking frameworks to assess the potential impact of interventions before they are implemented.
Students will explore frameworks for modeling decision scenarios, identifying biases in data, and estimating the counterfactual—what would happen if a different path were chosen. By mastering these methods, students will be better equipped to optimize resource allocation, evaluate policy effectiveness, and make better high-stakes decisions. The course ultimately aims to transform data analysis from a descriptive exercise into a prescriptive engine for strategic action.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101824,'IBA6301','电子商务创新与数据智能','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6301','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
