2026-27 Term 1','FIN2010 Financial Management
ECO3121 Introductory Econometrics','','金融科技(Fintech)正以革命性的方式与速度改变金融服务行业。本课 程的目的是向学生介绍金融科技的理论与实践，主要涵盖新技术在金融 服务中的应用，例如大数据、区块链、机器学习与人工智能等。通过本 课程的学习，学生将对近期金融科技发展态势和金融服务的创新形式有 广泛了解，包括 P2P 借贷(和众筹)、智能投顾、保险科技和加密货币 等。此外，我们将讨论金融科技转型过程中出现的监管挑战和隐私问 题;金融公司、大型科技公司与保险公司的代表们也将会与班级分享金 融科技在各自行业中的最新进展。','Financial technology (FinTech) is revolutionary and rapidly changing the financial services industries. The objective of this course is to introduce students to the theory and practice of Fintech. This course covers the applications of new technologies in financial services such as big data, blockchain, machine learning and artificial intelligence (AI). Students are expected to develop a broad understanding of the recent FinTech developments and the new forms of financial services such as peer-to- peer lending and crowdfunding, robo-advisors, InsurTech and cryptocurrencies. In addition, we will discuss the regulatory challenges and privacy concerns that emerge as part of the Fintech transformation. Representatives from financial firms, big technological companies or insurance companies will be invited to share with the class the recent development in FinTech in the industry.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101833,'IBA6310','项目管理','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6310','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1
2023-24 Summer','','','本课程系统介绍当代组织中项目发起、规划、执行、监控、控制与收尾所需的管理理念、分析工具和数字化能力。课程内容包括项目管理基础、项目选择、项目组织、项目经理角色、谈判与冲突管理、项目活动计划、工作分解结构、预算与成本估算、进度计划、资源配置、监控系统、项目控制、项目审计与项目终止。在经典项目管理技术基础上，课程将在适当主题中嵌入AI辅助项目管理实践。学生将培养项目管理技术能力，并学习如何使用AI工具支持适当的项目管理任务。','This course introduces the managerial concepts, analytical tools, and digital capabilities required to initiate, plan, execute, monitor, control, and close projects in contemporary organizations. It covers project selection, project organization, the role of the project manager, negotiation and conflict management, project activity planning, work breakdown structure, budgeting and cost estimation, scheduling, resource allocation, monitoring, project control, auditing, and project termination. In addition to classical project management techniques, the course embeds AI-enabled project management practices into appropriate topics. Students will develop technical project management skills and learn how to use AI tools to support project management tasks.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101834,'IBA6311','区块链科技与应用','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6311','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','Nil','Nil','圆满完成本课程后，学生可以期望 (1) 了解区块链的基本概念，例如加密货币和共识算法，(2) 能够在专业环境中阅读和讨论区块链问题，(3) 了解金融、医疗保健和制造业等各种商业环境开发区块链解决方案的概念、方法、技术和工具，以及 (4) 批判性地评估区块链技术的当前趋势及其在各个工业领域的表现。本课程将要求学生分组使用区块链框架和用户友善工具（如 Hyperledger composer 和 fabric）开发原型系统。','Upon satisfactory completion of this course, students can expect to (1) understand the fundamental concepts in blockchain, such as cryptocurrency and consensus algorithms; (2) be able to read and argue about blockchain issues in a professional setting; (3) know the core concepts, methods, techniques, and tools for the development of blockchain solutions for various business contexts, such as finance, healthcare, and manufacturing; and (4) critically evaluate current trends in blockchain technology and their manifestation in various industrial sectors. This course requires students to work in group to develop a prototype system by using a blockchain framework and user-friendly tools. such as Hyperledger composer and fabric.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101835,'IBA6312','数据通信与网络','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6312','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程介绍现代数据通信的基本概念、体系结构以及管理议题。除了理解数据通信的基础概念以外，学生将学习局域网与广域网、互联网、无线与移动通信系统，并探讨网络安全、性能管理与网络设计等关键问题。课程特别强调网络技术在商业中的管理意义，包括成本、可扩展性、风险管理及对数字化转型的支持。通过课程讲授与小组活动，学生不仅能够掌握技术基础，还能将知识应用于实际场景，如企业网络、云服务及新兴技术。本课程旨在帮助学生从管理视角理解与分析数据网络部署、运行与战略决策，培养面向未来的信息管理能力。','The course introduces students to the fundamental concepts, architectures, and managerial issues of modern data communications. With understanding the fundamental concepts of data communications, students will gain an understanding of local and wide area networks, the Internet, wireless and mobile systems, as well as key issues in network security, performance, and design. Special attention is given to business implications of networking technologies, including cost, scalability, risk management, and support for digital transformation. Through lectures and group activities, students will not only grasp technical foundations but also apply concepts to real-world scenarios such as enterprise networks, cloud services, and emerging technologies. The course equips students with the knowledge and managerial perspective to make informed decisions about data network deployment, operation, and strategy in business contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
