2025-26 Summer','1.CGPA at CUHK-Shenzhen (e.g., Term 2, 2025-26) should be no less than 2.0;
2.If you are on the probation list, you are not eligible to apply for this course.

Students who choose to take the practicum course during the academic term are required to submit: 1) a course application form containing the student, employer, and internship information; and 2) a signed contract with the employer. The required documents should be submitted to the MSc in IMBA Programme Office at mscimba_reg@cuhk.edu.cn, with smepg@cuhk.edu.cn copied, at least fifteen days before the beginning of each term. The deadline to enroll in this course is 15:00 on September 7, 2026 for the fall term of the 2026-27 academic year.
Late add/drop applications for this course will not be considered.
The internship may commence only after the student intern(s) have obtained official approval from the MSc in IMBA Programme Office. The Programme will add approved students to this course in SIS on September 12, 2026.','','本课程包括一个学生执行的项目，适合他们各自的专业，导致一个正式的报告，展示了深入的实践经验。实习课程通过关注学生使用正式方法执行的现实生活开发项目，解决了在特定商业环境中整合各种观点、技术和方法的需求。项目通常包括概念化、分析、设计和开发一个可用的、功能性的可交付物，作为概念的证明。学生可以完成该课程作为实习计划的一部分，同时由工业专业人士建议。本课程将采用P/U评分制。
（*本课程以中英文授课。）','This course consists of a student-executed project adapted to their respective concentration, leading to a formal report that demonstrates an in-depth practical experience. The practicum course addresses the need of integrating various perspectives, techniques, and methodologies in a particular business setting by focusing on a real-life development project that students execute using a formal methodology. The project will typically cover the conceptualization, analysis, design, and development of a working, functional deliverable that serves as a proof of concept. Students may complete the course as part of the internship program while advised by an industrial professional. The P/U grading scheme will be adopted for this course.
(* This course is conducted in English and Chinese.)','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101837,'IBA6314','自然语言处理与文本学习','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6314','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Statistics and probability theory, linear algebra, basic knowledge of Python (do not need to master). Basic machine learning theory.','','本课程将教授如何应用机器学习技术来分析来自商业世界的文本。本课程的主要目的是向学生揭示数据挖掘技术的强大功能，在商业领域中海量数据集的价值以及从文本中提取的丰富信息。学生将学习如何利将现实世界中的问题转换为可以通过ML算法解决的数学模型，并在解决方案空间中找到最佳的ML算法。学生将了解和熟悉自然语言处理模型，并学会通过词袋，词嵌入和序列模型对文本进行建模。还鼓励学生了解最新的NLP方向的进展，例如GPT系列，Gemini系列，多模态语言模型，AI智能体和AI辅助编程，获得每种算法背后的数学基础的基本知识。','Text analytics has become an important tool in business and economics. It is a field that lies on the interface of information retrieval, machine learning, and natural language processing. This course carefully covers a coherently organized framework drawn from these intersecting topics. We will start with basic algorithms of machine learning from text. We then discuss the learning methods from text via advanced technique from NLP. Finally, we cover hot topics in NLP such as LLMs, AI agents, etc. Course grade will be based on class discussions, a group project, homework assignments and a final exam.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101838,'IBA6315','商务深度学习导论','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6315','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Students are expected to have experience coding in Python and solid understanding of linear algebra and general probability theory.','None','这是一门创新性的课程，深入探讨了最新的人工智能工具及其在商业中的实际应用。学生通过学习将获得开发和运用先进编程技能和知识，包括先进的人工智能工具，如GPT（生成式预训练转换器）。通过项目实际应用，学生将提升编程技能，并全面了解人工智能如何在商业环境中创造价值。课程涵盖了机器学习、自然语言处理和大数据分析等多个主题。该课程的主要目标是为学生提供开发和实施基于人工智能的解决复杂业务问题所需的技能和知识。通过深入了解这些新兴技术，学生还将在不断变化的人工智能和商业领域中获得竞争优势。','This is an innovative course that delves into the latest artificial intelligence tools and their practical applications in business. Students will acquire the skills and knowledge to develop and utilize advanced programming techniques, including cutting-edge AI tools such as GPT (Generative Pre-trained Transformer). Through hands-on projects and real-world applications, students will enhance their programming skills and gain a comprehensive understanding of how AI can be utilized to create value in the business environment. The course covers a range of topics such as on how to apply machine learning, natural language processing, and big data analytics. The primary goal of this course is to equip students with the skills and knowledge required to develop and implement AI-based solutions to complex business problems. Students will also gain a competitive advantage in the ever-changing landscape of AI and business by developing a thorough understanding of these emerging technologies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101839,'IBA6316','生成式人工智能商业应用：无代码/低代码实践','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6316','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','•	Basic understanding of system/software development
•	Basic knowledge of programming languages','None','本课程向学生介绍如何使用无代码和低代码平台，为商业场景开发实用的生成式人工智能（GenAI）应用。课程专为没有深厚编程背景的学生设计，借助 Dify、n8n、Coze 及相关工具，实现 AI 驱动的商业解决方案的快速原型设计与部署。课程涵盖 GenAI 和大型语言模型（LLM）的基本概念、完整的 GenAI 项目生命周期，并强调智能体系统的动手构建。通过理论讲授、实践教程、行业嘉宾邀请演讲及小组项目，学生将开发真实的 GenAI 应用并展示可运行的原型。完成课程后，学生将能够：理解 GenAI 的基本原理并评估不同模型；为商业场景设计和实施完整的 GenAI 解决方案；使用无代码/低代码平台构建和优化智能体系统；将外部数据源和工具集成到 GenAI 应用中；并批判性地评估各商业领域的 GenAI 应用。

说明：本课程侧重实际商业应用，而非技术研究或算法开发。','This course introduces students to the practical development of Generative AI (GenAI) applications for business using no-code and low-code platforms. Designed for students without extensive programming backgrounds, this course enables rapid prototyping and deployment of AI-powered business solutions using platforms such as Dify, n8n, Coze, and related tools. The course covers fundamental concepts of GenAI and Large Language Models (LLMs), the complete GenAI project lifecycle, and emphasizes hands-on construction of intelligent agentic systems. Through theoretical lecture, practical tutorials, invited industry speakers, and a group project, students will develop real-world GenAI applications and present working demonstrations. Upon completion, students will be able to: understand GenAI fundamentals and evaluate different models; design and implement complete GenAI solutions for business contexts; construct and optimize intelligent agentic systems using no-code/low-code platforms; integrate external data sources and tools into GenAI applications; and critically assess GenAI applications across various business sectors.

Note: The course focuses on practical business application rather than technical research or algorithm development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101840,'IBA6317','商务数据可视化策略','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6317','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','Basic knowledge of Python.
Basic knowledge of statistics and probability, some linear algebra, calculus.','本课程旨在培养学生掌握将复杂数据转化为有说服力、可操作的可视化叙事技巧，以支持商业决策。课程涵盖设计原则、认知心理学和故事讲述方法，并探索Excel、Tableau、Python（Matplotlib、Seaborn）及D3.js等工具，用于创建交互式仪表板、信息图和动态报告。学生将学习针对不同利益相关者定制可视化方案，确保清晰度和影响力，同时避免误导性呈现等常见陷阱。通过案例研究和动手项目，课程强调道德数据呈现、可扩展性以及可视化在推动数据驱动型商业成果中的战略作用。','This course aims to equips students with techniques to transform complex data into compelling, actionable visual narratives for business decision-making. Covering principles of design, cognitive psychology, and storytelling, the course explores tools like Excel, Tableau, Python (Matplotlib, Seaborn), and D3.js to create interactive dashboards, infographics, and dynamic reports. Students learn to tailor visualizations to different stakeholders, ensuring clarity and impact while avoiding common pitfalls like misleading representations. Through case studies and hands-on projects, the course emphasizes ethical data presentation, scalability, and the strategic role of visualization in driving data-driven business outcomes.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101841,'IBA6318','AI辅助应用开发：商业专业人士视角','','IBA - Information Management and Bus','6318','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','No prerequisite.','No co-requisite.','本课程旨在引导研究生了解并掌握人工智能辅助编程在商业应用中的新兴实践。通过与人工智能编程工具的协作，学生将学习如何设计、开发与部署融合前端界面、后端逻辑、数据管理与自动化工具的数据驱动型解决方案。课程重点在于帮助学生理解编程逻辑、系统结构、工作流程管理，以及对人工智能生成代码的批判思考与审慎使用。通过每周的实践练习、小组合作项目与测试，学生将同时获得技术与概念层面的基础能力，能够在现代商业环境中将人工智能作为开发伙伴，开展创新性的开发实践','This course introduces postgraduate students to the emerging practice of AI-assisted coding for business applications. By collaborating with AI coding tools such as Tencent CodeBuddy, students will learn how to design, develop, and deploy data-driven solutions that integrate front-end interfaces, back-end logic, data management, and automation tools. The course emphasizes understanding programming logic, system structure, workflow management, and responsible use of AI-generated code. Through weekly hands-on exercises, collaborative projects, and tests, students will gain both the technical and conceptual foundation to use AI as a development partner in modern business environments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
