(101884,'ICS6210','集成微系统','','ICS - Integrated Circuits and System','6210','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101885,'ICS6215','微纳加工技术','','ICS - Integrated Circuits and System','6215','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Summer','None','None','本课程旨在帮助学生全面理解微纳尺度器件制造所涉及的原理、流程与技术，涵盖微电子、光电子以及微机电系统（MEMS）等领域。课程内容包括一系列基础概念，如晶体生长、薄膜沉积（化学气相沉积 CVD、物理气相沉积 PVD）、热氧化、扩散、离子注入、光刻，以及湿法刻蚀与干法刻蚀技术。学生将学习如何将这些独立工艺整合为完整的器件制造流程，应用于金属 - 氧化物 - 半导体场效应晶体管（MOSFET）、鳍式场效应晶体管（FinFET）、氮化镓（GaN）基电子/光电子器件等产品，同时也会涉及极紫外（EUV）光刻、3D 集成等新兴技术。该课程既注重理论认知，也强调实践应用，目标是为学生未来从事半导体制造、光子器件及微机电系统 / 纳机电系统（MEMS/NEMS）开发，以及先进材料加工相关工作奠定基础，同时也为其在纳米工程领域开展进一步研究提供知识支撑。','This course is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of the principles, processes, and technologies used in manufacturing of micro- and nano-scale devices, spanning microelectronics, optoelectronics, and microelectromechanical systems (MEMS). the course covers fundamental concepts such as crystal growth, thin-film deposition (CVD, PVD), thermal oxidation, diffusion, ion implantation, photolithography, and both wet and dry etching. Students learn how these individual processes are integrated into complete fabrication flows for devices such as MOSFETs, FinFETs, and GaN-based electronics/optoelectronics, as well as emerging technologies like EUV lithography and 3D integration. The curriculum emphasizes both theoretical understanding and practical application, with an aim to prepare students for careers in semiconductor manufacturing, Photonics and MEMS/NEMS development, and advanced materials processing, while also providing a foundation for further research in nanoengineering.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101886,'ICS6216','高级信号与系统','','ICS - Integrated Circuits and System','6216','I',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','None','None','本模块旨在介绍基于模型的先进信号处理方法与系统设计理论，并通过案例研究展示如何将这些知识应用于具有挑战性的实际工程问题。课程内容包括：将基于模型的信号处理与系统设计方法应用于实际问题、设计与实现基于模型的控制系统、从含噪声测量数据中估计未知系统参数、使用蒙特卡洛方法评估随机系统性能，以及从噪声测量中估计系统状态信息。','This graduate-level course provides a deep dive into the principles and algorithms of advanced signals and systems. Moving beyond introductory signal processing, it focuses on optimal filtering, adaptive systems, spectral estimation, and modern statistical signal processing techniques. The course bridges theoretical foundations—such as the Principle of Orthogonality, Wiener filtering, and eigenanalysis—with practical algorithms like LMS, RLS, and particle filters. Key topics include parametric and non-parametric spectral analysis, multi-rate processing, and an introduction to wavelet concepts and Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) methods for Bayesian inference. The students taking are expected to have some basic background knowledge on calculus, linear algebra, probability, statistics and random process as a prerequisite.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
