2022-23 Summer','NIL','NIL','本课程是日语（一）的后续课程，旨在为语言专业的学生（以及有兴趣学习一门新语言的非语言专业学生）提供继续学习日本语的机会。 同日语（一）一样，本课程侧重于培养学生具有较强的“阅读和写作”基础能力以及“听说”的实践能力。课程主要通过基础的语法项目学习，并辅之以大量的例句和练习，为学习者打下更坚实的基础。 课程将秉承“精讲多练，以练为主”的原则，通过课前、课中、以及课后的多种练习，使同学们获得逐步熟练的日语基础能力。同学们会了解到一些关于日本社会以及文化方面的知识；理解日语的语言基本特点、语法结构和日常生活的基本词汇；掌握日语词形的变化，能够表达出简单的句式以及进行简短的生活场景对话。','Japanese II is a higher level introductory Japanese course targeting language majors (and non-language majors who are interested in learning a new language) who have completed JPN1001. Similar to JPN1001, this course focuses on developing students’ basic literacy skills (i.e., reading and writing) and their practical skills in listening and speaking in Japanese. To achieve these goals, the course will take the key Japanese grammar topics as major themes for teaching and supplement them with ample authentic examples and intensive in- and after-class practice. Upon completion of this course, students will develop a deeper understanding of the basic features of the Japanese language in terms of grammatical structure (such as changes of Japanese word forms) and learn to use basic vocabulary in daily life. They will also be able to better understand the Japanese society and culture and conduct simple daily conversations in Japanese.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
