(101913,'LAW2101','合同法原则','','LAW - Law','2101','L',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Successful completion of English for Academic Purposes (I) (ENG1002) or equivalence as defined by HSS.','N/A','本课程面向未曾在普通法地区（如香港特别行政区）学习过合同法的本科生。课程内容涵盖合同法的核心概念，包括要约与承诺、对价、建立法律关系的意图以及违约救济等。学生将通过课程深入探讨合同在法律与商业环境中如何促进经济与社会互动，重点学习合同义务的形成、执行方式以及普通法对这些过程的影响。课程结束后，学生将掌握扎实的合同法基础，能够分析相关法律问题，并在实际场景中灵活运用合同原则。','This course is designed for undergraduate students who have not previously studied contract law as it applies in common law jurisdictions, such as the Hong Kong SAR. The course covers key concepts such as offer and acceptance, consideration, intention to create legal relations, and remedies for breach of contract. Throughout the course, students will explore the role of contracts in facilitating economic and social interactions within a legal and business environment. Emphasis will be placed on understanding how contractual obligations arise, how they are enforced, and how the common law approach shapes these processes. By the end of the course, students will have a solid foundation in contract law, enabling them to analyse legal issues and apply contractual principles in practical scenarios.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
