2026-27 Term 1','MAT 1001 (Calculus I)
MAT 1002 (Calculus II)
MAT 2040 (Linear Algebra) at least in the same semester','','本课程为学过《微积分上、下》(MAT 1001 and 1002)后需要或者感兴趣继续学习怎样严格定义和严格证明在微积分中碰到过的或者相关的的概念或者定理的学生。此课程将覆盖严格的极限定义、连续性、微分、积分、级数和函数序列的收敛、泰勒级数、反函数和隐函数定理， 多重积分，曲线积分与曲面积分等内容。学生在此课程中将系统地学习怎样写通顺而详细的数学证明。 在此课中学生所学到的知识和被培养出来的能力在后续课程如常微分方程、复变函数、实变函数、泛函分析和概率论等中将起到不可缺少作用。','This course is designed for students who have taken Calculus I & II (MAT 1001 and 1002) and need to be trained or are simply interested in learning how to rigorously define definitions and prove theorems that may or may not have been encountered in Calculus, such as the “ε-δ” definition of limits, continuity, differentiation, integration, convergence of series of numbers and sequences of functions, Taylor series, inverse function theorem, implicit function theorem, multiple integrals. This is the first calculus-related course in which the students will be trained systematically to write cohesive and comprehensive mathematical proofs.  The knowledge and the ability gained in this course are indispensable for advanced and rigorous mathematics courses such as Ordinary Differential equations, Complex Analysis, Real Analysis, Functional Analysis, Probability.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101971,'MAT2060','数学分析荣誉课程','Honours Mathematical Analysis','MAT - 数学','2060','M',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MAT 1011 (Calculus I)
MAT 1012 (Calculus II)','','选修本门课程的学生须已修习了微积分精讲（一）与微积分精讲（二）（MAT1011和MAT1012）。本课程面向对数学或应用数学感兴趣的优秀学生，是一门高水平、高难度的课程，旨在为学生打下扎实的分析知识基础、培养数学创新人才。因此，本课程的教学内容和教学方法更强调对数学分析理论和方法的全面解析，培养学生深入分析、严谨推理、勇于创新的能力。其内容包括实数和复数、欧几里得空间的点集拓扑、度量空间、拜耳范畴定理、微分与积分、隐函数定理及其应用、函数序列与级数、连续函数空间、傅立叶级数、傅立叶变换与拉普拉斯变换、向量场理论与应用、Stokes定理与散度定理。','This course is for students who have taken the courses Calculus Extended I and II (MAT1011 and MAT1012). This course is designed for outstanding students who are interested in mathematics or applied mathematics, and it aims to build a solid foundation of analysis for students. This course is a high-level course with high degree of difficulty, and it intends to cultivate innovative mathematics talents. The contents and teaching methods of this course emphasize comprehensive understanding of the theory and methods of mathematical analysis, and cultivate students'' ability of in-depth analysis, rigorous reasoning, and courage to innovate. Topics include the systems of real and complex numbers, point set topology in Euclidean spaces, metric spaces, Baire category theorem, differentiation and integration, implicit function theorem and its application, sequences and series of functions, space of continuous functions, Fourier series, Fourier transform and Laplace transform, vector field theory and applications, Stokes’ and DivergenceTheorems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101972,'MAT2240','人工智能中的应用数学','Applied Mathematics for AI','MAT - 数学','2240','M',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','MAT1001 Calculus I, MAT1002 Calculus II, MAT2040 Linear Algebra','Basic knowledge in MAT3280 Probability Theory, and basic programming skills (Python will be used in this course)','本课程是一门基础课程，旨在为学生提供理解人工智能 (AI) 技术所需的数学知识和技能。课程涵盖线性代数、微积分、概率论和统计学等一系列主题，这些主题对于分析和解决人工智能中的复杂问题至关重要。学生将学习如何应用这些数学工具来构建人工智能算法、优化流程并做出数据驱动的决策。课程还将向学生介绍人工智能研究和应用中常用的数值方法和计算技术。通过课堂讲授、问题解决辅导和动手计算练习相结合的方式，学生将为人工智能领域的高级研究和职业发展奠定坚实的数学基础。','This course is a foundational course designed to provide students with the mathematical knowledge and skills essential for understanding artificial intelligence (AI) techniques. The course covers a range of topics from linear algebra, calculus, probability, and statistics, which are crucial for analyzing and solving complex problems in AI. Students will learn how to apply these mathematical tools to build AI algorithms, optimize processes, and make data-driven decisions. The course will also introduce students to numerical methods and computational techniques that are commonly used in AI research and applications. Through a combination of lectures, problem-solving tutorials, and hands-on computational exercises, students will develop a strong mathematical foundation necessary for advanced studies and careers in AI.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
