2025-26 Term 2','MAT3007 or MAT3007H','','本课程旨在深入介绍连续最优化领域。课程内容包括最优条件，梯度法，牛顿法，凸集与凸函数，对偶理论，以及先进一阶算法等。同时将讨论机器学习，统计，信号处理等领域的应用。','This course aims to present an in-depth introduction to the field of continuous optimization. Course materials cover optimality conditions, gradient method, Newton’s method, convex sets and convex functions, duality theory, and advanced first-order algorithms. Applications in machine learning, statistics, signal processing etc. will also be discussed.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101984,'MAT3240','数值线性代数','Numerical Linear Algebra','MAT - 数学','3240','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','(MAT1001 or MAT1010 or MAT1011); (MAT2040 or MAT2042 or MAT2041 or MAT2041A or MAT3040 or MAT3042)','','本课程介绍数值线性代数的基本概念和方法。内容包括线性代数和数值计算的基础知识、矩阵正交分解、三角分解的数值方法、计算复杂度分析、数值稳定性、线性系统求解的直接法和迭代法、特征值问题求解的Krylov子空间方法、Matlab编程，以及在机器学习和偏微分方程中的应用。','This course introduces the fundamental concepts and methods of numerical linear algebra. Topics include the basics of linear algebra and numerical computation; numerical methods for the orthogonal decompositions and triangular decompositions of matrices; computational complexity analysis and numerical stability; direct and iterative methods for solving linear systems; Krylov subspace methods for eigenvalue problems; MATLAB programming; and applications in machine learning and partial differential equations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(101985,'MAT3250','数学博弈论导论','Introduction of Mathematical Game Theory','MAT - 数学','3250','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','MAT2050 Mathematical Analysis, MAT2040 Linear Algebra','','博弈论的研究起始于约翰·冯·诺依曼的开创性论文，他在其中利用布劳威尔不动点定理证明了二维零和博弈中的极小极大定理。此后，博弈论发展成为一个多学科交叉的领域，广泛应用于数学、工程以及社会科学等多个学科。本课程属于应用数学范畴，旨在运用严谨的数学工具对博弈论中的基本概念进行证明，例如极小极大定理、纳什均衡的存在性、纳什议价解等。选修本课程的学生应已完成数学分析和线性代数的相关课程','Game Theory was initiated by John von Neumann’s seminal paper in proving the Minimax Theorem in 2-person zero-sum games using the Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem. It has since developed into a multi-disciplinary subject with wide applications in mathematics, engineering and social science. This is a course in applied mathematics. It aims to apply rigorous mathematical tools to provide proofs of basic concepts in game theory such as Minimax Theorem, Existence of Nash Equilibrium, Nash Bargaining solutions etc. Students should have completed a course on mathematical analysis and linear algebra before enrolling in this course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
