2026-27 Term 1','-	Required: MAT1001 Calculus I, MAT1002 Calculus II, MAT3280 Probability Theory (or equivalent)
-	Basic knowledge of the following is recommended but not required: Ordinary Differential Equations, Mathematical Analysis, Real Analysis','None','随机微分方程（SDEs）模型变量在噪声和随机扰动影响下的演化。在生物学，物理学，化学和风险管理等不同学科中都能找到许多应用。 常微分方程的经典适定性理论不适用于随机微分方程。随机积分的发展为解决这样的方程给出方法（伊藤积分）。 这导致了许多关于在随机性下发展的变量的新的和有趣的见解，这些发现已经有许多真实世界的应用。 本课程是对随机微分方程的介绍。','Stochastic differential equations (SDEs) model quantities that evolve under the influence of noise and random perturbations. They have found many applications in diverse disciplines such as biology, physics, chemistry and the management of risk. Classic well-posedness theory for ordinary differential equations does not apply to SDEs. However, stochastic integration allows to develop a new calculus for such equations (Ito calculus). This leads to many new and interesting insights about quantities that evolve under randomness, that have found many real-world applications. This course is a introduction to stochastic differential equations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102002,'MAT4600','应用范畴论','Applied Category Theory','MAT - 数学','4600','M',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MAT2040 Linear Algebra','','本课程介绍范畴论，和一些在数学、计算机科学、电子工程的应用。内容包括：范畴、函子、自然变换、伴随、通用属性、极限、米田引理、接线图、信号流图、层和单子。','This course provides an introduction to category theory, which is a versatile field with applications in mathematics, computer science, electronic engineering, chemistry, linguistics, and social science. Category theory explores the relationships among mathematical objects rather than their internal structure. It was first developed to formulate universal properties and natural isomorphisms in abstract algebra.

Throughout the course, students will explore a variety of mathematical tools, such as categories, functors, natural transformations, adjoints, universal properties, limits and colimits, symmetric monoidal categories, wiring diagrams, signal flow graphs, sheaves and cosheaves, spans and cospans, and monads. These tools provide a powerful framework for expressing and analyzing high-level relationships among concepts, making it possible to prove theorems across a broad range of fields.

Category theory has also been found to have emerging applications in AI and neural networks. In computer science, it has practical applications in databases, functional programming, and lambda calculus. By the end of the course, students will have a solid understanding of the fundamentals of category theory and be able to apply these tools to solve problems in a variety of fields.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102003,'MAT5110','测度论与积分','Measure Theory and Integration','MAT - 数学','5110','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2','None','None','本研究生课程讨论一般的测度论和积分论。内容包括一般测度空间：可测集合与测度空间、外测度诱导的测度；常用的测度：Lebesgue 测度、Borel 测度、Hausdorff 测度、符号测度；一般测度空间上的积分：可测函数、Egoroff 定理与 Lusin 定理、控制收敛定理、Radon-Nickodym 定理、乘积测度与 Fubini定理；一般的 L^p 空间:完备性、Riesz 表示定理、对偶、弱收敛。','This graduate-level course discusses the general theory of measure and integration. Topics include general measure spaces: measurable sets and measure spaces, measures induced by an outer measure; particular measures: Lebesgue measure, Borel measure, Hausdorff measure, signed measure; integration over general measure spaces: measurable functions, Egoroff theorem and Lusin theorem, dominated convergence theorem, Radon-Nikodym theorem; product measures and Fubini theorem; general L^p spaces: completeness, Riesz representation theorem, duality, and weak convergence.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102004,'MAT5120','泛函分析','Functional Analysis','MAT - 数学','5120','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','','','本研究生课程将深入探讨泛函分析的关键概念和基本结果。泛函分析是数学的一个分支，研究函数空间及其上的算子。本课程强调严格的证明、理论理解以及这些定理的实际应用意义。学生将培养理解和进行泛函和线性分析研究所必需的技能。课程内容包括：Hahn-Banach 定理、一致有界性原理、开映射定理、闭图像定理、弱拓扑和弱*拓扑、Hilbert 空间、Hill-Yosida 理论和 Sobolev 空间。','This graduate-level course provides an in-depth exploration of key concepts and foundational results in functional analysis, the branch of mathematics that studies spaces of functions and the operators acting upon them. The course emphasizes rigorous proofs, theoretical understanding, and the practical implications of these theorems. Students will develop the skills necessary to understand and conduct research in functional and linear analysis. Topics include Hahn-Banach theorem, uniform boundedness principle, open mapping theorem, closed graph theorem, weak and weak* topologies, Hilbert spaces, Hill-Yosida theory and Sobolev spaces.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
