2026-27 Term 1','This course builds upon foundational knowledge in numerical analysis and mathematical methods typically acquired at the undergraduate level. Students are expected to have completed coursework equivalent to Numerical Analysis (e.g., CUHK Shenzhen''s MAT-4001), which provides essential grounding in fundamental numerical techniques including computer arithmetic, computational error analysis, convergence and stability of numerical algorithms, solution methods for nonlinear equations and linear systems, interpolation, numerical differentiation and integration, as well as basic approximation theory. While this course assumes familiarity with these core numerical concepts, it significantly extends beyond traditional numerical analysis by introducing advanced analytical approximation methods that transition students from purely computational approaches to sophisticated asymptotic and perturbation techniques for solving complex problems where standard numerical methods may be insufficient or ine','None.','MAT5620是一门研究生课程，旨在培养学生掌握现代科研与工程应用中所需的高级分析与计算工具。课程系统讲授渐近展开、摄动方法、边界层分析和多尺度建模等核心方法，强调在传统数值方法受限时构建近似解析解的能力。课程特色在于融合人工智能与科学计算，引导学生批判性评估AI生成代码，并提升调试、优化及科研思辨能力。通过理论讲授、实践演练与协作研讨，学生将建立起贯通数学严谨性与物理、工程、数据科学等跨学科应用的方法论框架，为前沿研究奠定坚实基础。','MAT5620 is an graduate-level course, aiming to equip them with sophisticated analytical and computational tools essential for modern scientific research and engineering applications. The course systematically covers core methodologies such as asymptotic expansions, perturbation methods, boundary layer analysis, and multiscale modeling, emphasizing the construction of approximate analytical solutions in scenarios where conventional numerical methods fall short. A distinctive feature of the course is its integration of artificial intelligence with scientific computing, guiding students to critically evaluate AI-generated code and enhance their debugging, optimization, and scientific reasoning skills. Through a balanced blend of theoretical instruction, hands-on practice, and collaborative discussion, students develop a methodological framework that bridges mathematical rigor with interdisciplinary applications in physics, engineering, data science, and beyond laying a solid foundation for cutting-edge research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102011,'MAT6110','偏微分方程（一）','Partial Differential Equations I','MAT - 数学','6110','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
