(102018,'MAT6330','代數拓撲','Algebraic Topology','MAT - 数学','6330','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','MAT4002 Introduction to geometry and topology, or permission of
instructor.','You are required to make up on your own on whatever is missing in your
background.','课程覆盖基本代数拓扑。','The course will cover most of the fundamental topics
of algebraic topology. We start with concept of
homotopy, and fundamental groups of topological
spaces. All maps are taken to be continuous
throughout the course, and properties of topological
spaces are studied up to homeomorphism or
homotopy. We study the basic concepts of
representing topological objects by algebraic objects,
such as groups and rings, and modules. This is done
through the construction of fundamental group and 
(co)homology (singular, simplicial and cellular)
theory. The advantage of algebraization is
demonstrated with powerful theorems such as,
Lefschetz fixed point theorem, Poincare-Lefschetz
duality. In addition, we will also cover some topics of
universality of these constructions, such as UCH etc.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
