(102027,'MAT7220','表徵論專題','','MAT - 数学','7220','M',3.00,7000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','Basic knowledge in Abstract Algebra and Lie groups.','','表示理论是通过线性变换对向量空间的作用来理解代数结构。它起源于傅里叶分析和在数学和理论物理的许多最新发展中起着重要作用。最突出的部分是还原群的表示理论，它是纯数学和数学物理中代数、几何和分析相互作用的中心。本课程的主题每年都有所不同。','Representation theory is to understand the algebraic structure through its action on vector spaces by linear transformations. It originates from the Fourier analysis and plays important role in many recent developments of mathematics and theoretical physics. The most prominent part is representation theory of reductive groups, which is at the center of the interaction of algebra, geometry and analysis in pure mathematics and mathematical physics. The topics of this course varies from year to year and is focused on the central problems in representation theory related to the Langlands program. Those problems are typically associated with classifying irreducible unitary representations, the orbit method, unipotent representations, Dirac series, endoscopy and Langlands functoriality.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
