2026-27 Term 1','','','This course introduces the basics of information theory and channel coding. It covers Shannon''s information measures; Entropy rate of a stationary process; the source coding theorem; Kraft inequality; Huffman code; redundancy of a prefix code; rate-distortion theory and universal data compression. It also covers the capacity for different channel models (e.g., discrete memoryless channels and Gaussian channels), finite field theory, design and analysis of error correcting codes (with a focus on linear block codes), introduction to network information theory.','This course introduces the basics of information theory and channel coding. It covers Shannon''s information measures; Entropy rate of a stationary process; the source coding theorem; Kraft inequality; Huffman code; redundancy of a prefix code; rate-distortion theory and universal data compression. It also covers the capacity for different channel models (e.g., discrete memoryless channels and Gaussian channels), finite field theory, design and analysis of error correcting codes (with a focus on linear block codes), introduction to network information theory.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
