2025-26 Term 2','None','None','随着医学领域的技术应用逐步增加，本课程旨在为医学生提供统计学及数据科学基础知识，并概述机器学习、人工智能、大数据、生物信息学和生物医学工程现状及它们在医学领域中的应用。','With the increasing use of technology in the field of medicine, this course is designed to give students in the medical school the foundations of physics and its application to the human body. Additionally, the course provides an overview of the current state of machine learning, artificial intelligence, big data, bioinformatics, biomedical engineering and bionanotechnology, and their applications in the field of medicine.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102180,'MED1100','伦理与专业（一）','Bioethics and Professionalism I','MED - Medicine','1100','M',1.00,1000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','None','None','临床医学专业将提供为期六年的伦理与专业课程。

在本课程的学习过程中，学生将学习伦理学术语、资源，以及伦理分析主要概念的相关知识。本课程将通过伦理学的历史基础、公共卫生伦理，及研究伦理，来探究伦理学的主要问题。

课堂上的案例讨论能够有效地培养学生解决伦理问题的能力，从而帮助学生为以后临床情境中存在的复杂现象做好充分的准备。

此外，这门课程还介绍了什么是职业素养，以及它对医学生在学习期间和未来从事医疗行业时的意义。我们期望学生遵守职业素养方面的行为准则，导师和同学将追踪学生在医学院整个学习过程中的行为。同时我们会给学生提供在线课程及活动，以进一步提升他们对职业素养的理解（包括行医准则及人体标本的学习）。','The bioethics and professionalism curriculum will be offered throughout the six-year Clinical Medicine programme.

This course provides an overview of the major areas of bioethics. Students will gain familiarity with the terminology, resources, and major frameworks of ethical analysis in the field. Issues that will be examined and analyzed include historical foundations of bioethics, public health ethics, and research ethics.

Extensive use of case discussions will help to develop ethical problem-solving skills in order to prepare students for complex social dynamics present in clinical scenarios.

Additionally, this course provides an introduction to what professionalism is and what it means for medical students during their medical schooling and as future health care professionals. Students will be expected to follow the code of conduct which outlines expectations of professionalism, and they will be tracked by instructors and potentially peers throughout their entire medical schooling. Students will be given short online modules and activities to further develop their understanding on professionalism (including the code of conduct and learning from human specimens).','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102181,'MED1200','医生与病人','Doctor and Patient','MED - Medicine','1200','M',1.00,1000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','None','None','医患关系对于医疗服务至关重要，是一种动态的关系。本课程描述了有效医患关系和社区沟通中的关键因素，同时向学生介绍了健康和疾病的生物学、社会学和伦理学的知识。

本课程由两部分组成。

第一部分通过对医生的一系列拜访，观察、了解并获得医生面对病人时表现的洞察力，同时观察并理解家庭医生在社区和医患关系中的作用。

第二部分通过对新生儿家庭进行纵向追踪、观察和与新生儿家庭进行互动，理解家庭的社会经济背景、健康观念与措施、家庭为新生儿做出的调整、社会与社区的支持等因素对儿童发展的影响。学生将持续与新生儿家庭进行接触和互动直到儿童满 3 岁，观察其家庭动态、儿童发展、健康观念以及社会、医疗和社区的支持。

课程通过一系列讲座、小组辅导、演示、拜访社区的家庭医生，以及在病房或社区对目标家庭进行随访等形式开展。','The doctor and patient relationship is essential to medical care and is a dynamic relationship. This course describes key elements in an effective doctor-patient relationship and in effective communication with the community. The course also introduces students to the biological, social and ethical aspects of health and illness.

The course has two components.

Part I (Family Doctor Attachment) is a series of visits with a medical doctor to provide early clinical exposure to observe, understand and acquire insight into the patient presentation and the role of a family doctor in the community and the doctor-patient relationship.

Part II (Family Follow-up Project) is longitudinal follow-up of a family with a newborn baby in order to observe and interact with a family with a newborn to be able to understand and describe influences on child development e.g. socio-economic background of the family, health beliefs and practices, family adjustment to the newborn, social support, community support, assessment of milestones etc. The student will continue to engage with the family until the child reaches 3 years old and interact, observe family dynamics, child development, health beliefs and social, medical and community support.

This course is delivered by a series of lectures, small group tutorials, presentations, visits to family doctors in the community, and interviews with a family on wards and in the community.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
