2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED1001 Human Structure I
MED1002 Human Structure II','None','人体结构（三）和（四）的重点是人体头颈部解剖学。第一部分介绍颅外结构组织；第二部分重点介绍中枢神经系统组织。该课程通过讲课形式进行知识传授，并辅以解剖实验和其他实践环节进行体验式学习。该课程的授课内容主要为头颈部的不同部位，包括骨组成及相关系统器官，同时着重在血液供应和颅神经支配。接着探讨大脑和脊髓组织和它们对头颈部的控制机制。讨论头部及中枢神经系统的胚胎发育过程，如眼睛、耳朵等感觉器官的形成。课程开始，先讲授下肢的局部解剖学，结合已讲授的背部与上肢 (人体结构（一）背部，作为连接中枢神经系统（CNS）与周围神经系统（PNS）的桥梁。本课程有助于增强学生对身体区域的整体复杂性理解。','The primary focus of Human Structure III & IV is the anatomy of the head and neck in the human body. First part introduces organization of the extra-cranial structures; second part focuses on the organization of the central nervous system (CNS). The course is taught through lectures, supplemented with experiential learning in dissecting laboratory and other practical sessions. Different regions of the head and neck, including the bony components and associated organ systems are examined. The detailed blood supply and cranial nerve innervation are emphasized. This is followed by the study of the organization of the brain and spinal cord, and their control of the structures of the head and neck. The embryonic development of the head and central nervous system including sense organs such as the eye and ear are discussed. At the beginning of the Human Structure III course, regional anatomy of the lower limb is taught, together with that of the back and upper limb (Human Structure I), as a bridge between the CNS and the peripheral nerve system (PNS). The course helps to enhance students’ understanding in the overall complexity of this body region.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
