MED2001 Human Structure III','None','人体结构（三）和（四）的重点是人体头颈部解剖学。第一部分介绍颅外结构组织；第二部分重点介绍中枢神经系统组织。该课程通过讲课形式进行知识传授，并辅以解剖实验和其他实践环节进行体验式学习。该课程的授课内容主要为头颈部的不同部位，包括骨组成及相关系统器官，同时着重在血液供应和颅神经支配。接着探讨大脑和脊髓组织和它们对头颈部的控制机制。讨论头部及中枢神经系统的胚胎发育过程，如眼睛、耳朵等感觉器官的形成。课程开始部分，先讲授背部，上肢和下肢的局部解剖学，作为连接中枢神经系统（CNS）与周围神经系统（PNS）的桥梁，并涵盖四肢中的相关结构。本课程有助于提高学生对身体区域的整体复杂性理解。','The primary focus of Human Structure III & IV is the anatomy of the head and neck in the human body. First part introduces organization of the extra-cranial structures; second part focuses on the organization of the central nervous system (CNS). The course is taught through lectures, supplemented with experiential learning in dissecting laboratory and other practical sessions. Different regions of the head and neck, including the bony components and associated organ systems are examined. The detailed blood supply and cranial nerve innervation is emphasized. This is followed by the study of the organization of the brain and spinal cord, and their control of the structures of the head and neck. The embryonic development of the head and central nervous system including sense organs such as the eye and ear is discussed. At the beginning of the course, regional anatomy of the back, upper and lower limbs is taught as a bridge between the CNS and the peripheral nerve system (PNS), along with its associated structures in the limbs. The course helps to enhance students’ understanding in the overall complexity of this body region.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102184,'MED2003E','组织学与显微诊断实践','','MED - Medicine','2003E','M',2.00,2000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Summer','N/A','The students show interest in Histology in clinical application and eager to improve scientific writing.','本课程为每年6月举办的为期5天的夏季选修课，通过整合实验室操作与临床病理学，提供“从实验室到临床”的高级组织学探索。课程面向具备基础人体组织知识的1-2年级临床医学专业学生（每年最多40人），重点培养显微镜操作、组织切片手工制备能力，以及区分正常与病变组织（如炎症、恶性肿瘤）的能力。

课程邀请香港中文大学（深圳）附属第二医院2名客座病理学家参与，学员将在配备显微镜-相机混合系统及大量正常与病变组织切片的实验室中，了解从组织取样到病理报告出具的临床流程，并在1-2名教员的指导下分析切片。

课程以竞争性项目收尾：学员将选择疾病模型、采集显微证据并撰写论文，在专家指导下衔接基础形态学研究与临床诊断应用。','This annual five-day summer elective, held in June, offers an advanced, comprehensive "bench-to-bedside" exploration of histology through integrated laboratory proficiency and clinical pathology. Designed for Years 1-2 CMED students with foundational human tissue knowledge (max 40 students/year), the course focuses on mastering microscopy techniques, manual histological slide preparation, and interpreting abnormal structural patterns, specifically distinguishing normal tissue architecture from pathological states (e.g., inflammation, malignancy/neoplasia).
Collaborating with 2 guest pathologists from The Second Affiliated Hospital of The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen, participants gain insight into clinical workflows (tissue sampling to pathological reports) in general-purpose laboratories equipped with Microscope-Camera Hybrid Systems and extensive normal/pathological human tissue slides. Under supervision of 1-2 faculty members, they use these systems to analyze slides.
The program culminates in a competitive project: students select disease models, capture microscopic evidence, and draft scientific articles, bridging basic morphological study and clinical diagnostic application under expert supervision.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
