2025-26 Term 2','MED1011 Human function I, MED1012 Human function II','N/A','本科探讨药物基本机转，包括药效学，药动力学，临床用药及药物副作用。本科学生应完成基本解剖、生理、及生物化学等学科才能理解本科的药理概念。协同本课程的基础知识以及高年级的课程（如病理学），学生可以针对性提出临床问题的主要用药方案，以及获取对药物效应的基本认知。

(先修科目﹕MED1011, MED1012)','This course provides students with an understanding of the principles of drug action including pharmacodynamics (mechanisms of pharmacological actions), pharmacokinetics, clinical indications, and adverse effects of major classes of drugs. Since pharmacology is built upon the understanding of basic human structure and functions, students should have completed basic courses in anatomy, physiology, and biochemistry to understand the pharmacological concepts described in this course. Together with advanced courses such as General Pathology in Year 3 and a foundation of information already assimilated in this course, students are able to specifically address the clinical choice and use of essential drugs in patients and the monitoring of their effects. (prerequisite: MED1011, MED1012)','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
