MED1022 Biochemistry and Organic Chemistry II','None','课程包括先天性免疫、获得性免疫、黏膜免疫及免疫耐受等基本免疫学概念。本课程还将讲授传染病、自身免疫学疾病、免疫缺陷、过敏、移植和肿瘤等临床疾病背后的免疫学原理。通过修读此课程，学生将掌握免疫学基本概念，和机体防御病原体及肿瘤细胞的基础知识，以便学习其他进阶课程，比如第三学年的病理学。','The course will cover general concepts of innate immunity, adaptive immunity, mucosal immunity, and immune tolerance. The immunological basis for various clinical diseases, such as infectious diseases, autoimmune diseases, immunodeficiency, allergy, transplantation and cancer, will also be covered. By taking this course, students are expected to gain the general concepts of immunity and how the host deals with microbial pathogens and tumor cells, setting up the stage for their studies of advanced courses, such as General Pathology in Year 3.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102191,'MED2100','伦理与专业（二）','Bioethics and Professionalism II','MED - Medicine','2100','M',1.00,2000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED1100 Bioethics and Professionalism I','None','本课程向学生介绍了生物伦理学领域的基础理论、概念和历史发展。课程中涉及的主题包括：
•	保健资源分配的公正性和在现代都市环境中公平地提供保健服务；
•	生命开始和结束时的伦理考虑；
•	青少年保健；
•	医生的责任和病人的权利；
•	对平衡个人自由、公共健康和公共安全的关注；
•	新兴技术发展中的争议。
此外，这门课程持续介绍了职业素养，以及它对医学生在学习期间和未来从事医疗行业时的意义。我们期望学生遵守职业素养方面的行为准则，导师和同学将追踪学生在医学院整个学习过程中的行为。同时我们会给学生提供在线课程及活动，以进一步提升他们对职业素养的理解（包括公共卫生方面及医患关系）。','This course introduces students to foundational theories, concepts and historical developments in the field of bioethics. Topics covered in the course include:
•	justice in the allocation of health care resources and fair delivery of healthcare in a modern metropolitan setting
•	ethical considerations at the beginning and the end of life
•	adolescent healthcare
•	physician responsibilities and patient right
•	concerns for balancing individual liberties, public health and public safety
•	controversies in the development of emerging technologies
Additionally, this course provides further introduction to what professionalism is and what it means for medical students during their medical schooling and as future health care professionals. Students will be expected to follow the code of conduct which outlines the expectations of professionalism, and they will be tracked by instructors and potentially peers throughout their entire medical schooling. Students will also be given short online modules and activities to further develop their understanding on professionalism (including public health professionalism and the doctor patient relationship).','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102192,'MED2200','医生与病人','','MED - Medicine','2200','M',1.00,2000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2','None','None','醫患關係對於醫療服務至關重要，是一種動態的關係。本課程描述了有效醫患關係和社區溝通中的關鍵因素，同時還向學生介紹了健康和疾病的生物學、社會學和倫理學等知識。

本課程由兩部分組成。

第一部分通過對醫生的一系列拜訪，觀察、瞭解並獲得醫生面對病人時表現的洞察力，同時觀察並理解家庭醫生在社區和醫患關係中的作用。

第二部分通過對新生兒家庭進行縱向跟蹤、觀察和互動，從而理解家庭的社會經濟背景、健康觀念與措施、家庭針對新生兒做出的調整措施、社區與社會支援等因素對兒童發展的影響。（這部分已從一年級開始）。隨著孩子滿三歲，學生還需繼續與家庭互動並觀察家庭動態、兒童發展、健康理念以及社會、醫療和社區支援服務。

課程通過講座、小組輔導、演示、拜訪社區醫生，以及在病房或社區對家庭進行訪談等形式開展。','The doctor and patient relationship is essential to medical care and is a dynamic relationship. This course describes key elements in an effective doctor-patient relationship and in effective communications with the community. The course also introduces students to the biological, social and ethical aspects of health and illness.

The course has two components.

Part I (Family Doctor Attachment) is a series of visits with a medical doctor to observe, understand and acquire insight into the patient presentation and the role of a family doctor in the community and the doctor-patient relationship.

Part II (Family Follow-up Project) is longitudinal follow-up of a family with a new born baby in order to observe and interact with a family with a newborn to be able to understand and describe influences on child development e.g. socio-economic background of the family, health beliefs and practices, family adjustment to the newborn, social support, community support, assessment of milestones etc. (This part started at the end of Year 1). The student will continue to engage with the family until the child reaches 3-year-old and interact, observe family dynamics, child development, health beliefs and social, medical and community support.

This course is delivered by a series of lectures, small group tutorials, presentations, visits to family doctors in the community, and interviews with a family on wards and in the community.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102193,'MED2301A','人工智能医学的计算机科学基础（一）','','MED - Medicine','2301A','M',2.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This course welcomes all Y2-Y5 students in the School of Medicine who passed all their courses in Year 1 (including School Package and Major required).','None','由于人工智能是以计算机科学为基础建立，本课程的目的在于为医学生学习人工智能教授必要的编程技能和计算机科学基础知识。以人工智能医学为驱动，本课程将讲授Python编程基础，计算机组成原理和体系结构，操作系统，计算机网络和数据库。通过课上课下编程实践，以及学期实践项目，培养学生的实践能力。课程安排在晚上，以便更多学生参与。','Since artificial intelligence (AI) is built based on computer science, this course is designed to introduce essential computer science concepts as the foundation for medical students to learn AI. Motivated by AI in medicine, this course will introduce Python basic programming, computer organization and architecture, operating systems, computer networks, and databases. Through in-class and out-of-class programming exercises, as well as a semester-long project, students will develop practical skills. The course is scheduled into evenings to maximize participation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102194,'MED2302A','人工智能医学的计算机科学基础（二）','','MED - Medicine','2302A','M',2.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','(MED1031+MED1032) or MAT1008 for Clinical Medicine students;
MAT1001 for other majors’ students in School of Medicine','None','人工智能（AI）在医学中的应用依赖于坚实的计算机科学基础。本课程面向不同专业、不同年级的学生开放，旨在为学习者提供必要的计算机科学知识，以便深入理解并应用人工智能技术于医疗领域。课程以医学应用为背景，系统讲授数据结构、算法设计与分析以及 Python 编程。为适应不同学生的学业安排，课程采用混合教学模式，结合专题研讨与实操工作坊，课堂会在傍晚进行，以便更多学生参与。通过这种灵活的学习安排，学生将掌握数组、链表、栈、队列、树、映射、堆以及多种排序算法的实现与应用，并学习递归、动态规划、贪心算法、回溯等典型算法设计范式。课程结束后，学生将能够结合技术能力与临床视角，解决人工智能驱动的医学问题。','Artificial Intelligence (AI) in medicine relies on a solid understanding of computer science principles. This course equips students—regardless of major or year of study—with the essential computational foundations to engage meaningfully with AI technologies in healthcare. Using medical applications as the motivating context, students will explore core topics including data structures, algorithm design and analysis, and Python programming. To accommodate diverse academic timetables, the course is delivered in a hybrid format, combining seminars with hands-on workshops. The course is scheduled into evenings to maximize participation. Through this flexible learning structure, participants will develop the ability to implement and apply arrays, linked lists, stacks, queues, trees, maps, heaps, and sorting algorithms, as well as master algorithmic paradigms such as recursion, dynamic programming, greedy algorithms, and backtracking. By the end, students will be prepared to approach AI-driven problem solving with both technical proficiency and clinical relevance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
