MED2050 Genetics and Bioinformatics','','本课程贯穿临床医学六年制培养全程，系统地介绍生物伦理学核心领域。学生将掌握专业术语、学术资源及伦理分析框架。在第三学年，课程将在前两年基础知识基础上深化探讨道德理论、脑死亡、医助自杀、残障与机能增强等前沿议 题。选择题测试将基于课堂课件生成。
课程后期将系统地讲授医学法律专题，涵盖医患关系、患者行为能力、知情同意、医疗保密、医疗过失与疏忽、法医病理学相关法律问题及临终医疗等内容，使学生深入理解法律体系，明确医师作为守法公民在维护正义、保护弱势群体及预防犯罪等方面的社会责任。
此外，医学职业素养的培养将贯穿本课程全程。学生将通过简短的在线学习模块或实践活动来进一步加深对职业素养的理解，内容涉及如：职业精神与患者权益倡导、医患关系等主题。学生需遵守行为准则（其中明确了职业素养的具体要
求），并通过师生评估机制全程被持续追踪评估。','The bioethics and professionalism curriculum will be offered throughout the six-year Clinical Medicine programme. This course provides an overview of the major areas of bioethics. Students will gain familiarity with the terminology, resources, and major frameworks of ethical analysis in the field. Year 3 the course builds on the foundational knowledge introduced during Year 1 and 2, by covering advanced topics and contemporary issues, including moral theories, brain death, physician-assisted suicide, disability and enhancement and other topical issues. Formative Multiple Choice Questions will be based on lecture material.
Topics related to Law and Medicine will then be covered in a series of lectures in the latter part of the course. Areas considered include the doctor-patient relationship, patient capacity, consent, confidentiality, medical error and negligence, forensic pathology and related medical-legal issues and end of life care. Students gain insights into the legal system. Students should learn their important role in society as physicians and as law-abiding citizens, in upholding justice and being a role model for others, in protecting the weak and vulnerable and in the prevention of crime.
Additionally, this course continues students'' education on professionalism in the medical field. Students will be given short online modules and activities to further develop their understanding on professionalism, covering topics such as Professionalism and advocating for patients, and The Doctor Patient Relationship. Students will be expected to follow the code of conduct which outlines expectations of professionalism, and they will be tracked by instructors and potentially peers throughout their entire medical schooling.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
