(102206,'MED3301A','临床人工智能医学（一）','','MED - Medicine','3301A','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MED2301A or MED2302A or AIE1001 or CSC1001.

This course is open to all students in the School of Medicine and the School of Artificial Intelligence who have met the prerequisites.','None','人工智能已广泛渗透并深刻影响临床医学的各个领域。本课程的目标在于为学生教授必要的人工智能基础知识以及如何将其转化到临床实践中。课程内容包括知识表示和推理，搜索与优化，计算智能，机器学习等基础知识，并结合临床医学场景介绍其典型应用。通过课上课下编程实践和学期实践项目，培养学生运用人工智能方法分析和解决临床问题的实践能力。课程安排在晚上，以便更多学生参与。','Artificial intelligence (AI) has widely influenced various fields of clinical medicine. This course aims to provide students with essential foundational knowledge of AI and to teach them how to translate it into clinical practice. The course covers fundamental topics such as knowledge representation and reasoning, search and optimization, computational intelligence, machine learning, and deep learning, while introducing typical applications in clinical scenarios. Through in-class and after-class programming practice, as well as a term project, the course cultivates students’ practical ability to use AI methods to analyze and solve the clinical problems. The course is scheduled in the evening to facilitate participation by more students.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102207,'MED3800S','微创外科基础课','','MED - Medicine','3800S','M',2.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102208,'MED4010','预防医学与全科医学','Preventive Medicine and General Practice','MED - Medicine','4010','M',9.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','门诊','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED3001 General Pathology    MED3200 Communication Skills I    MED3002 Systemic Pathology    MED3011 Basic Clinical Radiology    MED3100 Bioethics and Professionalism    MED3003 Chemical Pathology    MED3031 Clinical Microbiology    MED3300 Clinical Skills    MED3020 Junior Medical Practice    MED3021 Junior Surgical Practice','','预防医学和全科医学（PMGP）是临床医学课程第四年的四个学科之一。 PMGP课程由为期10周的综合教学组成，旨在向学生传授当代中国社区和家庭医学的内容。

PMGP课程有五个组成部分，包括（1）预防和家庭医学实践、（2）流行病学和生物统计学、（3）公共卫生实践、（4）职业与环境健康和（5）中医学基础。

在本模块的前四周，学生将参加一系列讲座、研讨会、案例式学习(Case-Based Learning, CBL)以及技能工作坊；随后，学生将进行为期六周的临床见习和社区参访。

在整个课程中，学生将通过小组分享、工作坊等进行持续评估。课程亦设有课程结束考试和年终考试为学生做总结性评估。','Preventive Medicine and General Practice (PMGP) is one of the four modules of Year 4 of the Clinical Medicine Program. PMGP course consists of 10 weeks of integrated teaching to educate students different aspects of Community and Family medicine in contemporary China.

There are five components in PMGP course, including (1) Preventive and Family Medicine, (2) Epidemiology and Biostatistics, (3) Public Health Medicine, (4) Occupation and Environmental Health and (5) Traditional Chinese Medicine.

Students will be engaged in a series of lectures, seminars, Case-Based Learning tutorials and skill workshops in the first four weeks of the module, then rotate through six weeks of clinical clerkship and community visits.

Students will be assessed continuously throughout the module through tutorial and workshop presentations. Summative assessment will comprise an end-of-module examination and an end-of-year examination.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102209,'MED4011','妇产科学','Obstetrics & Gynaecology','MED - Medicine','4011','M',9.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','门诊','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED3001 General Pathology    MED3200 Communication Skills I    MED3011 Basic Clinical Radiology    MED3100 Bioethics and Professionalism    MED3003 Chemical Pathology    MED3020 Junior Medical Practice    MED3021 Junior Surgical Practice    MED3031 Clinical Microbiology    MED3300 Clinical Skills    MED3002 Systemic Pathology','None','妇产科的学习为期 9 周。该课程模块的大部分时间（8 周）将在以下地点进行临床轮转：

1)深圳市宝安区妇幼保健院妇产科
2)南山人民医院妇产科
3)其他教学医院，如，深圳中山妇产医院-生殖医学，深圳新风和睦家医院等。

除了临床轮转外，课程将通过现场讲座、辅导、基于案例的讨论和临床演示/床边教学来涵盖核心课程材料。

临床轮转将涵盖以下主题：

1. 产前门诊和病房轮转；学生将了解正常怀孕、胎儿发育，并获得进行产科检查的技能。

2. 产房实习；允许学生参与正常怀孕的护理和分娩，以及观察手术分娩。学生将学习分娩和产后期间的常见问题和紧急情况。

3. 妇科门诊和病房轮换；学生将学习常见的妇科疾病和女性生殖道肿瘤。他们还将培养妇科检查技能。重点将放在沟通技巧上，包括记录患者病史和讨论与性和生殖相关的问题。

4. 辅助生殖门诊；学生将研究不孕不育的常见原因，并接触辅助生殖的临床程序和医疗技术。他们还将深入了解患者护理和咨询，培养妇科内分泌的解读技能。

5. 附属医院及社区中心的妇产科服务。学生还将有机会在本模块中轮换到计划生育协会。

总体而言，本模块为妇产科实践所需的知识和临床技能奠定了坚实的基础。','This 9-week module provides a comprehensive introduction to the fields of obstetrics and gynecology. The majority of the module (8 weeks) will be spent on clinical rotations at the following locations:

1)Shenzhen Bao''an Women’s and Children’s Hospital for Obstetrics
2)NanShan People Hospital for Gynecology
3)Other teaching hospitals, such as ShenZhen ZhongShan Obstetrics & Gynecology Hospital for Reproductive Medicine and ShenZhen New Frontier United Family Hospital for outside vists

Beyond the clinical rotations, the core course materials will be covered through onsite lectures, tutorials, case-based discussions, and clinical demonstrations/bedside teaching.

The clinical rotation will cover the following:
1. The antenatal clinic and ward rotation; students will gain an understanding of normal pregnancy, fetal development, and acquire skills in performing obstetric examinations.

2. The labor ward attachment, which allows students to participate in the care and delivery of normal pregnancies, as well as observe operative deliveries. Students will learn about common problems and emergencies in childbirth and the postpartum period.

3. The gynaecological clinic and ward rotation; students will study common gynecological conditions and neoplasms of the female reproductive tract. They will also develop skills in gynecological examination. Emphasis will be placed on communication skills for taking patient histories and discussing issues related to sexuality and reproduction.

4. The assistant reproductive clinic; students will study common cause of infertility and exposure to clinical procedure and medical technologies of assisted reproductive. They will also gain insights into patient care and counseling, develop skills in interpretation of gynecological endocrinology.

5. O&G services in the affiliated hospitals. Students will also have the opportunity to rotate through the Family Planning Association during this module.

Overall, this module provides a solid foundation in the knowledge and clinical skills required for the practice of obstetrics and gynecology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
