2026-27 Term 1','MED3001 General Pathology    MED3200 Communication Skills I    MED3002 Systemic Pathology    MED3011 Basic Clinical Radiology    MED3100 Bioethics and Professionalism Ⅲ   MED3003 Chemical Pathology    MED3031 Clinical Microbiology    MED3300 Clinical Skills    MED3020 Junior Medical Practice    MED3021 Junior Surgical Practice','None','在临床医学专业第四年，将有四个临床模块和一个年终综合模块考试。在为期8周的儿科学临床模块中，学生将参与医院与社区的多种学习模式。医院的轮转包括深圳儿童医院、龙岗区人民医院（香港中文大学(深圳)附属第二医院）和龙岗区妇幼保健院的病房和门诊。学生在附二院所属的社康中心观摩儿科基础医疗。此外，还将在深圳新风和睦家医院及其他儿童医疗中心进行外访。授课模式包括讲座、床旁教学和小组讨论。在导师计划中，学生将就伦理与职业素养相关主题进行演讲，并进行角色扮演以增强沟通技能。导师还通过评估学生病历记录来监测学生在医院轮转及学习情况。','During MED Year 4 there will be four clinical modules and a final integrated Combined Clinical End-of-Year examination. During the 8-week Paediatric Medicine clinical module, students participate in a range of learning activities both in the hospital and in the community. Hospital-based experiences include the wards and outpatient clinics of the Shenzhen Children’s Hospital, Longgang District Hospital (2nd Affiliated Hospital of the Chinese University of Hong Kong-Shenzhen) and the Longgang District Maternity & Child Healthcare Hospital. Students are exposed to primary care paediatrics in the Community Health Centres affiliated to the 2nd Affiliated Hospital. Additional experiential visits are to Shenzhen New Frontier United Family Hospital and other centres responsible for the care of children. Lectures are combined with bedside and tutorial teaching. During the mentorship programme, students will present on topics related to bioethics and professionalism and undertake role plays to enhance their communication skills. Mentors also monitor students’ hospital experience by assessing records of patients that have been clerked.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102211,'MED4013','心理学与精神科学','Psychology & Psychiatry','MED - Medicine','4013','M',9.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','门诊','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED3001 General Pathology    MED3200 Communication Skills I    MED3011 Basic Clinical Radiology    MED3100 Bioethics and Professionalism    MED3003 Chemical Pathology    MED3020 Junior Medical Practice    MED3021 Junior Surgical Practice    MED3031 Clinical Microbiology    MED3300 Clinical Skills    MED3002 Systemic Pathology','None','临床医学专业第四学年将进行4个为期10周的临床模块课程学习及1个综合临床年终考试。这10周的心理学与精神病学课程的目标是使学生:

1.将医学心理学的核心原则应用于临床实践，包括在医疗服务中体现心理学素养，识别心理健康问题、心理应激及心身疾病，恰当运用心理评估、心理治疗与心理咨询，并与受精神障碍影响的患者及其家属进行有效的医患沟通；
2.运用生物—心理—社会模式解释精神障碍，理解并阐明心理、生物和社会因素在精神障碍的发生、临床表现及病程发展中的相互作用；
3.在常见且具有重大公共卫生意义的精神障碍的评估、诊断和管理方面展现基本临床能力，包括采集相关精神科病史、进行精神状态检查、识别风险、形成鉴别诊断，并提出适当的管理方案；
4.描述粤港澳大湾区精神卫生服务的组织与实施方式，包括医院、门诊和社区精神卫生服务， 并认识多学科团队及转诊路径在支持有精神健康需求患者方面的作用。。

教学方式包括课堂授课、研讨会、小组讨论、参加病房查房、病例讨论和门诊观摩,以及参观精神健康设施(包括医院和社区设施)。','During MED Year 4 there will be four clinical modules of 10 weeks each and a final integrated Combined Clinical End-of-Year examination. The goal for this 10-week course in psychology and psychiatry is to enable students to:

1. Apply core principles of medical psychology to clinical practice, including psychological competence in medical care, recognition of mental health problems, psychological stress and psychosomatic conditions, appropriate use of psychological assessment, psychotherapy and psychological counselling, and effective doctor–patient communication with patients and families affected by psychiatric conditions；.
2. Explain psychiatric disorders using a biopsychosocial framework, demonstrating an understanding of the interactions between psychological, biological and social determinants in the development, presentation and course of mental disorders；
3. Demonstrate basic clinical competence in the assessment, diagnosis and management of common psychiatric disorders of major public health importance, including taking a relevant psychiatric history, conducting a mental state examination, identifying risk, formulating differential diagnoses and outlining appropriate management plans；
4. Describe the organisation and delivery of psychiatric services in the Guangdong–Hong Kong–Macao Greater Bay Area, including hospital-based, outpatient and community psychiatric care, and recognise the roles of multidisciplinary teams and referral pathways in supporting patients with mental health needs.

A variety of teaching methods are employed including lectures, seminars, small-group tutorials, attendance of ward rounds, case conferences and outpatient clinics and visits to psychiatric facilities (hospitals and community facility).','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
