MED4011 妇产科学；MED4012 儿科学；MED4013 心理学与精神科学）和四年级学生时间表中提供的复习期之后，进行此评估。 计算的CCE分数包括书面论文（扩展匹配问题和多项选择问题）、结构化临床检查和家庭随访项目的分数。','This assessment occurs after completion of the four module（MED4010Preventive Medicine & General Practice; MED4011 Obstetrics & Gynaecology; MED 4013 Paediatrics Medicine; MED4013 Psychology & Psychiatry ） in Year 4 and a revision period that is provided in the schedule for students in Year 4.  The computed CCE mark includes the marks obtained for a Written Paper (Extended Matching Questions and Multiple Choice Questions), a structured clinical examination and the Family Follow-up Project.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102213,'MED4015','临床医学专业（本科）水平测试','Standardized Competence Test for Clinical Medicine Undergraduates','MED - Medicine','4015','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','门诊','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED3020, MED3021, MED3001, MED3002, MED3003, MED3011, MED3031 MED3100, MED3200, MED3300 (MED Year 3 courses)','','临床医学专业（本科）水平测试（以下简称“国家水平测试”）由国家医学考试中心与全国医学教育发展中心联合发起，为评估五年制临床医学专业本科四年级末学生的能力水平和进一步临床实践学习的知识能力需要而设计的考试，旨在科学测评医学院校医学生学业水平，并为医学生毕业后准备执业医师资格考试提供参考。
水平测试分为医学基本知识考试和临床基本技能考试。
医学基本知识考试包括基础医学（人体解剖学、生物化学、生理学、病理生理学、医学微生物学、医学免疫学、病理学、药理学）、医学人文（医学心理学、医学伦理学和卫生法规）、预防医学（预防医学、医学统计学、临床流行病学、）和临床医学（诊断学和内科学、外科学、妇产科学、儿科学）。考试采用选择题形式，考试时间共180分钟。
临床基本技能考试以OSCE形式进行，主要考查病史采集、体格检查和基本操作技能，同时对沟通交流能力与人文关怀进行评价，共设6个考站，分别是病史采集（第一、二站）、体格检查（第三、四站）和基本操作（第五、六站），考试时间共60分钟。
本课程对中国国籍学生（包括来自香港、澳门和台湾的学生）是必修课程。对于毕业后不计划在中国执业的国际学生，本课程为选修。选择不修读本课程的国际学生需提前提交免修申请，并获得院长出具的证明信。','The Standardized Competency Test For Clinical Medicine Undergraduate in mainland China (hereinafter referred to as the "National Competency Test") is jointly initiated by the National Medical Examination Center and the National Center For Health Professions Education Development. It is designed to evaluate the competency level of fourth-year students in the five-year Clinical Medicine undergraduate program and their knowledge required for further clinical practice learning. The test aims to scientifically assess the academic level of medical students in medical schools and provide a reference for medical students preparing for the National Medical Licensing Examination after graduation.
The National Competency Test consists of two parts: the Medical Knowledge Examination and the Clinical Skills Examination.
The Medical Knowledge Examination consists of four domains: basic medicine (including human anatomy, biochemistry, physiology, pathophysiology, medical microbiology, medical immunology, pathology, pharmacology), medical humanities (including medical psychology, medical ethics, health regulations), preventive medicine (including preventive medicine, medical statistics, clinical epidemiology), and clinical medicine (including internal medicine, surgery, obstetrics and gynecology, pediatrics). The examination is in multiple-choice-question (MCQ) format with a total examination time of 180 minutes.
The Clinical Skills Examination is conducted in OSCE format, assessing history taking, physical examination, and basic clinical procedures, while also evaluating communication skills and humanistic care. It consists of six stations: history taking (Stations 1 and 2), physical examination (Stations 3 and 4), and basic operations (Stations 5 and 6), with a total examination time of 60 minutes.
This course is mandatory for all students with Chinese nationalities (including students from Hong Kong, Macau and Taiwan). It is optional for international students who do not seek to practice in China after graduation. International students who choose not to take this course must submit a undertaking letter for exemption in advance and obtain a justification letter from the Dean.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
