Students may apply for elective attachment in any country, region, and institute by themselves. If they choose overseas, they need to prepare their visa in a timely fashion.
All students must pay their insurance, travel expenses, accommodations, and other expenses.','选修课程安排在第四年（2027年6月至7月）进行，为期4至6周，旨在通过在香港、中国大陆或海外的大学、临床部门或研究项目中进行实习，拓宽学生在教学、研究或临床管理方面的视野。学生可以自行安排实习，也可以通过香港中文大学（深圳）医学院进行安排，并在被接收单位接受后获得正式批准。根据实习类型，指导由临床医生或科学家提供。活动包括参加查房和学习研究技术。学生必须为选修期间购买旅行和健康保险，且其表现将由指导老师进行评估。','The elective, scheduled for 4 to 6 weeks starting at the end of MED 4 (June-July 2027), aims to broaden students'' perspectives in teaching, research, or clinical management through attachments at universities, clinical departments, or research projects in Hong Kong, Mainland China, or overseas. Students can arrange placements themselves or through the School of Medicine, CUHK-Shenzhen, and must obtain formal approval after acceptance by the host institution. Supervision is provided by a clinician or scientist, depending on the attachment type. Activities include attending ward rounds and learning research techniques. Students must secure travel and health insurance for the elective period and will be evaluated by their supervisors based on performance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102215,'MED4020','高级内科实习','Senior Medical Rotation & Practice','MED - Medicine','4020','M',17.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','门诊','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Programme. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme. This course is a continuation of the Junior Medical Practice MED3020 when the didactic teachings should have been completed. 
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','高年级内科临床实习课程让学生深入且全面地接受各个核心内科领域的临床训练。学生将轮流参与一般内科及其各次专科，包括心脏科、内分泌科、呼吸系统科、肠胃肝胆科、神经科、肿瘤科、老人医学科、皮肤科以及急诊医学科的临床实务。课程强调临床评估、鉴别诊断、管理规划、跨专科团队合作，以及以病人为中心的照护。教学方式涵盖病房巡诊、门诊诊疗、床边教学及结构化个案学习，培养学生具备未来医疗实务所需的临床能力与有效决策技巧。','The Senior Medical Clerkship immerses students in comprehensive clinical training across core medical disciplines. Students rotate through internal medicine and subspecialties including cardiology, endocrinology, respiratory medicine, gastroenterology, neurology, oncology, geriatrics, dermatology, and emergency medicine. The course emphasizes clinical assessment, differential diagnosis, management planning, interdisciplinary teamwork, and patient-centered care. Teaching involves clinical ward rounds, outpatient clinics, bedside teaching, and structured case-based learning, enabling students to develop clinical competence and effective decision-making skills essential for future medical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
