2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Program. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Program. This course is a continuation of the Junior Surgical Practice MED3021 when the didactic teachings should have been completed. 
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','高级外科临床实习课程让学生完整接触各项外科核心专科，结合临床知识与手术技能。学生将依序轮科于普外科、血管外科、大肠直肠外科、神经外科、心胸外科、泌尿外科及外科重症医学。课程强调病人评估、围手术期照护、手术观察及急症处理。临床教学方式包含病房巡诊、门诊诊疗、临床技能工作坊及手术室体验，培养学生在多元医疗环境下具备胜任的外科病患管理及完善的临床决策能力。','The Senior Surgical Clerkship provides students comprehensive exposure to core surgical specialties, integrating clinical knowledge and surgical skills. Students rotate through general surgery, vascular, colorectal, neurosurgery, cardiothoracic, urology, and  surgical critical care. Emphasis is placed on patient assessment, perioperative care, operative observation, and emergency management. Clinical teaching includes ward rounds, outpatient clinics, procedural skills workshops, and operative theatre experience, preparing students for competent surgical patient management and informed clinical decision-making in diverse healthcare settings.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102217,'MED4030','临床肿瘤学','Clinical Oncology','MED - Medicine','4030','M',2.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Program. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme:
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','临床肿瘤学课程向学生介绍癌症的诊断、分期、治疗与后续照护。学生将参与门诊诊疗、多专科团队会议及住院病患管理，实际学习化学治疗、放射治疗及安宁缓和医疗的临床应用。课程强调整合临床推理、实证医学与以病人为中心的沟通技巧。评估重点包括临床决策能力、肿瘤治疗原则与副作用处理，以及诊断结果之判读，使学生未来能够自信地处理临床肿瘤个案。','The Clinical Oncology course introduces students to cancer diagnosis, staging, treatment, and follow-up care. Students actively engage in oncology outpatient clinics, multidisciplinary team meetings, and inpatient management, gaining experience with chemotherapy, radiotherapy, and palliative care approaches. The course emphasizes integrating clinical reasoning, evidence-based medicine, and patient-centered communication. Assessments focus on clinical decision-making, understanding oncology treatment principles, side effect management, and interpreting diagnostic results, equipping students to confidently handle oncology cases in future clinical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102218,'MED4031','矫形外科及创伤学','Orthopaedic and Traumatology','MED - Medicine','4031','M',2.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Programme. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme:
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','骨科课程提供完整的肌肉骨骼系统疾病之诊断、治疗与管理训练。学生透过临床检查、门诊诊疗及手术观察，获取实务技能。主要内容涵盖骨折、关节炎、运动损伤与骨科急症，并着重诊断影像判读及手术原则。课程结合实务临床操作、交互式研讨及病例讨论，使学生在多样化的临床情境中，有效处理各类骨科问题，并提升未来医疗执业所需之程序操作能力。','The Orthopedics course offers comprehensive training in the diagnosis, treatment, and management of musculoskeletal disorders. Students gain practical skills through clinical examinations, outpatient clinics, and operative theater experiences. Key topics include fractures, arthritis, sports injuries, and orthopedic emergencies, emphasizing diagnostic imaging interpretation and surgical principles. The course integrates hands-on clinical practice, interactive seminars, and case discussions, preparing students to effectively manage orthopedic conditions and injuries in diverse clinical settings and enhancing their procedural competencies for future practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102219,'MED4032','耳鼻喉科学','Ear, Nose and Throat','MED - Medicine','4032','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Programme. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme:
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','耳鼻喉科课程为学生提供全面的临床训练，涵盖耳、鼻、喉及头颈部的常见疾病。学生将透过参与门诊诊疗、病房照护、手术观察及病例讨论，掌握临床评估、诊断判断与治疗方案。主要学习内容包括处理耳鼻喉急症、相关临床操作技术，以及了解手术适应症。评估方式包含临床技能考核与理论知识测试，使学生具备处理耳鼻喉疾病所需的基础临床能力。','The ENT course provides students comprehensive clinical exposure to common conditions affecting the ears, nose, throat, head, and neck. Students gain proficiency in clinical assessment, diagnostic interpretation, and management strategies through participation in outpatient clinics, inpatient care, surgical observations, and case-based tutorials. Key learning areas include managing ENT emergencies, procedural techniques, and understanding indications for surgery. Assessment involves clinical skills evaluation and theoretical knowledge testing, equipping students with foundational expertise for managing otolaryngological disorders in clinical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102220,'MED4033','眼科学','Ophthalmology','MED - Medicine','4033','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','门诊','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Program. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme:
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','眼科学课程为医学生提供全面的临床训练，涵盖常见眼疾的诊断与治疗。学生参与临床活动，包括门诊诊疗、手术观察及病例讨论，课程强调实务技巧，例如眼科检查技术、诊断检查的判读以及眼科急症的处理策略。考核方式为结构化的多项选择题考试，以确保学生掌握必要的眼科医学知识，为日后从事医疗工作时能准确诊断并有效管理病人。','The Ophthalmology rotation provides medical students with comprehensive training in diagnosing and managing common ocular conditions. Students participate in clinical activities, including outpatient clinics, surgical observations, and interactive case-based discussions. The course emphasizes practical skills such as ophthalmic examination techniques, interpretation of diagnostic tests, and management strategies for ocular emergencies. Assessment includes a structured multiple-choice examination, ensuring students understand essential ophthalmic principles, crucial for accurate diagnosis and effective patient management in their future medical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102221,'MED4034','临床放射学','Clinical Radiology','MED - Medicine','4034','M',2.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Programme. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme. This course is a continuation of the Basic Clinical Radiology MED3011 when the didactic teachings should have been completed. 
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','高级临床见习中的临床放射学为学生提供全面的影像诊断培训。学生将学习影像检查结果的基本解读技巧，强调其在临床决策中的应用。此外，学生还会通过以循证医学为基础的小组演讲，探索介入放射学的最新进展。考核方式包括测试，以考察学生的影像解读实际能力，并确保学生理解患者安全、准备流程以及正确选择诊断方法的重要性，这些对于临床实践中准确、及时地管理患者至关重要。','Clinical Radiology in the senior clerkship provides comprehensive training in diagnostic imaging. Students learn essential skills for interpreting radiological investigations, emphasizing their application in clinical decision-making. Students also explores the advancement of interventional radiology by small group evidence based presentation. Assessment is conducted through tests, integrating practical image interpretation skills, and ensuring students understand patient safety, preparation procedures, and appropriate selection of diagnostic modalities, crucial for accurate and timely patient management in clinical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102222,'MED4035','麻醉及重症监护','Anaesthesiology & Critical Care','MED - Medicine','4035','M',2.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Programme. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme.
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','本课程整合麻醉学、重症医学与急诊医学三个领域，训练学生掌握急重症病患照护的必要技能。麻醉学内容涵盖气道处置、术前评估及麻醉技术；重症医学强调危重病患处理、机械通气及血液动力学监测；急诊医学则着重内外科急症、创伤评估与紧急医疗处置。学生将透过临床实习、模拟情境与操作工作坊，强化临床急症应变能力，为未来医疗工作做好准备。','This course integrates Anaesthesia, Critical Care, and Accident & Emergency training, equipping students with essential skills for acute patient care. In Anaesthesia, students learn airway management, perioperative assessment, and anaesthetic techniques. Critical Care emphasizes managing critically ill patients, mechanical ventilation, and haemodynamic monitoring. Accident & Emergency training covers acute medical and surgical emergencies, trauma assessment, and urgent care management. Learning includes clinical rotations, simulation scenarios, and practical workshops, preparing students for effective response in acute clinical situations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102223,'MED4036','口腔医学','Stomatology','MED - Medicine','4036','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','This is a core course for Year 5 of Clinical Medicine Programme. The students are required to have completed and passed all courses in Year 1 to 4 of the Clinical Medicine Programme.
MED4010, MED4011, MED4012, MED4013, MED4014, MED4015, MED4016, MED4100, MED4200, MED1200','N/A','口腔医学课程向医学生介绍口腔及牙科医学之基础理论，强调其与整体病患照护之相关性。课程内容涵盖口腔解剖学、牙科生理学、常见口腔疾病，以及全身性疾病的口腔表现。学生透过讲课、案例研讨及临床示范学习重要知识。主要主题包括龋齿、牙周病、口腔感染及口腔癌筛检。课程评估着重将口腔健康评估融入一般医疗实务，提升学生提供全面性病患照护的能力。','Somatology introduces medical students to the fundamental principles of oral and dental medicine, emphasizing their relevance to overall patient care. This course covers oral anatomy, dental physiology, common oral diseases, and oral manifestations of systemic conditions. Students gain essential knowledge through lectures, case studies, and clinical demonstrations. Key topics include dental caries, periodontal diseases, oral infections, and oral cancer screening. Assessments focus on integrating oral health evaluation into general medical practice, enhancing students’ ability to provide comprehensive patient management.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102224,'MED4100','伦理与专业（四）','Bioethics and Professionalism IV','MED - Medicine','4100','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED1100 Bioethics and Professionalism    MED3100 Bioethics and Professionalism    MED2100 Bioethics and Professionalism','None','伦理与专业课程将在临床医学专业贯穿六年。该课程提供了生物及医学伦理学主要领域的概述。学生将熟悉该领域的术语、资源和伦理分析的主要框架。第四学年的课程将建立在前三年所涵盖的基础知识之上。
本课程将在本学年的四个临床学科模块中进行：儿科、妇产科、预防医学与全科医学、心理学与精神科学，并将涵盖与这些临床学科相关的更高级主题和当代问题。
学生在第四学年轮转四个临床模块的同时，将在床边进行由各学科临床实践中特殊情况引起的临床伦理问题和决策。
在儿科模块中，学生将学习儿科医生在对儿童治疗时面临的伦理思考。与成年患者不同，对于儿童，医疗决策通常由患儿以外的他人做出，即父母/主要照顾者。患者隐私保护、治疗知情同意以及儿童保护等问题要求医生了解儿童的具体需求和愿望，能够尊重并充分应对当儿童和父母的看法和需求不一致时的情况。作为儿科导师计划的一部分，学生将进行小组汇报。
在妇产科模块中，学生将通过互动学生论坛和研讨会学习伦理问题，如终止妊娠、面对新兴技术的生育自主权，以及产科医生在孕妇和潜在胎儿之间决策中的角色。
在预防医学与全科医学模块中，学生将学习常见临床问题，包括询问性史、告知真相、告知坏消息以及处理临床错误。通过小组教学，学生能够与经验丰富的当地医务人员观察并讨论共同面对的挑战。
在心理学与精神科学模块中，学生将学习在治疗精神患者时所面临常见的和特殊的伦理考虑，如患者隐私保护、精神疾病治疗知情同意以及能力鉴定。
此外，该课程将继续对学生在医学领域的职业素养进行教学。学生将接受短期线上教学活动，以进一步培养其对职业素养的理解，如涵盖专业素养和为患者发声，以及医患关系。学生须遵守规范的行为准则，明确对职业素养的期望，并将在整个医学教育过程中由教师和潜在的同辈进行跟踪。','The bioethics and professionalism curriculum will be offered throughout the six-year Clinical Medicine programme. This course provides an overview of the major areas of bioethics. Students will gain familiarity with the terminology, resources, and major frameworks of ethical analysis in the field. Year 4 the course builds on the foundational knowledge covered in previous 3 years.
The course work will be undertaken within the four Year 4 clinical modules: Paediatrics (PAE); Obstetrics & Gynaecology (O&G); Preventive Medicine & General Practice (PMGP); Psychology and Psychiatry (PSY). More advanced topics and contemporary issues will be covered that relate to these clinical disciplines.
During Year 4 while students rotate through the 4 clinical modules they will experience clinical ethical issues and decision at the bedside arising from some special circumstances in the clinical practice of each discipline.
In the PAE module, students will learn about bioethical considerations that paediatricians face while treating children for health conditions. For children, unlike for adult patients, healthcare decisions are often made by someone other than the person to be treated, i.e. by the parents/primary carers. Issues of patient confidentiality, consent for treatment, and child protection require the treating doctor to be aware of the specific needs and desires of the child, and to be able to respect and adequately address situations when the child''s and parents'' views and needs diverge. As part of the PAE mentorship programme students will do group bioethics presentations.
In the O&G module, students will learn about ethical issues through the interactive student forum and seminar, such as termination of pregnancy, reproductive autonomy in the face to emerging technologies, as well as obstetricians'' role in the decision-making between pregnant women and the potential human fetus.
In the PMGP module, students will learn about issues in common clinical encounter, including taking a sexual history, truth-telling, breaking the bad news, and dealing with clinical errors. Through small group teachings, students able to observe and discuss challenges with experienced local practitioners.
In the PSY module, students will learn about common and unique bioethical considerations that psychiatry faces while treating patients with mental health conditions, such as patient confidentiality, consent for treatment in psychiatric illness, and capacity determination.
Additionally, this course continues students’ education on professionalism in the medical field. Students will be given short online modules and activities to further develop their understanding on professionalism, covering topics such as Professionalism and advocating for patients, and The Doctor Patient Relationship. Students will be expected to follow the code of conduct which outlines expectations of professionalism, and they will be tracked by instructors and potentially peers throughout their entire medical schooling.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102225,'MED4110','伦理与专业（五）','Bioethics and Professionalism V','MED - Medicine','4110','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED1100, MED2100, MED3100, MED4100','N/A','生物伦理与专业精神课程为六年制临床医学课程的其中一个纵向课程。此课程概述生物伦理学的主要领域。学生将熟悉该领域的术语、资源及主要伦理分析框架。至第五年，课程将在前四年的基础知识上，涵盖有关生死照护及临床试验的高阶主题及当代议题。','The bioethics and professionalism curriculum will be offered throughout the six-year Clinical Medicine program. This course provides an overview of the major areas of bioethics. Students will gain familiarity with the terminology, resources, and major frameworks of ethical analysis in the field. In Year5 the course builds on the foundational knowledge introduced during Year 1 to 4, by covering advanced topics and contemporary issues in end-of-life care and clinical trials.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102226,'MED4120','伦理与专业（六）','Bioethics and Professionalism VI','MED - Medicine','4120','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MED4020;MED4021;MED4030;MED4031;MED4032;MED4033;MED4034;MED4035;MED4036;MED4110;MED4210','N/A','本课程是临床医学课程纵向临床实习项目的第二阶段。在第五学年完成内科学和外科学核心轮转的基础上，学生将在附属教学医院及社区医疗卫生机构中，在监督指导下参加妇产科学、儿科学、家庭医学与社区健康以及选修专科的临床实习。

本课程提供沉浸式、以工作场所为基础的临床学习体验，学生将作为多学科医疗团队成员积极参与患者照护。在合格临床教师的监督指导下，学生应能够将生物医学、临床医学、行为科学和社会科学知识加以应用和整合，用于不同医疗环境中患者的评估、诊断和管理。

通过直接参与患者照护、临床操作、病例讨论、病房工作、门诊服务、社区医疗服务以及跨专业协作，学生将逐步提升临床推理、患者管理、沟通、职业素养、患者安全和反思性实践等方面的能力。学生应在实践中表现出不断增强的责任感和问责意识，同时认识到自身能力的局限，并在适当监督下开展临床实践。

本课程旨在巩固毕业医学生所需的知识、技能、态度和职业行为，并帮助学生为进入毕业后医学培训和在监督下开展临床实践做好准备。','This course constitutes the second phase of the longitudinal clinical internship programme of the Clinical Medicine Programme. Building upon the core Internal Medicine and Surgery rotations completed during Year 5, students undertake supervised clinical placements in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Paediatrics, Family Medicine and Community Health, and elective specialties across affiliated teaching hospitals and community healthcare settings.
The course provides immersive workplace-based clinical learning in which students participate actively in patient care as members of multidisciplinary healthcare teams. Under the supervision of qualified clinical teachers, students are expected to apply and integrate biomedical, clinical, behavioural and social sciences knowledge in the assessment, diagnosis and management of patients across a range of healthcare settings.
Through direct patient care, clinical procedures, case discussions, ward activities, outpatient services, community-based healthcare, and interprofessional collaboration, students progressively develop competence in clinical reasoning, patient management, communication, professionalism, patient safety, and reflective practice. Students are expected to demonstrate increasing responsibility and accountability while recognising the limits of their competence and practising within appropriate supervision.
The course aims to consolidate the knowledge, skills, attitudes and professional behaviours required of a graduating medical student and to prepare students for the transition to postgraduate medical training and supervised clinical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102227,'MED4200','沟通技巧（二）','Communication Skills II','MED - Medicine','4200','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED3200 Communication Skills I','None','良好沟通能力是核心的临床技能，在问诊、诊断、治疗计划和团队协作中至关重要。本课程采用纵向发展方法，涵盖了从临床前阶段（家庭探访计划MED1200）到临床阶段（MED3200）的全过程。
本课程将在儿科、妇产科、预防医学与全科医学、心理学与精神科学等不同专业模块采用不同的教学模式，如研讨会、自我和同行评议以及导师反馈。
学习成果和教学模式将在专科轮转中体现。','The ability to communicate well is a core clinical skill and essential in medical consultations, determining a diagnosis, management planning and teamwork coordination.
This course adopts a longitudinal developmental approach spanning preclinical (Family Follow-up Project MED1200) through to the clinical years (MED3200).
Different teaching modalities will be used during the different specialty modules of Paediatrics, Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Public health and General Practice and Psychiatry e.g. workshops, self and peer review and tutor feedback.
Learning outcomes and teaching modalities are interwoven within the specialist rotations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102228,'MED4210','沟通技巧（三）','Communication Skills III','MED - Medicine','4210','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','MED1200, MED3200, MED4200','N/A','良好的沟通能力是核心临床技能，在医疗咨询、确定诊断、管理计划和团队协调中至关重要。本课程采用纵向发展方法，涵盖从临床前阶段（家庭跟进项目 MED1200）到临床阶段（MED3200 和 MED4200）。在专科见习和实习期间，将使用不同的教学模式。学习成果和教学模式在专科轮转中交织在一起。','The ability to communicate well is a core clinical skill and essential in medical consultations, determining a diagnosis, management planning and teamwork coordination.
This course adopts a longitudinal developmental approach spanning preclinical (Family Follow-up Project MED1200) through to the clinical years (MED3200 & MED4200). Different teaching modalities will be used during the speciality clerkship and internship. Learning outcomes and teaching modalities are interwoven within the specialist rotations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102229,'MED4220','沟通技巧（四）','Communication Skills IV','MED - Medicine','4220','M',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MED4020;MED4021;MED4030;MED4031;MED4032;MED4033;MED4034;MED4035;MED4036;MED4110;MED4210','N/A','本课程旨在培养医学生于临床实践中所需之进阶沟通能力，协助学生在复杂、多元及具挑战性的医疗情境中，与病人、家属、医疗团队及其他持份者进行有效、专业及具同理心的沟通。课程建基于学生于临床培训期间所建立的基础沟通能力，进一步探讨共享决策、冲突处理、跨专业协作、困难对话及涉及伦理争议之临床沟通技巧。

课程强调以病人为中心的沟通理念，并培养学生在面对价值观差异、不确定性及道德两难时，能够清晰表达观点、理解不同立场，以及运用适当的沟通策略促进理性讨论与共同决策。本课程采用互动及体验式学习模式，包括专题研讨、案例分析、小组讨论、角色扮演及结构化辩论等活动。学生将与《生物医学伦理与专业素养》课程共同进行跨课程学习，以真实或模拟临床案例为基础，分析相关伦理议题，建立论证，并透过团队辩论展示其沟通能力、批判思维及专业判断。

透过课程学习，学生将提升其在临床及专业环境中的表达能力、倾听能力、论证能力及协商能力，并培养尊重、多元、理性及反思的专业态度，为未来临床执业及终身专业发展奠定基础。','The Communication Skills (IV) course aims to develop the advanced communication competencies required for effective, compassionate, and professional medical practice. Building upon the communication skills acquired during clinical training, the course focuses on communication in complex clinical situations involving uncertainty, conflict, ethical dilemmas, cultural diversity, and shared decision-making.
Students will explore the principles and practices of patient-centred communication, interprofessional communication, difficult conversations, conflict resolution, negotiation, and communication in ethically challenging clinical scenarios. Emphasis is placed on the ability to communicate effectively with patients, families, caregivers, healthcare professionals, and the wider community while maintaining professionalism, empathy, respect, and ethical integrity.
The course adopts an interactive and experiential learning approach through workshops, case discussions, role-play exercises, reflective activities, and structured debates. In collaboration with the Bioethics and Professionalism course, students will analyse authentic clinical cases involving ethical controversies, develop evidence-based arguments, and participate in team-based debates that require the integration of communication skills, ethical reasoning, and professional judgment.
Through these learning activities, students will strengthen their ability to articulate clinical and ethical viewpoints, respond constructively to differing perspectives, and communicate effectively in situations where there may be no single correct answer. The course aims to prepare students for the communication challenges encountered in clinical practice and to support their development as reflective, ethical, and patient-centred healthcare professionals.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102230,'MED4230','专科实习','Specialty Rotations','MED - Medicine','4230','M',24.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实习','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MED4020;MED4021;MED4030;MED4031;MED4032;MED4033;MED4034;MED4035;MED4036;MED4110;MED4210','N/A','本课程为临床医学专业临床实习计划的第二阶段。在完成五年级内科学及外科学核心轮转的基础上，学生将在附属教学医院及社区医疗机构继续完成儿科学、妇产科学、社区医学及选修专科的临床实习轮转。

课程以岗位实践学习为核心，学生将在临床督导下作为医疗团队成员参与患者诊疗工作，并在真实医疗环境中逐步提高临床评估、患者管理、基本操作技能、临床沟通及职业决策能力。课程特别强调儿童健康、妇女健康、预防医学、群眾健康、连续性医疗服务以及以患者为中心的医疗实践。

通过不同专科及社区医疗环境的学习，学生将进一步整合和巩固本科阶段所获得的医学知识、临床技能及职业素养，建立医学生向初级临床医生转变所需的专业身份认同，并达到进入毕业后医学教育阶段所要求的核心胜任力水平。','This course constitutes the second phase of the longitudinal clinical internship programme of the Clinical Medicine Programme. Building upon the core Internal Medicine and Surgery rotations completed during Year 5, students undertake supervised clinical placements in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Paediatrics, Family Medicine and Community Health, and elective specialties across affiliated teaching hospitals and community healthcare settings.
The course provides immersive workplace-based clinical learning in which students participate actively in patient care as members of multidisciplinary healthcare teams. Under the supervision of qualified clinical teachers, students are expected to apply and integrate biomedical, clinical, behavioural and social sciences knowledge in the assessment, diagnosis and management of patients across a range of healthcare settings.
Through direct patient care, clinical procedures, case discussions, ward activities, outpatient services, community-based healthcare, and interprofessional collaboration, students progressively develop competence in clinical reasoning, patient management, communication, professionalism, patient safety, and reflective practice. Students are expected to demonstrate increasing responsibility and accountability while recognising the limits of their competence and practising within appropriate supervision.
The course aims to consolidate the knowledge, skills, attitudes and professional behaviours required of a graduating medical student and to prepare students for the transition to postgraduate medical training and supervised clinical practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102231,'MED4400','选修学科（一）(专科深造)','Selected Study Modules I (Clinical Elective in Specialties)','MED - Medicine','4400','M',24.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','临床实践','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MED4020;MED4021;MED4030;MED4031;MED4032;MED4033;MED4034;MED4035;MED4036;MED4110;MED4210','N/A','本课程旨在为高年级医学生提供自主选择临床专科领域的进阶学习机会。学生可根据个人兴趣及未来职业发展规划，于认可的临床专科部门、教学医院、医疗机构或企业进行为期四个月的临床选修实习，以深入了解特定专科的临床工作模式、专业范畴及培训要求。

在合资格临床导师的督导下，学生将参与与其培训程度相符的专科临床活动，包括门诊服务、病房工作、查房、手术或操作观摩、多学科会议、病例讨论及其他教学活动。透过直接接触不同专科的患者群体及医疗团队，学生可进一步理解相关疾病的诊疗原则、专科医疗服务模式及跨专业协作的重要性。

本课程强调自主学习、专业发展及反思实践。学生须于实习开始前制定个人学习目标，于实习期间完成学习纪录或学习档案，并于课程结束时提交反思报告，以总结其学习成果及专业成长经历。

课程旨在协助学生深化对特定临床专科的认识，探索个人职业兴趣与发展方向，培养终身学习能力，并为毕业后医学教育及专科培训作充分准备。','The Clinical Specialties Elective provides final-year medical students with an opportunity to pursue advanced study and experiential learning in one or more clinical specialties of their choice. Building upon the core knowledge, clinical skills, and professional competencies acquired throughout the Clinical Medicine Programme, students undertake supervised attachments designed to deepen their understanding of specific medical and surgical disciplines and to support informed career planning.

Students may be attached to approved clinical departments, specialist centres, teaching hospitals, healthcare institutions or industries in Mainland China, Hong Kong, or overseas. Under the supervision of qualified clinical mentors, students are expected to participate in specialty-specific clinical activities appropriate to their level of training, including outpatient clinics, inpatient care, multidisciplinary meetings, ward rounds, operating theatres, procedural services, case discussions, and educational activities.

The course emphasises self-directed learning, professional development, reflective practice, and exploration of future career interests. Through direct exposure to specialty practice, students will gain a deeper appreciation of the clinical scope, professional responsibilities, patient populations, healthcare systems, and training pathways associated with their chosen disciplines.

Students are expected to establish individual learning objectives in consultation with their supervisors, maintain a learning portfolio or logbook documenting their experiences, and reflect critically on their professional development and career aspirations. The course aims to facilitate the transition from undergraduate medical education to postgraduate training by fostering professional maturity, specialty awareness, and lifelong learning skills.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102232,'MED4500','选修学科（二）(医学硏究)','Selected Study Modules II (Medical Research)','MED - Medicine','4500','M',24.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','研究','Main Campus','医学院','医学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','MED4020;MED4021;MED4030;MED4031;MED4032;MED4033;MED4034;MED4035;MED4036;MED4110;MED4210','N/A','本课程旨在为高年级医学生提供自主选择研究方向及参与科研工作的机会。学生可根据个人兴趣及未来发展规划，加入临床医学、基础医学、生物医学工程、公共卫生、医学教育、人工智能、转化医学或其他经批准之研究团队，接受为期四个月的研究训练及学术实践。

在认可学术导师的指导下，学生将参与与其培训程度相符之科研活动，包括文献研读、研究设计、研究方案制定、数据收集与分析、实验技术学习、临床研究、学术讨论、研究生课程修读或其他相关学术活动。学生可根据研究项目性质及学习需要，于大学、研究机构、医院、实验室或其他学术单位完成课程要求。

本课程强调自主学习、科学思维、批判性分析及循证医学精神。透过参与真实研究环境及跨学科合作，学生将加深对医学知识产生、验证、转化及应用过程的理解，并认识科研工作在推动医疗服务、健康促进及医学发展中的重要作用。

学生须与导师共同制定个人学习目标，保存学习纪录或研究历程档案，并就其学习成果及专业成长进行反思。学术成果如研究报告、学术会议发表、摘要投稿、论文撰写或其他研究产出均予以鼓励，但并非课程之必须要求。','The Medical Research Elective provides final-year medical students with an opportunity to undertake an extended period of supervised research training and scholarly inquiry in an area of interest. Students may join established research groups or academic units in clinical medicine, basic sciences, biomedical engineering, public health, health services research, medical education, translational medicine, artificial intelligence, or other approved disciplines relevant to healthcare and medicine.

Under the supervision of an approved academic mentor, students are expected to participate actively in research-related activities appropriate to their background and training. Depending on the nature of the attachment, these activities may include literature review, research design, protocol development, data collection, laboratory work, clinical research activities, data analysis, scientific communication, postgraduate coursework, or participation in academic meetings and seminars.

The course emphasizes self-directed learning, critical thinking, scientific inquiry, and professional development. Students are encouraged to explore how scientific evidence is generated, evaluated, translated, and applied to improve patient care, healthcare systems, and population health. Students are expected to establish individual learning objectives in consultation with their supervisors, maintain a learning portfolio or record of activities, and reflect on their academic and professional development throughout the attachment. While scholarly outputs such as presentations, abstracts, publications, research reports, or project deliverables are encouraged where appropriate, they are not required for successful completion of the course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
