2026-27 Term 1','MGT2020 Principles of Management','No co-requisite.','人力资源是组织的重要资源。识别、吸引、招募、保存和激励人力资源对于组织的成功至关重要。本科目将以行为科学的概念和理论为基础，讨论人力资源管理的若干话题，包括工作分析、人力资源计划、招募与甄选、培训与开发、绩效管理、薪酬管理以及员工关系等。','Human capital is an essential resource in organizations. Identifying, attracting, recruiting, retaining, and motivating human capital is critical for organizational success. Drawing on behavioral science concepts and theories, we examine topics including job analysis, manpower planning, recruitment, training and development, performance management, compensation and motivation, benefit, employee relations, and employee security and safety.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102300,'MGT3310','商业沟通之商业叙事 I','','MGT - Management','3310','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','故事是成功商业的无形支柱。它们将抽象战略转化为共同目标，将产品转化为体验，将领导者转化为鼓舞者。《商业沟通系列之商业叙事I》作为商业沟通领域的基础性入门课程，旨在为本科生提供一套以框架为支撑的实用指南，帮助他们掌握这项在传统商学课程中常被忽略的关键软技能。

在本课程中，你将学习创作、表达、表演并传递令人记忆深刻的故事的技能。此外，通过模仿叙事大师，你还将逐步形成拥有个人色彩的叙事风格。课程结业时，你不仅会理解为何叙事是商业领域最强大的工具，更将掌握如何运用它脱颖而出、取得成功。','Stories are the invisible backbone of successful business. They turn abstract strategies into shared purpose, products into experiences, and leaders into inspirations. Storytelling in Business I, as a fundamental introductory course in the field of business communication, is designed to give undergraduate students practical, framework-driven guide to mastering this critical soft skill—one that’s often overlooked in traditional business curricula. In this course, you will develop skills to write, express, stage, and deliver stories that stick. What is more, you will gradually form your own style of storytelling by imitating the storytelling masters. Upon completion, you will not only understand why storytelling is the most powerful tool in business—you will have mastered how to use it to stand out and succeed.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
