(102314,'MGT4130','组织理论与设计','Organization Theory and Design','MGT - Management','4130','M',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2','No prerequisite or co-requisite.','','本课程专为有兴趣理解有关“组织”的基本知识的学生而设计，例如：什么是组织？组织为什么是这样的？为什么一些组织有特定的行为方式？组织的内部特征（例如，结构、设计）扮演什么角色？组织的外部环境（例如，媒体、政府）如何影响组织流程，以及组织如何影响社会——反之亦然。由于组织在全球社会的背景下发挥着重要作用，因此本课程也将有助于我们更好地了解社会生活。学生将有机会接触来自于各种行业的从业者和专家 (如剧本杀、ChatGPT、婴幼儿奶粉、营养师等)。
    从更广阔的视角来说，本课程还将培养学生的批判性思维、道德意识、团队合作能力和沟通技巧。本课程所学习的所有分析方式，都需要在实践中能够传达、因地制宜地应用，才有意义。MGT4130 旨在为学生提供一个安全的环境，练习以连贯和令人信服的方式表达他们的观点。','This course is designed for students interested in actively building an understanding about key foundational “organizational topics”, such as what is an organization, why do organizations look and behave the way they do, what roles do an organization’s internal characteristics (e.g., structure, design) and external environment (e.g., media, government) play in organizational processes, and how do organizations influence society – and vice versa. Because organizations play such a central role in the context of a worldwide society, this class will also be useful for developing a better understanding of social life. Students will have opportunities to interact with practitioners and experts from a variety of industries (e.g., live action role-playing game (LARP), ChatGPT, dietitians, infant formula, and more).
    More broadly, this course will also encourage students’ critical thinking, ethical awareness, teamwork abilities and communication skills. The best analysis in the world means nothing if it is not well communicated and contextualized, and MGT 4130 is designed to provide students with a safe environment to practice articulating their viewpoints in a coherent and persuasive manner.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
