2025-26 Summer','Students enrolled in this course are required to work in an internship position a minimum of 2-3 days per week, which can cover at least 200 contract hours in total. They are expected to work under the guidance of a Supervisor and possibly other colleagues employed at the company.Students shall seek internship by themselves.

Before enrolling this course, students are required to submit: 1) the details of the employment including a copy of the ad/announcement of the internship position, 2) the name and position of the company Supervisor, 3) copies of salary pay slips, and a signed contract/agreement for verification and 4) the most updated unofficial English transcript.','','实习为学生提供了宝贵的实践经验，让他们亲身体验实际工作的样子。它旨在架起正规大学教育与职场生活之间的桥梁，促进专业知识的整合与综合运用，并培养人际交往和沟通技能。

这门3学分的课程采用“通过/不通过”（Pass/Fail）的评分方式，且学生须在满足以下注册条件的前提下，获得课程讲师的事先同意方可注册。

如果MGT4188在相应年级专业的培养方案中被列为专业选修课，那么学生选择的实习内容应与其专业/方向相关，因为该课程与专业课程体系紧密相连。课程注册资格最终由课程讲师或助教酌情决定。','An internship provides students with an invaluable hands-on experience of what an actual job would be like. It serves to bridge formal university education and work life, facilitate the integration and synthesis of subject knowledge, and the development of interpersonal and communication skills.

This 3-credit course is offered on a Pass/Fail basis and is only open for registration with the prior consent of the Course Instructor subject to the Registration conditions described below.
If MGT4188 is listed as a Major Elective course in the corresponding cohort major study scheme, the internship chosen should be related to the student’s major/stream considering it is highly connected with the major programme course. The course enrollment qualification will be subject to the discretion of the course instructor/TA.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
