2017-18 Summer','MGT2020','Required','人每天都在做决策以及谈判。当我们与父母、室友、房东、同事、潜在雇主、或者服务人员谈话时，我们也许都不知道其实我们正在进行某种形式的谈判。虽然我们如此频繁地谈判，很多人对有效决策及谈判中的心理和战略却知之甚少。这门课旨在帮助学生们了解在不同情境中决策和谈判当中涉及的理论以及培养有效决策及谈判的实战策略。本课程一个重点在于人作为一个非完美决策者是如何决策和谈判的。我们将会讨论指导我们谈判的理论和原则（谈判是门科学）。学生将会从与其他人的谈判练习实战经验中培养并磨炼技巧 （谈判是门艺术）。
本课程将包括授课，讨论，谈判模拟练习等，让学生在实践中学习从而达到学习目标。谈判模拟练习包括但不局限于谈判计划、双方谈判、群组谈判、跨文化谈判等。','We make decisions and negotiate every day. We may not even realize that we have already engaged in negotiations when we talk to parents, roommates, landlords, colleagues, potential employers, service providers, etc. Yet, while we negotiate often, many of us know very little about the psychology and strategy of effective decision-making and negotiation. This course is designed to help students understand the underlying theories as well as develop practical strategies of decision makings and negotiations in a variety of settings. A core focus of the course will be the human beings as less-than-perfect decision makers in decision-making and negotiation contexts. We will discuss theories and principles to guide our negotiations (the science). And students will develop and sharpen their bargaining skills by negotiating with other students in experiential exercises (the art).

The course will incorporate lectures, discussions, and negotiation exercises to provide a learning-by-doing approach to achieve the learning goals. Negotiation exercises include but are not limited to negotiation planning, two-party negotiation, team negotiation, cross-cultural negotiation, etc.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
