2018-19 Summer','MGT2020','No co-requisite.','本课程聚焦创业与创新的动态机制。第一部分将探讨初创企业的构建与发展历程，介绍实践中的经典模型与工具，包括创意生成、市场验证、商业模式选择、融资渠道、商业路演等。通过该部分的学习，学生将学会如何作为投资者及利益相关者对初创企业进行评估。第二部分将深入解析组织内部的创新生成与管理体系，介绍创新领域的核心理论与概念，包括S曲线、知识产权保护、开放式与封闭式创新等。学生将了解如何如何评估新技术对企业的影响力，怎样发掘高价值商业机遇，并成功实现企业的转型。本课程注重互动式与沉浸式学习。除理论讲授外，学生需积极参与课堂讨论及模拟游戏、案例研究、商业路演演练等实践活动。课程将视情况邀请具有创业实战经验的嘉宾进行经验分享。','This course focuses on the dynamics of entrepreneurship and innovation. The first part of the course is about how startups are built and developed. The course will cover some widely applied models and tools regarding entrepreneurial thinking and practice, covering topics including idea generation, market validation, business model selection, sources of funding, business pitch delivery, etc. Through this process, students will also learn how to evaluate a startup as an investor or a stakeholder. The second part delves into the generation and management of innovation within organizations, introduce concepts and theories related to innovation, such as the S-curve, intellectual property, and open and closed innovation. Students will understand how organizations evaluate the influence of new technologies, identify lucrative business opportunities, and navigate their transformations. This course values interactive and first-hand learning. In addition to lecturing, students are expected to participate in class discussions and activities such as simulation games, case presentations, and mock business pitches. Guest speakers with experience building a venture will be invited to the class upon availability.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
