2018-19 Summer','MGT2020','','本课程是一个博士研讨会，旨在为研究生提供战略管理领域的概述。

从广义上讲，战略研究（主要）侧重于解释企业的经济行为和绩效。战略研究中涉及的问题的说明性清单包括确定行业的利润潜力，探索企业规模、范围和绩效之间的关系，以及了解企业的管理和组织决定因素以及业务层面的结果。

该课程借鉴了经济学、社会学、组织理论和心理学的理论观点，补充了更传统的理解企业绩效和相关问题的战略方法。所研究的许多问题，如企业多元化、行业结构、组织和组织间网络，也是其他学科的共同主题，如行业组织经济学、市场营销、会计、金融以及组织和经济社会学。因此，本课程可能对在这些领域有研究兴趣的学生有用。','This course is a doctoral seminar that is designed to give graduate students an overview of the field of strategic management.

Broadly speaking, research in strategy focuses (primarily) on explaining the economic conduct and performance of firms. An illustrative list of the issues addressed in strategy research includes identifying the profit potential of industries, exploring relationships between firm scale, scope and performance, and understanding the managerial and organizational determinants of firm, and business-level outcomes.

The course draws upon theoretical perspectives from economics, sociology, organization theory, and psychology to supplement more traditional strategy approaches towards understanding firm performance and related issues. Many of the issues examined, such as firm diversification, industry structure, organizational and inter-organizational networks, are also common themes in other disciplines such as industrial organization economics, marketing, accounting, finance, and organizational and economic sociology. Accordingly, this course may be useful to students with research interests in these areas.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
