(102330,'MGT4560','商业可持续与利益相关者管理','Business Sustainability and Stakeholder Management','MGT - Management','4560','M',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2020-21 Summer
2021-22 Summer
2022-23 Summer','No prerequisites','No co-requisites','本课程关注的是国际商务管理的主要话题。它旨在让学生了解国际视角下的商业管理与战略的相关理论。话题包含国际贸易，外商直接投资，跨国企业，国际商业环境，以及国际商业战略。学生需要运用学到的知识与分析能力去研究当代全球竞争环境中企业面临的问题。','Today’s businesses are increasingly dealing with the risks and opportunities of environmental, social and governance (ESG) issues, due to the scarcity of resources, conflicts in community and labor relations, and climate change. These issues also highlight the importance of properly managing various stakeholders of a company. Bridging the gap between traditional business logics and a new context of shared economic and social value, business sustainability and stakeholder management are quickly becoming a core part of the mission of companies.

This course couples established and emerging theory on how businesses address sustainability challenges and effectively manage stakeholder relationships. It covers diverse aspects of business sustainability and stakeholder management, including ESG measurement, socially responsible and impact investing, integrated reporting, risk management, product market competition, and ESG issues along the supply chain to provide sophisticated and rigorous training at the nexus of sustainability and financial management. The course will also explore the meaning and importance of sustainable business practices that respect and adhere to ethical social responsibility standards through several case studies and simple econometric analyses. By the end of this course, students will gain a foundation in the understanding of how regulations and market forces provide incentives that encourage desired corporate behaviors.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102331,'MGT5001','领导力: 理论与实践','','MGT - Management','5001','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','No prerequisite','No co-requisite','领导力：理论与实践是管理学的高阶课程，通过这门课学生会接触到理解组织中人的行为的若干理论与概念。领导力：理论与实践是为了解释、预测、影响组织中个体与团队的行为。在这门课中，我们将会运用相关知识增强学生对自身的洞见，以及提高理解他人的能力，开发人际与领导技能，以及诊断和发现组织的问题。','This is an advanced course in management designed to give your exposure to essential
theories and concepts for understanding and managing leadership and human behavior in organizations. Leadership: Theory and Practice is concerned with explaining, predicting, and enhancing the effectiveness of individuals and groups in work organizations. In this course, we will discuss this knowledge and use it to develop self-insight and your ability to understand others, develop interpersonal and leadership skills, and diagnose and intervene on organizational problems','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102332,'MGT5002','战略管理与公司治理','','MGT - Management','5002','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','N/A','N/A','本课程介绍了关于战略决策与竞争分析的关键概念，工具，与原理。他们与管理行为以及商业企业的存活与表现有着重要关系。这门课程旨在让学生理解如何利用竞争战略去创造竞争优势，保护市场地位，以及为实现长期商业利益而进行关键资源分配。学生需要运用学到的知识分析组织战略决策。','This course introduces the key concepts, tools, and principles of strategy formulation and competitive analysis. They are concerned with managerial decisions that affect the performance and survival of business enterprises. The course aims to familiarize students with the approaches to choose competitive strategies, create competitive advantages, take advantage of internal and external opportunities, secure market positions, and allocate critical resources for long-term business success. Students are expected to integrate and apply their prior learning to strategic decision making in organizations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102333,'MGT5003','创业与科技创新','','MGT - Management','5003','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','本课程聚焦创业与创新的动态机制。第一部分将探讨初创企业的构建与发展历程，介绍实践中的经典模型与工具，包括创意生成、市场验证、商业模式选择、融资渠道、商业路演等。通过该部分的学习，学生将学会如何作为投资者及利益相关者对初创企业进行评估。第二部分将深入解析组织内部的创新生成与管理体系， 介绍创新领域的核心理论与概念，包括S曲线、知识产权保护、开放式与封闭式创新等。学生将了解如何如何评估新技术对企业的影响力，怎样发掘高价值商业机遇，并成功实现企业的转型。本课程注重互动式与沉浸式学习。除理论讲授外，学生需积极参与课堂讨论及模拟游戏、案例研究、商业路演演练等实践活动。课程将视情况邀请具有创业实战经验的嘉宾进行经验分享。','This course focuses on the dynamics of entrepreneurship and innovation. The first part of the course is about how startups are built and developed. The course will cover some widely applied models and tools regarding entrepreneurial thinking and practice, covering topics including idea generation, market validation, business model selection, sources of funding, business pitch delivery, etc. Through this process, students will also learn how to evaluate a startup as an investor or a stakeholder. The second part delves into the generation and management of innovation within organizations, introduce concepts and theories related to innovation, such as the S-curve, intellectual property, and open and closed innovation. Students will understand how organizations evaluate the influence of new technologies, identify lucrative business opportunities, and navigate their transformations. This course values interactive and first-hand learning. In addition to lecturing, students are expected to participate in class discussions and activities such as simulation games, case presentations, and mock business pitches. Guest speakers with experience building a venture will be invited to the class upon availability.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102334,'MGT5004','商业谈判和冲突管理','','MGT - Management','5004','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','None.','None.','谈判与冲突管理能力是当代领导者必备的核心素养。无论是组织内部还是外部的协商场景都无处不在，然而多数从业者缺乏系统认知，往往仅依赖模仿、传统或直觉行事。本课程致力于培养未来领导者，系统构建从谈判流程到冲突理论及解决策略的知识体系。通过学习这些技能在工作场景中的实际应用，学生将能更从容应对薪资谈判、利益相关方管理、自下而上/自上而下的沟通、职场权力博弈等常见挑战。课程提供全新视角和实用技巧，所有内容均可立即运用于日常工作与生活实践','Negotiation and conflict management capabilities are essential to leaders nowadays. Internal and external negotiations are ubiquitous, yet not many professionals know what they should do but simply rely on imitation, tradition, or intuition. This course aims to prepare the future leaders to equip with comprehensive knowledge ranging from negotiation process to conflict theories and approaches.  Applications of these skills can help students to handle work-related issues better, such as job offer negotiation, stakeholder management, bottom-up /top-down communication, power play in the workplace, etc. This class provides students new perspectives and techniques that can be immediately applied in your everyday work and life.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102335,'MGT6201','组织行为','','MGT - Management','6201','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','本课程的目标是使你熟悉构成组织行为学（OB）研究的理论、方法和研究路径。组织行为学主要关注组织科学中的“微观”心理学基础。我希望通过本课程，你能够对组织行为学领域形成初步认识，并开始培养在该领域开展研究所需的基本能力，从而成为具有生产力的研究贡献者。
为实现这一目标，我们将探讨经典与当代的理论、长期存在的争议与辩论，以及围绕组织行为学若干核心主题的实证研究。同时，我们还将学习如何解读、评估、整合，并在组织行为学及相关领域的研究基础上进行延展。
本课程并不以让你全面掌握该领域的所有内容为目标——在一个学期内这是不可能实现的。相反，我们将重点选取该领域的一些重要内容——包括经典文献和近期具有代表性的研究——以此为基础，帮助你对组织行为学已有的研究成果及未来研究方向形成一个整体性的认识。
与此同时，本课程也旨在提升你提出研究问题和构思研究想法的能力，使其能够对该领域产生有意义的贡献。','The purpose of this course is to familiarize you with the theories, methods, and approaches that characterize the study of organizational behavior (OB), which involves the “micro” psychological foundations of organization science. I hope that you will gain a preliminary understanding of the field of OB and begin to develop the necessary skills to become a productive contributor to research in the field. Toward this end, we will explore classic and contemporary theories, enduring controversies and debates, and empirical research on a variety of major topics in OB. We will also learn how to interpret, evaluate, integrate, and extrapolate from research on topics in OB and beyond. The course will not culminate in a comprehensive understanding of every single thing there is to know about the field; that would be impossible for a semester-long course. Rather, I’d like us to cover some highlights of the field— some “classics” and noteworthy recent papers—that, when put together, give a broad introduction into what has been done and what is left to do in OB. In tandem with this, the course is designed to hone your ability to generate research ideas that can make meaningful contributions to the field.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
