2026-27 Term 1','Marketing Management (MKT2010)','No','本课程将详细介绍营销传播的战略组成部分，和战略制定中所应该考虑的因素。学生通过学习营销传播中主要工具的相关理论和技术，为制定有效的营销传播战略打下基础。','The subject aims to provide an overview of the components and considerations involved in marketing communication strategy decisions. It examines the theory and techniques applicable to major marketing communication functions, and thus provides a knowledge base which allows students to develop effective communication strategies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102352,'MKT3050','环球营销','Global Marketing','MKT - Marketing','3050','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102353,'MKT3060','人工智能时代的量化营销方法','Quantitative Marketing Methods in the AI Age','MKT - Marketing','3060','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','MKT2010 Marketing Management','','在人工智能时代，每天都会产生海量的数据。要把数据变成价值，营销人不仅要会用工具，更要懂统计和因果推断。本课程致力于让学生掌握实用的量化分析方法，以解决人工智能时代下数据驱动的营销问题。这门课是人工智能营销方向学习的基础课程。
学生将学习如何用数学和统计模型表述传统的4P营销问题（产品、价格、渠道和促销），并在营销数据上应用他们。这门课涵盖了基本概率和统计、数据可视化、A/B 测试与实验设计、线性回归与逻辑回归、以及准实验方法（双重差分、回归不连续、工具变量）。课程的重点是为管理决策读懂结果，同时认识到纯预测（非因果）方法的局限性。
本课程非常注重实践和应用。我们将用一种实践化的方式来学习如何分析现实世界的营销数据并做出推断。这门课程会提供从零开始的R 语言学习指导，帮助你把分析做扎实，结果讲清楚。','Enormous volumes of data are generated every day in the era of AI. To extract value, marketers must pair modern tools with sound statistical and causal reasoning. This course equips students with practical quantitative methods to solve data-driven marketing problems and serves as a foundation for advanced study in the AI marketing stream.
Students learn to formulate marketing questions in product, price, place, and promotion as statistical models and causal estimands, then apply them to real data. Core topics include basic probability and statistics, data visualization, A/B testing and experimental design, linear (OLS) and logistic regression, and quasi-experimental methods such as Difference-in-Differences, Regression Discontinuity, and Instrumental Variables. Emphasis is on interpreting results for managerial decisions, and recognizing the limits of purely predictive (non-causal) approaches.
The course has a strong practical and applied emphasis, using a hands-on approach with real marketing datasets. Instructional support for R is provided to implement analyses and communicate findings clearly.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
