2026-27 Term 1','Recommended prerequisite: completion of an introductory marketing course, such as Marketing
Management or equivalent. Students should also have completed, or be concurrently familiar with,
introductory statistics, business analytics, quantitative methods, or an equivalent course. Prior Python
programming experience is not required, but students are expected to be comfortable with basic
spreadsheets and quantitative reasoning.','No','本课程以真实/仿真商业案例和数据应用为主线，介绍市场营销分析如何支持
管理决策。课程以核心应用能力为重点，包括问题界定、Python 工作流程、
数据可视化、客户细分、回归式营销组合分析、客户流失预测与分类、创作者
经济、营销中的 AI 应用和管理沟通。图像分析等较高级主题将作为概念性应
用进行介绍，而非作为重度编程内容。学生将学习如何把营销问题转化为分析
任务，在 Python 中完成基础建模与结果解释，并形成可执行的管理建议，例
如细分市场选择、预算配置、渠道归因、客户留存、品牌定位与需求规划。','This course introduces marketing analytics through practical business cases
and hands-on data applications in Python. The course prioritizes core
applied skills, including problem formulation, Python workflow, data
visualization, customer segmentation, regression-based marketing mix
evaluation, churn prediction and classification, creator economy, AI in
marketing, and managerial communication. More advanced areas, such as
image analytics, are introduced as conceptual applications rather than
coding-intensive modules. Students learn to translate marketing questions
into analytical tasks, implement selected models in Python, interpret outputs,
and turn findings into actionable managerial recommendations such as
segment targeting, budget allocation, channel attribution, retention targeting,
positioning, and demand planning.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
