2023-24 Summer','MKT2010 Marketing Management','No co-requisite.','无论是在公司总部、业务部门还是营销一线，不同层级的管理人员都需要制定自己的营销战略。虽然这些战略在结构上大抵相似，但应对的挑战却截然不同，且每一层的战略都直接关系到企业的成败。基于此，本课程旨在让学生：（1）在理论上理清不同管理层级的战略营销到底是什么、如何运作，以及为什么在当今商业环境下如此重要；（2）在实践中学习为各级管理层制定战略营销计划（特别是学习如何利用市场研究来支撑规划）。

课程结束时，学生应能够熟练地：（1）识别、解读并分析消费者和市场数据，以支持不同管理层级战略营销的有效制定与执行；（2）基于市场研究的证据，独立撰写一份战略营销计划。','Managers at different levels of management (corporate versus business-level versus marketing) need to formulate their marketing strategies. These strategies have similar components but have different issues. Each level of these strategies plays a critical role for the success of the firm. As such, this course aims at providing students with (1) conceptual/theoretical understanding on what strategic marketing at different levels of management is, how each of them works, and why each of them is so important in the contemporary business world, and (2) hands-on experience in developing a strategic marketing plan for each level of management (with focus on how to use marketing research for strategic marketing planning purpose). 

Upon completion of this course, students are expected to have adequate knowledge and skills to (1) identify, interpret, and analyze consumer and marketing data for effective strategic marketing formulation and execution at different levels of management, and (2) use evidence from marketing research to write a strategic marketing plan.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
