2025-26 Term 2','No','No','N/A','This course is an introduction to the theory and practice of consumer behavior. The present course aims to make students comprehend various consumer behavior theories that relate to both marketing communications and real-world advertising. During the first part of the term, student will study the micro-level constructs of consumer behavior including perceptions, learning and memory, affect, and the self. Students will then proceed with more macro-level influences on consumer behavior that include group and situational effects, identity, social class, family structure, and cross-cultural influence. Students will also have an opportunity to apply the theories they learn in the classroom via group assignments that resemble real-world marketing phenomena.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102385,'MKT5014','服务营销','','MKT - Marketing','5014','M',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2020-21 Term 1
