2026-27 Term 1','Fundamental statistics, programming language, i.e., Java or Python','','随着数字技术的指数级增长，营销专业人员正面临着前所未有的海量数据——这些数据源自客户互动、数字平台以及各类市场生态系统。这门研究生课程旨在帮助营销学生掌握高级知识与实践技能，学会运用大数据和机器学习进行战略决策。

课程首先全面概述营销领域的大数据应用，涵盖其定义、可视化技术、分析工具集，以及在客户细分、定价优化和活动定向等领域的应用。学生将通过 Hadoop 和 Spark 等行业标准平台，获得预处理、存储和处理大规模数据的实战经验。课程还将介绍一系列分析算法——包括监督学习与无监督学习、聚类分析和预测建模——用于从复杂数据集中提取可操作的洞察。

课程后半部分聚焦于深度学习及机器学习的最新进展，如强化学习、自然语言处理（NLP）和推荐系统。学生将学习设计和训练神经网络，以建模复杂的消费者行为和商业现象。整个课程中，真实的营销案例研究（例如亚马逊的个性化营销、旅游业的动态定价、社交媒体的情感分析）将展示数据驱动决策如何创造竞争优势。通过项目实践和作业任务，学生不仅能培养技术专长，还将建立起将分析结果转化为可执行营销策略的管理判断力。','With the exponential growth of digital technologies, marketing professionals are faced with unprecedented volumes of data generated from customer interactions, digital platforms, and market ecosystems. This graduate-level course equips marketing students with advanced knowledge and practical skills to harness big data and machine learning for strategic decision-making. The course begins with a comprehensive overview of big data in marketing, covering its definitions, visualization techniques, analytical toolkits, and applications in areas such as customer segmentation, pricing optimization, and campaign targeting. Students will gain hands-on experience with industry-standard platforms like Hadoop and Spark to preprocess, store, and manipulate large-scale data. The course introduces a range of analytical algorithms—including supervised and unsupervised learning, clustering, and predictive modeling—used to extract actionable insights from complex datasets. The second half of the course focuses on deep learning and other recent advances in machine learning, such as reinforcement learning, natural language processing (NLP), and recommendation systems. Students will learn to design and train neural networks to model complex consumer behavior and business phenomena. Throughout the course, real-world marketing case studies (e.g., personalized marketing at Amazon, dynamic pricing in travel, and sentiment analysis in social media) illustrate how data-driven decision-making can create competitive advantage. Through projects and assignments, students will not only develop technical expertise but also build the managerial judgment to translate analytics into actionable marketing strategies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
