(102402,'MKT6037','营销管理实践','','MKT - Marketing','6037','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2021-22 Summer
2022-23 Summer','MKT5011 Strategic Marketing Management','','本课程的目标是让学生获得解决实际商业环境中的管理营销问题的实际操作经验。课程内容涵盖小组项目、研讨会、报告和演讲等多种形式。学生将参与由企业提供的真实项目，并与教授紧密合作，共同为行业面临的管理营销挑战提供解决方案。本课程包含一个小组项目（即营销实践）和一些关于高级实用市场调研技巧的讲座（以支持小组项目）。在小组项目中，学生（4-5人一组）将与赞助公司的市场经理紧密合作，运用一手市场调研方法解决其营销问题。课程结束时，学生将向赞助公司的市场营销和/或管理团队汇报调研结果和建议。此外，学生还需要提交一份基于项目的详细书面报告或营销计划。

完成本课程后，学生应具备足够的知识和技能，能够识别问题、设计调研方案、收集数据、分析数据、解读调研结果，并制定有效解决营销问题的营销计划。','The objective of this course is to provide students with hand-on experience to solve managerial marketing problems in the real-world environment. The course consists of group projects, meetings, reports and presentations. Student will work on the real-world projects and collaborate closely with professors to deliver joint solutions to the managerial marketing problems in the industry.

The course consists of a group project (i.e., Marketing Practicum) and some lectures on advanced but practical marketing research techniques (to support the group project).  In the group project, students (in a small group of 4-5 students) will work closely with the marketing manager of a sponsoring firm to solve his or her marketing problem(s) by using primary marketing research.  Students will present the findings and recommendations to the sponsor’s marketing and/or management team at the end of the course. Students will also a detailed written report or marketing plan based on the project.

Upon completion of the course, students are expected to have adequate knowledge and skills to identify problem, design research, collect data, analyze data, interpret findings, and formulating marketing plan that effectively addresses the marketing problem.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102403,'MKT6038','营销分析及数字化时代的消费者','','MKT - Marketing','6038','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 2
2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Basic understanding of statistics and data analysis.','No co-requisite.','本课程包括两个模块:市场情报和数字消费者行为。第一部分，市场情报，是关于收集、分析和解释有关市场和客户的数据。它专为将使用市场研究的分析师和经理而设计，因此适用于想要进入营销管理、咨询、战略、综合管理和创业的学生。学生将从基本的角度了解研究信息最有用的营销决策问题类型——目标市场选择、新产品或服务的引入或修改、客户保留、定价等问题。
第二个模块侧重于数字消费者行为。仅在过去十年中，新的数字技术就从根本上重塑了营销理论和实践。技术改变了企业与消费者互动的沟通方式。摩尔定律使消费者数据的存储和分析具有可扩展性，为细粒度行为分析创造了机会。新的监控工具促进了精确和个性化的客户关系管理实践。移动电话和平板电脑的兴起使基于位置的消息传递和互惠通信成为可能。无处不在的视频内容催生了丰富的原生广告计划。社交网络的全球兴起使基于网络的预测建模以及基于消费者同行偏好的新形式的定位和推荐策略成为可能。最后，新的社交媒体将所有这些都带到了公共舞台上，口耳相传推动了品牌知名度和品牌忠诚度， 该模块将对 21 世纪数字营销和社交媒体分析的理论和实践提供详细的应用视角。这门课程将覆盖的主题包括电子商务的行为基础、社交网络营销、社交媒体分析、用户生成的内容管理和营销、大数据和数字广告时代的客户关系管理策略、广告定位的预测建模、病毒式产品设计、多渠道体验、随机实验、A/B 测试和营销策略中的因果推断。','This course consists of two modules, market intelligence and digital consumer behavior. The first part, market intelligence, is about gathering, analyzing, and interpreting data about markets and customers. It has been designed for analysts and managers who will be using market research, and so is intended for students wanting to go into marketing management, consulting, strategy, general management, and entrepreneurship. Students will learn about the types of marketing decision problems in which research information is most useful -- problems of target market selection, new product or service introduction or modification, customer retention, pricing, etc., from a fundamental perspective.
The second module is focused on digital consumer behavior. New digital technologies have fundamentally reshaped marketing theory and practice in the last decade alone. Technology has changed the modes of communication through which firms engage with consumers. Moore’s law has made the storage and analysis of consumer data scalable, creating opportunities for fine-grained behavioral analytics. New monitoring tools have fostered precise and personalized customer relationship management practices. The rise of mobile phones and tablets has enabled location based messaging and reciprocal communication. The ubiquity of video content has promulgated rich, native advertising programs. The global emergence of social networking has enabled networked based predictive modelling and new forms of targeting and referral strategies based on the preferences of consumers’ peers. And finally, new social media have brought all of this onto the public stage, with word of mouth conversations driving brand awareness and brand loyalty, and user generated content on review and ratings sites marketing or breaking demand for products or services. module will provide a detailed, applied perspective on the theory and practice of Digital Marketing and Social Media Analytics in the 21st century. We will cover topics like Behavioral Foundations of eCommerce, Social Network Marketing, Social Media Analytics, User Generated Content Management and Marketing, CRM Strategy in the Age of Big Data and Digital Advertising, Predictive Modeling for Ad Targeting, Viral Product Design, the Multichannel Experience, Randomized Experimentations, A/B Testing and Causal Inference in Marketing Strategy.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
