2026-27 Term 1','na','na','本课程旨在全面介绍社会心理学中的信息处理理论。学生将熟悉社会心理学理论在消费者判断和决策情境中的应用，并能够在学习期间形成研究思路。','This course aims to provide a complete introduction of information processing theories documented in social psychology. Students will be familiar with applications of social psychology theories in a consumer judgment and decision-making context, and be able to generate research ideas that they would continue to pursue during the course of the study programme.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102407,'MKT6330','市场学专题研究 - 消费者行为学理论 （一）','','MKT - Marketing','6330','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','No','No','本门课程将介绍与消费者行为相关的各种理论和问题。除了帮助学生构建基础的消费者行为研究知识框架，还有另外三个目标。首先，了解用于研究理论问题的各种方法论/范式。其次，学习质疑和批判已有的研究，以推动创新思维的产生。最后，开始构建自己的研究议程。','This course will introduce you to a wide variety of theories and issues related to consumer behavior. In addition to building your knowledge base of some of the literatures that are foundational to consumer behavior research, this course has three additional goals. First, you will develop an understanding of the range of methodologies/paradigms used to investigate theoretical issues. Second, you will learn to question and critique prior research in an effort to advance idea generation. Third, you will begin to develop your own research agenda.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102408,'MKT6331','市场学专题研究 - 消费者行为学理论 （二）','','MKT - Marketing','6331','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','No','','本课程侧重于研究消费者的决定。它涵盖了目标导向行为、决策和影响的相互作用、态度、选择、文化、无意识目标等主题。本课程侧重于理解当前消费者行为各个方面的理论和方法，以及通过开发建立在当前知识基础上的可检验的假设和理论观点来推进这方面的知识。','This course focuses on studying consumers'' decisions. It covers topics on goal-directed behavior, the interplay of decisions and effects, attitudes, choice, culture, non-conscious goals, etc. This course focuses on the understanding of current theoretical and methodological approaches to various aspects of consumer behavior, as well as advancing this knowledge by developing testable hypotheses and theoretical perspectives that build on the current knowledge base.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
