(102410,'MKT6351','市场学专题研究 - 实证模型','','MKT - Marketing','6351','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','该博士研讨会旨在让学生熟悉定量营销领域的基本研究技术、方法和主要发现，特别关注实证模型。研讨会将从离散选择建模中的一般问题和经济理论开始，讨论有关品牌选择的经典文献。余下的课程内容将讨论特定主题，例如消费者异质性、选择惯性、搜索摩擦、社会影响、总需求建模和非结构化数据分析。将要讨论的论文和主题将被组织在阅读列表中。
研讨会将在讲座和讨论的基础上进行。在每次研讨会会议开始时，讲师将简要介绍论文中的背景和关键概念。然后，一位学生将对论文进行介绍。随后将进行涉及全班的一般性讨论。
学生应提前阅读论文并充分参与论文讨论。除了讨论之外，学生还应提出研究想法，将其形成研究计划并在课堂上展示。','This doctoral seminar is designed to acquaint students with the basic research techniques, approaches, and key findings in quantitative marketing areas with a particular focus on empirical models. The seminar will start with general issues and economic theories in discrete choice modeling by discussing classical literature on brand choices. The following seminar sessions will be devoted to the discussion of specific topics such as consumer heterogeneity, choice inertia, search frictions, social influences, aggregate demand modeling, and unstructured data analysis. The papers and topics to be discussed will be organized in a reading list.
The seminar will be delivered based on lectures and discussions. At the start of each seminar session, the instructor will briefly introduce the background and key concepts in the papers. Then, a student will make a presentation about the paper. This will be followed by a general discussion involving the whole class.
The students are expected to read the papers in advance and get fully involved in the paper discussions. In addition to the discussion, students are expected to propose a research idea, formulate it in a research proposal, and present it in class.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102411,'MKT6380','市场学专题研究 - 基于大数据行为学研究方法论','','MKT - Marketing','6380','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','经管学院','经管学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Prior coursework in marketing, consumer behaviour, econometrics, statistics, research methods, or related social science methods is recommended.','','本研究生研讨课旨在培养学生运用大规模数字行为数据评估并设计实证研究的能力。课程
聚焦数字平台、社交媒体、创作者生态、线上市场平台与 AI 介入环境中的行为数据，并围绕授课教师在数字平台、社交媒体、创作者经济、平台设计、数字工具、基于机器学习的测量、因果推断与生成式人工智能等方面的研究兴趣展开。学生将学习如何批判性阅读前沿实证论文，评估数据构建与实证可信度，并形成关于平台设计与数字工具如何影响创作者、消费者、品牌和社会结果的原创研究问题和研究计划。课程重点不是对每一种方法进行完整技术训练，而是通过选择性介绍技术工具来支持研究评估和研究计划设计。','This postgraduate research seminar develops students'' ability to evaluate and design empirical research using large-scale digital trace data from digital platforms, social media, creator ecosystems, online marketplaces, and AI-mediated environments. The course is organized around the instructor''s research interests in digital platforms, social media, the creator economy, platform design, digital tools, machine-learning-based measurement, causal inference, and generative AI. Students learn to read frontier empirical papers critically, assess data construction and empirical credibility, and develop original research ideas on how platform design and digital tools shape the behaviour and outcomes of creators, consumers, brands, and society. The course is not designed as comprehensive technical training in every method covered; technical tools are introduced selectively to support research evaluation and proposal development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
