(102435,'MSE1000','基本材料科学','','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','1000','M',1.00,1000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Summer','','','本课程针对不具备大学物理、化学及工程背景的学生。本课程旨在提供材料学的基础知识，介绍材料科学在日常生活及现代科技中的重要性。','This course is not for students having Physics, Chemistry and Engineering background at the university-level. It aims to provide basic knowledge in the Science of Materials. Different topics will be introduced to demonstrate how important materials are; and identify their roles in our civilization, daily life, and modern technology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102436,'MSE2001','材料的化学基础','Chemical Foundation for Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','2001','M',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','CHM1001 General Chemistry','','本课程面向材料科学等相关专业学生，系统介绍有机化学的基本概念，是学习现代有机化学高级内容的基础。
课程将讲解有机分子中常见的化学键类型及其在分子结构、反应性和立体化学中的作用，重点强调手性在有机与生物体系中的重要性及其化学与生物化学意义。
本课程将系统介绍多种有机官能团，包括醇、酚、醚、环氧化物、醛、酮、羧酸、胺、氨基酸、碳水化合物及杂环化合物等，分析其结构特征、相对反应性以及典型反应机制。同时，课程将探讨有机反应的热力学与动力学规律，帮助学生定量理解反应选择性与效率。
此外，课程还将通过实例讲解多步有机合成，阐释官能团之间的互相转化及其在有机合成中的应用策略。','This course provides a foundational introduction to organic chemistry, tailored for students pursuing studies in materials science. It emphasizes the essential concepts necessary for understanding more advanced topics in modern organic chemistry.
Students will explore the nature and types of chemical bonds commonly encountered in organic molecules, with a focus on how bonding influences molecular structure, reactivity, and stereochemistry. The course will highlight the importance of chirality in organic and biological systems and discuss its implications in chemical and biochemical processes.
A broad range of organic functional groups—including alcohols, phenols, ethers, epoxides, aldehydes, ketones, carboxylic acids, amines, amino acids, carbohydrates, and heterocycles—will be introduced. The structural features, relative reactivities, and underlying mechanisms of their reactions will be analyzed in detail. Quantitative aspects of organic reactivity and selectivity, particularly those related to thermodynamic and kinetic considerations, will also be addressed. In addition, selected examples of multi-step organic syntheses will be discussed to illustrate the principles of reactivity and functional group transformations in practice.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102437,'MSE2002','材料的物理基础','Physics Foundation for Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','2002','M',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','CHM1001 General Chemistry','本课程旨在为学生提供材料所需的基本物理知识，包括原子结构、分子结构、晶体结构、热力学定律、相变等。','This course provides students with the basic physical knowledge needed to understand the properties of materials, including atomic structure, molecular structure, crystalline structure, thermodynamics, phase transitions, etc.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102438,'MSE2003','材料实验 I','Materials Laboratory I','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','2003','M',2.00,2000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Completion of MSE 2001 and MSE 2002 prior to enrollment in this course is required.','','\\','This laboratory course covers basic techniques for materials synthesis and characterization. These experiments provide students with comprehensive training on (1) the safe handling of chemical reagents and chemical wastes; (2) the correct use of laboratory instruments and equipment commonly used in synthesis; (3) basic characterization techniques in materials science; (4) Recording, processing and reporting experimental data and results. This course allows students to gain experience in basic experimental practice in materials science. Lab manuals are available from the course instructor','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102439,'MSE2012','材料的微纳结构','* Micro and Nano Structures of Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','2012','M',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','/','/','本课程旨在介绍材料的微观结构与纳米结构及其对材料物理、化学和力学性能的影响。主要内容包括晶体结构、晶体缺陷、界面、相变以及微纳结构的形成与调控原理。课程还将涵盖现代材料结构表征技术，如电子显微镜和X射线衍射等。通过课堂讲授、案例分析以及作业实践，学生将深入理解材料工程与纳米技术中“结构–性能–加工”之间的内在关系。','This course explores the microstructural and nanostructural features of materials and their critical role in determining physical, chemical, and mechanical properties. Students will learn about crystal structures, defects, interfaces, phase transformations, and the principles behind the formation and control of micro- and nanostructures. The course also covers modern synthesis and characterization techniques, such as electron microscopy and X-ray diffraction. Through lectures, case studies, and hands-on assignments, students will develop a deep understanding of the structure–property–processing relationship that underpins materials engineering and nanotechnology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102440,'MSE2021','材料力学','* Materials Mechanics','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','2021','M',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','PHY1001 Mechanics; MAT1001Calculus I or MAT1003 Analysis I','None','本课程通过加深对材料的结构、性能和应用的理解，介绍材料的结构和物理特性。将通过介绍材料的局部键合和原子排列来探讨材料特性的物理起源，进而加深对各种固体的结构和特性的理解。本课程将着重介绍固体的机械和热学性能。','This course will introduce the structural and physical properties of materials by developing a better understanding of the structure, properties, and applications of materials. A fundamental approach will be used to define the structure and properties of a wide range of solids on the basis of the local bonding and atomic order present in the material by emphasizing the physical origins of material properties. Particular attention will be paid to studying the mechanical and thermal behavior of solids.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102441,'MSE2023','材料实验','','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','2023','M',1.00,2000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','MSE2012 Materials Chemistry','N.A','这门实验课程涵盖了材料合成和表征的基本技术。这些实验为学生提供了全面的培训，包括：（1）安全处理化学试剂和化学废物的技巧；（2）正确使用有机合成常用的实验室仪器和设备；（3）材料科学中的基本表征技术；（4）记录、处理和报告实验数据和结果。本课程使学生能够在材料科学的基本实验实践中获得经验。实验手册可从课程讲师处获取。','This laboratory course covers basic techniques for materials synthesis and characterization. These experiments provide students with comprehensive training on (1) the safe handling of chemical reagents and chemical wastes; (2) the correct use of laboratory instruments and equipment commonly used in organic synthesis; (3) basic characterization techniques in materials science; (4) Recording, processing and reporting experimental data and results. This course allows students to gain experience in basic experimental practice in materials science. Lab manuals are available from the course instructor.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102442,'MSE3001','計算材料科學與人工智能','Computational Materials Science with AI','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','3001','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本課程以循序漸進的方式介紹用於材料分析、性能預測及設計的計算與人工智能輔助方法，並提供材料數據與機器學習方面的引導式入門訓練。內容亦涵蓋跨尺度計算建模概覽、模型評估與解釋、代理模型、優化及逆向設計。案例學習強調材料學判斷、方法選擇，以及對假設與局限的理解。無需編程或機器學習先修經驗。','This course provides an accessible introduction to computational and AI-assisted approaches for materials analysis, property prediction and design. It offers guided, introductory training in materials data and machine learning, alongside an overview of computational modelling across scales, model evaluation and interpretation, surrogate modelling, optimisation and inverse design. Examples and case studies emphasise materials reasoning, method selection, assumptions and limitations. No prior programming or machine-learning experience is required.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
