(102450,'MSE3013','化工原理','Principles of Chemical Engineering','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','3013','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','For students who have studied some courses such as Advanced Mathematics, Physical Chemistry, General Chemistry, and Introduction to Materials Science and Engineering.','None.','本科目是一門重要的技术基礎課程，為學習材料科學与工程、化學、新能源工程或环境工程及相關專業的學生提供化學工程知識。

本課程對學生專業知識和工程能力的培養起著至關重要的作用。本科目提供了一門綜合應用數學、物理和化學等基礎知識來分析和解决化工生產中各種化工過程的物质平衡和能量平衡等重要問題的工程學科。本課程是從理論到工程，從基礎到專業知識的橋樑。該課程主要側重於基本過程分析：過程變數的定義、量測和計算；控制過程效能的守恒定律和熱力學關係；以及過程材料的物理特性。 它介紹了解决工藝相關問題的工程方法，並為後續的熱力學、單元操作和輸送現象、動力學和反應器設計以及工藝動力學和控制課程奠定了基礎。

工程中的重要原理和方法將應用於討論實際工業應用的各種化工过程操作。其中重要目標是訓練學生解決工程疑難，幫助學生成為有創造力的工程問題解决者。','This is a major technical foundation course to provide chemical engineering knowledge for students whose study majors such as materials science & engineering, chemistry, or new energy or environmental engineering and related ones.

This course plays a crucial role in cultivating the professional knowledge and engineering solving ability of students. It provides an engineering discipline that comprehensively applies basic knowledge such as mathematics, physics, and chemistry to analyze and solve important material and energy balance issues in various chemical processes in chemical production. This course serves as a bridge from theory to engineering, and from foundation to professional knowledge. The course mainly focuses on elementary process analysis: definitions, measurement, and calculation of process variables; conservation laws and thermodynamic relations that govern the performance of processes; and physical properties of process materials. It introduces the engineering approach to solving process-related problems and lays the foundation for subsequent courses in thermodynamics, unit operations and transport phenomena, kinetics and reactor design, and process dynamics and control.

Important principles and methodology in engineering will be applied in the discussion of various chemical processes for practical industrial application. The process and strategy of problem solving will be used to help students become creative problem solvers.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102451,'MSE3022','高分子材料','* Polymer Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','3022','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1','CHM2002 Physical Chemistry
CHM2310 Organic Chemistry I','','本课程全面介绍高分子化学与反应工程的原理及应用。课程内容包括缩合、自由基、阳离子、阴离子以及配位聚合等基本聚合机理。学生将探讨多种聚合工艺，包括本体聚合、溶液聚合、乳液聚合、气相聚合和淤浆聚合方法。课程重点讲解聚合反应的动力学、反应器设计以及高分子结构与性能的关系。','This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the principles and applications of polymer chemistry and reaction engineering. Topics include fundamental polymerization mechanisms such as condensation, free radical, cationic, anionic, and coordination polymerizations. Students will explore various polymerization processes, including bulk, solution, emulsion, gas phase, and slurry methods. Emphasis is placed on the kinetics of polymerization reactions, reactor design, and polymer structure-property relationships.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102452,'MSE3023','材料试验 II','Materials General Laboratory II','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','3023','M',2.00,3000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','CHM1001 General Chemistry or CHM1011 Honours General Chemistry','','本实验课程介绍材料的制备、加工与表征技术，涵盖表面改性、纳米材料、聚合物乳液、胶黏剂及复合材料。学生将接受以下训练：(1) 化学试剂、仪器及废物的安全处理；(2) 正确使用实验设备；(3) 基础表征方法，如接触角测量、荧光光谱和力学测试；(4) 实验数据的准确记录、分析与报告。课程最后一周，学生将自主设计并开展一次开放性实验，以培养独立科研能力。本课程为学生提供全面的材料科学实验实践。','This laboratory course introduces practical techniques in materials synthesis, processing, and characterization, covering surface modification, nanomaterials, polymer latex, adhesives, and composites. Students will receive training in: (1) safe handling of chemicals, instruments, and wastes; (2) correct use of laboratory equipment; (3) fundamental characterization methods such as contact angle measurement, fluorescence spectroscopy, and mechanical testing; (4) accurate recording, analyzing, and reporting of experimental data. In the final week, students will design and conduct an open-ended experiment to develop independent research skills. This course provides comprehensive experimental practice in materials science.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102453,'MSE3306','芯片材料','Chip Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','3306','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','Basic knowledge of physics，chemistry，mathematics，and materials at the undergraduate level is required.','','本课程面向本科三年级学生，无需半导体器件或晶体管物理先修基础。课程开篇以科普视角介绍半导体材料的全貌(什么是半导体材料、有哪些类型、关键性能指标以及如何制备),再建立MOS晶体管基本结构与电特性的理解基础。在此基础上，课程系统介绍现代芯片制造中涉及的各类材料：半导体衬底材料（Si、SOI、化合物半导体）、栅介电材料（SiO2、high-k）、栅电极材料（多晶硅、HKMG）、互连金属（Al、Cu、W、Co）、硅化物、掺杂材料、光刻胶与硬掩模、CMP磨料、以及二维半导体等新兴材料。课程强调材料选择如何影响器件性能的直观理解，平衡材料科学、制造工艺与器件物理三者关系，为学生后续深入学习微电子与半导体工程奠定基础。','This course is an introductory-level course designed for undergraduate Year 3 students with no prior background in semiconductor devices or transistor physics. The course begins with a broad, accessible overview of semiconductor materials — what they are, what types exist, what properties matter, and how they are prepared — before building the fundamentals of MOS transistor structure and electrical characteristics. From this foundation, the course systematically introduces the full spectrum of materials used in modern chip manufacturing: semiconductor substrates (Si, SOI, compound semiconductors), gate dielectrics (SiO2, high-k), gate electrodes (polysilicon, HKMG), interconnect metals (Al, Cu, W, Co, Ru), silicides, dopant materials, photoresists and hard masks, CMP slurries, and emerging materials such as 2D semiconductors. Emphasis is placed on intuitive understanding of how materials choices directly affect device performance, striking a balance between materials science, manufacturing processes, and device physics. The course prepares students with the foundational knowledge and practical perspective needed for advanced study in microelectronics and semiconductor engineering.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102454,'MSE3404','环境材料','(MSE6110) Environmental Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','3404','M',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','《环境材料》课程主要概述环境处理中的材料，讲解其基本原理、全球挑战、污染控制等，以及材料的制备方法。','The course of "Environmental Materials" mainly gives an overview of materials in Environmental treatment. It explains the fundamentals and global challenges, pollution controls etc, as well as the materials preparation methods.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
