2017-18 Summer','For students who have studied some courses such as General Chemistry (CHM1001) and Physical Chemistry (CHM2002).','','本课程是新能源科学与工程专业的一门专业选修课。它研究纳米材料的结构、性能与制备方法，以及纳米材料的应用与纳米科技的新进展。
主题包括纳米材料的基本概念，纳米结构制备，纳米尺度的表征，纳米材料在能源、生物与复合材料等方面的应用，以及纳米材料的安全性。
本课程主要任务是使学生对纳米材料这种新的材料具有一个比较广泛的了解，为以后学习和工作提供必要的知识和方法。','This course is a major elective course for New Energy Science and Engineering. It studies the structures, properties and preparation methods of nanomaterials, as well as the application of nanomaterials and the new progress of nanotechnology.
The topics include basics of nanomaterials, fabrication of nanostructures, characterization at nanoscale, nanomaterials for energy applications, nanobiomaterials, nanocomposite materials, and nanomaterial safety.
The main task of this course is to enable students to have a wider understanding of nanomaterials, which will provide necessary knowledge and methods for future study and work.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102458,'MSE4020','毕业论文','Thesis','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','4020','M',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','•	Final-year students in the Materials Science and Engineering program','','本課程旨在培養學生獨立進行材料科學與工程領域研究或設計專案的能力。在學術指導老師的監督下，學生將選定研究主題，執行實驗研究與理論分析，並完成系統化的畢業專題計畫。研究領域涵蓋金屬材料、高分子材料、陶瓷與複合材料、功能材料、奈米材料等範疇。
課程著重於理解材料結構、性質、製程與應用之間的關聯性，並培養學生在材料表徵、數值模擬、製程優化等先進技術領域的綜合能力。課程要求學生提交完整論文，並於結業時進行口頭答辯。','This course aims to develop students’ ability to independently conduct research or design projects in the field of Materials Science and Engineering. Under the supervision of an academic advisor, students will select a topic, carry out experimental studies, theoretical analyses, and complete a systematic final-year thesis project. Research areas may include metallic materials, polymers, ceramics and composites, functional materials, nanomaterials, etc.
It emphasizes understanding the relationships between material structures, properties, processing, and applications, as well as developing comprehensive skills in advanced technologies, such as material characterization, numerical simulation, and processing optimization. The course requires students to submit a full thesis and deliver an oral defense at the end.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
