(102462,'MSE4640','太阳能电池','Solar Cells','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','4640','M',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','太阳能电池课程介绍了太阳能电池运行和发展的基础物理原理，以满足可再生能源的需求。课程内容涵盖了对基础半导体材料的研究，重点关注其在太阳能电池应用中相关的结构、光学和电子特性。本课程强调对太阳能电池创新材料的全面理解，既涉及基本原理，也关注实际应用和产业层面。学生将接触最新的研究进展，参与讨论，并解决从实验室到产业中的实际挑战。这将帮助学生深入理解如何将基础的太阳能电池与工程概念相结合，以突破光伏技术的局限性，设计出更高效的太阳能光伏组件。','The Solar Cell course offers an introduction to the fundamental physics underlying the operation and development of solar cells to meet renewable energy demands. The curriculum encompasses the exploration of basic semiconductor materials, focusing on their structural, optical, and electronic properties relevant to solar cell applications. This course emphasizes a comprehensive understanding of innovative materials for solar cell applications, covering fundamental principles as well as real-world and industrial aspects. Students will engage in current research updates, participate in discussions, and address real-world challenges from the laboratory to industry. This will provide insights into how fundamental solar cells and engineering concepts can contribute to overcoming the limitations of solar photovoltaics and designing more efficient solar photovoltaic modules for the future.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102463,'MSE4650','光电材料','Optoelectronic Materials','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','4650','M',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'CHM1001, General Chemistry; MAT1001 or MAT1011 or MAT1002 or MAT1012, Calculus; MAT2040 or MAT2041 or MAT3040, Linear Algebra; PHY1001, Mechanics;','','本课程全面介绍光电材料的基本原理，重点探讨新型分子光电材料及其在功能器件中的集成与应用。课程首先从固体物理和半导体物理的基础理论入手，为学生构建理解光与电在分子层面相互作用的理论框架，随后将教学内容分为基础理论与实际应用两个核心部分。基础理论部分深入探讨光电材料的结构特性、光学性质以及电荷传输机制；实际应用部分则将这些理论转化为对具体器件运行机制的分析，涵盖发光器件、太阳能电池、光电探测器以及薄膜晶体管等实用光电器件。','This course provides a comprehensive introduction to the principles of optoelectronic materials, with a specialized focus on novel molecular systems and their integration into functional devices. The curriculum begins with the essential foundations of solid-state and semiconductor physics, providing the theoretical framework necessary to understand how light and electricity interact at the molecular level. The course is structured into two primary modules: Foundations and Applications. The Foundations section examines the structural, optical, and charge transport properties of optoelectronic materials. The Applications section translates these principles into the operation of practical devices, including light emitters, solar cells, photodetectors, and thin-film transistors.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
