2025-26 Term 1','elementary quantum mechanics, electrodynamics, and thermodynamics and statistics.','Calculus, linear algebra and differential equations.','现代固体是许多粒子以凝聚态存在的物理学，数量级为1023原子/ cm3。然而，传统的固体物理学只涉及原子形成周期性结构的晶体。固体物理学将主要涵盖传统材料。这个领域有许多多样化的主题和现象。一个学期不可能涵盖所有这些主题，甚至不可能涵盖一些主要主题，这个领域有许多涵盖各种主题的书籍。我将使用的材料来自下面列出的各种书籍。如果你只想看一本书，那么我建议通读 Giuseppe Grosso 和 Giuseppe Pastori Parravicini：固体物理学。本课程假设你具备初等量子力学、电动力学、热力学和统计学的知识。','Modern solid states is the physics of many particles in condensed form, order of 1023atoms/cm3 . However, the traditional solid-state physics is only about crystals in which atoms form a periodic structure. Solid state physics I will mostly cover the traditional materials. There are many diversified subjects and phenomena in this field. It is impossible to cover all of them, or even some main subjects, in one semester, there are many books in this field covering various subjects. The materials that I will use come from various books listed below. If you want to go through one book only, then I recommend to read through Giuseppe Grosso and Giuseppe Pastori Parravicini: Solid-State Physics. A knowledge of elementary quantum mechanics, electrodynamics, and thermodynamics and statistics will be assumed.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102499,'MSE6306','半導體器件物理','','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','6306','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
