PHY3950 Basic Electronics, OR,
PHY4001 Solid-State Physics','None.','该课程为硕士生和博士生设计，旨在学习和探索半导体器件的物理
和运行机制。本课程讲授基础的和先进的半导体器件及其物理原
理。课程涵盖半导体基础理论(电子和空穴、费米能级、载流子生
成和复合等)、掺杂效应、PN 结的形成、电性能和设计、PN 结光
学特性、双极结型晶体管、MOS 电容及电荷、电荷耦合器件、
CMOS 有源像素传感器、典型 MOSFET 电流电压特性、MOSFET
迁移率降级和载流子速度饱和模型、CMOS 技术缩放和短沟道效
应、纳米 CMOS 晶体管(FinFET, GAA etc.)及先进晶体管器件等。
课程还讲述必要的半导体器件制备工艺和表征方法。学生将学习半
导体器件的核心知识、工作机理、设计方法和发展趋势。','The course is designed for Master/PhD students to learn and explore the
physics and operation mechanisms of semiconductor devices. This
course teaches the fundamental and advanced semiconductor devices
and the physics. The course covers Semiconductor material
fundamentals (electron and hole, Fermi energy, carrier generation and
recombination), Doping effect, PN junction electrical performance and
designs, PN junction optical properties, Bipolar Junction Transistor
(BJT), Metal-oxide-semiconductor (MOS) capacitor and related charge,
Charge coupled device, CMOS active-pixel sensor, typical metal-oxide semiconductor field transistor(MOSFET) characteristics, MOSFET
mobility degradation and carrier velocity saturation, CMOS technology
scaling and short-channel effect, Nano-CMOS (FinFET, GAA etc.) and
advanced transistors. It could also involve the necessary device process
and characterization knowledge. The students will learn the core
knowledge, operation mechanisms, design methods and future trend of
semiconductor devices.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102500,'MSE6307','磁學和自旋電子學','','MSE - Materials Science& Engineering','6307','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2019-20 Summer
2020-21 Summer','Quantum Mechanics, Solid State Physics','None','在传统的微电子学中，一般是利用电子的荷电性由电场来控制电子的输运过程的。在后摩尔时代，利用电子的自旋作为信息载体可以进一步提高信息处理速度和存储密度，由此发展出一门新的学科—— 自旋电子学。自旋电子学(Spintronics or spin electronics)，是一门结合磁学与微电子学的交叉学科。巨磁电阻的发现是自旋电子学发展的里程碑。自从1997年至今大约有280亿个巨磁电阻和隧穿磁电阻读出头投放市场，产生了巨大的科技与社会济效益，基于电子自旋属性的巨磁电阻效应也因此于2007年获得了诺贝尔奖，标志着以自旋为核心的电子信息技术新时代的到来。诺贝尔奖委员会将其评价为开启了通向技术新世界的大门。本门课程主要是给研究生及部分感兴趣的高年级本科生介绍自旋电子学的一些基本物理机制以及利用电子自旋的产品，如电脑硬盘、磁存储器、磁存储芯片、磁感应器及自旋微波振荡器等。','This course discusses magnetic and spintronic properties of solids based on quantum mechanics and solid state physics. Fundamental theories of magnetism (ferromagnetism, antiferromagnetism, and ferrimagnetism), and spintronic phenomena (anisotropic magnetoresistance, giant magnetoresistance, tunneling magnetoresistance, spin Hall effect, and spin injection into semiconductors) will be covered. Magnetic and spintronic devices (magnetic recording, magnetic sensor, MRAM, semiconductor spintronic devices) will also be investigated.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
