(102602,'MUS2603','钢琴练习（指挥） III','','MUS - Music','2603','M',1.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','','','本科目是MUS1604的延续。系一对一课程，主要是提高学生的高级钢琴演奏水平和钢琴技术的应用能力，以保证学生能够有足够的钢琴演奏能力完成总谱读法、歌剧等课程的相关内容。','This course is the continuation of MUS1604. This is a personalized one-on-one piano course that focuses on improving student conductors'' advanced piano performance level and technical application skills. The aim is to ensure that students have sufficient piano playing ability to confidently complete related coursework such as score reading and opera.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102603,'MUS2604','钢琴练习（指挥）IV','','MUS - Music','2604','M',1.00,2000,'Major','已评分','个人学习','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2','','','本科目是MUS2603的延续。系一对一课程，主要是提高学生的更高级钢琴演奏水平和钢琴技术的应用能力，以保证学生能够有足够的钢琴演奏能力完成总谱读法、歌剧等课程的相关内容。','This course is the continuation of MUS2603. This is a personalized one-on-one piano course that focuses on improving student conductors'' more advanced piano performance level and technical application skills. The aim is to ensure that students have sufficient piano playing ability to confidently complete related coursework such as score reading and opera.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102604,'MUS2605','第二乐器练习 III','','MUS - Music','2605','M',1.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本科目是MUS1606的延续。系一对一课程，根据学生的第一乐器情况选择第二乐器，对于以钢琴为主乐器的学生需要选择一件弦乐、管乐或打击乐器作为第二乐器，了解乐队乐器的演奏特点和技术特点。','This course is the continuation of MUS1606. This course offers personalized one-on-one instruction, with the selection of a secondary instrument based on the student''s primary instrument. For students whose primary instrument is piano, the course requires the selection of a secondary instrument from the categories of strings, winds, or percussion. The curriculum is designed to provide students with an understanding of the unique performance and technical aspects of various orchestra instruments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102605,'MUS2606','第二乐器练习 IV','','MUS - Music','2606','M',1.00,2000,'Major','已评分','个人学习','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本科目是MUS2605的延续。系一对一课程，根据学生的第一乐器情况选择第二乐器，对于以钢琴为主乐器的学生需要选择一件弦乐、管乐或打击乐器作为第二乐器，了解乐队乐器的演奏特点和技术特点。','This course is the continuation of MUS2605. This course offers personalized one-on-one instruction, with the selection of a secondary instrument based on the student''s primary instrument. For students whose primary instrument is piano, the course requires the selection of a secondary instrument from the categories of strings, winds, or percussion. The curriculum is designed to provide students with an understanding of the unique performance and technical aspects of various orchestra instruments.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
