(102800,'MUS6283','歌剧指挥工作坊 II','','MUS - Music','6283','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1','MUS5283 Opera Conducting Workshop I','','本科目是MUS5283的延续，旨在培训指挥学生进行歌剧指挥，涵盖从排练到演出的整个过程。','This is the continuation of MUS5283 that trains conducting students in conducting operas from rehearsal to performance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102801,'MUS6284','艺术实践 III','','MUS - Music','6284','M',2.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本科目是实践类课程，根据学生在专业课程中所学到的内容为基础进行乐队排和指挥的实践，并完成音乐会。学生通过实践与职业乐手进行合作，积累指挥与排练的经验。
学生将通过实践课程和实际指挥乐队来提高自己的技能和知识水平。实践项目包含:
1.	参加观摩彩排
2.	专业指挥家指导
3.	艺术实践练习
4.	音乐会等等','Practical training is essential for learning orchestral conducting because it allows conductors to develop technical skills, understand ensemble dynamics, build communication skills, develop rehearsal techniques, and gain performance experience. Through hands-on experience with an ensemble, conductors can gain a deeper understanding of the intricacies of conducting, experiment with different techniques, and receive feedback from experienced mentors and musicians. Practical Training includes the following components:
1.	Attending Rehearsal
2.	Mentorship
3.	On Stage Practice
4.	Studio Concert
etc.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102802,'MUS6285','艺术实践 IV','','MUS - Music','6285','M',2.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102803,'MUS6286','进阶总谱研读与剖析II','','MUS - Music','6286','M',1.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','','','本科目是集体授课，主要强化学生对总谱的阅读能力，提高学生对各种C谱号和移调乐器阅读的熟练程度，并通过讲授让学生了解阅读总谱的要点，并且能够形成自己的音乐解释思路。在此基础上，还会向学生讲授如何处理乐队合唱作品、乐队艺术歌曲这类作品的阅读与解释内容。','This course focuses on improving students’ ability to read scores, including various C clefs and transposing instruments. Through instruction, students will learn key techniques for interpreting and forming their own musical ideas. Additionally, the course will cover reading and interpreting choral and band works.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102804,'MUS6288','乐队文献与风格简史 II','','MUS - Music','6288','M',2.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','','','本科目为乐队文献与风格简史I的延续。本科目将围绕着乐队文献的历史发展，探讨音乐文化的形成和演变，以及乐队文献在音乐史上的地位和影响。课程将涉及不同的时期、地区和风格的乐队文献。本科目的教学方法将采用多种形式，包括课堂讲授、音乐鉴赏、文献分析等，旨在帮助学生全面理解乐队文献的历史演进和音乐文化的形成，同时提高学生的音乐鉴赏能力和文献分析能力。同时，我们将探讨乐队文献所体现的人文精神，包括音乐与社会、身份认同、文化传承等方面的关系，旨在让学生更好地领悟音乐的艺术美感和社会文化意义。','This course is a continuation of I, which will explore the historical development of band literature, its status and influence in music history, and its role in the formation and evolution of music culture across different periods, regions, and styles. Teaching methods will include classroom lectures, music appreciation, and literature analysis to enhance students’ understanding of the topic and improve their music appreciation and literature analysis abilities. The course will also examine the humanistic spirit reflected in band literature, including its relationships with society, identity, and cultural inheritance, with the aim of deepening students’ appreciation of music’s artistic beauty and social-cultural significance.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(102805,'MUS6289','总谱读法技巧与练习','','MUS - Music','6289','M',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','音乐学院','音乐学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1','','','本科目是一门集体授课，旨在强化学生对总谱的阅读能力，提高学生对各种C谱号和移调乐器的阅读熟练程度，并通过讲授让学生了解阅读总谱的要点，形成自己的音乐诠释思路。在此基础上，还会向学生讲授如何处理乐队合唱作品、乐队艺术歌曲等作品的阅读与诠释内容。','This course focuses on improving students’ ability of score reading, including various C clefs and transposing instruments. Through instruction, students will learn key techniques for interpreting and forming their own musical ideas. Additionally, the course will cover reading and interpreting lieders, choral and orchestral works.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
