(102937,'PED2010','体力活动与幸福感','','PED - Physical Education','2010','P',2.00,2000,'PE','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2','','','PED2010这门课程旨在向来自不同学科的本科生广泛介绍体育活动的作用以及它如何影响公众健康。整个学期，我们将涵盖以下主题:当前体育活动的建议，体育活动对各种健康相关结果的有益影响，体育活动的决定因素，如何在个人和人群水平上衡量体育活动，以及用于促进体育活动的策略。不同学科领域(如医学、数据科学和心理学)的学生可以从这门课程中受益。','The PED2010 course is designed to give undergraduate students from a variety of disciplines a broad introduction to the role of physical activity and how it affects the public’s health. Throughout the semester, we will cover topics such as the current recommendations for physical activity, the beneficial effects of physical activity on various health-related outcomes, determinants of physical activity, how to measure physical activity at both the individual and population levels, and strategies used to promote physical activity. Students within different areas of disciplines (e.g., medicine, data science, and psychology) could benefit from this course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
