2025-26 Term 2','Calculus I
Calculus II
Mechanics','','本科介绍光学、狭义相对论、量子物理与其应用和粒子物理的基本原理，当中利用到微积分。本科适合物理专业，准备副修物理的学生修读。内容包括：几何光学、干涉和衍射、狭义相对论、量子物理及其有关原子、分子、固体和核子的应用、粒子物理。学生宜同时修读微积分的科目。','This introductory calculus-based course discusses the basic principles of optics, special relativity, and quantum physics and its applications, plus an introduction to particle physics.  It is suitable for potential majors in science and engineering, and for those who intend to minor in physics. Topics include: Geometric optics, interference, diffraction, special relativity, quantum physics and its applications to atoms, molecules, solids, and nuclei, particle physics. Students are advised to take this course concurrently with a course in calculus.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103016,'PHY2210','学生自主习题讨论班（二）','Student Oriented Learning II','PHY - Physics','2210','P',1.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程为学生提供了在小组环境中进行自主学习的机会。课程将安排一系列物理入门研讨会，学生需独立探讨选定领域的相关问题。学生需在课堂上展示其对问题的理解，并与同学和授课教师积极讨论。课程重点培养学生的自学能力、团队合作精神、解决问题的能力、文献检索与阅读能力，尤其注重提升学生的展示与沟通技巧。','This course offers students an opportunity for self-directed learning in a small-group setting. A series of introductory physics seminars will be provided, and students are expected to independently explore specific problems in selected areas. Students will be required to present their understanding during class sessions and actively participate in discussions with their peers and the instructor. The course places a strong emphasis on developing skills in self-study, teamwork, problem-solving, literature research, and reading. Special focus is placed on enhancing students'' presentation and communication abilities.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
