2026-27 Term 1','PHY1001 or PHY1011, MAT1002 Calculus II or MAT1012 Honours Calculus II and MAT2040, or MAT2041, Linear Algebra or MAT2042 Honours Linear Algebra','None.','本课程致力于介绍物理里常用的求解微分方程的方法。课程将涉及傅里叶级数和傅里叶变换，Sturm-Liouville理论，1阶，2阶常微分方程，偏微分方程（拉普拉斯方程，热方程，波动方程），简正振动等。','This course provides a survey of various analytical techniques commonly used to solve differential equations in physics. The course aims to provide an introduction to Fourier Series and Fourier Transforms, Sturm-Liouville Theory, 1st and 2nd ODEs and PDEs such as the Laplace, heat and wave equations and normal vibrations.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103018,'PHY2650','计算物理与人工智能工具','Computational Physics and AI Tools','PHY - Physics','2650','P',2.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Linear Algebra, Calculus, Introductory Classical Mechanics, Basic Programming skills (Python or C++ recommended)','','课程将介绍物理学和其他科学计算中的基本数值方法，包括内插法/外推法、求根法、数值积分、微分方程求解、机器学习和神经网络。本基础课程不要求学生具备计算方面的知识。','The course will provide introduction to basic numerical methods in physics and other scientific computations, including interpolation/extrapolation, root finding, numerical integration, differential equation solving, machine learning and neural networks. This Basic course assumes no prior knowledge in computing methods.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103019,'PHY2910','普通物理实验（三）','Physics Laboratory III','PHY - Physics','2910','P',2.00,2000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','PHY1001 – Mechanics 力學
PHY1002 - Physics Laboratory 物理實驗
或PHY1910 - Physics Laboratory I 普通物理實驗I
或PHY1920 - Physics Laboratory II 普通物理實驗II','','本课程涵盖光电效应等多项经典现代物理实验，旨在深化学生对现代物理理论原理的理解，并培养其掌握重要实验测量技术与仪器操作的能力。透过实验操作与数据分析训练，学生将进一步提升实验技能、科学探究素养，以及观察、分析与解决问题的能力。课程亦强调数据处理方法的学习，学生将熟练运用常用科学数据处理软体，并借此提升实验报告与科学论文的撰写能力。','This course includes a series of classical modern physics experiments, such as the photoelectric effect, designed to illustrate key principles taught in modern physics courses. It aims to equip students with essential experimental techniques and instrumentation skills, while enhancing their experimental proficiency, scientific inquiry abilities, and capacity for observation, analysis, and problem-solving. The course also emphasizes data analysis methods, enabling students to become proficient in using scientific softwares. Through these data-processing tools, students will further develop their skills in writing laboratory reports and scientific papers.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103020,'PHY3002','电动力学（一）','Electrodynamics I','PHY - Physics','3002','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1
2020-21 Summer','PHY2610 – Mathematical Methods in Physics I, or equivalent;
(can be replaced by MAT2002 – Ordinary Differential Equation, or equivalent;
MAT2040 – Linear Algebra, or equivalent;)','','这是一门在修读PHY2001（电学与磁学）之后的进阶课程。它的内容衔接PHY2001 和PHY3007（光电子学），并且是很多诸如无线通信、电子器件和电路等应用场景的技术基础。

这门课程深入讲解在真空和材料中电磁辐射的产生、传播和操控。它的主要内容包括静电学、静磁学、电磁波、狭义相对论下电磁波及带电粒子和电磁场的相互作用。','This is an advanced course on electromagnetic theory after taking PHY2001(Electricity and Magnetism). It works as a bridge connecting PHY2001 to PHY3007(Optoelectronics)/NSE6031(Spintronics) and as a foundation for many application scenarios, such as wireless communication, electronic devices and circuits etc.

This course provides a thorough understanding of the generation, propagation and manipulation of electromagnetic radiation in both vacuum and materials. Its main contents include electrostatics, magnetostatics, electromagnetic waves, special relativity and the interaction between electric particles with electromagnetic field.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103021,'PHY3006','半导体器件物理','Physics of Semiconductors Devices','PHY - Physics','3006','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2017-18 Term 2
2018-19 Term 2
2019-20 Term 2
2020-21 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','这是一门为材料科学与工程专业以及物理本科生而设计关于现代半导体器件的物理原理的导论课。首先从载流子的量子力学性质, 简述诸如硅, 锗及砷化镓等重要半导体内的电子能带结构及能隙概念。然后推导出它们的输运特性。接着, 再分别讨论一系列现代半导体器件，诸如二极管, 三极管, 场效应管, 发光二极管, 半导体激光器, 光探测器, 太阳能电池的结构和物理原理。完成本课程后, 学生能体会到他们从基础物理学及化学所学到的原理, 如何能应用到现代半导体器件上, 导致在信息科投和新能源科技的创新。','This is an introductory undergraduate course to explore the physical principles of modern semiconductor devices, catering for students in the Materials and Science Engineering as well as Physics Discipline. It begins with the description of energy band structures and energy band gaps in some technologically important semiconductors such as Si, Ge and GaAs, as a consequence of quantum mechanical nature of charge carriers. The transport properties will then be derived. Furthermore, the physical principles behind the operation of different devices, such as p-n junction diode, bipolar transistor, MOSFET, MESFET, LED, semiconductor laser, photodetector, and solar cell, will be discussed. At the completion of this Course, students will appreciate how the principles they learnt from basic physics and chemistry courses are useful for the application of modern semiconductor devices, which leads to innovation of both information and new energy technologies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103022,'PHY3007','光电子学','Optoelectronics','PHY - Physics','3007','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2019-20 Term 1
