(103033,'PHY3260','人工智能统计物理基础','Statistical Physics Foundation for AI','PHY - Physics','3260','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Linear Algebra, Calculus, Introductory Classical Mechanics, Basic Programming skills of Python, Basica Probability Theory, Thermodynamics','','本课程探讨了统计物理中的核心概念——如熵、自由能和玻尔兹曼分布——如何为现代深度学习（尤其是生成模型）提供统一的理论框架。学生将学习推导并应用重要的统计物理技术，包括变分与平均场方法、玻尔兹曼机与能量模型，以及基于评分的扩散模型，从而在理论与实践层面双双提升。','The course explores how foundational concepts from statistical physics—such as entropy, free energy, and the Boltzmann distribution—form a unified framework for modern deep learning, with a special focus on generative models. Students will learn to derive and apply key statistical-physics techniques—variational and mean-field methods, Boltzmann machines and energy-based models, and score-based diffusion models—gaining both theoretical insight and practical experience.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
