(103041,'PHY3710','材料科学物理','Physics of Materials Science','PHY - Physics','3710','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','PHY1001 Mechanics 力学
PHY1010 Principles of Physics II (thermodynamics and EM) 普通物理（二）(热学和电磁学)
PHY3410 Quantum Mechanics and its Applications I  量子力学与应用I','/','本课程探讨材料结构与性能的基本物理原理，旨在建立原子尺度结构（如晶体结构、缺陷）与宏观行为（如力学、电学、光学性质）之间的直接联系。本课程还将深入探讨加工参数如何调控材料的微观结构，并进而影响上述各项性能。 课程以经典理论和能带理论为基础，进一步深入到量子力学起主导作用的现代前沿主题，研究拓扑绝缘体、低维系统等量子材料的独特性质，并探索量子霍尔效应、自旋电子学等量子输运现象。其目标是提供一个全面的物理图像，用以理解和预测从传统金属、半导体到推动纳米技术与量子计算创新的尖端材料在内的各种材料行为。','This course explores the fundamental physical principles that govern the structure and properties of materials, establishing a direct link between atomic-scale structure, such as crystal lattices and defects with macroscopic behaviour, including mechanical, electrical, and optical properties. We will also try to understand how processing parameters control a material''s microstructure and affect the above properties. Building from a foundation in classical and band theory, the curriculum extends into modern topics where quantum mechanics dominates, examining the unique characteristics of quantum materials like topological insulators and low-dimensional systems, and exploring quantum transport phenomena such as quantum Hall effect and spintronics. The goal is to provide a comprehensive physical picture for understanding and predicting material behaviour, from traditional metals and semiconductors to the cutting-edge materials driving innovation in nanotechnology and quantum computing.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103042,'PHY3810','现代光学物理','Modern Optical Physics','PHY - Physics','3810','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','实验室','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
