2026-27 Term 1','None','None','本课程介绍近代光学物理的基本原理与应用。 课题包括：几何光学、波光学、偏振、傅氏光学、激光物理和非线性光学导论。','This course provides an overview of the basic principles and applications of various branches of modern optics physics. Topics covered include: geometrical optics, waves optics, polarization, Fourier optics, introduction to laser physics and nonlinear optics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103043,'PHY3820','天文学和天体物理入门','Introduction to Astronomy and Astrophysics','PHY - Physics','3820','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Calculus, Principles of Physics I','Principles of Physics II, III','本课程提供了本科生阶段对天文学和天体物理学基本概念和原理的介绍。主要内容包括: 从早期天文学到现代天文学、天体力学、地球与月球、辐射与物质的相互作用、天文学中的光探测、太阳、太阳系、恒星的性质、形成及演化、星系和宇宙学。','This course provides an introduction to the basic concepts and principles in astronomy and astrophysics at the undergraduate level. Topics to be covered include: From early astronomy to modern astronomy, celestial mechanics, earth and moon, interaction of radiation and matter, the sun, solar system, properties of stars, formation and evolution of stars, galaxies, cosmology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103044,'PHY3950','电子学基础','Basic Electronics','PHY - Physics','3950','P',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1','','','本课程介绍实验物理中常用的电子电路，讲授电子元件和电路功能的基础知识。主要内容包括：基本电路定律、线路分析、二极管线路、整流电路、晶体管、运算放大器及逻辑线路。每课题均讲授基础概要。课程以设计和构建一个简单的电路作为一个应用的小型专题作结。本课程讲授在专题实验及研究院课程的实验须知，适合未曾修读电子学的学生选读。','This is an introductory course on electric circuits commonly used in experimental physics. It aims at providing basic knowledge on what electronic components and circuits can do. The main content includes basic circuit laws, circuit analysis, diode circuits, rectifying circuits, transistors, operational amplifiers, and logic circuits. Each topic introduces an overview of the fundamentals. The course ends with a short project to design and construct a simple circuit for a defined application. The course is essential for performing experimental work in senior projects and postgraduate studies. The course assumes no prior experience in electronics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103045,'PHY4001','固体物理','Solid-State Physics','PHY - Physics','4001','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2018-19 Term 1
