(103047,'PHY4003','光子晶体简介','Introduction to Photonic Crystals','PHY - Physics','4003','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2','Calculus, Linear algebra, Electromagnetism, Ordinary differential equation.','','這是一門主要介紹光子晶體為主的物理專業入門科目，內容包括：電磁學、量子力學和固體物理預備知識回顧，混合介質中的電磁學，對稱性和固體電磁理論，壹維光子晶體，二維和三維光子晶體，光子晶體仿真計算，拓撲光子晶體，光子晶體波導陣列，光子晶體平板，光子晶體實驗制備方法，光子晶體應用。','This is an introductory physics major course focusing on photonic crystals. Topics include: preliminary knowledge of electromagnetism, quantum mechanics and solid-state physics, electromagnetic waves in mixed dielectric media, symmetry and solid-state electromagnetism, one-dimensional photonic crystal, two-dimensional and three-dimensional photonic crystal, computational photonic crystals, topological photonic crystals, photonic-crystal slabs, experimental fabrication methods of photonic crystals, applications of photonic crystals','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103048,'PHY4004','自旋电子学简介','Introduction to Spintronics','PHY - Physics','4004','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2','PHY3410 Quantum Mechanics and its Applications I,
PHY3420 Quantum Mechanics and its Applications II,
PHY4001 Solid-State Physics','','在传统的微电子学中，一般是利用电子的荷电性由电场来控制电子的输运过程的。在后摩尔时代，利用电子的自旋作为信息载体可以进一步提高信息处理速度和存储密度，由此发展出一门新的学科—— 自旋电子学。自旋电子学(Spintronics or spin electronics)，是一门结合磁学与微电子学的交叉学科。巨磁电阻的发现是自旋电子学发展的里程碑。自从1997年至今大约有280亿个巨磁电阻和隧穿磁电阻读出头投放市场，产生了巨大的科技与社会济效益，基于电子自旋属性的巨磁电阻效应也因此于2007年获得了诺贝尔奖，标志着以自旋为核心的电子信息技术新时代的到来。诺贝尔奖委员会将其评价为开启了通向技术新世界的大门。本门课程主要是给研究生及部分感兴趣的高年级本科生介绍自旋电子学的一些基本物理机制以及利用电子自旋的产品，如电脑硬盘、磁存储器、磁存储芯片、磁感应器及自旋微波振荡器等。','In ubiquitous electronic devices such as PC/notebook computer/smart phone etc, electronic charges (typically electrons) are utilized as information carrier to process information. As we are entering the post-Moore’s era, spin electronics (or spintronics) provides alternative path to process and store information and data in addition to conventional semiconductor electronics. The Nobel prize in 2007 was awarded to the discovery of spintronics, which immediately opened the door to a wealth of new scientific and technological possibilities, including a tremendous influence on the technique of data storage and magnetic
sensors. The aim of this course is to provide the students basic knowledge of both the fundamental mechanism and device applications of spintronics. Typical commercial spintronic devices including hard disk read head, magnetic recording, magnetic sensor, Magnetic Random Access Memory (MRAM) and spintronic microwave oscillators etc. will also be introduced and investigated.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103049,'PHY4210','实验物理课题（三）','Experimental Physics Project Experience III','PHY - Physics','4210','P',1.00,4000,'Major','已评分','研究','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','Physics Laboratory I','Physics Laboratory II is suggested but not compulsory.','本课程旨在为学生提供实验物理学的高级课题学习经验。学生需要在教师的指导下完成一个短期的实验物理课题，并在课程结束时提交一份课题报告。','This course aims at providing students with advanced project learning experience in experimental physics. Students are required to finish a short experimental physics project under the guidance of an instructor, and submit a project report upon completion of the course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103050,'PHY4221','量子力学','Quantum Mechanics','PHY - Physics','4221','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2018-19 Term 2
