2024-25 Term 2','MAT-1001: Calculus I
MAT-1002: Calculus II
MAT-2040: Linear Algebra
General Physics','','量子力学主要总结了微观粒子的运行规律，是绝大多数物理学和整个化学和材料科学的基础。本课程以微积分和线性代数为数学工具，着力于构建量子力学的基本知识框架。课程将从量子力学的概率假设和薛定谔方程出发，探讨自由粒子、箱中粒子、谐振子、2维和3维转动等简单物理模型的表示和求解方法，过渡到量子力学的形式理论，然后对氢原子、氦原子等实际体系进行计算，最后介绍微扰论和变分法。此外，本课程还将对量子物理发展前沿作简单介绍。','Quantum mechanics, emerging from the description of nature in atomic and subatomic scale, is now the foundation of most parts of physics and entire part of chemistry and materials science. This course aims to construct a concise understanding of how quantum mechanic works and applies to microscopic systems using elementary math tools like calculus and linear algebra. It starts from the statistcal interpretation of wavefunction and Schrödinger equation to discuss the simple physical models such as free-particle, paricle-in-a-box, vibrational motion through harmonic oscillators, two-dimensional and three-dimenional rotational motions, proceeds to formal theory of quantum mechanics, before solving realistic system of hydrogen and helium atoms, and ends up in approximative methods such as perturbation theory and variational principles. In addition, most recent advances in quantum science and technology will be introduced as a complement.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103051,'PHY4230','理论物理课题（二）','Theoretical Physics Project Experience II','PHY - Physics','4230','P',1.00,4000,'Major','已评分','研究','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
