(103060,'PHY4960','材料表征方法','Methods of Materials Characterization','PHY - Physics','4960','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Summer','','','本课程介绍各种技术，如扫描电子显微镜 (SEM)、透射电子显微镜 (TEM)、原子力显微镜 (AFM)、X射线光电子能谱/紫外光电子能谱 (XPS/UPS)、X射线衍射 (XRD)、光致发光、拉曼光谱和光学光谱，用于表征薄膜, 块体和纳米材料的结构,物理、光学和电子特性。','This course introduces various techniques such as SEM, TEM AFM, XPS/UPS, XRD, GIWAXS, photoluminescence, Raman and optical spectroscopy to characterize the physical, optical and electronic properties of bulk materials, films and nanomaterials.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103061,'PHY5110','經典力學和狹義相對論','','PHY - Physics','5110','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','None','PHY3110/MSE6302 Classical Mechanics-I or equivalent courses.','本课程面向研究生层次，系统学习基于拉格朗日与哈密顿框架下的高等经典力学及狭义相对论。主要内容包括：最小作用量原理、正则变换、泊松括号、哈密顿-雅可比理论、连续系统表述，以及狭义相对论理论及其与经典动力学联系的深入探讨。','This course is designed for postgraduate students to study advanced classical mechanics and special relativity through the Lagrangian and Hamiltonian formalisms. Topics include the principle of least action, canonical transformations, Poisson brackets, Hamilton–Jacobi theory, and the formulation of continuous systems. The course also covers the special theory of relativity, emphasizing its conceptual and mathematical connection to classical dynamics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103062,'PHY5130','統計力學','','PHY - Physics','5130','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Classical Mechanics, Elementary Quantum Mechanics, College Thermodynamics and Statistics','Calculus, Linear Algebra and Differential Equations.','统计力学是包含许多平衡粒子（超过数百个）的系统的物理学。我将主要介绍传统材料，例如热力学的简要回顾（关于热现象的物候学学科，特别是在热平衡附近），统计力学希望对此提供微观解释。这一领域存在着许多多样化的主题和现象。不可能在一个学期内涵盖所有科目，甚至一些主要科目，这个领域有很多涵盖各个科目的书籍。我将使用的材料来自下面列出的各种书籍。假设您具备基本的经典力学和量子力学、电动力学和热力学知识。','Statistical mechanics is the physics of systems containing many particles (more than several hundreds) at equilibrium. I will mostly cover the traditional materials such as a brief review of thermodynamics (a phenological subjects on  heat phenomena, especially near the thermal equilibrium) on which the statistical mechanics want to provide a microscopic explanation. There are many diversified subjects and phenomena in this field. It is impossible to cover all of them, or even some main subjects, in one semester, there are many books in this field covering various subjects. The materials that I will use come from various books listed below. A knowledge of elementary classical and quantum mechanics, electrodynamics, and thermodynamics will be assumed.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103063,'PHY5410','高等量子力学','','PHY - Physics','5410','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
