(103068,'PHY5530','量子场论 I','','PHY - Physics','5530','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Quantum Mechanics (senior/postgraduate level), Classical Electrodynamics','None.','这是量子场论的入门课程。量子场论是描述粒子之间相互作用的一般理论框架。作为对量子力学的进一步发展，量子场论允许粒子的生成与毁灭，符合我们所观察到的粒子物理实验现象。

在本课程中，我们将研究标量、旋量和规范场的性质，它们之间如何通过基本相互作用相互转换，以及如何通过对称性分析来构建这些相互作用。我们将学习如何使用费曼图计算可观测量，例如散射截面和粒子衰变。我们将讨论重正化的必要性和基本应用方法。最后，我们将非阿贝尔规范理论和自发对称性破坏的基础知识，它们是粒子物理学标准模型的重要组成部分。','This is an introductory course to quantum field theory, the general theoretical framework describing the interactions between subatomic particles at the most fundamental level. As a generalization of quantum mechanics, quantum field theory allows the creation and destruction of particles reflecting experimental observations.

In this course, we will study the properties of scalar, spinor, and gauge fields and how they can be converted to one another through particle interactions, which can be constructed through symmetry considerations. We will learn how to compute observables such as cross sections and decay rates using the formalism of Feynman diagrams. We will discuss the necessity and the basic implementation of renormalization. Finally, we will learn the basics of non-Abelian gauge theories and spontaneous symmetry breaking, which are important ingredients of the Standard Model of particle physics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
