(103071,'PHY6100','半導體物理學','','PHY - Physics','6100','P',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','理工学院','理工学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Calculus, Ordinary differential equation','None.','本课程旨在介绍半导体基础知识和半导体器件的物理原理，包括MOSFET和结型场效应晶体管等。此外，还将涵盖半导体器件制造和功率半导体器件在电动汽车及可再生能源等领域的主要应用。本课程面向材料与科学工程、物理学、电子与计算机工程、新能源科学与工程、数据科学等多个学科的学生。学生将掌握必备知识，为学术生涯或半导体相关行业的要求做好准备。','This course is to introduce the fundamentals of semiconductors and the physics of semiconductor devices, including MOSFET and Junction Field-Effect Transistors. Moreover, device fabrications and major applications of power semiconductor devices such as electric vehicles (EV) and new energy field will be covered. The course is catering for students in a broad discipline such as Materials and Science Engineering, Physics, Electrical and Computer Engineering, New Energy Science and Engineering, and Data Science. Students will master essential knowledge and prepare themselves in either advancing their academic career or meeting the requirements of semiconductor-related industries.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
