2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','认知心理学是一门研究大脑如何处理信息的学科。用更日常的术语来说，它是关于获取和利用从我们的感官中获得的知识和经验所涉及的心理过程。本课程介绍认知心理学领域的理论和研究。它涵盖了有关心理如何运作的传统认知心理学知识。主题包括注意力和感知、意识、信息处理、学习和记忆、问题解决、推理和决策以及语言（即语言感知、语言理解和语言生成）。在此过程中，我们将考虑从神经系统疾病/综合症患者（如阿尔兹海默症、颞叶癫痫、健忘症、局灶性病变患者）身上获得的心理学证据，这些证据让我们更好地理解人类行为的认知过程。此外，我们还将讨论认知心理学领域常用的认知评估工具和方法（即用于学术研究/临床评估病人）。','Cognitive psychology is the study of how the brain processes information. In more everyday terms, it is about the mental processes involved in acquiring and making use of knowledge and experience gained from our senses. This course introduces the theories and research in the field of cognitive psychology. It covers the conventional cognitive psychology knowledge pertaining to how the mind works. Topics include attention and perception, consciousness, information processing, learning and memory, forgetting, problem solving, reasoning and decision making, and language (i.e., speech perception, language comprehension, language production). Doing so, we will consider psychological evidence acquired from patients with neurological diseases/syndromes (e.g., Alzheimer''s disease, Temporal lobe epilepsy, amnesia, patients with focal lesions) that let us better understand the cognitive processes that underly human behaviour. In addition, we will discuss popular cognitive assessment tools and method used in the field of cognitive psychology (i.e., in academic research / for clinical assessment of patients).','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
