2026-27 Term 1','NA','NA','本课程介绍了变态心理学的定义及研究，以及从当前和历史角度对各种心理健康问题的概述。本课程亦还涵盖了心理问题的评估、分类、诊断和治疗。学生将学会从心理学、生物学、社会文化和跨文化的角度研究各种具有代表性的心理和精神疾病，同时学生也将学习基于证据的心理治疗技术。本课程也会简要涉及《精神疾病诊断与统计手册》（DSM-5-TR）的相关知识，鼓励学生了解临床心理学中诊断方法的基本原理。','This course introduces the study of abnormal psychology, as well as an overview of diverse mental health issues from both a current and historical perspective. It also covers the evaluation, categorization, diagnosis, and treatment of psychological problems, with an emphasis on mental wellness and resiliency. Students investigate a wide range of psychological problems from psychological, biological, sociocultural, and intercultural perspectives, as well as evidence-based therapeutic treatment techniques. This course will briefly introduce the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5-TR) and encourages students to understand the basic principle of diagnostic methods in clinical psychology.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103112,'PSY4020','研究方法与构写研究报告 (I)','Research Method and Writing I','PSY - Psychology','4020','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','PSY1020 Quantitative Methods (I) and Experimental Design
PSY2010 Quantitative Methods (II)','None','此為最後一年的必修課，學生須連續兩個學期選擇並完成這兩門課程。每学期的课程均有两个班：一个班偏重教育和发展方向的研究，一个偏重社会与组织方向的研究。學生需要提交一份完整的研究方案，須在結束部分提及對結果的預期；而研究方案的撰寫須始於課程開始之初 。研究方法與構寫研究報告 (I) 是一門正規的研究方法課程，在第一學期每週上一次課，教師將講授和教導研究方法論。研究方案的撰寫將從課程一開始就分配給學生，並與方法學的學習保持相同的進度，以便學生可以立即將方法知識應用於其研究方案的撰寫。第二學期的研究方法與構寫研究報告 (II) 課程，將每週提供時間對學生進行個別指導，學生須在本學期完成研究方案的撰寫。教師主要對研究方案的撰寫提供個人指導和監督完成。

榮譽論文（選修項）：選修的學生可以在任课教师或一位志願導師的指導下寫一篇完整的論文。這些榮譽學生必須跟所有其他學生一樣，完成研究方法與構寫研究報告 I和II 兩門課，同時將獲得寫作榮譽論文的榮譽證書。','Students are required to take these two courses in two consecutive semesters of the last year. In each semester, the course has two sessions: one with a focus on the education and development research and one with a focus on the society and organization research. Students will need to write a full-blown research proposal, which includes a section of expected findings, in the end, whereas the writing of the proposal will start from the beginning of the course offering. Research Method and Writing I, which is a standard research method course, will meet weekly during the first semester and the instructor will lecture and coach students about research methodology. The proposal writing will be assigned to the students from the beginning and progresses at the same pace as the methodology instruction so that students can immediately apply the methodological knowledge to their proposal writing. Students complete the research proposal in the second semester in Research Method and Writing II which offers individual consultation sessions weekly. The instructor mainly provides individual coaching and supervision of the proposal writing in this second writing course.

Honors Thesis (Optional): Selected students can write a full-blown thesis under the supervision of the instructor or a willing supervisor. These honors students will need to complete Research Method and Writing I and II like every other student but will also receive recognition for writing an honors thesis.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
