2025-26 Term 2','Social Psychology PSY3010 OR Leadership PSY3130','','本课程为学生提供关于组织战略、组织变革以及团队管理方面的系统概念与理论。主题包括战略分析、组织设计、变革管理、团队设计、群体决策、冲突解决以及团队绩效等等。本课程不仅将会向学生介绍如何设计组织/团队以取得最佳成效，也会聚焦于学生在组织能力和团队技能方面的提升。理解这些重要的理论将会帮助学生在一个日益多样化的商业环境中做出卓有成效的工作。','This course provides students with the concepts and theories of organizational strategy, organizational change, and team management. Topics include strategic analysis, organization design, change management, team design, group decision-making, conflict resolution, team performance, and so on. The course not only provides directions about how organizations/teams can be designed to function optimally but also focuses on the skills necessary to be productive in the organization and team settings. Understanding the fundamental principles of organization and team processes is critical for students to work effectively in an increasingly diverse business environment.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103115,'PSY4130','决策过程','Decision Making Processes','PSY - Psychology','4130','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','PSY1010: Introduction to Psychology, or PSY 1005 General Psychology, or special permission of the instructor.','None','本课程将向高年级本科生介绍决策心理学的研究，包括理论基础(如预期效用理论、启发式与偏差、有限和生态理性、信号检测论、博弈论)与实证研究(来自认知心理学、社会心理学、进化心理学、管理科学、行为经济学及其他相关学科)。课程不仅涵盖决策的普遍原则，而且会讲解具体类别的决策，如配偶选择，消费选择，风险选择，亲社会决策，人事决策和群体决策。本课程将从三个角度教授决策心理学：“规范性”（人们在没有约束的情况下应该怎样决策），“诊断性”（ 人们在有约束的情况下应该如何决策），“描述性”（人们在现实世界中怎样做决策）。在对具体研究的讨论中，本课程还将介绍应用于决策研究中的不同研究方法，例如心理实验，问卷调查，二级数据分析，计算机模拟和机器学习算法。最后，本课程将从决策心理学的角度考虑一些挑战性的全球问题，如公共卫生和对以人工智能为驱动的工具和产品的监管。','This course introduces advanced undergraduate students to the psychology of decision making, including theoretical foundations (such as expected utility theory, heuristics and biases, bounded and ecological rationality, signal detection theory, and game theory), and empirical research (in cognitive psychology, social psychology, evolutionary psychology, management, behavioral economics, and other related fields). It will cover general principles as well as decision processes in specific domains, such as mate choice, consumer choice, risky choice, prosocial decisions, personnel decisions, and group decisions. This course will teach the psychology of decision making from three perspectives: normative (what people ought to do in absent of constraints), prescriptive (what people should do with constraints), and descriptive (what people actually do in reality). In discussions of specific studies, it will also introduce different methodologies applied in decision-making research, such as experiments, surveys, archival data analysis, computer simulations, and machine-learning algorithms. Finally, it will consider some challenging global issues, such as public health and the regulation of tools and products driven by artificial intelligence, from the perspective of the psychology of decision making.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103116,'PSY4140','记忆','Memory','PSY - Psychology','4140','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2021-22 Term 1
2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2
2021-22 Summer','N/A','N/A','本课程概述了人类记忆研究中的经典和当前的问题。 主题包括内隐记忆（例如，启动）和外显记忆系统（例如，情节记忆）。 我们将更深入地研究记忆获取、存储和检索的过程，以及使用神经心理学测试（例如，检索练习——集中与间隔、定向遗忘、识别与回忆测试）研究这些过程的技术。我们将专注于遗忘理论（即痕迹衰减理论、主动和追溯干扰、检索竞争），并讨论与健康衰老和健忘症（例如，由癫痫、痴呆症）相关的记忆力衰竭。我们会讨论睡眠在记忆中的作用、记忆增强技术和重建记忆与目击者证词的错误性相关：错误信息效应和虚构。','This course provides an overview of classic and current issues in the study of human memory. Topics include implicit memory (e.g., priming) and explicit memory systems (e.g., episodic memory). We will dive deeper into the processes of memory acquisition, storage and retrieval and the techniques to research these processes using neuropsychological tests (e.g., retrieval practice – massed vs spaced, directed forgetting, recognition versus recall tests). We will focus on theories of forgetting (i.e., the trace decay theory, proactive and retroactive interference, retrieval competition) and discuss memory failure in regard to healthy aging and amnesia (e.g., induced by epilepsy, dementia). We will talk about the role of sleep in memory, memory enhancement techniques, and reconstructive memory in relation to the fallibility of eyewitness testimonies: the misinformation effect and confabulation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
