2026-27 Term 1','PSY2020 Cognitive Psychology','N/A','本课程探讨支持注意力、视觉、运动控制、记忆、执行功能、社会行为和情感的认知和神经过程。课程将介绍基本神经解剖学、大脑功能成像技术（如 fMRI、ERP）和认知行为测量方法。还将介绍推断认知神经元基础的方法。我们会考虑来自神经系统疾病（阿尔茨海默病、帕金森病、亨廷顿病、健忘症）患者、脑部病灶（如中风）患者和健康人的证据，这些证据有助于我们更好地理解人类行为的认知和神经过程。','This course explores the cognitive and neural processes that support attention, vision, language, motor control, navigation, and memory. It introduces basic neuroanatomy, functional brain imaging techniques (e.g. fMRI, ERP), and behavioral measures of cognition. Methods by which interferences about the brain bases of cognition are made will be covered. We consider evidence from patients with neurological diseases (e.g. Alzheimer''s disease, Parkingson''s disease, amnesia, focal lesions from stroke) and from normal human participants that helped us better understand the cognitive and neural processes of human behavior.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103121,'PSY4190','认知心理学（二）','Cognitive Psychology II','PSY - Psychology','4190','P',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','PSY2020 Cognitive Psychology I','','认知心理学II旨在探究大脑的信息处理机制。该课关注个体通过感知获取知识经验并加以运用的心理过程。本课程系统阐释认知心理学领域的理论与研究成果，着重探讨认知心理学I课程中尚未深入讨论的主题，包括：运动知觉与行为、语言机制、思维过程与问题解决、决策形成、认知与情绪的交互作用，以及意识研究。通过认知心理学（Ⅰ）与（Ⅱ）的课程衔接，学生将形成对构成人类行为基础之认知过程的全面系统认识。gf','Cognitive psychology is the study of how the brain processes information. In more everyday terms, it is about the mental processes involved in acquiring and making use of knowledge and experience gained from our senses. This course introduces theories and research in the field of cognitive psychology whereby the focus is on topics that have not yet been discussed in PSY2020 Cognitive Psychology. Topics include motion perception and action; language; thinking, problem solving and decision making; cognition and emotion; and consciousness. The topics covered by both cognitive psychology I and II will provide students with a comprehensive overview of the cognitive processes that underly human behaviour.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
