2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','NA','NA','本课程介绍在积极心理学这一领域的理论与研究成果¬，即人一生中，从出生到去世，美好的东西。讨论的题目包括积极的体验如快乐、专注；积极的特征如人格力量、价值、才能；以及促进这些美好东西的社会因素。我们将特别关注在为儿童、青少年、成人和老年人设计干预时所涉及的跨文化议题以及不同年龄阶段的特殊需要。课程中我们也会涉及体验和实践性的学习，以促进我们的安康、提高我们对积极心理学中重要的理论和实证问题的理解。','This course examines the theories and research that contribute to the emerging field of positive psychology—the scientific study of what goes right in life, from childhood to older adulthood and across different cultural contexts. Major topics include positive experiences (e.g., pleasure, meaning, and flow), positive traits (e.g., character strengths, values, hope, and resilience), and the social environments and institutions that support well-being, such as schools, families, workplaces, and communities. We will pay particular attention to cross-cultural issues and to age-specific needs when designing interventions for children, adolescents, adults, and older adults. Throughout the course, students will engage in experiential self-care activities, review intervention studies, and design their own positive psychology interventions. These practical components are intended to deepen both theoretical understanding and empirical thinking about how to promote well-being in real-world contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
