2026-27 Term 1','Prior knowledge of the basic psychological concepts and principles of Educational Psychology is required.','','本高级研讨课程旨在探讨教育心理学研究与实践的前沿问题。本课程包含四大模块：教育心理学导论、教育中的个体/文化差异、教育内容领域以及未来教育发展方向。课程将系统涵盖教育心理学核心议题，例如：一般智力与资优教育、人格特质与学习动机、认知与学业发展、人工智能在教育心理学中的应用、以及个性化学习等主题。','This is an advanced seminar to discuss and examine current issues in the research and practice of educational psychology. This course includes four modules: introduction to educational psychology, individual/cultural differences in education, content domains in education, and the future of education.   The major issues in Educational Psychology will be covered, e.g., general intelligence & gifted education, personality traits and motivation in education, cognitive and academic development, AI in Educational Psychology, and personalized learning.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103146,'PSY6140','认知神经科学专题','','PSY - Psychology','6140','P',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','No formal prerequisite in cognitive neuroscience is required. Prior coursework in psychology, cognitive science, education, neuroscience, behavioral science, or research methods is helpful but not mandatory. Students from other backgrounds are welcome, provided they are willing to engage with interdisciplinary readings and participate in research-oriented discussions.','','本研讨课主要探讨认知神经科学如何帮助我们理解和研究应用心理学问题，同时也强调要谨慎解读与大脑有关的研究证据。本课程不会系统教授复杂的神经科学技术，而是围绕一些重要主题，介绍相关的理论、研究方法、代表性研究发现和争议问题。课程内容包括注意、学习、记忆、具身认知、元认知、个体差异，以及如何合理、负责任地应用神经科学研究成果。课程将结合教师讲授、学生主导的论文讨论和研究活动，帮助学生理解认知神经科学研究，并思考如何将这些知识应用到心理学研究中。','This seminar explores how cognitive neuroscience can help us understand and study questions in applied psychology. It also emphasizes the importance of interpreting brain-based evidence carefully. The course does not aim to provide comprehensive technical training in neuroscience. Instead, it introduces selected theories, research methods, key findings, and debates related to attention, learning, memory, embodied cognition, metacognition, individual differences, and the responsible use of neuroscience findings. Students will learn through instructor-led lectures, student-led seminars, and research activities. The course aims to help students understand cognitive neuroscience research and think about how it can be meaningfully applied to psychological research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
