(103161,'PUB5130','国际政治经济发展','','PUB - Public Policy','5130','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Not applicable','Not applicable','本课程旨在向学生介绍全球政治经济和国际发展。课程将审视政治和经济在国际层面的互动以及这些互动如何影响发展，尤其着眼于西方以外的欠发达地区。课程覆盖的议题包括国家和市场间的关系、国际安全与发展、全球化、国际经济组织、对外援助和可持续发展等。','This course will introduce students the research frontiers in the study of global political economy and contemporary issues that defines the future trends of global political economy in 21st century. It covers relevant and important topics not covered by other courses, such as the interaction among the economics, politics and international relations. In addition, this course encourages the teachers to reflect their own research interests and expertise in teaching, with a purpose of broadening students’ academic and intellectual horizon. Students are expected to carry out intensive pre-readings, presentations, in-class debate and discussions, and ultimately conduct their own research on specific topics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103162,'PUB5210','公共选择：理性与决策','','PUB - Public Policy','5210','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','N/A','N/A','公共选择是经济学和政治学的一个分支学科，这个学科试图通过经济学模型来解释公共政策过程。本课程将分析集体偏好是如何聚集以及如何影响非经济决策的。课程将回顾公共选择理论的经典作品，包括亚当·斯密和孔多塞的作品，以及一些二十世纪的学者，如：哈耶克、詹姆斯·布坎南、戈登·图洛克和其他理论家的作品。重要的主题包括市场和政府的失灵、集体行动、不同投票规则的性质、宪法的设计，以及候选人、当选官员、官僚和选民的行为。','Public choice is a sub-discipline of economics and political science that attempts to explain the public policy process via economic models. This course analyzes how the collective preferences are aggregated and shape the non-economic decision-making. It examines the classic works of public choice theory, dipping back into the works of Adam Smith and Marquis de Condorcet, and a number of 20th century scholars such as F.A. Hayek, James Buchanan, Gordon Tullock, and other theorists. Important topics include market and government failure, collective action, properties of different voting rules, design of constitutions, and the behavior of candidates, elected officials, bureaucrats, and voters.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103163,'PUB5220','财政治理与预算','','PUB - Public Policy','5220','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','','','这门课程使用微观经济学的工具来研究政府干预的基本原理、干预领域和公共融资的来源。 我们将介绍经济学中用于评估公共政策效果的经验方法，并讨论政府支出计划和税收制度对公民福利和行为的影响。 内容包括外部性、公共产品、社会保障、失业保险、健康保险、税收原则、税收对社会不平等的影响等。','This course examines contemporary issues in fiscal governance and public budgeting in developing countries, especially in Mainland China. The focus is on the institutional structures within which the budgetary choices are made. Following an introduction to theoretical approaches to the study of budgeting, topics will include medium-term frameworks, top-down budgeting, fiscal rules, performance budgeting, fiscal decentralization, and budget transparency.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103164,'PUB5230','公共行政、技术与创新','','PUB - Public Policy','5230','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','None','','本课程面向公共政策专业的学术型硕士（MPhil）与博士（PhD）研究生，强调理论学习与研究训练，系统讲授技术与创新研究。课程从创新研究的源头——熊彼特的创新与“创造性破坏”理论——出发，依次梳理创新研究的演化经济学传统、科学技术与社会（STS）研究，以及创新系统理论（国家、区域、部门与技术创新系统）。在此基础上，课程转向创新研究的当代前沿——可持续性转型研究，讲授其核心分析框架——多层次视角（MLP）、技术创新系统（TIS）与战略利基管理（SNM）——并讨论转型研究的地理、治理与企业维度。课程注重理论联系实际，重点关注中国的能源、环境与城市转型案例。教学以研讨和研究训练为主：学生以小组形式完成两次文献综述报告并研讨核心学术文献，并在两次写作课的指导下完成一篇个人研究论文。','This course is designed for MPhil and PhD students in public policy, with a strong emphasis on theory and research. It begins with the intellectual origins of innovation studies — Schumpeter''s theory of innovation and creative destruction — and traces the field''s development through the evolutionary economics of innovation, Science, Technology and Society (STS), and innovation systems (national, regional, sectoral, and technological innovation systems). Building on these foundations, the course then turns to sustainability transitions studies, a leading contemporary branch of innovation research, and examines its core frameworks — the Multi-Level Perspective (MLP), Technological Innovation Systems (TIS), and Strategic Niche Management (SNM) — together with the geographical, governance, and corporate dimensions of transitions. Throughout the course, theories are applied to empirical cases, with particular attention to China''s energy, environmental, and urban transitions. The course is seminar-based and research-oriented: students review and critically discuss the core academic literature through two group literature-review presentations, and each student develops an individual research essay under the guidance of two dedicated writing workshops.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103165,'PUB5240','领导力与决策力','','PUB - Public Policy','5240','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程旨在介绍与公共政策制定和实施相关的领导和决策技能，是一门跨学科的专题课。课程讨论领导力在公共政策制定过程中的范围、性质和作用，以及在制定政策实施步骤和战略目标时有用的决策工具。课程还将介绍公共决策者应考虑的重要政治、经济和社会因素。','This course is designed to introduce the leadership and decision-making skills relevant to public policy formulation and implementation. This course is interdisciplinary and thematic. It discusses the scope, nature and the role of leadership to public policy making process, as well as the useful decision-making tools in setting policy implement steps and strategic objectives. The course will also introduce important political, economic and social insights that public decision makers should consider.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103166,'PUB5310','外交政策分析','','PUB - Public Policy','5310','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','Not applicable','Not applicable','本课程带领学生了解国家尤其是大国制定和实施外交政策的过程。课程将介绍并强调外交政策决策中的各种理论及其在广泛问题领域中的适用性。课程将为学生提供一系列关于世界政治主要参与者的比较案例研究。这门课将讨论政治行动者所面临的制约因素，阐述它们之间如何互动，并阐明政治行动者如何解决分歧和制定政策的过程和机制。它特别关注可能影响政策执行过程和政策结果的因素或条件。','This course will prepare students to understand the process by which the state formulates and implements foreign policies, especially those greater nations. It will introduce and highlight a variety of theories in foreign policy decision-making and their applicability in a wide range of issue areas. The course will offer students a series of comparative cases studies in regard to major players in world politics. This course will discuss constraints that political actors face, elaborate on how they interact with each other, and make clear of the process and mechanism on how political actors resolve their differences and formulate policies. It pays special attention to factors or conditions that may influence the policy implementation process and policy outcomes.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103167,'PUB5320','当代中国公共治理与政策制定','','PUB - Public Policy','5320','P',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','本课程旨在向学生介绍改革开放以来中国国家治理模式的基本结构特征及其政策制定过程，并将这些具有代表性的公共政策议题置于中国政治、政府和公共管理的语境中加以探讨。这门课将帮助学生探索和理解中国深层次的治理问题及其政策制定逻辑。课程内容涵盖治理与行政改革、中央与地方政府间的动态变化，以及具有代表性的公共政策的主要争论。','This course is designed to introduce students to the characteristics of the basic structure of China’s state governance model and the policy-making process since the reform and opening up. It will discuss the represented public policy issues within the context of the politics, government, and public administration in China. The course helps students to explore and understand deep-rooted governance issues and policy-making logics of China. Topics will cover the governance and administrative reform, the dynamic changes between central and local governments, and main debates of represented public policies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
