2025-26 Term 2','No.','No.','本课程探讨人工智能与政府数据系统如何塑造当代公共政策与行政管理。学生将学习政府如何收集、管理及运用数据，并了解人工智能工具如何影响决策制定、公共服务供给、公平性及问责机制。课程涵盖数据质量、算法偏见、透明度、隐私保护、监管框架及实施挑战等议题，旨在培养学生评估公共部门人工智能系统的能力，并基于制度规范、伦理准则和法律原则设计负责任的治理策略。本课程采用国际比较的视角，以理解公共部门人工智能与数据治理领域的发展现状。','This course examines how artificial intelligence and government data systems shape contemporary public policy and administration. Students learn how governments collect, govern, and use data, and how AI tools influence decision‑making, service delivery, equity, and accountability. Covering data quality, bias, transparency, privacy, regulation, and implementation challenges, the course equips students to assess public‑sector AI systems and design responsible governance strategies grounded in institutional, ethical, and legal principles. This course adopts a comparative and international approach to understanding the state of the art in AI and data governance in public sectors.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
