ausal inference has emerged as an indispensable tool in many disciplines, including machine learning, economy, statistics, and etc. Moreover, its practical
applications have demonstrated its efficacy beyond academic interests. This
course aims to provide an introduction to the fundamental concepts, methods, and theoretical results related to causal inference. The course content covers the
following aspects: The potential outcome framework, The randomization
experiments, The observational study and propensity score, Double-robust
estimation and double-machine learning, Estimation of propensity score. After
that, we introduce causal inference from machine learning perspective, including
the following topics: Causal graph and d-separation, do-calculus, structural
causal model, and analysis of a linear structural causal model','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
