(103230,'STA4503','鞅、解耦与自归一化及其应用','','STA - Statistics','4503','S',1.00,4000,'Major','Pass/Fail','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'(STA2001 or ECO2121 or STA2003 or STA2001H) and (STA2002 or STA2004 or STA2002H);
(MAT2040 or MAT2042 or MAT2041 or MAT2041A)','','鞅（Martingale）是刻画一个过程随时间演化的自然数学模型。解耦（Decoupling）与自归一化（Self-normalization）则是为了将鞅方法拓展至高维乃至无穷维空间，以及处理复杂的非线性相依结构而发展起来的重要方向。

其中，解耦技术提供了一种工具，使我们能够像处理独立变量那样分析依赖变量；而自归一化过程的一个典型例子，就是用于依赖数据的 t-统计量。

本课程将介绍：鞅理论广泛应用于股票市场演化建模，而自归一化过程则在机器学习中用于构建最优算法。通过本课程，学生将掌握这些现代概率工具的核心思想及其实际应用场景。','A Martingale is the natural model of the evolution of a process over time. Decoupling and Self-normalization are areas that grew out of the need to extend Martingale methods to high and infinite dimensions as well as to complex nonlinear dependence structures.
Decoupling provides tools for treating dependent variables as if they were independent. A prototypical example of Self-Normalized processes is the t-statistic in dependent variables. As will be described in the course, Martingales are commonly used in the study of the evolution of the Stock Market and Self- Normalized processes are used in the development of optimal algorithms in Machine Learning.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103231,'STA4504','高级蒙特卡洛方法','','STA - Statistics','4504','S',1.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'Elementary analysis such as integration by parts, Taylor expansions, basic probability and statistics (random variables, expectation, variance, Bayes’ formula).','','本课程将涵盖蒙特卡洛方法及其应用领域中的相关主题。内容包括马尔可夫链蒙特卡洛（MCMC）和序贯蒙特卡洛（SMC）方法、量子蒙特卡洛和扩散蒙特卡洛技术，以及分支和相互作用粒子方法。

授课内容涵盖离散时间和连续时间随机模型，从传统的采样技术（完美模拟、Metropolis-Hastings 算法和 Gibbs-Glauber 模型）开始，逐步深入到更精细的方法，如约束状态空间和黎曼流形上的梯度流扩散，最后介绍近期快速发展的分支和平均场型相互作用粒子系统技术（前向/后向粒子滤波器、集合卡尔曼滤波器、相互作用卡尔曼滤波器、序贯蒙特卡洛、基于谱系树的采样器等）。

本课程将对这些高级随机模型的理论基础进行系统性教学介绍，并结合来自不同应用领域的具体实例进行说明。课程中涉及的应用领域包括：贝叶斯统计学习（隐马尔可夫链、统计机器学习）、风险分析与稀有事件采样（数学金融和工业风险评估）、运筹学（全局优化、组合计数与排序）、高级信号处理（随机非线性滤波与控制、数据关联及多目标跟踪）、计算与统计物理（路径空间上的 Feynman-Kac 公式、分子动力学、薛定谔基态、Boltzmann-Gibbs 分布以及自由能计算）。

课程的前半部分主要关注线性型马尔可夫链蒙特卡洛方法，后半部分则侧重于非线性粒子型方法，包括相互作用扩散过程、相互作用跳跃过程以及基于谱系树的采样器。','This course will cover topics in the general area of Monte Carlo methods and their application domains. The topics include Markov chain Monte Carlo and Sequential Monte Carlo methods, Quantum and Diffusion Monte Carlo techniques, as well as branching and interacting particle methodologies. The lectures cover discrete and continuous time stochastic models, starting from traditional sampling techniques (perfect simulation, Metropolis-Hasting, and Gibbs-Glauber models) to more refined methodologies such as gradient flows diffusions on constraint state space and Riemannian manifolds, ending with the more recent and rapidly developing Branching and mean field type Interacting Particle Systems techniques (forward/backward particle filters, Ensemble Kalman filers, interacting Kalman filters, Sequential Monte Carlo, genealogical tree based samplers, and many others).

The course offers a pedagogical introduction to the theoretical foundations of these advanced stochastic models, combined with a series of concrete illustrations taken from different application domains. The applications considered in these lectures will range from Bayesian statistical learning (hidden Markov chain, statistical machine learning), risk analysis and rare event sampling (mathematical finance, and industrial risk assessment), operation research (global optimization, combinatorial counting and ranking), advanced signal processing (stochastic nonlinear
filtering and control, and data association and multiple objects tracking), computational and statistical physics (Feynman-Kac formulae on path spaces, molecular dynamics, Schrödinger’s ground states, Boltzmann-Gibbs distributions, and free energy computation). Approximately the first half of the course will be concerned with linear type Markov chain Monte Carlo methods, and the second part to nonlinear particle type methodologies, including interacting diffusions, interacting jump processes and genealogical tree based samplers.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103232,'STA4606','生物医学研究中的机器学习','Machine Learning for Biomedical Research','STA - Statistics','4606','S',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','Undergraduate level probability and statistics.','','本课程涵盖基本的机器学习理论和技术。主题包括基本理论、分类方法、模型泛化、聚类和降维。材料将通过一系列讲座和项目来传达。课程中例子和项目是专门为生物医学研究专业的学生量身定制的。','This course covers fundamental machine learning theory and techniques. The topics include basic theory, classification methods, model generalization, clustering, and dimension reduction. The material will be conveyed by a series of lectures and projects. The examples and projects are specifically tailored to students in biomedical research.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103233,'STA5001','贝叶斯和计算统计','','STA - Statistics','5001','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程介绍贝叶斯统计的基本方法。课程首先讲解常用的分布及其对应的共轭先验分布。对于复杂的模型和先验分布，学生将学习如何在R语言中应用马尔可夫链蒙特卡洛（MCMC）算法进行后验推断。课程还将涉及贝叶斯方法的一些实际应用，包括贝叶斯回归、分层模型和潜在变量模型，以解决现实世界中的问题。','This course introduces fundamental Bayesian methodology. It first presents commonly used distributions and their corresponding conjugate priors. For sophisticated models and priors, students will learn to apply Markov Chain Monte Carlo algorithms in R for posterior inference. Some applications of Bayesian methods will be involved to solve real-world problems, including Bayesian regression, hierarchical models and latent variable models.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103234,'STA5002','高等回归方法','','STA - Statistics','5002','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程介绍线性和非线性回归技术，包括线性模型和广义线性模型（如逻辑回归和泊松回归）、样条和局部多项式回归、核方法与筛方法。此外，课程还介绍现代线性回归技术，如稳健回归和分位数回归。本课程是一门高级回归方法的入门课程。虽然课程中会涵盖一些基本理论和简单编程，但不会深入讨论复杂的理论结果和高级编程内容。','This course introduces linear and nonlinear regression techniques, including linear and generalized linear model, such as logistic regression and Poisson regression, spline and local polynomial regression, kernel and sieve methods. Besides, it introduces modern linear regression techniques such as robust regression and quantile regression. This is an introductory course on advanced regression methods. While there will be some basic theories and simple programming, deeper theoretical results and complex programming will not be discussed.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103235,'STA5011','多元统计分析','','STA - Statistics','5011','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','NA','NA','本课程讲授多元统计分析方法及其在现实世界中的应用。学生将学习多种多元数据分析的统计方法，包括多元分布与推断、方差分析、多元回归、降维技术（如主成分分析）、因子分析、典型相关分析、判别与分类方法以及聚类方法。课程将重点强调这些技术在分析实际问题中的综合应用。','This course deals with multivariate statistical analysis and their applications in the real world. Students will examine a variety of statistical methods for multivariate data, including multivariate distributions and inferences, analysis of variance, multivariate regression, dimension reduction techniques such as principal component analysis, factor analysis, canonical correlation analysis, discrimination and classification, and clustering methods. The integrated use of these techniques in analyzing real problems will be emphasized throughout the course.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103236,'STA5012','统计学习','','STA - Statistics','5012','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','CSC1001, MAT2040, STA3001','','本课程系统介绍统计学习——统计学与机器学习之间的现代交叉领域。课程内容涵盖判别模型与生成模型，强调对核心概念的理解、方法论的构建以及现代学习技术在实际中的应用。课程将贯穿讲解偏差–方差权衡、模型复杂度控制等基本原理。实践环节将使用 Python 进行数据分析与示例演示，帮助学生将理论概念与现实问题中的具体实现相结合。通过本课程的学习，学生将建立对数据建模与预测相关理论基础和实践工具的扎实理解。','This course provides a comprehensive overview to statistical learning — the modern interface between statistics and machine learning. It covers both discriminative and generative modeling, emphasizing conceptual understanding, methodological development, and practical applications of modern learning techniques. Core principles such as the bias–variance tradeoff and model complexity control are highlighted throughout. Practical data analysis and demonstrations will be conducted using Python, enabling students to connect theoretical concepts with real-world implementation. By the end of the course, students will develop a solid understanding of the theoretical foundations and practical tools for data modeling and prediction.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103237,'STA5013','因果推理','','STA - Statistics','5013','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','STA2002H Honours Probability and Statistics  or   STA2002 Probability and Statistics II or having permission from academic advisor.','','发现事件间的因果关系是现代统计学的一个基础问题。本课程旨在介绍因果推断的基本概念及方法。课程包括：1.随机化试验：潜在结果模型， 完全随机实验与费雪随机化检验，分层。 2. 观察性研究：倾向得分及逆概加权估计，双稳健估计， E-值。 3. 工具变量','Investigating causality between events is an important topic in modern-ear statistics. This class introduces basic concepts, methods, and theoretical results on causal inference. Topics include: 1) Randomization experiment: Potential outcomes, Complete randomization experiment and Fisher Randomization Test, Stratification, Regression Adjustment. 2) Observational study: Selection bias, Propensity score and Inverse propensity score weighting estimator, Doubly Robust estimation, E-Value. 3) Instrumental Variable: Definition, Linear IV model, Fuzzy Regression Discontinuity.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103238,'STA5014','高维统计','','STA - Statistics','5014','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103239,'STA5020','毕业设计（一）','','STA - Statistics','5020','S',3.00,5000,'Major','Pass/Fail','实习','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','',NULL,'Refer to the specific requirements of each project','','本课程为学生提供实践机会，使其能够将数据科学技能应用于现实场景。通过本课程，学生将参与实际项目，运用包括计算机编程与软件工程、机器学习算法、统计模型等在内的多种技术，解决跨领域的复杂问题。课程强调跨学科协作，学生在利用多元视角应对多方面挑战的同时，也能积累团队合作经验。课程结束时，学生将掌握行业标准工具与方法论的实践经验。','This course offers students a hands-on experience to apply their data science skills in real-world scenarios. Through this course, students work on practical projects, utilizing various techniques, including computer programming and software engineering, machine learning algorithms, statistical models, etc. to solve complex problems across various domains. Emphasizing interdisciplinary collaboration, students gain teamwork experience while leveraging diverse perspectives to address multifaceted challenges. By the course’s end, students will gain experience in industry-standard tools and methodologies.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103240,'STA5021','毕业设计（二）','','STA - Statistics','5021','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','实习','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','Refer to the specific requirements of each project','','综合项目旨在为学生提供与他人合作解决实际问题的经验。在综合项目中，学生将在导师的指导下以小组形式开展工作。','The capstone project aims to provide students with experience of working on a real-world problem in cooperation with others. In the capstone project, students will work in small groups under the guidance of their supervisors, typically a faculty member.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103241,'STA5022','校外实习','','STA - Statistics','5022','S',0.00,5000,'Major','Pass/Fail','实习','Main Campus','数据科学学院','数据科学学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103242,'SUD5010','环境与自然资源政策','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5010','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','N.A.','N.A.','本课程探讨当代不同层面的环境与资源政策及管理问题。学生将学习可持续发展原则、政策工具以及在公司、城市、国家和超国家层面有效、公平地解决环境与资源问题的实践经验。主要议题包括渔业资源政策、水资源政策、污染治理、气候变化、企业环境管理等。本课程旨在帮助学生评估、设计和预测应对复杂环境与资源挑战的政策和管理措施中可能遇到的困难。','The transition to low-carbon and resource-efficient economies presents an urgent question to humanity. This course tackles contemporary environmental and resource policies and management issues across scales. Students will examine sustainability principles, policy instruments, and practical experiences relevant for addressing environment and resource issues efficiently and equitably at company, city, national and supranational levels. Major topics include fishery resources, water resources, pollution control, climate change, and corporate environmental management. This course enables students to evaluate, design and foresee difficulties in policy and management responses to complex environmental and resource challenges.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103243,'SUD5020','社会科学研究方法','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5020','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','NA','NA','本课程专为可持续发展领域学生打造，介绍社会科学研究方法在可持续发展议题中的的逻辑与实践步骤，引导学生从研究问题的界定和文献综述出发，逐步学习研究策略、抽样、数据收集、研究伦理、数据分析与研究报告写作。课程比较定量、定性和混合研究方法，强调研究问题、证据与方法之间的一致性。案例将涵盖社会学、教育、公共政策、健康、商业、城市研究及可持续发展等领域。本课程面向先修背景多样的学生，不要求具备高级统计或专业软件技能。','This course is specifically designed for students in the field of sustainable development. It introduces the logic and practical steps of applying social science research methods to sustainable development issues, guiding students from defining research questions and conducting literature reviews to gradually learning research strategies, sampling, data collection, research ethics, data analysis, and research report writing. The course compares quantitative, qualitative, and mixed research methods, emphasizing the consistency between research questions, evidence, and methods. Case studies will cover fields such as sociology, education, public policy, health, business, urban studies, and sustainable development. This course is open to students with diverse prerequisites and does not require advanced statistical or professional software skills.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103244,'SUD5030','可持续研究当代议题','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5030','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程探讨全球可持续发展的基本概念，以及解决可持续发展相关问题的全球和地方治理举措。主要议题包括全球可持续发展理论框架、可持续发展治理和可持续金融。通过考察主要的地方、多边和国际机构，本课程还探讨了影响可持续发展举措发展和成果的关键参与者、政策和因素，例如解决贫困、气候变化、安全和生态问题的举措。本课程旨在让学生对环境、社会和经济之间的动态关系有深入的理论理解和实证研究，并采用一种鼓励学生积极参与协作学习的形式。','Sustainable development is at the center of politics. Understanding global and local governance and overcoming collective action problems at different levels for sustainable development are of utmost importance.  This course explores foundational concepts in global sustainable development, as well as global and local governance initiatives in addressing issues related to sustainability. Major topics addressed include global sustainability theoretical frameworks, sustainability governance, and sustainable finance. By examining key local, multilateral and international institutions, this course also discusses key actors, policies, and factors that shape the development and outcomes of sustainability initiatives, such as ones that address poverty, climate change, security and ecology. It aims to provide students with a theoretically sophisticated and empirically grounded understandings of the dynamic relations between environment, social and economics, and employs a format that engages students in active and collaborative learning.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
