(103252,'SUD5210','可持续发展中的地理信息系统','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5210','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','NA','NA','本硕士课程旨在培养研究生掌握GIS核心理论与QGIS实操技能，赋能可持续发展领域的空间研究与应用。课程核心内容包含四大模块：1）GIS基础理论，涵盖地理空间数据模型、软硬件体系、数据库构建与坐标投影系统；2）基于QGIS平台的空间数据处理、定量分析与地图可视化全流程实操技术；3）服务于多尺度可持续发展、监测社会‑生态动态演变的前沿GIS方法；4）聚焦空间治理、生态保护与可持续规划的可持续发展实战案例。课程结合理论授课、QGIS实操训练与课外文献研读的多元教学模式，帮助学生建立标准化空间分析思维，具备独立开展可持续发展相关研究与解决实际问题的能力。','This postgraduate course aims to equip students with core GIS theories and practical QGIS skills for sustainable development research. It covers four key components: 1) fundamental GIS concepts including geospatial data models, infrastructure, geodatabase construction, and coordinate projection systems; 2) full geospatial workflows of data processing, quantitative analysis, and cartographic visualisation implemented on the open-source QGIS platform; 3) advanced GIS techniques for monitoring socio‑ecological dynamics and supporting multi‑scale sustainability; 4) real-world sustainable development cases focusing on spatial governance, ecological conservation, and sustainability planning. Students will strengthen their competencies through lectures, QGIS hands-on practice, and supplementary readings to build professional spatial analysis and problem-solving capabilities for sustainability applications.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103253,'SUD5220','数据分析：高级定量方法','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5220','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103254,'SUD5230','可持续文化未来','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5230','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程旨在探索文化政策研究的新领域，重点研究艺术和文化如何为更可持续的未来做出贡献。在我们探索当代文化景观的复杂性时，本课程将为学生提供必要的工具和见解，以理解和塑造文化、社会和可持续性之间不断发展的关系。我们的探索围绕三个核心主题展开：（1）文化价值和公众参与；（2）文化工作、劳动和机构；（3）文化数字化和生成式人工智能。“可持续文化未来”旨在激励学生设想和倡导可持续的文化政策，这些政策不仅丰富了我们的社会，而且还促进了艺术的包容性、创造力和韧性。我们将共同探索如何建立一个文化与可持续实践和谐发展的未来，使文化艺术成为促进社会积极发展的重要力量。','The course aims to explore new frontiers in cultural policy studies, focusing on how arts and culture can contribute to a more sustainable future. Through navigating the complexities of the contemporary cultural landscape, it will equip students with the tools and insights necessary to understand and shape the evolving relationship between culture, society, and sustainability. The exploration is structured around three core themes: (1) Cultural value and public engagement; (2) Cultural work, labor and institutions; and (3) Digitalization of culture and generative AI. Ultimately, this course aims to inspire students to envision and advocate for sustainable cultural policies that not only enrich our societies but also promote inclusivity, creativity, and resilience in the arts. Together, students will explore how to build a future where culture thrives in harmony with sustainable practices, ensuring that the arts remain a vital force for positive change in our communities.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
