(103257,'SUD5310','中国经济发展','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5310','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','NA','NA','本课程深入探讨世界最大发展中国家--中国的经济改革与发展。通过对中国经济的批判性分析，学生将探究阻碍中国经济增长的因素，以及自1978年以来经济改革取得成功的原因。本课程还将探讨中国持续经济发展面临的挑战。课程将对中国制度进行深入分析，并运用实证数据进行全面考查。','This course delves into the economic reforms and development in China, the world''s largest developing economy. Through a critical analysis of the Chinese economy, students will examine the factors hindering China''s economic growth and the reasons behind the success of economic reforms since 1978. This course will also explore the challenges faced in China''s ongoing economic development. It combines an in-depth analysis of Chinese institutions with a thorough investigation using empirical data.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103258,'SUD5320','发展与国家','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5320','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','本课程旨在帮助学生熟悉政治经济学研究中相互竞争和互补的方法，以及国家与经济、工业和可持续发展之间的关系。课程旨在帮助学生批判性地评估既往研究成果，并为学生在国际和比较政治经济学领域的独立研究奠定基础.','The course familiarizes students with competing and complementary approaches to the study of political economy and the relationship between the state and economic, industrial and sustainable development. It helps students critically evaluate past research and establishes foundation for independent research in the study of international and comparative political economy with a theoretical focus on late development and an area focus on the global south.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103259,'SUD5330','移民与可持续发展','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5330','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','none','none','移民不仅是推动可持续发展的强劲动力，更是《2030年可持续发展议程》确立的核心跨领域议题。本课程将深入剖析移民现象背后的复杂成因及其深远影响，重点探讨如何利用移民促进包容性增长。学生将系统研究全球及国内的移民趋势与政策框架，理解其在构建社会韧性中的关键作用。课程注重知行合一，引导学生将可持续发展理念与人口流动规律相融合，从而设计出切实可行的综合发展方案，以应对现实世界中的人口流动挑战。','Migration is a powerful driver of sustainable development and is recognized as a cross-cutting priority in the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. This course explores the complex causes and impacts of migration while analyzing strategies for fostering inclusive growth. Students will gain critical insights into global and internal migration trends, policy frameworks, and their roles in building resilient societies. By bridging theory with practice, students will integrate concepts of sustainability and human mobility to design development plans addressing real-world migration challenges.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103260,'SUD5350','可持续城市交通','','SUD - Sustainable Development','5350','S',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','N.A.','N.A.','本课程将深入探讨可持续城市交通系统，考察其在全球城市化和气候变化背景下所产生的社会、经济与环境影响。学生将分析旨在促进韧性低碳社区建设的关键交通政策、项目以及创新工具，并重点关注公平性、可达性和资源效率等可持续发展原则的融合。本课程主要聚焦于城市环境中个人出行、公共交通和多模式交通网络所面临的挑战与机遇，同时涵盖人工智能驱动的规划和数据分析等新兴技术。通过批判性讨论、案例研究和实践练习，学生将全面理解在未来设计和实施高效、包容且环境可持续的城市交通策略所涉及的复杂问题。','This course offers an in-depth exploration of sustainable urban transport systems, examining their social, economic, and environmental implications in the context of global urbanization and climate change. Students will analyze key transport policies, programs, and innovative tools designed to promote resilient, low-carbon communities, with a strong emphasis on integrating sustainability principles such as equity, accessibility, and resource efficiency. The primary focus is on addressing the challenges and opportunities in personal mobility, public transit, and multimodal networks within urban environments, including emerging technologies like AI-driven planning and data analytics. Through critical discussions, case studies, and practical exercises, students will develop a comprehensive understanding of the complexities involved in designing and implementing efficient, inclusive, and environmentally sustainable urban transportation strategies for the future.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103261,'SUD6010','环境经济学与可持续发展','','SUD - Sustainable Development','6010','S',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程将向学生介绍现代环境问题的经济学视角。通过学习经济理论，学生将理解诸多环境问题的成因，并运用政策工具来应对市场失灵。课程主题包括：可再生资源和不可再生资源、环境保护和污染控制经济学、经济活动对环境的影响、气候变化经济学以及可持续发展。','This course introduces students to economic perspectives on modern environmental issues, with special attention on sustainable development. Students will learn economic theory to understand the causes of many environmental problems and the tools of policy analysis to address market failures. Topics include renewable and non-renewable resources, economics of environmental protection and pollution control, environmental impacts of economic activity, economics of climate change and sustainable development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
