2025-26 Term 1','','','本課程為具有理論依據的實踐導向課，目的在於為學生提供高中級 水平的中英文學文本互譯訓練， 所涉及文本類型主要為散文小説， 也可包括詩歌。其設計旨在加强學生對文本細節重要性的意識， 内 容涵蓋詞語選擇、句法經營及文本構成等各個層次， 並與信息結構 及其交際和美學效果相聯繫， 以此加强學生的翻譯能力，以便更爲 準確及貼切地翻譯此類文本。授課重點在於講解與實際翻譯相關的 問題，鼓勵學生在授課老師指導下反思與翻譯文學文本相關的各種 問題，以及所採用的應對策略。根據需要，會運用AI工具來練習翻譯中的人工編輯。','Translation is both an art and the deployment of skills for cross-linguistic communication, most clearly manifested in the translation of creative compositions. This course will expose students to a range of translations of both classic and modern literature such as novels, poetry and drama. The course will sensitize students to the techniques, strategies and, more importantly, the creativity involved in dealing with such genres, and will enhance their ability to understand multi-layered meanings involved in literary texts and the impact of cultural differences.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103318,'TRA5115','数字和人工智能多媒体翻译','','TRA - Translation','5115','T',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','N/A','N/A','本课程致力于探索视听翻译的理论基础与实践技能。课程重点培养学生在现代传媒环境下的专业翻译能力，包括字幕制作、配音翻译、口述影像及多媒体本地化等核心技能。学生将通过使用行业专业软件进行实践，了解视听翻译的技术规范、多维限制和文化适应策略。
课程内容涵盖不同类型视听材料的翻译方法、无障碍传播原则，以及流媒体平台的发展趋势。通过项目式学习，学生将参与视听材料的拍摄、剪辑和制作，将理论知识应用于实际案例，并针对复杂的翻译问题提供解决方案。
完成课程后，学生将建立专业作品集，展示其处理多样化视听翻译项目的专业能力。','This course explores the theoretical foundations and practical skills of audiovisual translation in modern media environments. Students will develop professional competencies in subtitling, dubbing, audio description and multimedia localization through hands-on practice with industry-standard software. The course covers technical specifications, multidimensional constraints, and cultural adaptation strategies specific to audiovisual content.
Topics include translation methods for various types of audiovisual materials, accessibility principles, and development trends in streaming platforms. Through project-based learning, students will participate in shooting, editing and producing audiovisual materials, apply theoretical knowledge to real-world cases, and develop solutions for complex translation challenges.
By course completion, students will have created a professional portfolio demonstrating their ability to handle diverse audiovisual translation projects.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
