(103369,'TRA6114','西学东渐与中国的现代化','','TRA - Translation','6114','T',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2','NIL','NIL','本课程旨在帮助学生从殖民、后殖民和全球化的角度理解中国翻译西方的实践。通过查阅明末至今主要译者和译作的相关文献，学生将捋顺中国翻译实践发展的脉络。本课程采用一系列解释框架，为学生提供理论基础，用于近代早期到当代的汉译研究，以践行中国摆脱西方现代性、建设中国式现代化的承诺。','This course is designed to help students understand the Chinese experiences of translating the West from colonial, postcolonial, and globalized perspectives. Through examining relevant literatures on the major translators and translations from the late Ming to the present and students are expected to discern the thread that binds all the translational efforts together. By resorting to a number of interpretive frameworks, this course will provide students with a theoretical foundation upon which to conduct research on Chinese translation from the early modern to the contemporary period, which carries the promise of China moving away from Western modernity to build a modernity with Chinese characteristics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103370,'TRA6115','中国翻译理论研究','','TRA - Translation','6115','T',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2','','','本课程旨在帮助学生了解中西方对翻译的不同观点。通过阅读相关历史背景下的主要文本及其文本解析，学生可学习中国翻译话语的传统，识别其显著特征，审视其发展过程中停滞和动态发展的重要时刻，并批判性地反思其现实意义。本课程与《西方翻译理论》相辅相成，共同为学生夯实基础，在此基础上开展比较研究、探索摆脱当代西方理论模式的可能性，培养对翻译和跨文化交流独立思考的能力。','This course is designed to help students understand both ancient and modern Chinese views and ideas on translation in comparison with those of the West. Through the reading of primary texts and the analysis of these texts in their historical contexts, students are encouraged to develop a sense of the Chinese tradition of discourse on translation, identify its distinctive features, examine important moments of disruption and dynamic growth, and reflect critically on the contemporary relevance of such a heritage. This course works in tandem with “Western Translation Theory” to provide students with a sound foundation upon which to conduct comparative studies, explore possibilities of moving away from contemporary Western models of theorization, and develop their own thinking about translation and intercultural exchange.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
