2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在为城市研究项目提供入门指导和学习路线图。课程将介绍城市研究领域的关键问题、概念、理论和争论，探讨城市对现代社会的重要性，以及经济发展、城市化、郊区化、规划、治理、人口迁移、文化、环境变化和社会不平等如何塑造城市。课程采用多学科视角，并结合国际和中国案例，帮助学生理解城市问题的产生、解读和解决方式。课程结束时，学生应具备城市研究领域的扎实基础，能够将学术文献与现实世界的城市问题联系起来。','This course is designed as an introduction and a road map for the Urban Studies programme. The course introduces key questions, concepts, theories, and debates in urban studies. It examines why cities matter to modern societies and how cities are shaped by economic development, urbanisation, suburbanisation, planning, governance, migration, culture, environmental change, and social inequality. The course draws on multidisciplinary perspectives and uses both international and Chinese examples to help students understand how urban problems are produced, interpreted, and addressed. By the end of the course, students should have a broad foundation for further study in urban studies and should be able to connect academic literature with real-world urban issues.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
