2026-27 Term 1','None','','本课程讨论复杂的城市问题，并结合政策制定，从而建立更具可持续性的城市。它介绍城市化进程中城市面临的常见问题，并运用公共政策理论来考虑对这些问题的不同解读和解决方案。 学生将使用不同的分析技术来研究这些多层面的问题。课程还探究针对复杂城市问题的当代实践和解决方案。学生们将站在城市政策制定者和治理过程中其它角色的视角理解并体悟不同的观点，从而达到求同存异，不避免冲突也不谋求一致。','This course discusses complex urban problems and integrates policy making to build more sustainable cities. It introduces common problems faced in cities over time as part of urbanisation processes and utilises theories in public policy to consider different interpretations of these problems and solutions to the problems. Students will use different analytical techniques to study these multifaceted problems. Then, some contemporary practices and solutions designed to resolve complex urban problems are examined. Students will be invited to imagine themselves in the situation of other actors in the urban policy making and governance process so as to understand and empathise with different perspectives in a way that seeks agreement without avoiding conflict nor striving for consensus.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
