2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','N/A','N/A','在以快速技术变革、经济转型和全球化为特征的全球经济中，城市和区域的经济发展正变得越来越重要。本课程探讨城市和区域的动态和挑战，特别强调粤港澳大湾区、中国和亚太地区的可持续发展。主要议题包括大城市区域治理、协同治理、跨境合作、城市管理和治理中的公众参与以及现代化的公共服务。','The economic development of cities and regions is becoming increasingly important in a global economy characterised by rapid technological change, transforming economies and globalisation. This course examines urban and regional dynamics and challenges, with special emphasis on sustainable development in Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, China and Pacific-Asia. Key topics include the governance of megacity region, collaborative governance, cross-border cooperation, public participation and engagement in urban management and governance, and modernisation of public service delivery.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103384,'URB5210','城市环境政策与管理','','URB - Urban Studies','5210','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','no prerequisites','no Co-requisites','本课程聚焦于城市环境政策与管理的制定与研究，旨在剖析城市核心环境问题，梳理环境政策制定的关键理论体系——涵盖政府监管与经济激励等机制。课程将探讨公共与商业领域实施的政策措施类型，并通过与中国密切相关的案例分析环境问题及应对政策，同时兼顾其他全球城市的实践经验。','This course focuses both on how to make and how to study urban environmental policy and management. It will identify key environmental problems in urban areas and review major theories related to the formulation of environmental policies, including government regulation and economic incentives. This course discusses the types of policy measures implemented in various public and business sectors. The discussion of environmental problems and policies will focus on examples that are relevant for China and will also include the experience of other global cities.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103385,'URB5220','资源评估与规划','','URB - Urban Studies','5220','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','城市及其日益增长的资源需求威胁着全球资源安全。本课程将回顾可持续城市资源管理中的概念理论和实践案例。课程将教授学生一套基本的用于资源评估和规划的定量和定性分析方法，并通过案例实践帮助学生们初步掌握该方法。学生还将了解影响资源规划和使用政策以及政策评估方法。','Cities and their growing resource demands threaten global resource security. This course reviews concepts, theories, processes for achieving sustainable urban resource management. The course provides students with a basic toolkit of quantitative and qualitative techniques used in resource evaluation and planning, together with case studies with which to gain experience of their application. Students will also gain knowledge of local, regional and global directives affecting resource use, and approaches to policy evaluation.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103386,'URB5310','城市发展与全球化','','URB - Urban Studies','5310','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','','','发展与全球化是相互关联的历史进程，深刻改变了城市、区域、国家、市场以及人们的日常生活。然而，全球化并未使世界变得“平坦”；相反，它导致了在增长、不平等、人口流动、治理模式及城市变迁等方面呈现出的不均衡格局。本课程将介绍发展研究与国际政治经济学领域的核心理论及相关争论，涵盖依附理论、世界体系分析、新自由主义、“全球化工程”以及发展型国家等议题。随后，课程将探讨全球经济一体化、消费、人口迁移、基础设施、技术、不平等、可持续性、全球性疫情、反全球化思潮及民粹主义如何塑造当代的城市与区域。通过分析来自“全球北方”和“全球南方”的案例，本课程旨在帮助学生建立对全球城市发展及主要城市挑战的批判性与比较性认知。','Development and globalisation are interrelated historical processes that have transformed cities, regions, states, markets, and everyday life. However, globalisation has not made the world “flat”. Instead, it has produced uneven patterns of growth, inequality, mobility, governance, and urban change. The course introduces key theories and debates in development studies and international political economy, including dependency theory, world-systems analysis, neoliberalism, the globalisation project, and the developmental state. It then examines how global economic integration, consumption, migration, infrastructure, technology, inequality, sustainability, pandemics, anti-globalisation, and populism shape contemporary cities and regions. Using cases from both the Global North and the Global South, the course helps students develop a critical and comparative understanding of global urban development and major global urban challenges.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103387,'URB5320','住房与土地管理','','URB - Urban Studies','5320','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1','No Prerequisites','No co-requisites','住房与土地是城市空间生产的关键问题，城市发展根植于土地和资本，多学科的城市理论可以应用于中国城市住房与土地问题的讨论。随着中国改革开放后住房与土地市场发展，城市住房与土地产权成为理解大规模住房与土地开发的出发点。本课程聚焦于中国和国际住房与土地制度结构和管理实践，考察住房与土地管理与国家发展模式、公共政策及城市规划的关系。课程第一部分考察中国城市住房管理体制的演变，包括计划经济时期住房的提供，改革时期的住房体制改革及其公平性，户籍改革与流动人口住房问题，公共住房体系的建设及其实施效应，住房政策的国际经验、住房与土地体制之间的关系等问题。课程第二部分考察土地管理与政策，包括国际土地管理的经验，中国“以土地谋发展”的城市化模式，工业与商住土地配置与利用，传统农村土地制度与管理，土地发展权转移与交易等问题， 课程第三部分考察城市更新的国际经验和中国实践，并进一步讲解城市更新的创新模式。','The questions of land and housing are essential to the analysis of the production of urban space. Urban development is rooted in the nexus of land and capital, and in this line of inquiry, urban theories from different disciplines can be brought into engaged dialogue with the Chinese context. After the establishment of land and housing markets in the reform era, property rights has been recognised as an important lens for comprehending the feverish pursuit of land and housing development, and associated conflicts and problems in Chinese cities. This course covers the institutional structure and management of housing and land both for China and for some major countries. It aims to provide students with a broad understanding of how housing and land management works and the role of national development model, public policy and planning in shaping China’s housing and land development. The first part of the course examines urban housing development and management in China. These include topics such as: housing provision in plan era and the transition in reform period, housing finance, Hukou reform and migrant housing, public housing and policy implementation, international housing policies as well as housing property rights and land development. The second part of the class focuses on land management and policies. These include topics such as international land management experiences, China’s land-based industrial and urbanization model, industrial versus residential & commercial land use, rural land property rights and management, transferrable land development rights. The third part of the class engages urban land redevelopment issues drawing on international experiences and domestic practices.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103388,'URB5330','交通、经济与政策','','URB - Urban Studies','5330','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 1
