2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','本课程的目的是让学生对城市背景下气候变化的话语有更广泛和全面的理解。课程也鼓励学生跨越学科壁垒，开展与城市和气候变化相关的深入讨论。课程探讨的关键主题包括城市发展和气候变化、城市能源和能源效率、气候治理、城市气象、未来气候变化的影响、低碳城市、城市碳管理等。','The aim of this course is to introduce students to a wider and comprehensive understanding of the climate change discourse in the urban context. It also seeks to encourage students to cut across their disciplinary barriers to develop a deep discussion related to the cities and climate change discourse. Key themes to be explored include urban development and climate change, urban energy and energy efficiency, governance, urban meteorology, the impacts of future climate change, low-carbon cities, carbon management in cities, etc.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103391,'URB5360','城市灾害风险与管理','','URB - Urban Studies','5360','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','N/A','N/A','快速城市化的一个结果是城市人口的增加，这些人口会经常受到灾害事件的影响，结果导致人口和基础设施更加脆弱。本课程带领学生了解城市灾害脆弱性的广泛因素，并为评估和管理与城市灾害政策和规划相关的社会和政治进程奠定基础。课程首先概述城市灾害风险、脆弱性和恢复力，然后重点介绍灾害制度、政策和政治。','An outcome of rapid urbanisation has been the expansion of urban populations which are frequently affected by disaster events. It results in an increased vulnerability of populations and infrastructure. This course provides students with an understanding of the breadth of factors that give rise to urban disaster vulnerability and a foundation for assessing and managing the social and political processes associated with urban disaster policy and planning. It will begin with an overview of urban disaster risk, vulnerability, resilience and then focus on disaster institutions, policy, and politics.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103392,'URB5370','城市学专题研讨会','','URB - Urban Studies','5370','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','N/A','本课程聚焦于中国及世界各大文明中城市规划、设计与建设的历史演变。课程选取不同地域和时期的代表性城市为例，探讨植根于当地文化、政治、社会及地理环境中的规划理念、实践及其所形成的城市形态。通过结合城市史、建筑史与考古学的视角，学生将深入了解城市实体形态的形成与变迁过程，以及这些形态所蕴含的文化与政治意义。此外，课程还将采用比较研究的方法，引导学生探讨不同文明与时代如何孕育出各具特色的城市类型，并思考历史经验如何为当代的城市发展提供启示。','This course focuses on the historical development of urban planning, design, and construction in China and major civilisations across the world. Using representative cities in different regions at different times as examples, this course examines the planning philosophies and practices and the resulting urban forms rooted in the local cultural, political, social, and geographical contexts. Drawing upon urban history, architectural history, and archaeology, students will be able to see how the physical forms of cities have come into being and changed over time, and what cultural and political meanings the urban forms bear. Adopting a comparative perspective, students will engage in discussions around how different civilisations and eras gave birth to different types of cities and how the historical experiences can inform current urban development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103393,'URB5380','专题研究','','URB - Urban Studies','5380','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2022-23 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Complete a semester of course work with satisfying academic performances in accordance with the university regulations and programme requirements.','URB5030 Social Science Research Methods','在修读该门课程之前，学生须至少已修读一个学期其它课程，且成绩符合大学规定和课程要求，学术表现令人满意。 在导师的指导监督下，学生应使用从课堂上学到的知识来独立开展与自己所选方向相关的并具有理论和实践意义的研究项目。学生应在项目报告中展示他们的实质知识、理论能力、分析能力和写作能力。学生应征得导师同意。','This course is designed for students who have completed a semester of course work with satisfying academic performances in accordance with the university regulations and programme requirements. Students conduct an independent research project on selected topics in urban studies under the supervision of a faculty member. Students are expected to use what they have learned from classes to conduct a research project pertinent to their concentration in the field of urban studies with both theoretical and empirical significance. They should demonstrate their substantive knowledge, theoretical competence, analytic skill, and writing capabilities in their project reporting. Approval from instructors is required.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103394,'URB5390','创意城市与文化产业','','URB - Urban Studies','5390','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程从特定的文化、经济和社会政治背景出发，探讨中国创意城市和文化产业的发展。课程将分析广义文化（尤其是艺术、遗产和流行文化）与商业之间错综复杂的互动关系，并深入探讨电影电视产业、文化遗产旅游和大型活动等多种商业模式。课程将文化研究和遗产研究的基础理论与城市研究相结合，回顾代表性案例，并考察与文化产业和创意城市相关的政策、规划和治理。由此，本课程将全面深入地评估创意城市的解读和实施方式，以及如何利用文化产业促进可持续和包容性的城市发展。','This course examines the creative cities and cultural industries in China in terms of their development within specific cultural, economic, and socio-political contexts. It analyses the complex interplay between the broadly defined culture, particularly art, heritage, and popular culture, and commerce through a wide range of ways, such as the film and television industry, heritage tourism, and mega-events. The lectures will connect the foundational theories in cultural studies and heritage studies to urban studies, review representative case studies, and investigate the policy, planning, and governance in relation to cultural industries and creative cities. The course will therefore provide a comprehensive and in-depth evaluation of how creative cities can be interpreted and implemented, and how cultural industries can be leveraged for sustainable and inclusive urban development.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103395,'URB5410','城市分析学','','URB - Urban Studies','5410','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','n.a.','','本课程旨在让学生全面了解城市环境中数据分析的原理、方法和应用。课程涵盖以城市交通、智慧城市、社会动态和环境可持续性为代表的广泛主题。在整个课程中，学生将参与实践练习、案例研究和小组项目，将他们的知识和技能应用到现实世界的城市问题中。学生将学习如何从各种城市数据集（包括地理空间数据、传感器数据、社交媒体数据和行政记录）中提取有意义的见解。完成本课程后，学生将掌握应对城市挑战所需的分析工具和技术，为城市规划、政策制定、交通管理和其他相关领域的循证决策做出贡献。','This course is designed to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of the principles, methods, and applications of data analytics in the context of urban environments. The course covers a wide range of topics represented by urban transportation, smart cities, social dynamics, and environmental sustainability. Throughout the course, students will engage in hands-on exercises, case studies, and group projects to apply their knowledge and skills to real-world urban problems. Students will learn how to extract meaningful insights from diverse urban datasets, including geospatial data, sensor data, social media data, and administrative records. Upon completion of this course, students will be equipped with the analytical tools and techniques necessary to tackle urban challenges and contribute to evidence-based decision-making in urban planning, policy development, transportation management, and other related fields.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103396,'URB5420','城市数字化：建设可持续韧性城市','','URB - Urban Studies','5420','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 1
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','There is no prerequisites for this course. Relevant knowledge in GIS is highly recommended.','There is no co-requisites for this course.','在城市研究领域，"数字城市 "和 "数字治理 "的呼声日益高涨，城市环境和进程必须实现数字化，以支持可持续发展和具有复原力的城市的发展。本课程涵盖广泛的主题和方法，让学生掌握调查城市建筑环境和动态所需的基本知识和技能，并将其转化为从二维矢量/栅格到三维模型的数字数据，以便进行管理、可视化和分析。学生将通过一系列实践练习、课程阅读和讨论，熟练掌握如何在实际应用中使用这些数字表征的技术和理论，以促进城市的可持续性和复原力。该课程将帮助下一代规划师驾驭复杂的城市环境，打造可持续发展和具有复原力的社区。','The course is specifically developed in response to the increasing call of “Digital City” and “Digital Governance” in the field of urban studies, which necessitate the digitalization of urban environment and processes to support the development of sustainable and resilient cities. This course covers a wide range of topics and methods to equip students with the essential knowledge and skills required to survey the urban built-environment and dynamics, and transform them into digital data, ranging from 2D vectors/rasters to 3D models, for management, visualization, and analysis. Students will gain proficiency in both techniques and theories regarding how such digital representations is used in real-world applications to promote urban sustainability and resilience through a set of hands-on excercises, course readings, and discussions. The course empowers next generation of planners to navigate the complexities of urban environment and shape sustainable and resilient communities.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103397,'URB5430','城市空间分析与规划','','URB - Urban Studies','5430','U',3.00,5000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','公共政策学院','公共政策学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2023-24 Term 2
2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','Students better have some basic knowledge about Python programming and statistics.','There is no co-requisites for this course, but it is recommended that students gain certain basic skills in Geographic Information System (GIS), Python, and statistics together with this course.','本课程旨在探索空间分析技术的交叉点及其在城市规划和政策领域的应用。课程通过授课、实践练习和实际案例研究相结合的方式，让学生深入了解用于分析空间数据和做出明智规划决策的理论、方法和实用工具。特别是，学生将掌握必要的技术：1）通过空间统计和制图总结空间现象；2）通过聚类分析和热点分析等方法评估空间模式；3）通过各种空间建模了解事件。此外，还将介绍其他相关概念和技术。课程结束时，学生将能够运用数据驱动方法，为规划决策和行动提供信息和依据，为建设充满活力的宜居城市做出贡献。','This course is designed to explore the intersection for spatial analysis techniques and their application in the realm of urban planning and policy. The course provides students with a deep understanding of the theories, methods, and practical tools used to analyze spatial data and make informed planning decisions through a combination of lectures, hands-on excercises, and real-world case studies. Particularly, students will be equipped with the necessary techniques to 1) summarize spatial phenomenon with spatial statistics and mapping; 2) assess spatial patterns with approaches such as clustering analysis and hot-spot analysis; 3) understand events with varied spatial modeling. Other related concepts and techniques will also be introduced. By the end of the course, students will be able to employ data-driven approaches to inform and shape planning decisions and actions contributing to the development of vibrant and livable cities.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103398,'URB6010','城市研究与政策高级研讨会','','URB - Urban Studies','6010','U',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 2','N/A','N/A','本课程对城市和社会进行跨学科研究，重点关注城市发展和治理的社会、经济、文化和环境层面。学生将获得城市研究和政策的主要概念框架和专题领域的基础知识。课程采用研讨会的形式，旨在让学生积极主动地合作学习。课程内容包括国际和国内问题以及城市研究的跨学科方法。','This course offers an interdisciplinary examination of cities and society focusing on social, economic, cultural, and environmental dimensions of urban development and governance. Students will gain a foundational knowledge of key conceptual frameworks and topical areas of urban studies and policy. The course employs a seminar format designed to engage students in active and collaborative learning. International and domestic issues and interdisciplinary approaches to urban studies are included.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103399,'URB6020','社会科学研究方法与设计','','URB - Urban Studies','6020','U',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
