(103400,'URB6030','城市经济与发展','','URB - Urban Studies','6030','U',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程运用严谨的微观经济理论与实证分析方法，考察塑造城市经济发展的各种力量。学生将接触有关城市增长的决定因素、空间经济结构以及影响城市繁荣的政策框架等方面的前沿研究。核心主题包括市场力量在城市形成与扩张中的作用、城市土地利用模式、住房市场动态与可负担性，以及城市交通系统经济学。本课程既强调理论建模，也注重对实证证据的批判性评估，使学生能够分析城市如何演变，以及公共政策如何影响城市发展轨迹。修完本课程，学生将具备开展城市经济问题原创性研究的能力，并能够参与关于促进公平、高效和可持续城市发展的政策讨论。','This course applies rigorous microeconomic theory and empirical analysis to examine the forces shaping urban economic development. Students will engage with cutting-edge research on the determinants of city growth, spatial economic structures, and the policy frameworks that influence urban prosperity. Core topics include the role of market forces in the formation and expansion of cities, urban land use patterns, housing market dynamics and affordability, and the economics of urban transportation systems. The course emphasizes both theoretical modelling and the critical evaluation of empirical evidence, enabling students to analyze how cities evolve and how public policies affect development trajectories. By the end of the course, students will be equipped to conduct original research on urban economic issues and to contribute to policy debates on fostering equitable, efficient, and sustainable urban growth.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103401,'URB6040','城市研究应用统计','','URB - Urban Studies','6040','U',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程旨在帮助学生掌握统计学的核心概念与方法，用于城市研究及其他社会科学领域中实验研究与相关性研究的设计、分析和报告写作。课程着重培养三方面能力：选对分析方法、读懂复杂的统计结果、审慎检验统计假设是否成立。内容涵盖描述性统计与假设检验、统计功效与效应量、相关分析与多元回归，并教授如何用 Stata 实现可复现的研究流程。修完本课程，学生将能够独立设计严谨的研究方案、处理复杂数据，并清晰呈现研究结果，为发表论文和撰写学位论文打下扎实基础。','This course equips students with the core statistical concepts and tools needed to design, analyze, and report experimental and correlational research in urban studies and other social sciences. Em-phasis is placed on selecting appropriate analytical techniques, interpreting complex output, and crit-ically evaluating statistical assumptions. Topics include descriptive statistics and hypothesis testing; statistical power and effect size; correlation and multiple regression; and reproducible research prac-tices using Stata. Students will develop the analytical fluency needed to design rigorous studies, ana-lyze complex datasets, and communicate findings effectively for publication and dissertation work.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
