(103405,'URB6320','土地、住房与城市转型','','URB - Urban Studies','6320','U',3.00,6000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2026-27 Term 1','Ph.D Students in Urban Studies and Sustainable Development','NA','本课程考察土地与住房如何塑造中国的城市空间，将理论与政策实践相结合。课程梳理中国的住房制度变迁、产权制度、土地市场和城市更新，并与国际模式进行比较。具体内容包括户籍制度改革、公共住房、以土地为驱动的城市化、农村土地权益，以及开发权转移等议题。通过制度、经济和空间三重视角，学生将深入理解国家发展战略、规划与政策如何推动中国的城市转型。','This course examines land and housing’s role in shaping Chinese urban space, linking theory to pol-icy and practice. It explores China’s housing transition, property rights, land markets, and redevel-opment, comparing them with global models. Topics include Hukou reform, public housing, land-based urbanization, rural land rights, and transferable development rights. Students gain critical in-sight into how national development, planning, and policy drive China’s urban transformation through institutional, economic, and spatial lenses.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
