(103411,'URM2010','城市、社会与环境','Cities, Society and Environment','URM - Urban Management','2010','U',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程向学生介绍城市和环境研究这一跨学科领域，分为两个主要部分。第一部分介绍城市化进程和城市社会的本质，把城市视为社会经济、政治和生态系统，从而去了解城市生活的机制和演化。第二部分探讨人类社会与自然环境的相互作用，并设想向更可持续未来的转型。','This course provides an overview of the interdisciplinary field of urban and environmental studies, structured into two main sections. The first section focuses on the process of urbanization and the nature of urban society, examining cities as complex socio-economic, political, and ecological systems to understand the mechanisms and dynamics of urban life. The second section investigates the interplay between human society and the natural environment, envisioning the transition toward a more sustainable future.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103412,'URM2020','城市经济学','Urban Economics','URM - Urban Management','2020','U',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','','这门综合科目使用微观经济学工具来研究城市经济学的关键问题，主题包括城市发展的原因以及个人和企业如何选择地点、城市化的集聚效益、住房和土地使用如何影响城市的发展、污染和交通拥堵等城市外部性。','This comprehensive course uses the tools of microeconomics to study the key issues in Urban Economics. Topics include why cities grow and how individuals and firms choose their locations, agglomeration benefits from urbanization, how housing and land use affect the growth of cities, urban externalities such as pollution and traffic congestion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103413,'URM2030','统计分析及应用','Statistical Analysis and Application','URM - Urban Management','2030','U',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','N.A.','N.A.','本入门课程的主要目标是帮助学生掌握提出问题、收集相关数据、分析数据以及解读结果的技能，以理解现实世界中的问题。我们将介绍基本的统计概念和方法，强调数据收集与分析的原则。课程的重要部分将集中于统计学在日常生活中的应用，同时提供统计软件包的数据分析培训。
本课程分为两个主要部分：
I. 数据与描述：在这一部分中，我们将通过图表描述变量的分布及其之间的关系。我们还将讨论数据收集的方法，重点关注如何有效设计调查和实验，收集具有代表性的样本，并避免常见的偏误。
II. 概率与推断：我们将探讨如何进行统计推断。学生将学习如何根据样本数据对总体进行推论，并评估这些结论的可靠性。主要讨论的题目包括比例和总体均值差异的检验，以及卡方检验。','The primary goal of this introductory course is to equip students with the skills to pose questions, collect relevant data, analyze that data, and interpret the results to understand real-world problems. We will introduce fundamental statistical concepts and methods, emphasizing the principles of data collection and analysis. A significant portion of the course will focus on the application of statistics in everyday life, along with training in a statistical software package for data analysis.
This course is divided into two major parts:
I. Data and Description: In this section, we will explore graphical and numerical summaries to describe the distribution of a variable and the relationships between two variables. We will also cover data production, focusing on how to design effective surveys and experiments, collect representative samples, and avoid common biases.
II. Probability and Inference: we will utilize the language of probability and the properties of numerical summaries derived from random samples. Students will learn to draw conclusions about populations based on sample data and to assess the reliability of these conclusions. Topics will include tests for the difference of proportions and population means, as well as the Chi-Square test.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103414,'URM2040','城市管理地理信息系统的原理和应用','Principles and Application of GIS in Urban Management','URM - Urban Management','2040','U',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 1
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','There is no prerequisites for this course.','There is no prerequisites for this course.','本科目旨在使学生掌握在城市管理中使用地理信息系统（GIS）的基本知识和技能。科目涵盖一系列主题，包括： 1）基本的 GIS 原理，例如不同的数据模型、软体/硬体组成和投影； 2）创建、地理处理、分析和可视化地理空间数据的方法； 3）用于调查城市环境和动态的趋势方法和技术； 4）GIS在城市管理中的案例应用，如应急管理、参与式治理等。学生将通过各种科目活动充分利用科目材料，包括讲座、实践练习、课外阅读、和课堂讨论。','This course aims to equip students with the essential knowledge and skills related to the use of Geographic Information System (GIS) in urban management. The course covers a range of topics, including: 1) basic GIS principles, such as different data models, software/hardware components, and projection; 2. Methods to create, geo-process, analyze, and visualize geospatial data; 3) trending techniques and technologies used to survey urban environment and dynamics; 4) case applications of GIS in urban management, such as participatory governance and disaster management. Students will sufficiently engage with course materials through a variety of course activities, including lectures, hands-on exercises, ex-curriculum readings, and in-class discussion.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103415,'URM2110','城市遥感简介','Introduction to Urban Remote Sensing','URM - Urban Management','2110','U',3.00,2000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','N.A.','','本课程著重于应用于城市环境的遥感原理。本课程介绍学生使用航空照片和卫星影像作为分析和了解城市景观、基础设施和动态的重要资料来源。结合理论讨论、案例研究和实作练习，学生将对遥感在城市研究和管理中的应用和重要性有全面的了解。','This course focuses on the principles of remote sensing as applied to urban environment. The course introduces students to the use of aerial photographs and satellite images as essential data sources to analyze and understand urban landscapes, infrastructure, and dynamics. Through a combination of theoretical discussions, case studies, and hands-on exercises, students will develop a comprehensive understanding of the applications and significance of remote sensing in urban studies and management.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103416,'URM3010','城市可持续性','Urban Sustainability','URM - Urban Management','3010','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','NA','NA','本课程探讨当代城市面临的可持续性挑战以及应对这些挑战的策略。课程将涵盖城市可持续性的核心概念，包括经济、社会以及环境。学生将学习分析城市系统中的复杂互动，例如土地利用、交通、能源消耗、水资源管理、废物处理以及城市气候变化适应。课程将培养学生分析城市可持续性问题并提出创新解决方案的能力。','This course examines the sustainability challenges that contemporary cities face and the strategies employed to address these issues. It covers the core concepts of urban sustainability, including economy, society, and environment. Students will learn to analyze the complex interactions within urban systems, such as land use, transportation, energy consumption, water resource management, waste treatment, and urban climate change adaptation. The course is designed to develop students'' abilities to critically assess urban sustainability problems and devise innovative solutions.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103417,'URM3020','城市学研究方法','Research Methods for Urban Studies','URM - Urban Management','3020','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 2','','','本课程面向希望培养理解、批判和开展城市问题社会科学研究实践技能的本科生。本课程将通过实践操作，介绍城市研究必备的定性和定量方法，包括扎根理论、民族志、案例研究、调查、访谈、内容与话语分析以及统计分析等。学生将获得解读和批判研究发现的能力，并设计和执行自己的研究项目，以解决城市背景下的具体问题。','This course is designed for undergraduate students seeking to develop practical skills in understanding, critiquing, and conducting social science research on urban issues. This course provides a hands-on introduction to qualitative and quantitative methodologies essential for urban studies, including grounded theories, ethnography, case study, survey, interview, content and discourse analysis, statistical analysis and so on. Students will gain the ability to interpret and critique research, and to design and execute their own research projects addressing specific questions within urban contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103418,'URM3030','城市环境管理与政策','Urban Environmental Management and Policy','URM - Urban Management','3030','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','现场研究','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1','Nil.','Nil.','这门课程深入探讨人类活动对城市环境的影响。学生将研究各种环境问题、其起源以及导致这些问题持续存在的因素。此外，课程还涉及多种管理策略以及应对环境问题的政策过程中的挑战。通过全面理解这些主题，学生将培养必要的技能，以制定有效的方案来促进城市环境中的可持续发展和环境保护。','This course provides an in-depth examination of the impact of human activities on urban environment. Students will explore various environmental issues, their origins, and the factors that contribute to their persistence. Furthermore, the course delves into diverse management strategies and the challenges within policy processes aimed at addressing environmental concerns. By acquiring a comprehensive understanding of these topics, students will develop skills necessary to devise effective approaches for promoting sustainable development and environmental conservation in urban contexts.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103419,'URM3050','城市形态、设计与场所营造','Urban Form, Design and Place Making','URM - Urban Management','3050','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','ghost_outline_unavailable','',NULL,'','',NULL,NULL,'0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103420,'URM3110','城市历史与文化学','Urban History and Culture','URM - Urban Management','3110','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程探讨与人们的日常生活息息相关的城市历史、青年文化、流行文化和创意产业之间的动态关系。我们将关注都市人的经验和表达，研究他们的文化参与、媒体消费、创造力和行动主义如何影响当代城市景观。通过对关键主题的批判性分析，学生将参与讨论例如人文景观、青年亚文化、数字媒体在都市身份塑造中的作用、旅游业和创意经济，以及文化产业对城市空间的影响等。通过整合文化研究的观点，学生将更加深入理解年轻人对于城市历史和文化叙事的贡献和挑战。','This course explores the dynamic interplay between urban history, youth culture, popular culture, and the creative industries that shape people''s daily lives. Focusing on the experiences and expressions of urban residents, we will examine how their cultural participation, media consumption, creativity, and activism influence contemporary urban landscapes. Through critical analysis of key themes, students will engage in discussions such as the human landscape, youth subcultures, the role of digital media in urban identification, tourism and the creative economy, and the impact of cultural industries on urban spaces. By integrating perspectives from cultural studies, students will gain a nuanced appreciation of the ways in which young people contribute to and challenge the narratives of urban history and culture.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103421,'URM3120','人口、城市化与可持续性','Population, Urbanization and Sustainable Development','URM - Urban Management','3120','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2024-25 Term 2
2025-26 Term 2','non','non','本课程深入探讨人口动态、城市增长与可持续发展之间的关系。学生将熟悉基本的人口学概念、过程和方法。通过人口学视角，他们将探索关键城市化问题及可持续发展目标的成因、后果及其意义。课程结合理论框架与案例研究，帮助学生理解人口趋势、城市化与可持续发展实践之间的互动关联，促进能够实现韧性、公平和环保的城市空间的解决方案。','This course delves into the intersection of demographic dynamics, urban growth, and sustainable development. Students will become familiar with fundamental demographic concepts, processes, and methods. Through a demographic lens, they will explore the causes, consequences, and implication of critical urbanization issues and sustainable development goals. The course combines theoretical frameworks with case studies to help students understand the interplay between demographic trends, urbanization, and sustainable practices, fostering solutions that promote resilient, equitable, and environmentally sustainable urban spaces.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103422,'URM3140','城市交通运输系统','Urban Transportation System','URM - Urban Management','3140','U',3.00,3000,'Major','已评分','现场研究','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N.A','N.A','本课程深入探讨城市运输问题，并考虑其对社会、经济及环境的影响。学生将学习各种促进可持续社区发展的交通政策、项目和工具。课程主要关注城市地区个人出行和可达性相关的挑战与机遇。通过本课程，学生将全面了解构建高效且可持续城市交通系统的复杂性及相关策略。','This course provides an in-depth exploration of urban transportation issues, considering their social, economic, and environmental implications. Students will be introduced to various transport policies, programs, and tools aimed at fostering sustainable communities. The primary focus is on examining the challenges and opportunities associated with personal mobility and accessibility within urban areas. Through this course, students will gain a comprehensive understanding of the complexities and strategies involved in developing efficient and sustainable urban transportation systems.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103423,'URM4010','智慧城市管理','Smart Cities and Management','URM - Urban Management','4010','U',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','讲演','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','','','本课程探讨技术与数据驱动下城市系统在核心领域的转型。课程重点包括透明治理、可持续交通、技术公平与效率之间的张力，以及隐私伦理等议题。学生将学习批判性分析上述问题对公民参与、公平获取资源及社区福祉的影响。通过社会学视角，课程将围绕治理、交通、环境、经济、生活和人口六大关键领域展开分析。基于以人为本的跨学科研究方法，学生将学习评估智慧城市生活的机遇与挑战。','This course examines the transformation of urban systems in core sectors enabled by technologies and data. Key topics include transparent governance, sustainable mobility, the tension between technology fairness and efficiency, and privacy ethics. Students will critically examine how these issues affect citizen participation, equitable access, and community well-being. Through social science perspectives, we will analyze smart cities across key domains including governance, mobility, environment, economy, living, and people. Using a human-centered, interdisciplinary approach, students will learn to assess both the opportunities and challenges of smart urban living.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,''),
(103424,'URM4030','城市管理与公共政策','Urban Management and Public Policy','URM - Urban Management','4030','U',3.00,4000,'Major','已评分','现场研究','Main Campus','人文社科学院','人文社科学院','saved_outline','saved_terms','2025-26 Term 1
2026-27 Term 1','N/A','','本科目将讨论公共政策在城市研究和管理这一主题中的关键作用，特别关注城市化和发展，以及围绕城市化过程的一系列问题，从城市化如何发生，到如何从公共政策视角来平衡不平等与经济发展。本科目涵盖几个主要城市公共政策领域的理论和实践，并探讨这些理论如何将城市概念化为一个研究领域，以及这些理论如何帮助理解全球范围内的城市公共政策实践。','This course will discuss the critical role of public policies in the topic of urban studies and management, with a specific attention on the urbanization and development, and a series of questions surrounding the process of urbanization, from how urbanization happened, to how to balance the inequality and the economic development in a public policy perspective. This course covers theories and practices of several major urban public policy areas and examines how the theories conceptualize city as a field of study and how these theories help to understand urban public policy practices around the globe.','0','0','seed:build_edu_seed','2026-11-15 00:00:00','',NULL,'');

